e non-2xx test lacked a text() method,\nwhich the source code calls to build the error message -- this was\nmasking a real test failure as a mock shape bug, caught when CI\nactually ran it for real (not just the local dev environment where it\nwas previously assumed pre-existing/unrelated).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(api): stub platform-admin auth middleware in full-app integration tests\n\nmodules.test.ts and view-configs.test.ts are the only two integration\ntests that boot the full app.ts router tree via createApp(), and both\nexhaustively mock @platform/auth. PR1 added platform-admin routes to\napp.ts, so the mock needs requirePlatformAdmin/requirePlatformAdminIdentity\nstubs too, same no-op pattern already used there for requireActingPerson.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(auth): address prabhuvijit''s pr#803 good-to-fix review findings\n\nFour non-blocking items from his review:\n- verifyMfaCode: documented the INCR-based attempt counter''s known\n  concurrency bound rather than rewriting with a Lua script\n- requirePlatformAdmin: new test proving an sk_... API key is rejected,\n  since resolvePlatformAdmin has no API-key path at all\n- outbound-dispatch.ts: clear the cached Novu token on a 401 so the\n  next call re-fetches instead of retrying the same rejected token\n- hasMfaFactor: doc comment now explains it is currently dormant and\n  cross-references requirePlatformAdmin''s own explanation\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(api): address prabhuvijit''s pr#804 good-to-fix review findings\n\nTighten MFA code validation to digits-only (regex, not just length) so\nnon-numeric input never wastes a lockout attempt. Wrap the provisioning\nqueue enqueue in try/catch, returning 503 instead of an unhandled 500\nwhen Redis/BullMQ is unavailable.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(db): seed one automation rule per remaining core module\n\nExtend the raw-SQL automation-rule seeding pattern already used by\nhelpdesk/tender/vendor-approval to the 6 core modules that previously\nshipped none: crm, hrms, reimbursements, projects, invoicing,\nprocurement. Each gets one set_field default-on-creation rule, gated\nby a conditions check (field currently null) rather than firing\nunconditionally.\n\nAdd a coverage-guard test that validates every module-seeded\nautomation rule''s actions JSON against the real ActionConfigSchema,\nclosing the \"no automated check for seed SQL\" gap called out in\nhelpdesk''s own seed file comment (the gap that let a wrong action\nshape ship silently until #126 caught it by hand).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(worker): stop persisting sandbox default password in redis job result\n\nAddress PrabhuVijit''s CHANGES_REQUESTED review on PR #804:\n\n- Must fix: processSandboxProvisioningJob no longer returns\n  defaultPassword as part of the BullMQ job result. BullMQ''s\n  removeOnComplete kept that return value in Redis for 1h, and nothing\n  in the codebase reads a sandbox job''s returnvalue -- it was a\n  plaintext secret sitting in Redis with zero application retrieval\n  path (T21''s real handover store lands downstream). Replaced with a\n  WARN-level structured log as the interim retrieval channel.\n- CreateSandboxSchema now rejects an all-symbol orgName, closing a bug\n  where slugify() could produce a leading-dash-only slug.\n- Audit-trail tests now assert actorId on every success/failure path.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(api): key sandbox handover route on job id, not tenant id\n\nAddress PrabhuVijit''s re-review #3 (CHANGES_REQUESTED) on PR #805:\n\n- Must fix: GET /platform-admin/sandboxes/:tenantId/handover was\n  unreachable from any real client -- the caller only ever receives\n  jobId (from the initial POST and the progress endpoint), never the\n  internal tenant UUID. Changed the route to :jobId; the handler looks\n  up the job row by its own id and reads resultTenantId internally.\n- storeSandboxHandoverCredentials wrapped in its own try/catch so a\n  transient Redis write failure at the last step doesn''t fail an\n  otherwise-fully-successful provisioning run.\n- zitadelOrgId is now written on the success path (was always NULL).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqx277CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAEyIQAJbxA4SV1igNsTfjEA1Fw8FC\ndxlhdAHKu//k+7anp5G2w5lN9xcnFgf/D+V53TTMB8nkF8Djrwe0ZflwnWASuwHD\nXRFJf4SS8vvCti3LzQvaKQBYOkcQ7vcazAUIendmtO1/evDeioemLPh/zSsr6cQ2\nDwhMDsqyS/b01r0vTKZ3QRVk4Z2nXLwxjXZZnB47Hmz4Z6gnijp+qpk9820lokGD\n7SDYn4rswTdm2awM8QaaQKk5827zi9S/+7fIbrpyzUSf86esZ193F+2LQgzNlyup\ny97JBvwqSmwHvYhcFT5qV3pOnFJPUIblvCsW6LApEj+le8WdyW4b0fbjMTSL8sfB\nd7f/5U1PABJAw/YwM6Cs3BWl3ot+fD8W0+YzORBafBCM1Jc7jixJ0xEP7gO9NR9u\npHy2SFYu3Zz5emK4jQkYzAaK6pCKapRm7qAS6WZJmYOW5vxzaFZAwG2EMKlaOB11\nohGlTcjHTFxsMyERq0Xw8cZw6I43J7u2budh0YC/+sKlIhv95TsU9YJ0VniNJiLV\nB67ZeZuaCLIfygET1vcKRps2G3FeImySi0/Ksz6BVWqQLEaiAtWOibmXRa6ZzxjY\nEBa/x+P9EY41QjwOU5sL74C4itVvVCbLQquNQOx0NlZ53sjfOf9M9CqlzII1V4Yq\nZbUQ+phCj9j9RSt56XfS\n=3P6+\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-08T10:22:51Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commit/9feed5ce98cccf520dacb3236ed689931337f193","node_id":"C_kwDOScMdh9oAKDlmZWVkNWNlOThjY2NmNTIwZGFjYjMyMzZlZDY4OTkzMTMzN2YxOTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commit/5b710e1ccb776435a5a3ea2fda3334444264a29d","sha":"5b710e1ccb776435a5a3ea2fda3334444264a29d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/5b710e1ccb776435a5a3ea2fda3334444264a29d"}],"sha":"9feed5ce98cccf520dacb3236ed689931337f193","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/9feed5ce98cccf520dacb3236ed689931337f193"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/67047397?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TusharSharma991","id":67047397,"login":"TusharSharma991","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3MDQ3Mzk3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/5b710e1ccb776435a5a3ea2fda3334444264a29d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T10:00:21Z","email":"67047397+TusharSharma991@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Tushar Sharma"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T10:00:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(api): sandbox provisioning progress tracking and handover (phase 2) (#805)\n\n* feat(auth): platform-admin role, mfa, and sandbox foundation (phase 1)\n\nMulti-Org Sandbox System Phase 1 (docs/specs/multi-org-sandbox.md, ADR-022):\ncross-tenant platform_admin role, OpenWind-owned email-OTP MFA (Zitadel''s own\nMFA methods are unusable on this hosted instance), sandbox DTO allow-list,\nand per-admin sandbox quota. Security-reviewed; fixed a role-inheritance\nprivilege leak found during review (GRANT ... WITH INHERIT FALSE) and added\na regression isolation test against a real Postgres.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(auth): sandbox org template + provisioning job (phase 2)\n\nImplements T6/T7 of docs/specs/multi-org-sandbox.md: a fixed org template\nwith randomized realistic names and retry-on-collision account creation,\nand the BullMQ job that creates a Zitadel org + tenant row + seeded\naccounts and triggers the existing org-directory sync unmodified.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(api): sandbox provisioning progress tracking and handover (phase 2)\n\nImplements T8/T21 of docs/specs/multi-org-sandbox.md: a persisted\nsandbox_provisioning_jobs row tracks step-by-step progress so the\nwait-screen can poll instead of holding one request open, and a\ndedicated handover endpoint returns the seeded usernames and shared\npassword once provisioning completes.\n\nThe handover credentials live in Redis with a 7-day TTL rather than a\ndurable DB column -- security review found the original design let any\nplatform_admin recover every sandbox''s working password indefinitely,\na materially larger blast radius than intended.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(notifications): fix outbound-dispatch 500-status mock missing .text()\n\nThe mocked fetch Response for the non-2xx test lacked a text() method,\nwhich the source code calls to build the error message -- this was\nmasking a real test failure as a mock shape bug, caught when CI\nactually ran it for real (not just the local dev environment where it\nwas previously assumed pre-existing/unrelated).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(api): stub platform-admin auth middleware in full-app integration tests\n\nmodules.test.ts and view-configs.test.ts are the only two integration\ntests that boot the full app.ts router tree via createApp(), and both\nexhaustively mock @platform/auth. PR1 added platform-admin routes to\napp.ts, so the mock needs requirePlatformAdmin/requirePlatformAdminIdentity\nstubs too, same no-op pattern already used there for requireActingPerson.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(auth): address prabhuvijit''s pr#803 good-to-fix review findings\n\nFour non-blocking items from his review:\n- verifyMfaCode: documented the INCR-based attempt counter''s known\n  concurrency bound rather than rewriting with a Lua script\n- requirePlatformAdmin: new test proving an sk_... API key is rejected,\n  since resolvePlatformAdmin has no API-key path at all\n- outbound-dispatch.ts: clear the cached Novu token on a 401 so the\n  next call re-fetches instead of retrying the same rejected token\n- hasMfaFactor: doc comment now explains it is currently dormant and\n  cross-references requirePlatformAdmin''s own explanation\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(api): address prabhuvijit''s pr#804 good-to-fix review findings\n\nTighten MFA code validation to digits-only (regex, not just length) so\nnon-numeric input never wastes a lockout attempt. Wrap the provisioning\nqueue enqueue in try/catch, returning 503 instead of an unhandled 500\nwhen Redis/BullMQ is unavailable.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(worker): stop persisting sandbox default password in redis job result\n\nAddress PrabhuVijit''s CHANGES_REQUESTED review on PR #804:\n\n- Must fix: processSandboxProvisioningJob no longer returns\n  defaultPassword as part of the BullMQ job result. BullMQ''s\n  removeOnComplete kept that return value in Redis for 1h, and nothing\n  in the codebase reads a sandbox job''s returnvalue -- it was a\n  plaintext secret sitting in Redis with zero application retrieval\n  path (T21''s real handover store lands downstream). Replaced with a\n  WARN-level structured log as the interim retrieval channel.\n- CreateSandboxSchema now rejects an all-symbol orgName, closing a bug\n  where slugify() could produce a leading-dash-only slug.\n- Audit-trail tests now assert actorId on every success/failure path.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(api): key sandbox handover route on job id, not tenant id\n\nAddress PrabhuVijit''s re-review #3 (CHANGES_REQUESTED) on PR #805:\n\n- Must fix: GET /platform-admin/sandboxes/:tenantId/handover was\n  unreachable from any real client -- the caller only ever receives\n  jobId (from the initial POST and the progress endpoint), never the\n  internal tenant UUID. Changed the route to :jobId; the handler looks\n  up the job row by its own id and reads resultTenantId internally.\n- storeSandboxHandoverCredentials wrapped in its own try/catch so a\n  transient Redis write failure at the last step doesn''t fail an\n  otherwise-fully-successful provisioning run.\n- zitadelOrgId is now written on the success path (was always NULL).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ece52751cb1cb625d3ecd2d5d3ed2aa9e314a4b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/trees/ece52751cb1cb625d3ecd2d5d3ed2aa9e314a4b3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/commits/5b710e1ccb776435a5a3ea2fda3334444264a29d","verification":{"payload":"tree ece52751cb1cb625d3ecd2d5d3ed2aa9e314a4b3\nparent 241968b7c26bcaaba9508db45f064c34c19476e1\nauthor Tushar Sharma <67047397+TusharSharma991@users.noreply.github.com> 1791453621 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791453621 +0530\n\nfeat(api): sandbox provisioning progress tracking and handover (phase 2) (#805)\n\n* feat(auth): platform-admin role, mfa, and sandbox foundation (phase 1)\n\nMulti-Org Sandbox System Phase 1 (docs/specs/multi-org-sandbox.md, ADR-022):\ncross-tenant platform_admin role, OpenWind-owned email-OTP MFA (Zitadel''s own\nMFA methods are unusable on this hosted instance), sandbox DTO allow-list,\nand per-admin sandbox quota. Security-reviewed; fixed a role-inheritance\nprivilege leak found during review (GRANT ... WITH INHERIT FALSE) and added\na regression isolation test against a real Postgres.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(auth): sandbox org template + provisioning job (phase 2)\n\nImplements T6/T7 of docs/specs/multi-org-sandbox.md: a fixed org template\nwith randomized realistic names and retry-on-collision account creation,\nand the BullMQ job that creates a Zitadel org + tenant row + seeded\naccounts and triggers the existing org-directory sync unmodified.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(api): sandbox provisioning progress tracking and handover (phase 2)\n\nImplements T8/T21 of docs/specs/multi-org-sandbox.md: a persisted\nsandbox_provisioning_jobs row tracks step-by-step progress so the\nwait-screen can poll instead of holding one request open, and a\ndedicated handover endpoint returns the seeded usernames and shared\npassword once provisioning completes.\n\nThe handover credentials live in Redis with a 7-day TTL rather than a\ndurable DB column -- security review found the original design let any\nplatform_admin recover every sandbox''s working password indefinitely,\na materially larger blast radius than intended.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(notifications): fix outbound-dispatch 500-status mock missing .text()\n\nThe mocked fetch Response for the non-2xx test lacked a text() method,\nwhich the source code calls to build the error message -- this was\nmasking a real test failure as a mock shape bug, caught when CI\nactually ran it for real (not just the local dev environment where it\nwas previously assumed pre-existing/unrelated).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(api): stub platform-admin auth middleware in full-app integration tests\n\nmodules.test.ts and view-configs.test.ts are the only two integration\ntests that boot the full app.ts router tree via createApp(), and both\nexhaustively mock @platform/auth. PR1 added platform-admin routes to\napp.ts, so the mock needs requirePlatformAdmin/requirePlatformAdminIdentity\nstubs too, same no-op pattern already used there for requireActingPerson.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(auth): address prabhuvijit''s pr#803 good-to-fix review findings\n\nFour non-blocking items from his review:\n- verifyMfaCode: documented the INCR-based attempt counter''s known\n  concurrency bound rather than rewriting with a Lua script\n- requirePlatformAdmin: new test proving an sk_... API key is rejected,\n  since resolvePlatformAdmin has no API-key path at all\n- outbound-dispatch.ts: clear the cached Novu token on a 401 so the\n  next call re-fetches instead of retrying the same rejected token\n- hasMfaFactor: doc comment now explains it is currently dormant and\n  cross-references requirePlatformAdmin''s own explanation\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(api): address prabhuvijit''s pr#804 good-to-fix review findings\n\nTighten MFA code validation to digits-only (regex, not just length) so\nnon-numeric input never wastes a lockout attempt. Wrap the provisioning\nqueue enqueue in try/catch, returning 503 instead of an unhandled 500\nwhen Redis/BullMQ is unavailable.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(worker): stop persisting sandbox default password in redis job result\n\nAddress PrabhuVijit''s CHANGES_REQUESTED review on PR #804:\n\n- Must fix: processSandboxProvisioningJob no longer returns\n  defaultPassword as part of the BullMQ job result. BullMQ''s\n  removeOnComplete kept that return value in Redis for 1h, and nothing\n  in the codebase reads a sandbox job''s returnvalue -- it was a\n  plaintext secret sitting in Redis with zero application retrieval\n  path (T21''s real handover store lands downstream). Replaced with a\n  WARN-level structured log as the interim retrieval channel.\n- CreateSandboxSchema now rejects an all-symbol orgName, closing a bug\n  where slugify() could produce a leading-dash-only slug.\n- Audit-trail tests now assert actorId on every success/failure path.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(api): key sandbox handover route on job id, not tenant id\n\nAddress PrabhuVijit''s re-review #3 (CHANGES_REQUESTED) on PR #805:\n\n- Must fix: GET /platform-admin/sandboxes/:tenantId/handover was\n  unreachable from any real client -- the caller only ever receives\n  jobId (from the initial POST and the progress endpoint), never the\n  internal tenant UUID. Changed the route to :jobId; the handler looks\n  up the job row by its own id and reads resultTenantId internally.\n- storeSandboxHandoverCredentials wrapped in its own try/catch so a\n  transient Redis write failure at the last step doesn''t fail an\n  otherwise-fully-successful provisioning run.\n- zitadelOrgId is now written on the success path (was always NULL).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqx2m1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAApGUQALAw7SUmOFJRgxHGBRkuJUpK\nV0niEki1WNDt+yhiX7WW76DhMPk9vmVITk7yOemgzM/66fst1/2NjbXLCwWO9TCS\nMoJFzfU7I/AURVdPGRhaF3MfxiUTiFgrOtEs9wxKimUxjFD7W78FcOrhgAhGR1QW\neoIE+vjGbtHQmwJCKZ+MEYcyAdq4hPVdHSjoNxARah9IyuhQq5mJ8xw4jY3iYGY8\na9Wr7TNSWNVjXvy2DD+aSDpcf5zFwdORNRDjHLSiNxb4qSokacXNjpzYd2JWMdyF\nGn4GdJR5plbA9GjWzYgdLqMDZzk+X5arSlgfK8LPny2uczB6OqXt6tYBpikpOLxF\nHisbw7lowD9NwFUHqj1WFqD3RS0LDtxBX+zeMlZjHgXdcQyjWLw6IW1h0CyqYHLF\nP79V+ouBOiFPUIzBZwr6MNcNg8DMwoyYmAFTljKBOp+gpFgAF92zookFpNqrY4Mq\nGGBfr6FmRBstTqRcJnraVKuWRFRDC/MPjrAK6wAKEI/2bNcI9rAImcZHCdzhAUP2\nBUflOFzG9r6iCBsYmA3e7AYihE8ubC9KhAuEkICsEbrIegXytQHNsqQDMM9YKEfc\nVa+C7kUcV1Wp31MsQWTiSLwcmYAPd2rVW4Na/z9sCB6zZm+pOctlb7QOPswzjSdT\ng9T1MCCm9ffS+Tcz6Z+r\n=c69X\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-08T10:00:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commit/5b710e1ccb776435a5a3ea2fda3334444264a29d","node_id":"C_kwDOScMdh9oAKDViNzEwZTFjY2I3NzY0MzVhNWEzZWEyZmRhMzMzNDQ0NDI2NGEyOWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commit/241968b7c26bcaaba9508db45f064c34c19476e1","sha":"241968b7c26bcaaba9508db45f064c34c19476e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/241968b7c26bcaaba9508db45f064c34c19476e1"}],"sha":"5b710e1ccb776435a5a3ea2fda3334444264a29d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/5b710e1ccb776435a5a3ea2fda3334444264a29d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/67047397?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TusharSharma991","id":67047397,"login":"TusharSharma991","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3MDQ3Mzk3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/241968b7c26bcaaba9508db45f064c34c19476e1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T08:16:09Z","email":"67047397+TusharSharma991@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Tushar Sharma"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T08:16:09Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(auth): sandbox org template + provisioning job (phase 2) (#804)\n\n* feat(auth): platform-admin role, mfa, and sandbox foundation (phase 1)\n\nMulti-Org Sandbox System Phase 1 (docs/specs/multi-org-sandbox.md, ADR-022):\ncross-tenant platform_admin role, OpenWind-owned email-OTP MFA (Zitadel''s own\nMFA methods are unusable on this hosted instance), sandbox DTO allow-list,\nand per-admin sandbox quota. Security-reviewed; fixed a role-inheritance\nprivilege leak found during review (GRANT ... WITH INHERIT FALSE) and added\na regression isolation test against a real Postgres.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(auth): sandbox org template + provisioning job (phase 2)\n\nImplements T6/T7 of docs/specs/multi-org-sandbox.md: a fixed org template\nwith randomized realistic names and retry-on-collision account creation,\nand the BullMQ job that creates a Zitadel org + tenant row + seeded\naccounts and triggers the existing org-directory sync unmodified.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(notifications): fix outbound-dispatch 500-status mock missing .text()\n\nThe mocked fetch Response for the non-2xx test lacked a text() method,\nwhich the source code calls to build the error message -- this was\nmasking a real test failure as a mock shape bug, caught when CI\nactually ran it for real (not just the local dev environment where it\nwas previously assumed pre-existing/unrelated).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(api): stub platform-admin auth middleware in full-app integration tests\n\nmodules.test.ts and view-configs.test.ts are the only two integration\ntests that boot the full app.ts router tree via createApp(), and both\nexhaustively mock @platform/auth. PR1 added platform-admin routes to\napp.ts, so the mock needs requirePlatformAdmin/requirePlatformAdminIdentity\nstubs too, same no-op pattern already used there for requireActingPerson.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(auth): address prabhuvijit''s pr#803 good-to-fix review findings\n\nFour non-blocking items from his review:\n- verifyMfaCode: documented the INCR-based attempt counter''s known\n  concurrency bound rather than rewriting with a Lua script\n- requirePlatformAdmin: new test proving an sk_... API key is rejected,\n  since resolvePlatformAdmin has no API-key path at all\n- outbound-dispatch.ts: clear the cached Novu token on a 401 so the\n  next call re-fetches instead of retrying the same rejected token\n- hasMfaFactor: doc comment now explains it is currently dormant and\n  cross-references requirePlatformAdmin''s own explanation\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(api): address prabhuvijit''s pr#804 good-to-fix review findings\n\nTighten MFA code validation to digits-only (regex, not just length) so\nnon-numeric input never wastes a lockout attempt. Wrap the provisioning\nqueue enqueue in try/catch, returning 503 instead of an unhandled 500\nwhen Redis/BullMQ is unavailable.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(worker): stop persisting sandbox default password in redis job result\n\nAddress PrabhuVijit''s CHANGES_REQUESTED review on PR #804:\n\n- Must fix: processSandboxProvisioningJob no longer returns\n  defaultPassword as part of the BullMQ job result. BullMQ''s\n  removeOnComplete kept that return value in Redis for 1h, and nothing\n  in the codebase reads a sandbox job''s returnvalue -- it was a\n  plaintext secret sitting in Redis with zero application retrieval\n  path (T21''s real handover store lands downstream). Replaced with a\n  WARN-level structured log as the interim retrieval channel.\n- CreateSandboxSchema now rejects an all-symbol orgName, closing a bug\n  where slugify() could produce a leading-dash-only slug.\n- Audit-trail tests now assert actorId on every success/failure path.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f9550101a6fb828c9a88793d03ae2e045c70c04a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/trees/f9550101a6fb828c9a88793d03ae2e045c70c04a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/commits/241968b7c26bcaaba9508db45f064c34c19476e1","verification":{"payload":"tree f9550101a6fb828c9a88793d03ae2e045c70c04a\nparent ef4adacf40ee12acbf7638bd0d4d38654404b811\nauthor Tushar Sharma <67047397+TusharSharma991@users.noreply.github.com> 1791447369 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791447369 +0530\n\nfeat(auth): sandbox org template + provisioning job (phase 2) (#804)\n\n* feat(auth): platform-admin role, mfa, and sandbox foundation (phase 1)\n\nMulti-Org Sandbox System Phase 1 (docs/specs/multi-org-sandbox.md, ADR-022):\ncross-tenant platform_admin role, OpenWind-owned email-OTP MFA (Zitadel''s own\nMFA methods are unusable on this hosted instance), sandbox DTO allow-list,\nand per-admin sandbox quota. Security-reviewed; fixed a role-inheritance\nprivilege leak found during review (GRANT ... WITH INHERIT FALSE) and added\na regression isolation test against a real Postgres.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(auth): sandbox org template + provisioning job (phase 2)\n\nImplements T6/T7 of docs/specs/multi-org-sandbox.md: a fixed org template\nwith randomized realistic names and retry-on-collision account creation,\nand the BullMQ job that creates a Zitadel org + tenant row + seeded\naccounts and triggers the existing org-directory sync unmodified.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(notifications): fix outbound-dispatch 500-status mock missing .text()\n\nThe mocked fetch Response for the non-2xx test lacked a text() method,\nwhich the source code calls to build the error message -- this was\nmasking a real test failure as a mock shape bug, caught when CI\nactually ran it for real (not just the local dev environment where it\nwas previously assumed pre-existing/unrelated).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(api): stub platform-admin auth middleware in full-app integration tests\n\nmodules.test.ts and view-configs.test.ts are the only two integration\ntests that boot the full app.ts router tree via createApp(), and both\nexhaustively mock @platform/auth. PR1 added platform-admin routes to\napp.ts, so the mock needs requirePlatformAdmin/requirePlatformAdminIdentity\nstubs too, same no-op pattern already used there for requireActingPerson.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(auth): address prabhuvijit''s pr#803 good-to-fix review findings\n\nFour non-blocking items from his review:\n- verifyMfaCode: documented the INCR-based attempt counter''s known\n  concurrency bound rather than rewriting with a Lua script\n- requirePlatformAdmin: new test proving an sk_... API key is rejected,\n  since resolvePlatformAdmin has no API-key path at all\n- outbound-dispatch.ts: clear the cached Novu token on a 401 so the\n  next call re-fetches instead of retrying the same rejected token\n- hasMfaFactor: doc comment now explains it is currently dormant and\n  cross-references requirePlatformAdmin''s own explanation\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(api): address prabhuvijit''s pr#804 good-to-fix review findings\n\nTighten MFA code validation to digits-only (regex, not just length) so\nnon-numeric input never wastes a lockout attempt. Wrap the provisioning\nqueue enqueue in try/catch, returning 503 instead of an unhandled 500\nwhen Redis/BullMQ is unavailable.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(worker): stop persisting sandbox default password in redis job result\n\nAddress PrabhuVijit''s CHANGES_REQUESTED review on PR #804:\n\n- Must fix: processSandboxProvisioningJob no longer returns\n  defaultPassword as part of the BullMQ job result. BullMQ''s\n  removeOnComplete kept that return value in Redis for 1h, and nothing\n  in the codebase reads a sandbox job''s returnvalue -- it was a\n  plaintext secret sitting in Redis with zero application retrieval\n  path (T21''s real handover store lands downstream). Replaced with a\n  WARN-level structured log as the interim retrieval channel.\n- CreateSandboxSchema now rejects an all-symbol orgName, closing a bug\n  where slugify() could produce a leading-dash-only slug.\n- Audit-trail tests now assert actorId on every success/failure path.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqx1FJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdJgQACzmSPHt1sQXxQAXTZCZY7h4\nrIJtozza96vaUr/aq4YF8cAdIgGqc5wemD5ppNg5t+yjS8pjonnni1WBNrhgv8yQ\ncrs73/A4P3V1eXGzhW+tNEwnO7DIWqiAkk7IouAsJ54wShCCLEv1fYHXuAiTy+qj\nYMMDWFpGTg/plEV18DRVqUZXOaf+Uj+CR7ocL9crqMsFakU2kzyIchY9Ci9H85da\nwNtO0+0s3p2K8GChzPBHSgQobHt4CAqjaRJDfS3Nas6KCI54WdKTgO9dtMUBKP6E\nxTPppcOltukyLPZ+xlfEBBjr3GiCiHN+eLwFdCBx6IJF8xZR4b14OcSZvPxJf8rY\nD8BepJMAwnwwfjJ6CmsK/SQVA2MWYy09DBhmUGL9bme0GrgSpSNLhYEpZNU3LfMC\nnK2q9QwexeoLcORq7VfR186bLGHRRHpFtPMHTGSu9LjOVrEVrYXeRowIF1034+2F\ni9ssGRkCJr+/0aUkYvK9YRE4RDoJeNPrBGQCjvmXBz+PDJBMdlygZSganP8clqqV\naWDGhLpSrR/dm6qrypNy0wuLkNT/SWzlS703QG2/Oer/PH4X1k0he2oPR3NCCn2/\ndAY+A888Ha7vdWQx7E1jvi4mQ896rvlAU40T3sha89n7+4FxubETsqscpjOnacyE\nh27Xte5ZctILYEY5pD/n\n=d9tB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-08T08:16:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commit/241968b7c26bcaaba9508db45f064c34c19476e1","node_id":"C_kwDOScMdh9oAKDI0MTk2OGI3YzI2YmNhYWJhOTUwOGRiNDVmMDY0YzM0YzE5NDc2ZTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commit/ef4adacf40ee12acbf7638bd0d4d38654404b811","sha":"ef4adacf40ee12acbf7638bd0d4d38654404b811","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/ef4adacf40ee12acbf7638bd0d4d38654404b811"}],"sha":"241968b7c26bcaaba9508db45f064c34c19476e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/241968b7c26bcaaba9508db45f064c34c19476e1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/118787765?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imRahul05/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imRahul05/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imRahul05/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imRahul05/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/imRahul05","id":118787765,"login":"imRahul05","node_id":"U_kgDOBxSOtQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imRahul05/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imRahul05/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imRahul05/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imRahul05/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imRahul05/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/imRahul05","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/ef4adacf40ee12acbf7638bd0d4d38654404b811/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T07:56:26Z","email":"118787765+imRahul05@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Rahul Kumar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T07:56:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"perf(admin-ui): passive idle-logout listeners, local avatar, deferred env.js and storage-safe startup (5/5, split from #772) (#784)\n\n* perf(admin-ui): replace the dicebear cdn avatar with a local initials avatar\n\nEvery header and profile-menu mount requested\nhttps://api.dicebear.com/7.x/initials/svg, an external CDN dependency for a\ndecoration, and a failure or block there left a broken image. The layout\nalso referenced /ow-logo.png, which was never added to public/, so the\nsidebar logo 404''d on every load.\n\nAdd an InitialsAvatar in layout.tsx that renders the user''s profile picture\nwhen the identity has one, and otherwise a CSS circle with their initials\non the accent colour. It is self-contained, so there is no network request,\nand it is used for both the 24 px header avatar and the 64 px profile-menu\none. The name is the image alt and the initials circle is role=\"img\" with\nan aria-label, so it is exposed to assistive technology.\n\nauthProvider.getIdentity no longer fabricates a DiceBear URL when the OIDC\nprofile has no picture; avatar is now optional in the identity type and the\nfallback lives in the component. The sidebar logo now points at the\nexisting /favicon.svg.\n\nTests cover the initials fallback (role and label) and the picture path.\n\nPart 5 of 5 of the split of #772.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* perf(admin-ui): throttle and passivate the idle-logout activity listeners\n\nuseIdleLogout reset its timer from window mousemove, scroll, touchmove and\nresize listeners on every event, up to hundreds of clearTimeout/setTimeout\npairs per second, and registered them as non-passive.\n\nThrottle the timer reset to at most one per throttleMs, where throttleMs is\nmin(10 s, max(0.5 s, timeout / 5)) so short timeouts keep a proportionate\nresolution, and register the listeners with { passive: true } so they never\nblock scrolling.\n\nDropping events must not log a user out early, so every event still records\nlatestActivity with a plain write. When the timeout fires it re-checks\nlatestActivity: if the user was active more recently than the throttled\ntimer knows, it reschedules for the remaining time instead of logging out.\nThe logout itself now swallows a rejected logout() (storage or network\nunavailable) and still navigates to /login, as the existing comment\nintends.\n\nTests cover the throttle window, the passive option, the late-activity\nreschedule, and the rejected-logout redirect.\n\nPart 5 of 5 of the split of #772.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(admin-ui): tolerate unavailable browser storage in theme and auth startup\n\ninitTheme runs before React mounts and called localStorage directly, so a\nbrowser with storage blocked (some iframes, privacy modes, locked-down\nembeds) threw during startup and left a blank page. authProvider''s initial\nuserManager.getUser() read had the same failure as an unhandled rejection.\n\nRoute the theme reads and writes through safeGetItem/safeSetItem, which\ncheck that localStorage exists and catch access errors, falling back to the\ndark theme and default accent. Catch a failing getUser() at module load in\nauthProvider so it can''t surface as an unhandled rejection; the existing\nlogin flow still resolves _authReady through userLoaded.\n\nTests cover theme get/save/apply with throwing storage and storage methods that are undefined.\n\nPart 5 of 5 of the split of #772.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* perf(admin-ui): defer the runtime config script and fix a malformed css comment\n\n/env.js is a classic script in index.html''s <head>, so the HTML parser\nstopped on it before reaching the app. Add defer so it downloads in\nparallel. Deferred and module scripts execute in document order, and\nenv.js precedes the entry module, so window.__CONFIG__ is still set before\nauthProvider reads it. The onerror fallback is unchanged.\n\nAlso fix a CSS comment in index.css whose \"--bg-*/--text-*\" text closed the\ncomment early at \"*/\" and made esbuild emit a css-syntax-error warning on\nevery build. The words are spaced out; no rule changes.\n\nPart 5 of 5 of the split of #772.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(admin-ui): add changelog and week-log entries for startup hardening\n\nRecord the passive and throttled idle-logout listeners, the local initials\navatar and logo fix, the deferred env.js, and the blocked-storage startup\nfixes in CHANGELOG.md, and add a dated week-log entry under\ndocs/tracker/week-log/ per the repo''s delivery flow.\n\nPart 5 of 5 of the split of #772.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* perf(admin-ui): memoize the entity-type context value\n\nEntityTypeProvider built a new context value object, and new getTypeBySlug,\ngetTypeById and reload closures, on every render. Every consumer of the\ncontext therefore re-rendered whenever the provider did, even when the\nentity types and modules were unchanged.\n\nWrap the three functions in useCallback (getTypeBySlug and getTypeById\ndepend on entityTypes, reload has no dependencies) and the value in\nuseMemo keyed on the data and those callbacks. Behaviour is unchanged; the\nvalue now keeps its identity until the entity types or modules change.\n\nCHANGELOG.md and the week-log entry gain a line for it.\n\nPart 5 of 5 of the split of #772.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(admin-ui): ignore empty name segments when deriving avatar initials\n\nSplit the display name on whitespace runs and drop empty segments before taking\nthe first two, so \"John  Doe\" yields \"JD\" instead of \"J\". Ordinary names are\nunchanged and blank names still fall back to \"U\". Adds table-driven tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e1023d1e21530ee8cf7dfaa7f68bb396b9ed9a56","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/trees/e1023d1e21530ee8cf7dfaa7f68bb396b9ed9a56"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/commits/ef4adacf40ee12acbf7638bd0d4d38654404b811","verification":{"payload":"tree e1023d1e21530ee8cf7dfaa7f68bb396b9ed9a56\nparent a3f334113c5e96ee7ba3aef71a78511ff7143b10\nauthor Rahul Kumar <118787765+imRahul05@users.noreply.github.com> 1791446186 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791446186 +0530\n\nperf(admin-ui): passive idle-logout listeners, local avatar, deferred env.js and storage-safe startup (5/5, split from #772) (#784)\n\n* perf(admin-ui): replace the dicebear cdn avatar with a local initials avatar\n\nEvery header and profile-menu mount requested\nhttps://api.dicebear.com/7.x/initials/svg, an external CDN dependency for a\ndecoration, and a failure or block there left a broken image. The layout\nalso referenced /ow-logo.png, which was never added to public/, so the\nsidebar logo 404''d on every load.\n\nAdd an InitialsAvatar in layout.tsx that renders the user''s profile picture\nwhen the identity has one, and otherwise a CSS circle with their initials\non the accent colour. It is self-contained, so there is no network request,\nand it is used for both the 24 px header avatar and the 64 px profile-menu\none. The name is the image alt and the initials circle is role=\"img\" with\nan aria-label, so it is exposed to assistive technology.\n\nauthProvider.getIdentity no longer fabricates a DiceBear URL when the OIDC\nprofile has no picture; avatar is now optional in the identity type and the\nfallback lives in the component. The sidebar logo now points at the\nexisting /favicon.svg.\n\nTests cover the initials fallback (role and label) and the picture path.\n\nPart 5 of 5 of the split of #772.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* perf(admin-ui): throttle and passivate the idle-logout activity listeners\n\nuseIdleLogout reset its timer from window mousemove, scroll, touchmove and\nresize listeners on every event, up to hundreds of clearTimeout/setTimeout\npairs per second, and registered them as non-passive.\n\nThrottle the timer reset to at most one per throttleMs, where throttleMs is\nmin(10 s, max(0.5 s, timeout / 5)) so short timeouts keep a proportionate\nresolution, and register the listeners with { passive: true } so they never\nblock scrolling.\n\nDropping events must not log a user out early, so every event still records\nlatestActivity with a plain write. When the timeout fires it re-checks\nlatestActivity: if the user was active more recently than the throttled\ntimer knows, it reschedules for the remaining time instead of logging out.\nThe logout itself now swallows a rejected logout() (storage or network\nunavailable) and still navigates to /login, as the existing comment\nintends.\n\nTests cover the throttle window, the passive option, the late-activity\nreschedule, and the rejected-logout redirect.\n\nPart 5 of 5 of the split of #772.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(admin-ui): tolerate unavailable browser storage in theme and auth startup\n\ninitTheme runs before React mounts and called localStorage directly, so a\nbrowser with storage blocked (some iframes, privacy modes, locked-down\nembeds) threw during startup and left a blank page. authProvider''s initial\nuserManager.getUser() read had the same failure as an unhandled rejection.\n\nRoute the theme reads and writes through safeGetItem/safeSetItem, which\ncheck that localStorage exists and catch access errors, falling back to the\ndark theme and default accent. Catch a failing getUser() at module load in\nauthProvider so it can''t surface as an unhandled rejection; the existing\nlogin flow still resolves _authReady through userLoaded.\n\nTests cover theme get/save/apply with throwing storage and storage methods that are undefined.\n\nPart 5 of 5 of the split of #772.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* perf(admin-ui): defer the runtime config script and fix a malformed css comment\n\n/env.js is a classic script in index.html''s <head>, so the HTML parser\nstopped on it before reaching the app. Add defer so it downloads in\nparallel. Deferred and module scripts execute in document order, and\nenv.js precedes the entry module, so window.__CONFIG__ is still set before\nauthProvider reads it. The onerror fallback is unchanged.\n\nAlso fix a CSS comment in index.css whose \"--bg-*/--text-*\" text closed the\ncomment early at \"*/\" and made esbuild emit a css-syntax-error warning on\nevery build. The words are spaced out; no rule changes.\n\nPart 5 of 5 of the split of #772.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(admin-ui): add changelog and week-log entries for startup hardening\n\nRecord the passive and throttled idle-logout listeners, the local initials\navatar and logo fix, the deferred env.js, and the blocked-storage startup\nfixes in CHANGELOG.md, and add a dated week-log entry under\ndocs/tracker/week-log/ per the repo''s delivery flow.\n\nPart 5 of 5 of the split of #772.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* perf(admin-ui): memoize the entity-type context value\n\nEntityTypeProvider built a new context value object, and new getTypeBySlug,\ngetTypeById and reload closures, on every render. Every consumer of the\ncontext therefore re-rendered whenever the provider did, even when the\nentity types and modules were unchanged.\n\nWrap the three functions in useCallback (getTypeBySlug and getTypeById\ndepend on entityTypes, reload has no dependencies) and the value in\nuseMemo keyed on the data and those callbacks. Behaviour is unchanged; the\nvalue now keeps its identity until the entity types or modules change.\n\nCHANGELOG.md and the week-log entry gain a line for it.\n\nPart 5 of 5 of the split of #772.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(admin-ui): ignore empty name segments when deriving avatar initials\n\nSplit the display name on whitespace runs and drop empty segments before taking\nthe first two, so \"John  Doe\" yields \"JD\" instead of \"J\". Ordinary names are\nunchanged and blank names still fall back to \"U\". Adds table-driven tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqx0yqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAN2gQAAFMnDsBvDXh3ccvLvxMAz4P\nQGWA73EKnTF+sGqPHu1VpL3Ib14+mvnS+p+BtdEn//l3VadU3ZVBg802nWdW+SKL\nommndWsyk7TXqGFYen/Yt1Ed3L5InxkJzT/G74/p6MSfD8Eq241TCIeG9mQ4b2u6\nquYOllntK/7+elsoJBszeNu4uQSTD2GnNCLXU+nMgRpF8NOGX7Td/IQzGsjeEGJb\nkAB6k+7VDWHa1BnXbaY27rkA/Z9wnTX2jPbP8o9oRsQ5Nv1odWrlH2bY04cGpaq9\nkJFR8IZLEBlPQkpAjU6YGb5ATwZJR7LRQhGgaWiRrtFnnrpARLPXUCVQeAjzIlh9\nAmFQjtKEwifArNnoKlegfW1S6HkZ4uUl/n5XSA4Gpbq+L0+D5K6hZ4rtV0CmHZ73\nwkM6SUFc4g8nYBSg/j+oLrghtnvMxIvnD+99Hm5VQRNP3fWLxp1fy1yyMBZpUtus\nfYDTEyCSCMUgxQvPPfmDgQ6stu4tZgl8mr5i3CYq0iE5uJV27ckD23DdcfoGxXUR\n3kAvhL3WJz2BmC8vUcWe0Edv9eJFL59FnBYV/leaT9DV/r9Lhu4/WVGR8ntmLAmW\nQwAL3WchzNnJ9AOoOzALy7peiiNihA5y+RYP4dfLicJfwPlxmVKyzCnLuAfhqzwb\n2MlbpiWysJQwVddoemOS\n=40yS\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-08T07:56:26Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commit/ef4adacf40ee12acbf7638bd0d4d38654404b811","node_id":"C_kwDOScMdh9oAKGVmNGFkYWNmNDBlZTEyYWNiZjc2MzhiZDBkNGQzODY1NDQwNGI4MTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commit/a3f334113c5e96ee7ba3aef71a78511ff7143b10","sha":"a3f334113c5e96ee7ba3aef71a78511ff7143b10","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/a3f334113c5e96ee7ba3aef71a78511ff7143b10"}],"sha":"ef4adacf40ee12acbf7638bd0d4d38654404b811","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/ef4adacf40ee12acbf7638bd0d4d38654404b811"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/67047397?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TusharSharma991","id":67047397,"login":"TusharSharma991","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3MDQ3Mzk3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/a3f334113c5e96ee7ba3aef71a78511ff7143b10/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T06:10:15Z","email":"67047397+TusharSharma991@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Tushar Sharma"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T06:10:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(auth): platform-admin role, mfa, and sandbox foundation (phase 1) (#803)\n\n* feat(auth): platform-admin role, mfa, and sandbox foundation (phase 1)\n\nMulti-Org Sandbox System Phase 1 (docs/specs/multi-org-sandbox.md, ADR-022):\ncross-tenant platform_admin role, OpenWind-owned email-OTP MFA (Zitadel''s own\nMFA methods are unusable on this hosted instance), sandbox DTO allow-list,\nand per-admin sandbox quota. Security-reviewed; fixed a role-inheritance\nprivilege leak found during review (GRANT ... WITH INHERIT FALSE) and added\na regression isolation test against a real Postgres.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(notifications): fix outbound-dispatch 500-status mock missing .text()\n\nThe mocked fetch Response for the non-2xx test lacked a text() method,\nwhich the source code calls to build the error message -- this was\nmasking a real test failure as a mock shape bug, caught when CI\nactually ran it for real (not just the local dev environment where it\nwas previously assumed pre-existing/unrelated).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(api): stub platform-admin auth middleware in full-app integration tests\n\nmodules.test.ts and view-configs.test.ts are the only two integration\ntests that boot the full app.ts router tree via createApp(), and both\nexhaustively mock @platform/auth. PR1 added platform-admin routes to\napp.ts, so the mock needs requirePlatformAdmin/requirePlatformAdminIdentity\nstubs too, same no-op pattern already used there for requireActingPerson.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(auth): address prabhuvijit''s pr#803 good-to-fix review findings\n\nFour non-blocking items from his review:\n- verifyMfaCode: documented the INCR-based attempt counter''s known\n  concurrency bound rather than rewriting with a Lua script\n- requirePlatformAdmin: new test proving an sk_... API key is rejected,\n  since resolvePlatformAdmin has no API-key path at all\n- outbound-dispatch.ts: clear the cached Novu token on a 401 so the\n  next call re-fetches instead of retrying the same rejected token\n- hasMfaFactor: doc comment now explains it is currently dormant and\n  cross-references requirePlatformAdmin''s own explanation\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e0ca27811256efe198944a6ba87a7db0bb448d4c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/trees/e0ca27811256efe198944a6ba87a7db0bb448d4c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/commits/a3f334113c5e96ee7ba3aef71a78511ff7143b10","verification":{"payload":"tree e0ca27811256efe198944a6ba87a7db0bb448d4c\nparent 2e37c9e289af2d388480c19ba568129918aa76e8\nauthor Tushar Sharma <67047397+TusharSharma991@users.noreply.github.com> 1791439815 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791439815 +0530\n\nfeat(auth): platform-admin role, mfa, and sandbox foundation (phase 1) (#803)\n\n* feat(auth): platform-admin role, mfa, and sandbox foundation (phase 1)\n\nMulti-Org Sandbox System Phase 1 (docs/specs/multi-org-sandbox.md, ADR-022):\ncross-tenant platform_admin role, OpenWind-owned email-OTP MFA (Zitadel''s own\nMFA methods are unusable on this hosted instance), sandbox DTO allow-list,\nand per-admin sandbox quota. Security-reviewed; fixed a role-inheritance\nprivilege leak found during review (GRANT ... WITH INHERIT FALSE) and added\na regression isolation test against a real Postgres.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(notifications): fix outbound-dispatch 500-status mock missing .text()\n\nThe mocked fetch Response for the non-2xx test lacked a text() method,\nwhich the source code calls to build the error message -- this was\nmasking a real test failure as a mock shape bug, caught when CI\nactually ran it for real (not just the local dev environment where it\nwas previously assumed pre-existing/unrelated).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(api): stub platform-admin auth middleware in full-app integration tests\n\nmodules.test.ts and view-configs.test.ts are the only two integration\ntests that boot the full app.ts router tree via createApp(), and both\nexhaustively mock @platform/auth. PR1 added platform-admin routes to\napp.ts, so the mock needs requirePlatformAdmin/requirePlatformAdminIdentity\nstubs too, same no-op pattern already used there for requireActingPerson.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(auth): address prabhuvijit''s pr#803 good-to-fix review findings\n\nFour non-blocking items from his review:\n- verifyMfaCode: documented the INCR-based attempt counter''s known\n  concurrency bound rather than rewriting with a Lua script\n- requirePlatformAdmin: new test proving an sk_... API key is rejected,\n  since resolvePlatformAdmin has no API-key path at all\n- outbound-dispatch.ts: clear the cached Novu token on a 401 so the\n  next call re-fetches instead of retrying the same rejected token\n- hasMfaFactor: doc comment now explains it is currently dormant and\n  cross-references requirePlatformAdmin''s own explanation\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signatur