A","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commit/2e37c9e289af2d388480c19ba568129918aa76e8","sha":"2e37c9e289af2d388480c19ba568129918aa76e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/2e37c9e289af2d388480c19ba568129918aa76e8"}],"sha":"a3f334113c5e96ee7ba3aef71a78511ff7143b10","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/a3f334113c5e96ee7ba3aef71a78511ff7143b10"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/184391486?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bikash-barnwal","id":184391486,"login":"bikash-barnwal","node_id":"U_kgDOCv2XPg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/2e37c9e289af2d388480c19ba568129918aa76e8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T05:55:34Z","email":"bikashprasadbarnwal@gmail.com","name":"Bikash"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T05:55:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(security): audit sql lab queries and exports under superset 6.1.0''s event names (#799)\n\n* fix(security): audit sql lab queries and exports under superset 6.1.0''s event names\n\nThe audit logger listened for sql_json / csv / export_csv, which 6.1.0 never\nemits, and read sql from a kwarg Superset does not pass, so SQL Lab queries and\nexports wrote no reporting.* audit row.\n\n- Classify the events 6.1.0 really logs (SqlLabRestApi execute and\n  export_streaming / export_csv, chart data csv and xlsx) from the request.\n- The chart \"Export to .CSV\" button is a form post carrying the format in\n  form_data; read it once per request.\n- Key the trail to the Zitadel subject: every login carries an owsub:<subject>\n  role (no permissions); the audit row records it, never the login name.\n- SQL Lab results are downloaded from the browser''s results grid, with no\n  server request, so the query row is their record; the server-side SQL Lab\n  export routes are mapped for any role that is later granted can_export_csv.\n- A chart export records which chart, dataset and format it exported. Superset\n  reduces its own log record for the button''s form post to the first query''s\n  parameters, so the chart and dataset are read from the posted body.\n- An SQL Lab export quotes the query text only for a query the caller ran\n  themselves; a forged client_id naming another user''s query no longer copies\n  that user''s SQL into the caller''s audit row (reproduced before the fix).\n- Correct the standalone spec''s T11, which was marked done but wrote nothing.\n\nTests: mapping and actor unit tests, scope tests (including the real button''s\nrequest shape, recorded from a live Superset), and a real-database test that\nexactly one reporting.* row is written per query and per export.\n\nRefs #709\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(security): resolve the audit actor with the shared session resolver\n\nThe audit writer read flask_login''s current_user for the actor and for the\nowner-scoped query lookup, while the tenant came from the shared resolver\nadded in #798. Use that resolver for all three so a request can never be\naudited under a different user than the one whose tenant it was stamped with.\n\nThe real-database audit test now runs every scenario in both request states\n(SQL Lab: g.user set, current_user unauthenticated; ordinary: current_user set,\ng.user absent) and no longer patches both at once. Against the previous writer\nthe SQL Lab state fails.\n\nThe export format in a chart export''s audit detail is allowlisted (csv, xlsx;\nanything else is recorded as unknown:<start>) instead of only truncated.\n\nRefs #709\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4b1b268a3b97ffe2e504e2e9c81f85e9908ba712","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/trees/4b1b268a3b97ffe2e504e2e9c81f85e9908ba712"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/commits/2e37c9e289af2d388480c19ba568129918aa76e8","verification":{"payload":"tree 4b1b268a3b97ffe2e504e2e9c81f85e9908ba712\nparent 0d441524c6a90b32a5ef3c51b1496200f1d41cfb\nauthor Bikash <bikashprasadbarnwal@gmail.com> 1791438934 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791438934 +0530\n\nfix(security): audit sql lab queries and exports under superset 6.1.0''s event names (#799)\n\n* fix(security): audit sql lab queries and exports under superset 6.1.0''s event names\n\nThe audit logger listened for sql_json / csv / export_csv, which 6.1.0 never\nemits, and read sql from a kwarg Superset does not pass, so SQL Lab queries and\nexports wrote no reporting.* audit row.\n\n- Classify the events 6.1.0 really logs (SqlLabRestApi execute and\n  export_streaming / export_csv, chart data csv and xlsx) from the request.\n- The chart \"Export to .CSV\" button is a form post carrying the format in\n  form_data; read it once per request.\n- Key the trail to the Zitadel subject: every login carries an owsub:<subject>\n  role (no permissions); the audit row records it, never the login name.\n- SQL Lab results are downloaded from the browser''s results grid, with no\n  server request, so the query row is their record; the server-side SQL Lab\n  export routes are mapped for any role that is later granted can_export_csv.\n- A chart export records which chart, dataset and format it exported. Superset\n  reduces its own log record for the button''s form post to the first query''s\n  parameters, so the chart and dataset are read from the posted body.\n- An SQL Lab export quotes the query text only for a query the caller ran\n  themselves; a forged client_id naming another user''s query no longer copies\n  that user''s SQL into the caller''s audit row (reproduced before the fix).\n- Correct the standalone spec''s T11, which was marked done but wrote nothing.\n\nTests: mapping and actor unit tests, scope tests (including the real button''s\nrequest shape, recorded from a live Superset), and a real-database test that\nexactly one reporting.* row is written per query and per export.\n\nRefs #709\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(security): resolve the audit actor with the shared session resolver\n\nThe audit writer read flask_login''s current_user for the actor and for the\nowner-scoped query lookup, while the tenant came from the shared resolver\nadded in #798. Use that resolver for all three so a request can never be\naudited under a different user than the one whose tenant it was stamped with.\n\nThe real-database audit test now runs every scenario in both request states\n(SQL Lab: g.user set, current_user unauthenticated; ordinary: current_user set,\ng.user absent) and no longer patches both at once. Against the previous writer\nthe SQL Lab state fails.\n\nThe export format in a chart export''s audit detail is allowlisted (csv, xlsx;\nanything else is recorded as unknown:<start>) instead of only truncated.\n\nRefs #709\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP