.github.com/users/imRahul05/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imRahul05/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imRahul05/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imRahul05/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/imRahul05","id":118787765,"login":"imRahul05","node_id":"U_kgDOBxSOtQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imRahul05/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imRahul05/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imRahul05/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imRahul05/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imRahul05/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/imRahul05","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/332788e853c93208630ec551366a450fa1d4c788/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T05:15:39Z","email":"118787765+imRahul05@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Rahul Kumar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T05:15:39Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"perf(admin-ui): lazy-load page routes and add an entry size gate (1/5, split from #772) (#782)\n\n* perf(admin-ui): lazy-load all page routes behind a shell-preserving suspense\n\nEvery page route was statically imported in App.tsx, so the entry chunk was\nabout 1,436 kB raw and an unauthenticated user on /login still downloaded\nand parsed reactflow, dagre, d3, dnd-kit and the Superset embed SDK.\n\nMove the 32 page imports into src/lazy-routes.ts as React.lazy() wrappers\nand render them through a Suspense. The Suspense and a RouteErrorBoundary\n(keyed on the pathname, so it resets on navigation) sit inside Layout via a\nShellOutlet, so the sidebar and header stay mounted while a route loads or\nfails to load. Heavy dependencies are now isolated to their own route\nchunks: the workflow canvas (reactflow, dagre, d3) and the Superset SDK\n(Reporting only). The entry chunk drops to about 660 kB raw across 41 JS\nchunks.\n\nRouteErrorBoundary tells a missing dynamic-import chunk (the usual result\nof a redeploy while a tab is open) from any other render error. A chunk\nerror offers Reload; anything else offers Retry and is logged with its\ncomponent stack instead of being swallowed.\n\nTests cover all 32 lazy exports and paths, the boundary''s chunk and generic\nerror paths and reset behaviour, and shell stability across route changes.\n\nPart 1 of 5 of the split of #772.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(admin-ui): reload once when a lazy chunk is missing after a redeploy\n\nWith lazy routes, a tab left open across a deploy references chunk hashes\nthat no longer exist, so navigating to a not-yet-loaded route fails with a\ndynamic-import error.\n\nListen for Vite''s vite:preloadError in main.tsx and reload the page once to\npick up the new build. A sessionStorage timestamp guards the reload: if the\nlast chunk-triggered reload was under 10 s ago the error is left to the\nroute error boundary, so a genuine outage can''t cause a reload loop. If\nsessionStorage is unavailable (private mode, blocked storage) no reload is\nattempted and the boundary handles the error.\n\nPart 1 of 5 of the split of #772.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* perf(admin-ui): fail the build when the entry chunk exceeds 210 kb gzip\n\nVite''s chunkSizeWarningLimit only prints a warning, so nothing stopped the\nentry chunk growing back toward the old monolith.\n\nAdd scripts/check-entry-size.mjs, which finds the entry script in\ndist/index.html, gzips it and exits non-zero when it is over budget. The\nbudget is 210 kB gzip (1024-byte kB; the measured entry is 196.9 kB, so\nabout 6% headroom). The comment says to raise it in the same PR with a\nreason, and to prefer lazy-loading the new code instead.\n\nChain it onto admin-ui''s build script rather than adding a separate step:\nCI''s quality job and the Docker image both already run turbo build for this\npackage, so the gate is enforced without editing the protected workflow\nfiles. size:check remains for re-checking an existing dist.\n\nchunkSizeWarningLimit drops from 700 to 680 kB raw so\nthe warning tracks the real entry size. eslint.config.mjs gives .mjs files\nNode globals so the script lints.\n\nKnown gap: turbo''s build cache inputs (src/**, tsconfig.json, package.json)\ndon''t include vite.config.ts or scripts/, so a change to only the budget\ncan be served from cache without re-running the check. Changing turbo.json\nis left for a separate PR.\n\nPart 1 of 5 of the split of #772.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(admin-ui): add changelog and week-log entries for route code splitting\n\nRecord the lazy-route split, the route error boundary with its one-time\nchunk reload, and the 210 kB entry size gate in CHANGELOG.md, and add a\ndated week-log entry under docs/tracker/week-log/ per the repo''s delivery\nflow. The week-log notes the turbo cache-input gap for the size check.\n\nPart 1 of 5 of the split of #772.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8fb392ebc3af1466801527f2fb94832fe048cbc7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/trees/8fb392ebc3af1466801527f2fb94832fe048cbc7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/commits/332788e853c93208630ec551366a450fa1d4c788","verification":{"payload":"tree 8fb392ebc3af1466801527f2fb94832fe048cbc7\nparent 02099d9a971b0df64dc38cb322716f1c56f17dcb\nauthor Rahul Kumar <118787765+imRahul05@users.noreply.github.com> 1791436539 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791436539 +0530\n\nperf(admin-ui): lazy-load page routes and add an entry size gate (1/5, split from #772) (#782)\n\n* perf(admin-ui): lazy-load all page routes behind a shell-preserving suspense\n\nEvery page route was statically imported in App.tsx, so the entry chunk was\nabout 1,436 kB raw and an unauthenticated user on /login still downloaded\nand parsed reactflow, dagre, d3, dnd-kit and the Superset embed SDK.\n\nMove the 32 page imports into src/lazy-routes.ts as React.lazy() wrappers\nand render them through a Suspense. The Suspense and a RouteErrorBoundary\n(keyed on the pathname, so it resets on navigation) sit inside Layout via a\nShellOutlet, so the sidebar and header stay mounted while a route loads or\nfails to load. Heavy dependencies are now isolated to their own route\nchunks: the workflow canvas (reactflow, dagre, d3) and the Superset SDK\n(Reporting only). The entry chunk drops to about 660 kB raw across 41 JS\nchunks.\n\nRouteErrorBoundary tells a missing dynamic-import chunk (the usual result\nof a redeploy while a tab is open) from any other render error. A chunk\nerror offers Reload; anything else offers Retry and is logged with its\ncomponent stack instead of being swallowed.\n\nTests cover all 32 lazy exports and paths, the boundary''s chunk and generic\nerror paths and reset behaviour, and shell stability across route changes.\n\nPart 1 of 5 of the split of #772.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(admin-ui): reload once when a lazy chunk is missing after a redeploy\n\nWith lazy routes, a tab left open across a deploy references chunk hashes\nthat no longer exist, so navigating to a not-yet-loaded route fails with a\ndynamic-import error.\n\nListen for Vite''s vite:preloadError in main.tsx and reload the page once to\npick up the new build. A sessionStorage timestamp guards the reload: if the\nlast chunk-triggered reload was under 10 s ago the error is left to the\nroute error boundary, so a genuine outage can''t cause a reload loop. If\nsessionStorage is unavailable (private mode, blocked storage) no reload is\nattempted and the boundary handles the error.\n\nPart 1 of 5 of the split of #772.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* perf(admin-ui): fail the build when the entry chunk exceeds 210 kb gzip\n\nVite''s chunkSizeWarningLimit only prints a warning, so nothing stopped the\nentry chunk growing back toward the old monolith.\n\nAdd scripts/check-entry-size.mjs, which finds the entry script in\ndist/index.html, gzips it and exits non-zero when it is over budget. The\nbudget is 210 kB gzip (1024-byte kB; the measured entry is 196.9 kB, so\nabout 6% headroom). The comment says to raise it in the same PR with a\nreason, and to prefer lazy-loading the new code instead.\n\nChain it onto admin-ui''s build script rather than adding a separate step:\nCI''s quality job and the Docker image both already run turbo build for this\npackage, so the gate is enforced without editing the protected workflow\nfiles. size:check remains for re-checking an existing dist.\n\nchunkSizeWarningLimit drops from 700 to 680 kB raw so\nthe warning tracks the real entry size. eslint.config.mjs gives .mjs files\nNode globals so the script lints.\n\nKnown gap: turbo''s build cache inputs (src/**, tsconfig.json, package.json)\ndon''t include vite.config.ts or scripts/, so a change to only the budget\ncan be served from cache without re-running the check. Changing turbo.json\nis left for a separate PR.\n\nPart 1 of 5 of the split of #772.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(admin-ui): add changelog and week-log entries for route code splitting\n\nRecord the lazy-route split, the route error boundary with its one-time\nchunk reload, and the 210 kB entry size gate in CHANGELOG.md, and add a\ndated week-log entry under docs/tracker/week-log/ per the repo''s delivery\nflow. The week-log notes the turbo cache-input gap for the size check.\n\nPart 1 of 5 of the split of #772.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxyb7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVTwQAH46PRe1fQVCr1kQJgz923qt\nmf2fAddyMwQiFvkulWVkrUTUTeYzayl9LIxxC+M8M884Drx0T/CrG2Dacx7PQkUR\nbkLx+2XBb7HQAczsYPfVUkpx30+pgyLsX5Wpqxch73sb+5vSMVoi/N2OI9hozTc1\nuQC9BzKb9Vx9nT32L2ma3myoy1b8icHP9fVvrx4Fa/A+vYAOnkkMYoqjVqf8LK8t\nzT2H1fWrttFbXdghhTwyp2dniVh7PCgZ6goEUBGPFEkTgwxAz3DFwJlIH1+smVF/\nDXa/BRq4QIIvzx2OKhDRU8lcyuLz8qEtBtLc5e67/D967lZMCIg6B4Uz2bojYLQ7\nHQNla86sLPS+vtH08xdc4a1qn9q5cV3D9OdpXsA5R0045yums/CwKTXAsK8+IDQ2\nNYSDKdfZ9lE5+wX4/DONbtNUcGc7zO5dKGa0wTy8h8tdOKSbWgssw6Yppo2OQjQk\nZHveuXfb6HWysx9QVDK5Q73RiG6Rh+jfiuTt9vyaRNnYMuamg1hOKsRVCZNjDcOb\nZGhfkMbX5GF2/aVqvRtA2G1Wgv6NZuqD7fX6Nlqn7HT8dFnWB6ab9DrX72wGtgqQ\nQ2P/R7z1iwKqlcQ/KLZnsqGX6umXu1DPdaM1+pRR81hngZb0r+Mhk/+DMV6qAdZi\nlI9OHYxb5RHsx34Dg4Kd\n=SIKn\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-08T05:15:40Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commit/332788e853c93208630ec551366a450fa1d4c788","node_id":"C_kwDOScMdh9oAKDMzMjc4OGU4NTNjOTMyMDg2MzBlYzU1MTM2NmE0NTBmYTFkNGM3ODg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commit/02099d9a971b0df64dc38cb322716f1c56f17dcb","sha":"02099d9a971b0df64dc38cb322716f1c56f17dcb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/02099d9a971b0df64dc38cb322716f1c56f17dcb"}],"sha":"332788e853c93208630ec551366a450fa1d4c788","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/332788e853c93208630ec551366a450fa1d4c788"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/184391486?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bikash-barnwal","id":184391486,"login":"bikash-barnwal","node_id":"U_kgDOCv2XPg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/02099d9a971b0df64dc38cb322716f1c56f17dcb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T11:22:53Z","email":"bikashprasadbarnwal@gmail.com","name":"Bikash"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T11:22:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(security): stamp the user''s tenant on sql lab connections (#798)\n\nWhile SQL Lab runs a query Superset sets flask.g.user but flask_login''s\ncurrent_user is unauthenticated. The tenant and own-rows lookups read\ncurrent_user, found nobody, stamped no tenant, and row-level security returned\nzero rows. Both now resolve the user through one helper that reads g.user, so\nthe tenant and the own-rows narrowing always come from the same user.\n\nAdds a real-database test that SQL Lab, a chart and the database report the\nsame count for staff, an own-rows analyst and a second tenant. It fails on the\nold code (SQL Lab 0, chart 1015/1013/300) and passes with the fix.\n\nCloses #716\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f00220f84d5a7e78487080f9cfd40db23cf5982d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/trees/f00220f84d5a7e78487080f9cfd40db23cf5982d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/commits/02099d9a971b0df64dc38cb322716f1c56f17dcb","verification":{"payload":"tree f00220f84d5a7e78487080f9cfd40db23cf5982d\nparent 3d89abbdbc8a5067bf270f2df12603a73cc03543\nauthor Bikash <bikashprasadbarnwal@gmail.com> 1791372173 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791372173 +0530\n\nfix(security): stamp the user''s tenant on sql lab connections (#798)\n\nWhile SQL Lab runs a query Superset sets flask.g.user but flask_login''s\ncurrent_user is unauthenticated. The tenant and own-rows lookups read\ncurrent_user, found nobody, stamped no tenant, and row-level security returned\nzero rows. Both now resolve the user through one helper that reads g.user, so\nthe tenant and the own-rows narrowing always come from the same user.\n\nAdds a real-database test that SQL Lab, a chart and the database report the\nsame count for staff, an own-rows analyst and a second tenant. It fails on the\nold code (SQL Lab 0, chart 1015/1013/300) and passes with the fix.\n\nCloses #716\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxiuNCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAydMQADgJxEsM+UTaZZqhnKhy/1c0\neeIqq