om/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/fb939396d99d8ff2188c4aa92e5116f25e9e5574"}],"sha":"54ce3035586a5a7e3161663f570a7c137b35e198","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/54ce3035586a5a7e3161663f570a7c137b35e198"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/184391486?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bikash-barnwal","id":184391486,"login":"bikash-barnwal","node_id":"U_kgDOCv2XPg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/fb939396d99d8ff2188c4aa92e5116f25e9e5574/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T08:36:09Z","email":"bikashprasadbarnwal@gmail.com","name":"Bikash"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T08:36:09Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(security): fail superset startup if db connections could be pooled across tenants (#790)\n\n* fix(security): fail superset startup if db connections could be pooled across tenants\n\nRefs #729\n\nSuperset 6.1.0 has no SQLALCHEMY_POOL_CLASS setting, so the guard verifies\nthe source that decides pooling (Database.get_sqla_engine) and refuses to\nstart if the installed Superset no longer defaults to NullPool or anything\nopts out with nullpool=False. The opt-out check is a source-text scan for\nthe keyword form, not an AST walk; this and the lack of a CI job wiring the\nguard into the built image yet are disclosed in the docstring and ADR-019\nrather than overclaimed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(security): address review of the nullpool guard (#729)\n\n- Remove the ADR-019 edit from this PR: ADR files are human-authored. The text\n  is offered separately as a patch.\n- Read the `if nullpool:` block from the parsed syntax tree, so the one-liner\n  form and a comment between the `if` and its body are accepted, and a removed\n  block is refused.\n- Check only the public entry points (get_sqla_engine, get_raw_connection); the\n  private _get_sqla_engine no longer has to keep its name. A private default of\n  False is still refused by the opt-out scan, and a test says so.\n- Fail closed when models/core.py cannot be parsed.\n- Remove every test temp directory with addCleanup, including the copy of the\n  Superset source.\n- Add tests for the one-liner, the commented body, a removed block, a renamed\n  entry point, an unparseable file, and the known comment false positive.\n- Type annotations on assert_connections_not_pooled; document its startup cost.\n\nRefs #729\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2a7c38c584645899ad87d23be560ac78646f5735","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/trees/2a7c38c584645899ad87d23be560ac78646f5735"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/commits/fb939396d99d8ff2188c4aa92e5116f25e9e5574","verification":{"payload":"tree 2a7c38c584645899ad87d23be560ac78646f5735\nparent dafaa4630047b6683c9606be3eaa72a05e2a8773\nauthor Bikash <bikashprasadbarnwal@gmail.com> 1791362169 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791362169 +0530\n\nfix(security): fail superset startup if db connections could be pooled across tenants (#790)\n\n* fix(security): fail superset startup if db connections could be pooled across tenants\n\nRefs #729\n\nSuperset 6.1.0 has no SQLALCHEMY_POOL_CLASS setting, so the guard verifies\nthe source that decides pooling (Database.get_sqla_engine) and refuses to\nstart if the installed Superset no longer defaults to NullPool or anything\nopts out with nullpool=False. The opt-out check is a source-text scan for\nthe keyword form, not an AST walk; this and the lack of a CI job wiring the\nguard into the built image yet are disclosed in the docstring and ADR-019\nrather than overclaimed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(security): address review of the nullpool guard (#729)\n\n- Remove the ADR-019 edit from this PR: ADR files are human-authored. The text\n  is offered separately as a patch.\n- Read the `if nullpool:` block from the parsed syntax tree, so the one-liner\n  form and a comment between the `if` and its body are accepted, and a removed\n  block is refused.\n- Check only the public entry points (get_sqla_engine, get_raw_connection); the\n  private _get_sqla_engine no longer has to keep its name. A private default of\n  False is still refused by the opt-out scan, and a test says so.\n- Fail closed when models/core.py cannot be parsed.\n- Remove every test temp directory with addCleanup, including the copy of the\n  Superset source.\n- Add tests for the one-liner, the commented body, a removed block, a renamed\n  entry point, an unparseable file, and the known comment false positive.\n- Type annotations on assert_connections_not_pooled; document its startup cost.\n\nRefs #729\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxgR5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAav8QAFRf3BeT2dHGjdUGwB/gC9H5\np5oH0lW1LewEOzSPGnYbM/4oGPWDWNCralED5wN8S