Hub"},"message":"test(api): close transition-route test gaps from #733 review (#756)\n\n- cover TRANSITION_LOCKED -> 409 with Retry-After (#734)\n- add cross-tenant 404 test for GET /:id/transitions (#735)\n- use UUID-format tenant literals (#736)","tree":{"sha":"1e4dadd1e9d562ae401e782a36bfb6d3c50615d8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/trees/1e4dadd1e9d562ae401e782a36bfb6d3c50615d8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/commits/3ed7841a78218c428812435577900c25ba022608","verification":{"payload":"tree 1e4dadd1e9d562ae401e782a36bfb6d3c50615d8\nparent fc8a519c7667281103ab5998848e96df14c6e3da\nauthor Abhinav Mishra <needabhinav@gmail.com> 1790942672 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790942672 +0530\n\ntest(api): close transition-route test gaps from #733 review (#756)\n\n- cover TRANSITION_LOCKED -> 409 with Retry-After (#734)\n- add cross-tenant 404 test for GET /:id/transitions (#735)\n- use UUID-format tenant literals (#736)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqv53QCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAj1AQACzoDLjtKR8/V5mjR6P1Y7rZ\nMYnw7yICgU5GmRRh3PmyFz3r4EA/qL1GsINkv92KsHumLD/DCOVZBF076V4oSbPG\ndjNpo/K+Zu3bbsuehpkuoDjQQNarRo4LiMIyZwRgHrSQulGBQeuOoCb625oqDlPc\nZQdFmpsl4xJMDtxsGpiNvdwWTLslT6Z8aeG2kWuN8vd+EXLSpX9hbNNCxOvsKYPo\ngU6U52KgscSZwuWRfpSzzLnNYaHSDS1jSH6SmpG4DDHxW/fYZbFd/HZ6xcF6aGII\nfNhK3NV0PyWL45200O0WlYev0K7fLBXfmJLgSFqMot3mgqywWsW/aVK/IKdZYtvL\ngCpbOit48FFKtAQ+B2UIgENUaMfuz6tLCXerMmlj1AsAf7iBrVoeXRPaUWbIHH+4\nrekSdZaz12Mma8Ttpv8uWPtVc/+D/Bs4vLL6k2AvKHD9yu+oqagWqdhfmeblyiAF\nD/2s3xTG8S/hVVHjReHH1sMSkydc53+a+OkdEzRV+gmqI1OnCzuFPLsHv9Naot5e\nB0Yr1bwAYGr7cLlGTHOpnlId+wWLraiow34usqIZOVsCqTl8GYKszXB21ImAFEvh\ngsr83/V3Y//yuT87vHpcZ1q3kQnQl8POcwDwZyd+ShHP37DpyRTWGxBSDrN4tKL5\njjWQRN6pAWIkAvz21Grl\n=ZQhQ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T12:04:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commit/3ed7841a78218c428812435577900c25ba022608","node_id":"C_kwDOScMdh9oAKDNlZDc4NDFhNzgyMThjNDI4ODEyNDM1NTc3OTAwYzI1YmEwMjI2MDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commit/fc8a519c7667281103ab5998848e96df14c6e3da","sha":"fc8a519c7667281103ab5998848e96df14c6e3da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/fc8a519c7667281103ab5998848e96df14c6e3da"}],"sha":"3ed7841a78218c428812435577900c25ba022608","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/3ed7841a78218c428812435577900c25ba022608"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/67047397?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TusharSharma991","id":67047397,"login":"TusharSharma991","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3MDQ3Mzk3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/fc8a519c7667281103ab5998848e96df14c6e3da/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T19:09:56Z","email":"67047397+TusharSharma991@users.noreply.github.com","name":"TusharSharma991"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T19:09:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(ui): org-directory PR5 — admin-ui org chart page (#723)\n\n* feat(auth): add zitadel manager_id/department metadata read + org-directory scaffold\n\nNew @platform/org-directory package (docs/specs/org-directory.md) with the\nOrgSourceImporter/OrgNode/OrgTree contract that keeps the org-chart tree\nswappable across identity providers. Adds getOrgMetadataForUser to\npackages/auth/src/zitadel-management.ts, reading exactly the manager_id/\ndepartment metadata keys via the existing service-account token path,\nwith the same cache/single-flight pattern as the file''s other lookups.\n\nPR1 of the org-directory track (spec + tasks in docs/specs/). No schema,\nroutes, or UI yet — those land in follow-up PRs per the tasks file.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(db): add org_employees + org_directory_sync_runs tables, wire gdpr erasure\n\nNew tenant-scoped tables for the org-directory tree (docs/specs/org-directory.md\nT3): org_employees (self-referential parent_id tree, nullable user_id for the\nsynthetic per-tenant root card) and org_directory_sync_runs (sync status;\na partial unique index on (tenant_id) WHERE status=''running'' doubles as the\nper-tenant sync concurrency lock at the DB level). Plain Drizzle tables, not\nan entity-engine module -- same reasoning as packages/teams (ADR-016\nDecision 1): tree traversal is a hot path, not a JSONB walk.\n\nWires both tables into the platform''s GDPR erasure paths (#635, added to\ndb-conventions.md after this spec was drafted): tenant-purge.ts deletes them\non tenant deletion; user-erasure.ts reparents an erased employee''s direct\nreports one hop up (falling back to the tenant root if needed) then deletes\ntheir row, and redacts org_directory_sync_runs.triggered_by like other\ncreated_by-style columns. Fixture and DB-level isolation tests included.\n\nPR2 of the org-directory track, stacked on PR1. No routes/query API/UI yet.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(db): add org-directory importer, tree-build algorithm, and sync engine\n\nNew packages/org-directory modules (docs/specs/org-directory.md T4):\n\n- tree-builder.ts: pure algorithm resolving each employee''s parent from a\n  fresh pull + prior tree -- root attachment (R3), one-hop reparent on\n  manager removal (R5), cycle detection/break (R4), department\n  normalization (R6). No DB, no network -- 19 unit tests.\n- zitadel-importer.ts: ZitadelOrgSourceImporter, the sole module allowed to\n  call Zitadel. Concurrency-capped (10) metadata fetch per user. Also adds\n  a third metadata key, `title`, to packages/auth''s existing manager_id/\n  department contract -- Zitadel has no native job-title field.\n- sync.ts: runOrgDirectorySync orchestrates the above into one transactional\n  rebuild (R2 atomicity), with the external fetch kept outside any DB\n  transaction.\n\nConcurrency (R2) went through two rounds of security review. First: a\nDB row-based lock (partial unique index) with a 30-minute stale-run\nreclaim -- found to have a real race (a slow-but-healthy sync''s lock could\nbe stolen by a second caller, causing concurrent writes to the same\ntenant). Replaced with a session-scoped Postgres advisory lock\n(acquireTenantAdvisoryLock, new packages/db export) held on a reserved\nconnection for the sync''s full duration, released automatically if the\nconnection drops -- no timeout guess needed. Second review round found and\nfixed a connection-leak edge case in that helper, a result-masking bug in\nthe release path, and added a deterministic end-to-end test proving the\nlock is held across the external-fetch gap, not just around the DB writes.\n\nPR3 of the org-directory track, stacked on PR2. Sync engine has no caller\nyet -- the admin route and scheduled worker job are PR4/T5.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(auth): address pr711 review feedback -- vitest deps.inline, dead param\n\n- packages/org-directory/vitest.config.ts: add server.deps.inline for\n  @platform/* workspace deps, matching the existing packages/workflow-engine\n  convention -- without it, vitest''s per-package module isolation can break\n  instanceof checks across the @platform/* boundary.\n- zitadel-management.ts: remove parseOrgMetadataEntries''s unused _userId\n  param rather than keep it for a hypothetical future logging path.\n- zitadel-management.test.ts: tighten the malformed-base64 test to assert\n  the exact best-effort-decoded value (the function does not skip malformed\n  entries, despite the old test''s name implying it did); add a test proving\n  the no-token path evicts its cache entry instead of permanently caching\n  an empty result.\n\nAddresses PrabhuVijit''s review on PR #711.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(db): address pr712 review feedback -- renumber migration, fix erasure null-fallback\n\n- Renumber packages/db/migrations/0128_org_directory_tables.sql to\n  0129_org_directory_tables.sql -- 0128 collides with an already-merged\n  security advisory PR''s own migration (verified against upstream/main).\n  Updates the header comment and one sibling code comment in\n  packages/db/src/schema/org-directory.ts to match.\n- apps/api/src/services/user-erasure.ts: when reparenting an erased\n  employee''s direct reports (docs/specs/org-directory.md T12), throw\n  instead of silently writing parent_id = NULL when no root row exists for\n  the tenant. The prior fallback (root?.id ?? null) would detach reports\n  from the tree entirely on a corrupt/never-synced tenant instead of\n  surfacing the inconsistency. New isolation test proves both the throw\n  and that nothing gets detached when it fires.\n- Migration comment corrected: the partial unique index on\n  org_directory_sync_runs is a secondary DB-level backstop, not the\n  primary sync-concurrency lock -- that''s the Postgres advisory lock\n  (acquireTenantAdvisoryLock, landing in PR #713).\n\nAddresses PrabhuVijit''s review on PR #712.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(db): org-directory phase 2 -- sync triggers, query api, isolation tests\n\nAdds T5 (first-boot auto-seed + 24h worker reconcile + admin-only manual\nsync route) and T6 (getOrgTree/getChainToRoot/getReportsByLevel/getSyncStatus\nquery api, read-only, never touches the auth provider), plus T9 isolation\ncoverage proving cross-tenant reads return empty rather than leaking data.\n\nAlso fixes two real bugs found while getting isolation tests to actually\nrun: migrations/meta/_journal.json was missing PR3''s own 0129_org_directory_\ntables entry (that migration had never registered as applied anywhere), and\ntwo isolation test files used non-hex UUID literals Postgres now correctly\nrejects.\n\nStacked on feat/org-directory-03-importer-and-tree-build (PR713).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(ui): org-directory phase 3 -- admin-ui org chart page\n\nAdds T7: the org chart page (apps/admin-ui/src/pages/org-directory.tsx) --\na visual tree (boxes/lines, not a list/table), loaded expanded to depth 3\nby default with per-node fold/unfold beyond that, search by name/email that\nhighlights the match and auto-expands its ancestor path, a sync-status\nindicator (\"last synced X ago\" / \"last sync failed -- showing stale data\"),\nand an admin-only \"Sync now\" button. Any authenticated tenant user can view\nthe page; only the manual sync trigger is admin-gated (client-side as a UX\nnicety, server-side as the real enforcement via the existing requireRole\nroute guard).\n\nT10 (mandatory /security-review pass) is done: no blocking findings --\nclient-side admin check confirmed UX-only, no data leakage, no XSS vector\n(plain JSX text rendering throughout), no same-origin bypass, route\ncorrectly outside RequireAdmin matching the any-authenticated-user-can-view\ndesign.\n\nStacked on feat/org-directory-04-sync-triggers-and-query-api (PR722).\n\nThis completes docs/specs/org-directory-tasks.md Phases 1-3 (T1-T10).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(db): register 0129_org_directory_tables in the migration journal\n\nmigrations/meta/_journal.json was missing this migration''s entry, so a\nfresh db:migrate (including CI''s isolation-test job) never actually created\norg_employees/org_directory_sync_runs -- causing PR712''s CI to fail with\n\"relation org_employees does not exist\" across 6 isolation tests. Same fix\nalready applied on the stacked feat/org-directory-04 branch; backported\nhere since PR712''s own CI checks out this branch in isolation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(db): invalid uuid literals + missing root row in shared erasure fixture\n\norg-directory.isolation.test.ts used uuid literals with non-hex segments\n(org1 contains o/r/g), which Postgres now correctly rejects once the tables\nactually exist to test against.\n\nseed-every-tenant-table.sql seeded an org_employees row directly without\never creating the required synthetic root (R3: exactly one root per\ntenant) -- a state that can never occur in real operation, but tripped\neraseUserFromTenant''s no-root guard (PR712''s own review fix) in every\ngeneric per-user-erasure coverage test that uses this shared fixture.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(api): fix flaky advisory-lock race in org-directory sync test\n\nThe \"holds the lock across the external fetch gap\" test raced a slow\nsync against a polling second call, assuming the first call''s advisory\nlock acquisition had already landed before polling started. Under CI\nconnection-pool contention that ordering wasn''t guaranteed, letting the\nsecond call occasionally win the lock and flip the assertion.\n\nWait for a fetchAll-started signal (only fires once the lock is\nconfirmed held) before polling, removing the race instead of papering\nover it with more retries.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(deps): pin grpc-js to >=1.14.5 (ghsa-m9gg-hp2v-232j)\n\ngetAuthContext could return unauthorized certificates as though they\nwere authorized. Pulled in transitively by packages/telemetry via\n@opentelemetry/sdk-node''s otlp-grpc exporters.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(api): audit failed admin-triggered org-directory syncs\n\nA failed sync was only logged via logger.error, with no durable audit\nrecord -- the exact case compliance/incident review needs most, since\nit''s an admin-triggered write that didn''t complete. Adds a\nwriteAuditEntry call on the failure path with a new \"sync_failed\"\naction, wired into AuditAction, outcome.ts (allowed -- a worker/upstream\nfailure, not a denied caller request), and request-kind.ts (write).\nMigration 0130 extends the admin_audit_log CHECK constraint in the\nsame commit per the established rule.\n\nReview finding from PrabhuVijit on PR722.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(admin-ui): add search + ancestor auto-expand coverage (r9)\n\nThe search-highlights-and-auto-expands-ancestors requirement (R9) had\nno test coverage despite being the primary navigation mechanism for a\ncollapsed tree. Adds a depth-4 fixture node so one test can prove a\ngenuinely-collapsed node becomes visible after search (not just\nhighlighting an already-visible one), plus a no-match case and a\nmulti-match first-wins case that documents the current single-match\nbehaviour.\n\nReview finding from PrabhuVijit on PR723.","tree":{"sha":"7d7c072cac446dc9a2ba66ae687bfece466b048c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/trees/7d7c072cac446dc9a2ba66ae687bfece466b048c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/commits/fc8a519c7667281103ab5998848e96df14c6e3da","verification":{"payload":"tree 7d7c072cac446dc9a2ba66ae687bfece466b048c\nparent 4ddd9f5228fc271387afab6a7e4a28f6342700bd\nauthor TusharSharma991 <67047397+TusharSharma991@users.noreply.github.com> 1790881796 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790881796 +0530\n\nfeat(ui): org-directory PR5 — admin-ui org chart page (#723)\n\n* feat(auth): add zitadel manager_id/department metadata read + org-directory scaffold\n\nNew @platform/org-directory package (docs/specs/org-directory.md) with the\nOrgSourceImporter/OrgNode/OrgTree contract that keeps the org-chart tree\nswappable across identity providers. Adds getOrgMetadataForUser to\npackages/auth/src/zitadel-management.ts, reading exactly the manager_id/\ndepartment metadata keys via the existing service-account token path,\nwith the same cache/single-flight pattern as the file''s other lookups.\n\nPR1 of the org-directory track (spec + tasks in docs/specs/). No schema,\nroutes, or UI yet — those land in follow-up PRs per the tasks file.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(db): add org_employees + org_directory_sync_runs tables, wire gdpr erasure\n\nNew tenant-scoped tables for the org-directory tree (docs/specs/org-directory.md\nT3): org_employees (self-referential parent_id tree, nullable user_id for the\nsynthetic per-tenant root card) and org_directory_sync_runs (sync status;\na partial unique index on (tenant_id) WHERE status=''running'' doubles as the\nper-tenant sync concurrency lock at the DB level). Plain Drizzle tables, not\nan entity-engine module -- same reasoning as packages/teams (ADR-016\nDecision 1): tree traversal is a hot path, not a JSONB walk.\n\nWires both tables into the platform''s GDPR erasure paths (#635, added to\ndb-conventions.md after this spec was drafted): tenant-purge.ts deletes them\non tenant deletion; user-erasure.ts reparents an erased employee''s direct\nreports one hop up (falling back to the tenant root if needed) then deletes\ntheir row, and redacts org_directory_sync_runs.triggered_by like other\ncreated_by-style columns. Fixture and DB-level isolation tests included.\n\nPR2 of the org-directory track, stacked on PR1. No routes/query API/UI yet.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(db): add org-directory importer, tree-build algorithm, and sync engine\n\nNew packages/org-directory modules (docs/specs/org-directory.md T4):\n\n- tree-builder.ts: pure algorithm resolving each employee''s parent from a\n  fresh pull + prior tree -- root attachment (R3), one-hop reparent on\n  manager removal (R5), cycle detection/break (R4), department\n  normalization (R6). No DB, no network -- 19 unit tests.\n- zitadel-importer.ts: ZitadelOrgSourceImporter, the sole module allowed to\n  call Zitadel. Concurrency-capped (10) metadata fetch per user. Also adds\n  a third metadata key, `title`, to packages/auth''s existing manager_id/\n  department contract -- Zitadel has no native job-title field.\n- sync.ts: runOrgDirectorySync orchestrates the above into one transactional\n  rebuild (R2 atomicity), with the external fetch kept outside any DB\n  transaction.\n\nConcurrency (R2) went through two rounds of security review. First: a\nDB row-based lock (partial unique index) with a 30-minute stale-run\nreclaim -- found to have a real race (a slow-but-healthy sync''s lock could\nbe stolen by a second caller, causing concurrent writes to the same\ntenant). Replaced with a session-scoped Postgres advisory lock\n(acquireTenantAdvisoryLock, new packages/db export) held on a reserved\nconnection for the sync''s full duration, released automatically if the\nconnection drops -- no timeout guess needed. Second review round found and\nfixed a connection-leak edge case in that helper, a result-masking bug in\nthe release path, and added a deterministic end-to-end test proving the\nlock is held across the external-fetch gap, not just around the DB writes.\n\nPR3 of the org-directory track, stacked on PR2. Sync engine has no caller\nyet -- the admin route and scheduled worker job are PR4/T5.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(auth): address pr711 review feedback -- vitest deps.inline, dead param\n\n- packages/org-directory/vitest.config.ts: add server.deps.inline for\n  @platform/* workspace deps, matching the existing packages/workflow-engine\n  convention -- without it, vitest''s per-package module isolation can break\n  instanceof checks across the @platform/* boundary.\n- zitadel-management.ts: remove parseOrgMetadataEntries''s unused _userId\n  param rather than keep it for a hypothetical future logging path.\n- zitadel-management.test.ts: tighten the malformed-base64 test to assert\n  the exact best-effort-decoded value (the function does not skip malformed\n  entries, despite the old test''s name implying it did); add a test proving\n  the no-token path evicts its cache entry instead of permanently caching\n  an empty result.\n\nAddresses PrabhuVijit''s review on PR #711.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(db): address pr712 review feedback -- renumber migration, fix erasure null-fallback\n\n- Renumber packages/db/migrations/0128_org_directory_tables.sql to\n  0129_org_directory_tables.sql -- 0128 collides with an already-merged\n  security advisory PR''s own migration (verified against upstream/main).\n  Updates the header comment and one sibling code comment in\n  packages/db/src/schema/org-directory.ts to match.\n- apps/api/src/services/user-erasure.ts: when reparenting an erased\n  employee''s direct reports (docs/specs/org-directory.md T12), throw\n  instead of silently writing parent_id = NULL when no root row exists for\n  the tenant. The prior fallback (root?.id ?? null) would detach reports\n  from the tree entirely on a corrupt/never-synced tenant instead of\n  surfacing the inconsistency. New isolation test proves both the throw\n  and that nothing gets detached when it fires.\n- Migration comment corrected: the partial unique index on\n  org_directory_sync_runs is a secondary DB-level backstop, not the\n  primary sync-concurrency lock -- that''s the Postgres advisory lock\n  (acquireTenantAdvisoryLock, landing in PR #713).\n\nAddresses PrabhuVijit''s review on PR #712.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(db): org-directory phase 2 -- sync triggers, query api, isolation tests\n\nAdds T5 (first-boot auto-seed + 24h worker reconcile + admin-only manual\nsync route) and T6 (getOrgTree/getChainToRoot/getReportsByLevel/getSyncStatus\nquery api, read-only, never touches the auth provider), plus T9 isolation\ncoverage proving cross-tenant reads return empty rather than leaking data.\n\nAlso fixes two real bugs found while getting isolation tests to actually\nrun: migrations/meta/_journal.json was missing PR3''s own 0129_org_directory_\ntables entry (that migration had never registered as applied anywhere), and\ntwo isolation test files used non-hex UUID literals Postgres now correctly\nrejects.\n\nStacked on feat/org-directory-03-importer-and-tree-build (PR713).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(ui): org-directory phase 3 -- admin-ui org chart page\n\nAdds T7: the org chart page (apps/admin-ui/src/pages/org-directory.tsx) --\na visual tree (boxes/lines, not a list/table), loaded expanded to depth 3\nby default with per-node fold/unfold beyond that, search by name/email that\nhighlights the match and auto-expands its ancestor path, a sync-status\nindicator (\"last synced X ago\" / \"last sync failed -- showing stale data\"),\nand an admin-only \"Sync now\" button. Any authenticated tenant user can view\nthe page; only the manual sync trigger is admin-gated (client-side as a UX\nnicety, server-side as the real enforcement via the existing requireRole\nroute guard).\n\nT10 (mandatory /security-review pass) is done: no blocking findings --\nclient-side admin check confirmed UX-only, no data leakage, no XSS vector\n(plain JSX text rendering throughout), no same-origin bypass, route\ncorrectly outside RequireAdmin matching the any-authenticated-user-can-view\ndesign.\n\nStacked on feat/org-directory-04-sync-triggers-and-query-api (PR722).\n\nThis completes docs/specs/org-directory-tasks.md Phases 1-3 (T1-T10).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(db): register 0129_org_directory_tables in the migration journal\n\nmigrations/meta/_journal.json was missing this migration''s entry, so a\nfresh db:migrate (including CI''s isolation-test job) never actually created\norg_employees/org_directory_sync_runs -- causing PR712''s CI to fail with\n\"relation org_employees does not exist\" across 6 isolation tests. Same fix\nalready applied on the stacked feat/org-directory-04 branch; backported\nhere since PR712''s own CI checks out this branch in isolation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(db): invalid uuid literals + missing root row in shared erasure fixture\n\norg-directory.isolation.test.ts used uuid literals with non-hex segments\n(org1 contains o/r/g), which Postgres now correctly rejects once the tables\nactually exist to test against.\n\nseed-every-tenant-table.sql seeded an org_employees row directly without\never creating the required synthetic root (R3: exactly one root per\ntenant) -- a state that can never occur in real operation, but tripped\neraseUserFromTenant''s no-root guard (PR712''s own review fix) in every\ngeneric per-user-erasure coverage test that uses this shared fixture.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(api): fix flaky advisory-lock race in org-directory sync test\n\nThe \"holds the lock across the external fetch gap\" test raced a slow\nsync against a polling second call, assuming the first call''s advisory\nlock acquisition had already landed before polling started. Under CI\nconnection-pool contention that ordering wasn''t guaranteed, letting the\nsecond call occasionally win the lock and flip the assertion.\n\nWait for a fetchAll-started signal (only fires once the lock is\nconfirmed held) before polling, removing the race instead of papering\nover it with more retries.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(deps): pin grpc-js to >=1.14.5 (ghsa-m9gg-hp2v-232j)\n\ngetAuthContext could return unauthorized certificates as though they\nwere authorized. Pulled in transitively by packages/telemetry via\n@opentelemetry/sdk-node''s otlp-grpc exporters.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(api): audit failed admin-triggered org-directory syncs\n\nA failed sync was only logged via logger.error, with no durable audit\nrecord -- the exact case compliance/incident review needs most, since\nit''s an admin-triggered write that didn''t complete. Adds a\nwriteAuditEntry call on the failure path with a new \"sync_failed\"\naction, wired into AuditAction, outcome.ts (allowed -- a worker/upstream\nfailure, not a denied caller request), and request-kind.ts (write).\nMigration 0130 extends the admin_audit_log CHECK constraint in the\nsame commit per the established rule.\n\nReview finding from PrabhuVijit on PR722.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(admin-ui): add search + ancestor auto-expand coverage (r9)\n\nThe search-highlights-and-auto-expands-ancestors requirement (R9) had\nno test coverage despite being the primary navigation mechanism for a\ncollapsed tree. Adds a depth-4 fixture node so one test can prove a\ngenuinely-collapsed node becomes visible after search (not just\nhighlighting an already-visible one), plus a no-match case and a\nmulti-match first-wins case that documents the current single-match\nbehaviour.\n\nReview finding from PrabhuVijit on PR723.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvrAECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAH6gQADSbqI2F+LYWZOM6x0LqztmD\nRlhSGisbLd6zHvSJfaK3tVREwF8pPXM3F8rIXUSbdH4i7ZLDvGTbH29bDArr1Nfl\nWMWhjQ9MWjdqTFnBl/vUX/ujAyRAB1oYKKky/YSrltlxU164olpQuN3A4hq3WCwi\nrEHmFfGuWTW40Ap7rRSpidYrF3JN9JKhGtvpaZ66/sTDVh9qQfZhFV0P1CaEW6J6\nvNxR+7Ke0EF4dk9spuw88EfWuSfRYDirIbPkFxmNEqpH6Q7M5gP4V6ExxOonhLvR\nU41p0T1rfpzgsAazlxPp3khtJ1Va9WJP1u8bQkQnybVCqZxEuOuRYmOzFa4Dy975\nluWGg9KsjMNLv3zLBrDJjkPWwm3UpCwGybXfgRaTE/Cd7aSQ+oPhtx0WDxczbjvu\n4bVCQc5/tg+dOR/NEMDY7C1diIGWhuyyfRg7zmx2m4KOkJ5bSX77sTQ8w0LEQtXz\n08CjSqc2rAcqE2U3Qp4HwLfER1PERgETuhdlhp3kMlJXrS2EEwe6HFmqfFqLz68M\nlsz/KYj76ewalebc8FDOanQITaL4ZaHXo0utL54V2/oNeXuf4FO+fzrb+GnR0/TX\nlwyiPrhC6SxuDxY6hY7oGi4DHDiAOjBmMdHdDuTQUkd0lPnfe6iXCbWlvjpMWTpC\nXmq3F6XtGEPr2O46fwkZ\n=roHy\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-01T19:09:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commit/fc8a519c7667281103ab5998848e96df14c6e3da","node_id":"C_kwDOScMdh9oAKGZjOGE1MTljNzY2NzI4MTEwM2FiNTk5ODg0OGU5NmRmMTRjNmUzZGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commit/4ddd9f5228fc271387afab6a7e4a28f6342700bd","sha":"4ddd9f5228fc271387afab6a7e4a28f6342700bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/4ddd9f5228fc271387afab6a7e4a28f6342700bd"}],"sha":"fc8a519c7667281103ab5998848e96df14c6e3da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/fc8a519c7667281103ab5998848e96df14c6e3da"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/67047397?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TusharSharma991","id":67047397,"login":"TusharSharma991","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3MDQ3Mzk3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/4ddd9f5228fc271387afab6a7e4a28f6342700bd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T18:49:47Z","email":"67047397+TusharSharma991@users.noreply.github.com","name":"TusharSharma991"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T18:49:47Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(db): org-directory PR4 — sync triggers, query API, isolation tests (#722)\n\n* feat(auth): add zitadel manager_id/department metadata read + org-directory scaffold\n\nNew @platform/org-directory package (docs/specs/org-directory.md) with the\nOrgSourceImporter/OrgNode/OrgTree contract that keeps the org-chart tree\nswappable across identity providers. Adds getOrgMetadataForUser to\npackages/auth/src/zitadel-management.ts, reading exactly the manager_id/\ndepartment metadata keys via the existing service-account token path,\nwith the same cache/single-flight pattern as the file''s other lookups.\n\nPR1 of the org-directory track (spec + tasks in docs/specs/). No schema,\nroutes, or UI yet — those land in follow-up PRs per the tasks file.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(db): add org_employees + org_directory_sync_runs tables, wire gdpr erasure\n\nNew tenant-scoped tables for the org-directory tree (docs/specs/org-directory.md\nT3): org_employees (self-referential parent_id tree, nullable user_id for the\nsynthetic per-tenant root card) and org_directory_sync_runs (sync status;\na partial unique index on (tenant_id) WHERE status=''running'' doubles as the\nper-tenant sync concurrency lock at the DB level). Plain Drizzle tables, not\nan entity-engine module -- same reasoning as packages/teams (ADR-016\nDecision 1): tree traversal is a hot path, not a JSONB walk.\n\nWires both tables into the platform''s GDPR erasure paths (#635, added to\ndb-conventions.md after this spec was drafted): tenant-purge.ts deletes them\non tenant deletion; user-erasure.ts reparents an erased employee''s direct\nreports one hop up (falling back to the tenant root if needed) then deletes\ntheir row, and redacts org_directory_sync_runs.triggered_by like other\ncreated_by-style columns. Fixture and DB-level isolation tests included.\n\nPR2 of the org-directory track, stacked on PR1. No routes/query API/UI yet.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(db): add org-directory importer, tree-build algorithm, and sync engine\n\nNew packages/org-directory modules (docs/specs/org-directory.md T4):\n\n- tree-builder.ts: pure algorithm resolving each employee''s parent from a\n  fresh pull + prior tree -- root attachment (R3), one-hop reparent on\n  manager removal (R5), cycle detection/break (R4), department\n  normalization (R6). No DB, no network -- 19 unit tests.\n- zitadel-importer.ts: ZitadelOrgSourceImporter, the sole module allowed to\n  call Zitadel. Concurrency-capped (10) metadata fetch per user. Also adds\n  a third metadata key, `title`, to packages/auth''s existing manager_id/\n  department contract -- Zitadel has no native job-title field.\n- sync.ts: runOrgDirectorySync orchestrates the above into one transactional\n  rebuild (R2 atomicity), with the external fetch kept outside any DB\n  transaction.\n\nConcurrency (R2) went through two rounds of security review. First: a\nDB row-based lock (partial unique index) with a 30-minute stale-run\nreclaim -- found to have a real race (a slow-but-healthy sync''s lock could\nbe stolen by a second caller, causing concurrent writes to the same\ntenant). Replaced with a session-scoped Postgres advisory lock\n(acquireTenantAdvisoryLock, new packages/db export) held on a reserved\nconnection for the sync''s full duration, released automatically if the\nconnection drops -- no timeout guess needed. Second review round found and\nfixed a connection-leak edge case in that helper, a result-masking bug in\nthe release path, and added a deterministic end-to-end test proving the\nlock is held across the external-fetch gap, not just around the DB writes.\n\nPR3 of the org-directory track, stacked on PR2. Sync engine has no caller\nyet -- the admin route and scheduled worker job are PR4/T5.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(auth): address pr711 review feedback -- vitest deps.inline, dead param\n\n- packages/org-directory/vitest.config.ts: add server.deps.inline for\n  @platform/* workspace deps, matching the existing packages/workflow-engine\n  convention -- without it, vitest''s per-package module isolation can break\n  instanceof checks across the @platform/* boundary.\n- zitadel-management.ts: remove parseOrgMetadataEntries''s unused _userId\n  param rather than keep it for a hypothetical future logging path.\n- zitadel-management.test.ts: tighten the malformed-base64 test to assert\n  the exact best-effort-decoded value (the function does not skip malformed\n  entries, despite the old test''s name implying it did); add a test proving\n  the no-token path evicts its cache entry instead of permanently caching\n  an empty result.\n\nAddresses PrabhuVijit''s review on PR #711.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(db): address pr712 review feedback -- renumber migration, fix erasure null-fallback\n\n- Renumber packages/db/migrations/0128_org_directory_tables.sql to\n  0129_org_directory_tables.sql -- 0128 collides with an already-merged\n  security advisory PR''s own migration (verified against upstream/main).\n  Updates the header comment and one sibling code comment in\n  packages/db/src/schema/org-directory.ts to match.\n- apps/api/src/services/user-erasure.ts: when reparenting an erased\n  employee''s direct reports (docs/specs/org-directory.md T12), throw\n  instead of silently writing parent_id = NULL when no root row exists for\n  the tenant. The prior fallback (root?.id ?? null) would detach reports\n  from the tree entirely on a corrupt/never-synced tenant instead of\n  surfacing the inconsistency. New isolation test proves both the throw\n  and that nothing gets detached when it fires.\n- Migration comment corrected: the partial unique index on\n  org_directory_sync_runs is a secondary DB-level backstop, not the\n  primary sync-concurrency lock -- that''s the Postgres advisory lock\n  (acquireTenantAdvisoryLock, landing in PR #713).\n\nAddresses PrabhuVijit''s review on PR #712.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(db): org-directory phase 2 -- sync triggers, query api, isolation tests\n\nAdds T5 (first-boot auto-seed + 24h worker reconcile + admin-only manual\nsync route) and T6 (getOrgTree/getChainToRoot/getReportsByLevel/getSyncStatus\nquery api, read-only, never touches the auth provider), plus T9 isolation\ncoverage proving cross-tenant reads return empty rather than leaking data.\n\nAlso fixes two real bugs found while getting isolation tests to actually\nrun: migrations/meta/_journal.json was missing PR3''s own 0129_org_directory_\ntables entry (that migration had never registered as applied anywhere), and\ntwo isolation test files used non-hex UUID literals Postgres now correctly\nrejects.\n\nStacked on feat/org-directory-03-importer-and-tree-build (PR713).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(db): register 0129_org_directory_tables in the migration journal\n\nmigrations/meta/_journal.json was missing this migration''s entry, so a\nfresh db:migrate (including CI''s isolation-test job) never actually created\norg_employees/org_directory_sync_runs -- causing PR712''s CI to fail with\n\"relation org_employees does not exist\" across 6 isolation tests. Same fix\nalready applied on the stacked feat/org-directory-04 branch; backported\nhere since PR712''s own CI checks out this branch in isolation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(db): invalid uuid literals + missing root row in shared erasure fixture\n\norg-directory.isolation.test.ts used uuid literals with non-hex segments\n(org1 contains o/r/g), which Postgres now correctly rejects once the tables\nactually exist to test against.\n\nseed-every-tenant-table.sql seeded an org_employees row directly without\never creating the required synthetic root (R3: exactly one root per\ntenant) -- a state that can never occur in real operation, but tripped\neraseUserFromTenant''s no-root guard (PR712''s own review fix) in every\ngeneric per-user-erasure coverage test that uses this shared fixture.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(api): fix flaky advisory-lock race in org-directory sync test\n\nThe \"holds the lock across the external fetch gap\" test raced a slow\nsync against a polling second call, assuming the first call''s advisory\nlock acquisition had already landed before polling started. Under CI\nconnection-pool contention that ordering wasn''t guaranteed, letting the\nsecond call occasionally win the lock and flip the assertion.\n\nWait for a fetchAll-started signal (only fires once the lock is\nconfirmed held) before polling, removing the race instead of papering\nover it with more retries.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(deps): pin grpc-js to >=1.14.5 (ghsa-m9gg-hp2v-232j)\n\ngetAuthContext could return unauthorized certificates as though they\nwere authorized. Pulled in transitively by packages/telemetry via\n@opentelemetry/sdk-node''s otlp-grpc exporters.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(api): audit failed admin-triggered org-directory syncs\n\nA failed sync was only logged via logger.error, with no durable audit\nrecord -- the exact case compliance/incident review needs most, since\nit''s an admin-triggered write that didn''t complete. Adds a\nwriteAuditEntry call on the failure path with a new \"sync_failed\"\naction, wired into AuditAction, outcome.ts (allowed -- a worker/upstream\nfailure, not a denied caller request), and request-kind.ts (write).\nMigration 0130 extends the admin_audit_log CHECK constraint in the\nsame commit per the established rule.\n\nReview finding from PrabhuVijit on PR722.","tree":{"sha":"d824328145dfdbfe8cb7d6fadfddbaadafca5f7d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/trees/d824328145dfdbfe8cb7d6fadfddbaadafca5f7d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/commits/4ddd9f5228fc271387afab6a7e4a28f6342700bd","verification":{"payload":"tree d824328145dfdbfe8cb7d6fadfddbaadafca5f7d\nparent 89829cd39634a5b08a32fc7c890ca54ada127cdf\nauthor TusharSharma991 <67047397+TusharSharma991@users.noreply.github.com> 1790880587 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790880587 +0530\n\nfeat(db): org-directory PR4 — sync triggers, query API, isolation tests (#722)\n\n* feat(auth): add zitadel manager_id/department metadata read + org-directory scaffold\n\nNew @platform/org-directory package (docs/specs/org-directory.md) with the\nOrgSourceImporter/OrgNode/OrgTree contract that keeps the org-chart tree\nswappable across identity providers. Adds getOrgMetadataForUser to\npackages/auth/src/zitadel-management.ts, reading exactly the manager_id/\ndepartment metadata keys via the existing service-account token path,\nwith the same cache/single-flight pattern as the file''s other lookups.\n\nPR1 of the org-directory track (spec + tasks in docs/specs/). No schema,\nroutes, or UI yet — those land in follow-up PRs per the tasks file.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(db): add org_employees + org_directory_sync_runs tables, wire gdpr erasure\n\nNew tenant-scoped tables for the org-directory tree (docs/specs/org-directory.md\nT3): org_employees (self-referential parent_id tree, nullable user_id for the\nsynthetic per-tenant root card) and org_directory_sync_runs (sync status;\na partial unique index on (tenant_id) WHERE status=''running'' doubles as the\nper-tenant sync concurrency lock at the DB level). Plain Drizzle tables, not\nan entity-engine module -- same reasoning as packages/teams (ADR-016\nDecision 1): tree traversal is a hot path, not a JSONB walk.\n\nWires both tables into the platform''s GDPR erasure paths (#635, added to\ndb-conventions.md after this spec was drafted): tenant-purge.ts deletes them\non tenant deletion; user-erasure.ts reparents an erased employee''s direct\nreports one hop up (falling back to the tenant root if needed) then deletes\ntheir row, and redacts org_directory_sync_runs.triggered_by like other\ncreated_by-style columns. Fixture and DB-level isolation tests included.\n\nPR2 of the org-directory track, stacked on PR1. No routes/query API/UI yet.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(db): add org-directory importer, tree-build algorithm, and sync engine\n\nNew packages/org-directory modules (docs/specs/org-directory.md T4):\n\n- tree-builder.ts: pure algorithm resolving each employee''s parent from a\n  fresh pull + prior tree -- root attachment (R3), one-hop reparent on\n  manager removal (R5), cycle detection/break (R4), department\n  normalization (R6). No DB, no network -- 19 unit tests.\n- zitadel-importer.ts: ZitadelOrgSourceImporter, the sole module allowed to\n  call Zitadel. Concurrency-capped (10) metadata fetch per user. Also adds\n  a third metadata key, `title`, to packages/auth''s existing manager_id/\n  department contract -- Zitadel has no native job-title field.\n- sync.ts: runOrgDirectorySync orchestrates the above into one transactional\n  rebuild (R2 atomicity), with the external fetch kept outside any DB\n  transaction.\n\nConcurrency (R2) went through two rounds of security review. First: a\nDB row-based lock (partial unique index) with a 30-minute stale-run\nreclaim -- found to have a real race (a slow-but-healthy sync''s lock could\nbe stolen by a second caller, causing concurrent writes to the same\ntenant). Replaced with a session-scoped Postgres advisory lock\n(acquireTenantAdvisoryLock, new packages/db export) held on a reserved\nconnection for the sync''s full duration, released automatically if the\nconnection drops -- no timeout guess needed. Second review round found and\nfixed a connection-leak edge case in that helper, a result-masking bug in\nthe release path, and added a deterministic end-to-end test proving the\nlock is held across the external-fetch gap, not just around the DB writes.\n\nPR3 of the org-directory track, stacked on PR2. Sync engine has no caller\nyet -- the admin route and scheduled worker job are PR4/T5.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(auth): address pr711 review feedback -- vitest deps.inline, dead param\n\n- packages/org-directory/vitest.config.ts: add server.deps.inline for\n  @platform/* workspace deps, matching the existing packages/workflow-engine\n  convention -- without it, vitest''s per-package module isolation can break\n  instanceof checks across the @platform/* boundary.\n- zitadel-management.ts: remove parseOrgMetadataEntries''s unused _userId\n  param rather than keep it for a hypothetical future logging path.\n- zitadel-management.test.ts: tighten the malformed-base64 test to assert\n  the exact best-effort-decoded value (the function does not skip malformed\n  entries, despite the old test''s name implying it did); add a test proving\n  the no-token path evicts its cache entry instead of permanently caching\n  an empty result.\n\nAddresses PrabhuVijit''s review on PR #711.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(db): address pr712 review feedback -- renumber migration, fix erasure null-fallback\n\n- Renumber packages/db/migrations/0128_org_directory_tables.sql to\n  0129_org_directory_tables.sql -- 0128 collides with an already-merged\n  security advisory PR''s own migration (verified against upstream/main).\n  Updates the header comment and one sibling code comment in\n  packages/db/src/schema/org-directory.ts to match.\n- apps/api/src/services/user-erasure.ts: when reparenting an erased\n  employee''s direct reports (docs/specs/org-directory.md T12), throw\n  instead of silently writing parent_id = NULL when no root row exists for\n  the tenant. The prior fallback (root?.id ?? null) would detach reports\n  from the tree entirely on a corrupt/never-synced tenant instead of\n  surfacing the inconsistency. New isolation test proves both the throw\n  and that nothing gets detached when it fires.\n- Migration comment corrected: the partial unique index on\n  org_directory_sync_runs is a secondary DB-level backstop, not the\n  primary sync-concurrency lock -- that''s the Postgres advisory lock\n  (acquireTenantAdvisoryLock, landing in PR #713).\n\nAddresses PrabhuVijit''s review on PR #712.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(db): org-directory phase 2 -- sync triggers, query api, isolation tests\n\nAdds T5 (first-boot auto-seed + 24h worker reconcile + admin-only manual\nsync route) and T6 (getOrgTree/getChainToRoot/getReportsByLevel/getSyncStatus\nquery api, read-only, never touches the auth provider), plus T9 isolation\ncoverage proving cross-tenant reads return empty rather than leaking data.\n\nAlso fixes two real bugs found while getting isolation tests to actually\nrun: migrations/meta/_journal.json was missing PR3''s own 0129_org_directory_\ntables entry (that migration had never registered as applied anywhere), and\ntwo isolation test files used non-hex UUID literals Postgres now correctly\nrejects.\n\nStacked on feat/org-directory-03-importer-and-tree-build (PR713).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(db): register 0129_org_directory_tables in the migration journal\n\nmigrations/meta/_journal.json was missing this migration''s entry, so a\nfresh db:migrate (including CI''s isolation-test job) never actually created\norg_employees/org_directory_sync_runs -- causing PR712''s CI to fail with\n\"relation org_employees does not exist\" across 6 isolation tests. Same fix\nalready applied on the stacked feat/org-directory-04 branch; backported\nhere since PR712''s own CI checks out this branch in isolation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(db): invalid uuid literals + missing root row in shared erasure fixture\n\norg-directory.isolation.test.ts used uuid literals with non-hex segments\n(org1 contains o/r/g), which Postgres now correctly rejects once the tables\nactually exist to test against.\n\nseed-every-tenant-table.sql seeded an org_employees row directly without\never creating the required synthetic root (R3: exactly one root per\ntenant) -- a state that can never occur in real operation, but tripped\neraseUserFromTenant''s no-root guard (PR712''s own review fix) in every\ngeneric per-user-erasure coverage test that uses this shared fixture.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(api): fix flaky advisory-lock race in org-directory sync test\n\nThe \"holds the lock across the external fetch gap\" test raced a slow\nsync against a polling second call, assuming the first call''s advisory\nlock acquisition had already landed before polling started. Under CI\nconnection-pool contention that ordering wasn''t guaranteed, letting the\nsecond call occasionally win the lock and flip the assertion.\n\nWait for a fetchAll-started signal (only fires once the lock is\nconfirmed held) before polling, removing the race instead of papering\nover it with more retries.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(deps): pin grpc-js to >=1.14.5 (ghsa-m9gg-hp2v-232j)\n\ngetAuthContext could return unauthorized certificates as though they\nwere authorized. Pulled in transitively by packages/telemetry via\n@opentelemetry/sdk-node''s otlp-grpc exporters.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(api): audit failed admin-triggered org-directory syncs\n\nA failed sync was only logged via logger.error, with no durable audit\nrecord -- the exact case compliance/incident review needs most, since\nit''s an admin-triggered write that didn''t complete. Adds a\nwriteAuditEntry call on the failure path with a new \"sync_failed\"\naction, wired into AuditAction, outcome.ts (allowed -- a worker/upstream\nfailure, not a denied caller request), and request-kind.ts (write).\nMigration 0130 extends the admin_audit_log CHECK constraint in the\nsame commit per the established rule.\n\nReview finding from PrabhuVijit on PR722.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvqtLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAw5IQADRqIOMjX9QFZIFI8aFg0y6d\n5ELfObTufzRUDaZ+xoboSXvgDurnqmv/JMSPQ/cmu/XHu9LJmOwFCwT0vbyv7loE\nORNHkhO26NUGBdWYCLclRNLqDtUnFSMv+8h13CAAPvF++v5mdJBQ5e8uNc/c1IhE\n7qV/eOA/LlA3mgelCE5yKK5w28RiW4qgLvVTeJPqFtzYf2QUJM2IiIQLk3+IUQPt\nzgRs9f9uu5gQSjOhrjOROP6uv8ZEEXsDw3R8nCMTYNn8VRO/Q1xRRV7+wEwwv6mr\n2PYPEvYCn4jyrEhhKFI6gOMUIqZTyKJuocphpvU3uK24LLZ3LFV/R44FexQm64zz\nJM9SVaml5fnR2EJAWHDsq05n0EkZY06XWIkp+Ynm2OLjsPayL/PAp/iB2rU3FaE4\nlOR9agOWCxXZqsANXTWzGNDjGftqLXjeXnKyiaR++KWUIsU6OgYgCIP0jBwQSZYL\nbVSj0pSPK/vkwd965Vhp3Sdu1j+rPypQakQzU8t29l+CqHlAaMQMGlzUVCrezoD2\nNp5FFTqMt/QSTmgH8WrZnve+3lou4uOrFF+XjKsHH0OrO4gBjTSq750X+ni4Wng7\nbYJUzmJLDytquMy55Lcwgc0kw1nzzBZv7Nqrf9M5JN9eYU8T14LQT9WCX6ZovAoS\niWl0WAF5F8+F8Z2w8TXG\n=4nxB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-01T18:49:47Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.