narchive/2026-08/. The week-log README now documents the monthly\nroll-up rule.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvRzyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABZwQAAWmWlpcMAeQR4+m7MIBz90+\nBZQOvWEFuN2IJc8Ml4TTUmIGBHSpU7V4oNVYthHmMDFX+C2fovKbhxEtLMvD/o7h\nl8yL9z4mFhVXvMBZ/3V6+npbvSKDteGIYPqBEc85H+QP2byvNHW5D6QKEgU8QH45\n2a5bp6vyujCKYN1vaHmj46nY4RGQ0oBT9TBLYkfaTSy0kNc3dHvo0nhTx39CRrFU\nEJJVrTNpDU059XbYOK/xyUiunU8xDuelFKKcEdvbGX9/ycJeaWtgoz/yFcsUtfcd\nDOb48PFKM+C1zoQV5D0sezp8ZrMRo4jLmfkcE444NDP5Cc//YP+pXV+e1uCIQW9T\n6fhFbGeCXgHMEF0Tf1fGmwbLv4IMqN35DFMX66Bt1QWhVucomTLrSaXlGCsyCJ3F\nkZsLoX8PtYV08Akc7DeeWDsfAw2+Jr1PrsYXBHLwlFkrJGL5mTxiuLxU3GjKzV66\nd69Qivpdu6U3qgnMszlB8nGt0HOe7BLwRLxb2JUnuDP5zoRNdDDJaHhdR3K5/XiS\nFpY1cxP1vc5B07qaQqjXGz9dT6gabX7xJ29Zx3D7I3Ltc+LfZKcuQFmZ3EDwPL1n\nKVITJHjy6xp67EdVxuOxExDxLFRCJOXPQ5fa2rsIbI9CbE1MkjRKIhWzNve/eike\ncYN+t3NL+1Oa0w2rewqQ\n=9Lpg\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T14:30:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commit/9105da36ba98d85ff86255ca016d9bff51737088","node_id":"C_kwDOScMdh9oAKDkxMDVkYTM2YmE5OGQ4NWZmODYyNTVjYTAxNmQ5YmZmNTE3MzcwODg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commit/95116543f6a628e591afd5545bad864e5e26f72e","sha":"95116543f6a628e591afd5545bad864e5e26f72e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/95116543f6a628e591afd5545bad864e5e26f72e"}],"sha":"9105da36ba98d85ff86255ca016d9bff51737088","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/9105da36ba98d85ff86255ca016d9bff51737088"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/67047397?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TusharSharma991","id":67047397,"login":"TusharSharma991","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3MDQ3Mzk3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/95116543f6a628e591afd5545bad864e5e26f72e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T14:26:31Z","email":"67047397+TusharSharma991@users.noreply.github.com","name":"TusharSharma991"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T14:26:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(db): org-directory PR3 — importer, tree-build algorithm, sync engine (#713)\n\n* feat(auth): add zitadel manager_id/department metadata read + org-directory scaffold\n\nNew @platform/org-directory package (docs/specs/org-directory.md) with the\nOrgSourceImporter/OrgNode/OrgTree contract that keeps the org-chart tree\nswappable across identity providers. Adds getOrgMetadataForUser to\npackages/auth/src/zitadel-management.ts, reading exactly the manager_id/\ndepartment metadata keys via the existing service-account token path,\nwith the same cache/single-flight pattern as the file''s other lookups.\n\nPR1 of the org-directory track (spec + tasks in docs/specs/). No schema,\nroutes, or UI yet — those land in follow-up PRs per the tasks file.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(db): add org_employees + org_directory_sync_runs tables, wire gdpr erasure\n\nNew tenant-scoped tables for the org-directory tree (docs/specs/org-directory.md\nT3): org_employees (self-referential parent_id tree, nullable user_id for the\nsynthetic per-tenant root card) and org_directory_sync_runs (sync status;\na partial unique index on (tenant_id) WHERE status=''running'' doubles as the\nper-tenant sync concurrency lock at the DB level). Plain Drizzle tables, not\nan entity-engine module -- same reasoning as packages/teams (ADR-016\nDecision 1): tree traversal is a hot path, not a JSONB walk.\n\nWires both tables into the platform''s GDPR erasure paths (#635, added to\ndb-conventions.md after this spec was drafted): tenant-purge.ts deletes them\non tenant deletion; user-erasure.ts reparents an erased employee''s direct\nreports one hop up (falling back to the tenant root if needed) then deletes\ntheir row, and redacts org_directory_sync_runs.triggered_by like other\ncreated_by-style columns. Fixture and DB-level isolation tests included.\n\nPR2 of the org-directory track, stacked on PR1. No routes/query API/UI yet.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(db): add org-directory importer, tree-build algorithm, and sync engine\n\nNew packages/org-directory modules (docs/specs/org-directory.md T4):\n\n- tree-builder.ts: pure algorithm resolving each employee''s parent from a\n  fresh pull + prior tree -- root attachment (R3), one-hop reparent on\n  manager removal (R5), cycle detection/break (R4), department\n  normalization (R6). No DB, no network -- 19 unit tests.\n- zitadel-importer.ts: ZitadelOrgSourceImporter, the sole module allowed to\n  call Zitadel. Concurrency-capped (10) metadata fetch per user. Also adds\n  a third metadata key, `title`, to packages/auth''s existing manager_id/\n  department contract -- Zitadel has no native job-title field.\n- sync.ts: runOrgDirectorySync orchestrates the above into one transactional\n  rebuild (R2 atomicity), with the external fetch kept outside any DB\n  transaction.\n\nConcurrency (R2) went through two rounds of security review. First: a\nDB row-based lock (partial unique index) with a 30-minute stale-run\nreclaim -- found to have a real race (a slow-but-healthy sync''s lock could\nbe stolen by a second caller, causing concurrent writes to the same\ntenant). Replaced with a session-scoped Postgres advisory lock\n(acquireTenantAdvisoryLock, new packages/db export) held on a reserved\nconnection for the sync''s full duration, released automatically if the\nconnection drops -- no timeout guess needed. Second review round found and\nfixed a connection-leak edge case in that helper, a result-masking bug in\nthe release path, and added a deterministic end-to-end test proving the\nlock is held across the external-fetch gap, not just around the DB writes.\n\nPR3 of the org-directory track, stacked on PR2. Sync engine has no caller\nyet -- the admin route and scheduled worker job are PR4/T5.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(auth): address pr711 review feedback -- vitest deps.inline, dead param\n\n- packages/org-directory/vitest.config.ts: add server.deps.inline for\n  @platform/* workspace deps, matching the existing packages/workflow-engine\n  convention -- without it, vitest''s per-package module isolation can break\n  instanceof checks across the @platform/* boundary.\n- zitadel-management.ts: remove parseOrgMetadataEntries''s unused _userId\n  param rather than keep it for a hypothetical future logging path.\n- zitadel-management.test.ts: tighten the malformed-base64 test to assert\n  the exact best-effort-decoded value (the function does not skip malformed\n  entries, despite the old test''s name implying it did); add a test proving\n  the no-token path evicts its cache entry instead of permanently caching\n  an empty result.\n\nAddresses PrabhuVijit''s review on PR #711.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(db): address pr712 review feedback -- renumber migration, fix erasure null-fallback\n\n- Renumber packages/db/migrations/0128_org_directory_tables.sql to\n  0129_org_directory_tables.sql -- 0128 collides with an already-merged\n  security advisory PR''s own migration (verified against upstream/main).\n  Updates the header comment and one sibling code comment in\n  packages/db/src/schema/org-directory.ts to match.\n- apps/api/src/services/user-erasure.ts: when reparenting an erased\n  employee''s direct reports (docs/specs/org-directory.md T12), throw\n  instead of silently writing parent_id = NULL when no root row exists for\n  the tenant. The prior fallback (root?.id ?? null) would detach reports\n  from the tree entirely on a corrupt/never-synced tenant instead of\n  surfacing the inconsistency. New isolation test proves both the throw\n  and that nothing gets detached when it fires.\n- Migration comment corrected: the partial unique index on\n  org_directory_sync_runs is a secondary DB-level backstop, not the\n  primary sync-concurrency lock -- that''s the Postgres advisory lock\n  (acquireTenantAdvisoryLock, landing in PR #713).\n\nAddresses PrabhuVijit''s review on PR #712.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(db): register 0129_org_directory_tables in the migration journal\n\nmigrations/meta/_journal.json was missing this migration''s entry, so a\nfresh db:migrate (including CI''s isolation-test job) never actually created\norg_employees/org_directory_sync_runs -- causing PR712''s CI to fail with\n\"relation org_employees does not exist\" across 6 isolation tests. Same fix\nalready applied on the stacked feat/org-directory-04 branch; backported\nhere since PR712''s own CI checks out this branch in isolation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(db): invalid uuid literals + missing root row in shared erasure fixture\n\norg-directory.isolation.test.ts used uuid literals with non-hex segments\n(org1 contains o/r/g), which Postgres now correctly rejects once the tables\nactually exist to test against.\n\nseed-every-tenant-table.sql seeded an org_employees row directly without\never creating the required synthetic root (R3: exactly one root per\ntenant) -- a state that can never occur in real operation, but tripped\neraseUserFromTenant''s no-root guard (PR712''s own review fix) in every\ngeneric per-user-erasure coverage test that uses this shared fixture.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fb14ba2295de2d38748ddafaf1244fe60d2218b6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/trees/fb14ba2295de2d38748ddafaf1244fe60d2218b6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/commits/95116543f6a628e591afd5545bad864e5e26f72e","verification":{"payload":"tree fb14ba2295de2d38748ddafaf1244fe60d2218b6\nparent eff977b15cdf8a96d133f29de23e62b05c1cb851\nauthor TusharSharma991 <67047397+TusharSharma991@users.noreply.github.com> 1790778391 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790778391 +0530\n\nfeat(db): org-directory PR3 — importer, tree-build algorithm, sync engine (#713)\n\n* feat(auth): add zitadel manager_id/department metadata read + org-directory scaffold\n\nNew @platform/org-directory package (docs/specs/org-directory.md) with the\nOrgSourceImporter/OrgNode/OrgTree contract that keeps the org-chart tree\nswappable across identity providers. Adds getOrgMetadataForUser to\npackages/auth/src/zitadel-management.ts, reading exactly the manager_id/\ndepartment metadata keys via the existing service-account token path,\nwith the same cache/single-flight pattern as the file''s other lookups.\n\nPR1 of the org-directory track (spec + tasks in docs/specs/). No schema,\nroutes, or UI yet — those land in follow-up PRs per the tasks file.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(db): add org_employees + org_directory_sync_runs tables, wire gdpr erasure\n\nNew tenant-scoped tables for the org-directory tree (docs/specs/org-directory.md\nT3): org_employees (self-referential parent_id tree, nullable user_id for the\nsynthetic per-tenant root card) and org_directory_sync_runs (sync status;\na partial unique index on (tenant_id) WHERE status=''running'' doubles as the\nper-tenant sync concurrency lock at the DB level). Plain Drizzle tables, not\nan entity-engine module -- same reasoning as packages/teams (ADR-016\nDecision 1): tree traversal is a hot path, not a JSONB walk.\n\nWires both tables into the platform''s GDPR erasure paths (#635, added to\ndb-conventions.md after this spec was drafted): tenant-purge.ts deletes them\non tenant deletion; user-erasure.ts reparents an erased employee''s direct\nreports one hop up (falling back to the tenant root if needed) then deletes\ntheir row, and redacts org_directory_sync_runs.triggered_by like other\ncreated_by-style columns. Fixture and DB-level isolation tests included.\n\nPR2 of the org-directory track, stacked on PR1. No routes/query API/UI yet.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(db): add org-directory importer, tree-build algorithm, and sync engine\n\nNew packages/org-directory modules (docs/specs/org-directory.md T4):\n\n- tree-builder.ts: pure algorithm resolving each employee''s parent from a\n  fresh pull + prior tree -- root attachment (R3), one-hop reparent on\n  manager removal (R5), cycle detection/break (R4), department\n  normalization (R6). No DB, no network -- 19 unit tests.\n- zitadel-importer.ts: ZitadelOrgSourceImporter, the sole module allowed to\n  call Zitadel. Concurrency-capped (10) metadata fetch per user. Also adds\n  a third metadata key, `title`, to packages/auth''s existing manager_id/\n  department contract -- Zitadel has no native job-title field.\n- sync.ts: runOrgDirectorySync orchestrates the above into one transactional\n  rebuild (R2 atomicity), with the external fetch kept outside any DB\n  transaction.\n\nConcurrency (R2) went through two rounds of security review. First: a\nDB row-based lock (partial unique index) with a 30-minute stale-run\nreclaim -- found to have a real race (a slow-but-healthy sync''s lock could\nbe stolen by a second caller, causing concurrent writes to the same\ntenant). Replaced with a session-scoped Postgres advisory lock\n(acquireTenantAdvisoryLock, new packages/db export) held on a reserved\nconnection for the sync''s full duration, released automatically if the\nconnection drops -- no timeout guess needed. Second review round found and\nfixed a connection-leak edge case in that helper, a result-masking bug in\nthe release path, and added a deterministic end-to-end test proving the\nlock is held across the external-fetch gap, not just around the DB writes.\n\nPR3 of the org-directory track, stacked on PR2. Sync engine has no caller\nyet -- the admin route and scheduled worker job are PR4/T5.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(auth): address pr711 review feedback -- vitest deps.inline, dead param\n\n- packages/org-directory/vitest.config.ts: add server.deps.inline for\n  @platform/* workspace deps, matching the existing packages/workflow-engine\n  convention -- without it, vitest''s per-package module isolation can break\n  instanceof checks across the @platform/* boundary.\n- zitadel-management.ts: remove parseOrgMetadataEntries''s unused _userId\n  param rather than keep it for a hypothetical future logging path.\n- zitadel-management.test.ts: tighten the malformed-base64 test to assert\n  the exact best-effort-decoded value (the function does not skip malformed\n  entries, despite the old test''s name implying it did); add a test proving\n  the no-token path evicts its cache entry instead of permanently caching\n  an empty result.\n\nAddresses PrabhuVijit''s review on PR #711.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(db): address pr712 review feedback -- renumber migration, fix erasure null-fallback\n\n- Renumber packages/db/migrations/0128_org_directory_tables.sql to\n  0129_org_directory_tables.sql -- 0128 collides with an already-merged\n  security advisory PR''s own migration (verified against upstream/main).\n  Updates the header comment and one sibling code comment in\n  packages/db/src/schema/org-directory.ts to match.\n- apps/api/src/services/user-erasure.ts: when reparenting an erased\n  employee''s direct reports (docs/specs/org-directory.md T12), throw\n  instead of silently writing parent_id = NULL when no root row exists for\n  the tenant. The prior fallback (root?.id ?? null) would detach reports\n  from the tree entirely on a corrupt/never-synced tenant instead of\n  surfacing the inconsistency. New isolation test proves both the throw\n  and that nothing gets detached when it fires.\n- Migration comment corrected: the partial unique index on\n  org_directory_sync_runs is a secondary DB-level backstop, not the\n  primary sync-concurrency lock -- that''s the Postgres advisory lock\n  (acquireTenantAdvisoryLock, landing in PR #713).\n\nAddresses PrabhuVijit''s review on PR #712.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(db): register 0129_org_directory_tables in the migration journal\n\nmigrations/meta/_journal.json was missing this migration''s entry, so a\nfresh db:migrate (including CI''s isolation-test job) never actually created\norg_employees/org_directory_sync_runs -- causing PR712''s CI to fail with\n\"relation org_employees does not exist\" across 6 isolation tests. Same fix\nalready applied on the stacked feat/org-directory-04 branch; backported\nhere since PR712''s own CI checks out this branch in isolation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(db): invalid uuid literals + missing root row in shared erasure fixture\n\norg-directory.isolation.test.ts used uuid literals with non-hex segments\n(org1 contains o/r/g), which Postgres now correctly rejects once the tables\nactually exist to test against.\n\nseed-every-tenant-table.sql seeded an org_employees row directly without\never creating the required synthetic root (R3: exactly one root per\ntenant) -- a state that can never occur in real operation, but tripped\neraseUserFromTenant''s no-root guard (PR712''s own review fix) in every\ngeneric per-user-erasure coverage test that uses this shared fixture.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvRwXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAApzkQAAxTIUsc3YgudI+0ZPt1CNSz\ntxhBmS+z5qOYRT1fD547hNHJvY+nsGfmLXiXH9H67VWGk+bIFDLVXt2BGY2iHIRd\nkl/7Ddn32J3RO1QuIxtbIJFGz96hirmcGNWRG14QZAlkNGIoneQr+MeTV7p50X/k\nOAW7ZHaYI1OAfiNI3mQzHccQNedVw5eF4Ja0OhEemr+ItZkmLMdpAZkSGuwIBmR4\nyz6lAomvVXSe5CNzVbPiKpbPs6MSIOVcVN+1Mz4XrdqxCmdXGMU02VZivdXsHqmo\n9hvrmOHMJEGd5HlpbcFC8p67j5qlR/W0qHj14nVBijCiFSRs5RO3x7KoZsJdWJUd\nOD2CvDg7CmzCDqsK15Wk3YGEg4YfRu7W2y//Kalz10/shYt7QVBm8ZIdssoMJOpm\nlE6MfymxtiObqqLyPd16QVB3pN8ngT9filLt9xoR3Q1mh0+SaMJ3qqJpnLYp3H2c\n+7HhLguiN6e2dpRlMH7kbAjHUWUEL5J/d+qut56yg4ZYej9TILWNSAD01VvviL9+