b3545edb0bb"}],"sha":"eff977b15cdf8a96d133f29de23e62b05c1cb851","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/eff977b15cdf8a96d133f29de23e62b05c1cb851"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/184391486?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bikash-barnwal","id":184391486,"login":"bikash-barnwal","node_id":"U_kgDOCv2XPg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/60a0a325ed14480412379a6fc0cecb3545edb0bb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T11:01:03Z","email":"bikashprasadbarnwal@gmail.com","name":"Bikash"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T11:01:03Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(docs): propose adr-019 reporting tenant isolation [skip-tests-check] docs-only (#707)\n\n* docs(docs): propose adr-019 for reporting tenant isolation\n\nADR-019 records the 3G isolation design that Stages 1-2 already ship\n(#663-#671, migrations 0112-0124). Superset''s DB_CONNECTION_MUTATOR\nstamps app.tenant_id so platform RLS applies, a missing tenant fails\nclosed, and reporting reads only granted tables and columns. Payload\ncolumns are excluded, not redacted, which supersedes the option C\nchoice the issue describes. Status is Proposed so acceptance stays a\nseparate human step.\n\nChecked on a running Superset 6.1.0: stage 2 CSV export works and is\nrecorded as accepted (spec R7), while the Superset-side audit writes no\nreporting.* row because the logger maps action names 6.1.0 no longer\nemits. That gap is recorded for a separate fix.\n\nADR-008, ADR-009 and ADR-011 cited the gitignored docs/sup-docs/; they\nnow cite docs/tracker/, where the tracker moved in #619.\n\nRefs #695\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(docs): address adr-019 review round 1\n\nStage 2 is pending a private security review, so ADR-019 now says it\nmust stay disabled until that closes, drops the claim that user-written\nSQL cannot widen scope, and adds OQ-6. Decisions 2 and 6 will record\nthe outcome.\n\nAlso from review: link the audit gap to #709 and record audit as\nbest-effort, cite the anchored tenant and subject regexes, spell out\nthe unusable-binding behaviour, add the PgBouncer refusal, the init\nscript window (#708), the security_invoker requirement and the untested\nmutator, and name ADR-015 and the Redis cache in OQ-3.\n\nRefs #695\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(docs): link sql lab 0-row result to #716 in adr-019\n\nReview round 2 asked OQ-6 to carry a cause and a tracking issue for the\nSQL Lab 0-row result. OQ-6 now points at #716 and states that Stage 1\nhas no SQL Lab and is unaffected.\n\nRefs #695\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c91eee1fe19f6f7e7d3c3fe79de7ccc310d62c6c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/trees/c91eee1fe19f6f7e7d3c3fe79de7ccc310d62c6c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/commits/60a0a325ed14480412379a6fc0cecb3545edb0bb","verification":{"payload":"tree c91eee1fe19f6f7e7d3c3fe79de7ccc310d62c6c\nparent 6599d79a5e80c4df8c6e72350feca038a418971a\nauthor Bikash <bikashprasadbarnwal@gmail.com> 1790766063 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790766063 +0530\n\ndocs(docs): propose adr-019 reporting tenant isolation [skip-tests-check] docs-only (#707)\n\n* docs(docs): propose adr-019 for reporting tenant isolation\n\nADR-019 records the 3G isolation design that Stages 1-2 already ship\n(#663-#671, migrations 0112-0124). Superset''s DB_CONNECTION_MUTATOR\nstamps app.tenant_id so platform RLS applies, a missing tenant fails\nclosed, and reporting reads only granted tables and columns. Payload\ncolumns are excluded, not redacted, which supersedes the option C\nchoice the issue describes. Status is Proposed so acceptance stays a\nseparate human step.\n\nChecked on a running Superset 6.1.0: stage 2 CSV export works and is\nrecorded as accepted (spec R7), while the Superset-side audit writes no\nreporting.* row because the logger maps action names 6.1.0 no longer\nemits. That gap is recorded for a separate fix.\n\nADR-008, ADR-009 and ADR-011 cited the gitignored docs/sup-docs/; they\nnow cite docs/tracker/, where the tracker moved in #619.\n\nRefs #695\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(docs): address adr-019 review round 1\n\nStage 2 is pending a private security review, so ADR-019 now says it\nmust stay disabled until that closes, drops the claim that user-written\nSQL cannot widen scope, and adds OQ-6. Decisions 2 and 6 will record\nthe outcome.\n\nAlso from review: link the audit gap to #709 and record audit as\nbest-effort, cite the anchored tenant and subject regexes, spell out\nthe unusable-binding behaviour, add the PgBouncer refusal, the init\nscript window (#708), the security_invoker requirement and the untested\nmutator, and name ADR-015 and the Redis cache in OQ-3.\n\nRefs #695\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(docs): link sql lab 0-row result to #716 in adr-019\n\nReview round 2 asked OQ-6 to carry a cause and a tracking issue for the\nSQL Lab 0-row result. OQ-6 now points at #716 and states that Stage 1\nhas no SQL Lab and is unaffected.\n\nRefs #695\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvOvvCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4j8QAE2ZRdpYlBI6hBjnsq2tJO57\nBbuf2bK007g6IGoD0SWFcp42jM3IlCAQadOnvn9sulGcofQ6tlrUlwq7UzVPfGGG\n2FJeKCwxVZ7vfdR5TLiQs1BUpUwbid0g4VmvDGaarXz0RsW79ilFB90mFSjoJPID\nlisnrV5pey/RKJqdPprwbdxfJgLJJHMB6u7BkRj9Jy15by8eSrJ2zPakkd9Lk36j\nwG4sJ7XgNAhVfDgrwdj4983yGzWweRVuylLRoeAxJiFNntsCuLyz/n+PmzHE5lrf\nK/yDjopTuMKo2DIzitMidRdTU1EdemOAmsSG9t3Xu4J5rIDnv0EPEyKgeYrtTKFg\nPDxzUjGsPJc+egGX+LLFtdAEE8TWoQFaz1zWVypPwLg3RPc875zP8+DN8KSko5D0\nvZHDMTpw8KqG3mneYeH4uY+fsmm3rKy3ECZ0Z/yzCGB0H2Rxf2g0wpMZIXMuXtsF\nwjgiS+k4kzuem2Oq4lcaPFweyODoL1UD2wyg/aYn0ubWQ27VCC5ZyBV1gMME9BzP\nvQ4berrL/PxyzopwfeNmzaC+1+3o8QG7PAQLK09yjNyWVFir3o4/XDkCqjBL+Xyr\n6jsJlIx+eZfrBW59NMkYORevz5JPvU46EK/cQSt3yQEY0k87IZ7sAJva3HVIoQdH\nFef36AN4fzUUqxjLUPOb\n=B1/U\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T11:01:04Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commit/60a0a325ed14480412379a6fc0cecb3545edb0bb","node_id":"C_kwDOScMdh9oAKDYwYTBhMzI1ZWQxNDQ4MDQxMjM3OWE2ZmMwY2VjYjM1NDVlZGIwYmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commit/6599d79a5e80c4df8c6e72350feca038a418971a","sha":"6599d79a5e80c4df8c6e72350feca038a418971a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/6599d79a5e80c4df8c6e72350feca038a418971a"}],"sha":"60a0a325ed14480412379a6fc0cecb3545edb0bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/60a0a325ed14480412379a6fc0cecb3545edb0bb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/67047397?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TusharSharma991","id":67047397,"login":"TusharSharma991","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3MDQ3Mzk3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/6599d79a5e80c4df8c6e72350feca038a418971a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T10:52:50Z","email":"67047397+TusharSharma991@users.noreply.github.com","name":"TusharSharma991"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T10:52:50Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(db): org-directory PR2 — org_employees/org_directory_sync_runs schema + GDPR erasure wiring (#712)\n\n* feat(auth): add zitadel manager_id/department metadata read + org-directory scaffold\n\nNew @platform/org-directory package (docs/specs/org-directory.md) with the\nOrgSourceImporter/OrgNode/OrgTree contract that keeps the org-chart tree\nswappable across identity providers. Adds getOrgMetadataForUser to\npackages/auth/src/zitadel-management.ts, reading exactly the manager_id/\ndepartment metadata keys via the existing service-account token path,\nwith the same cache/single-flight pattern as the file''s other lookups.\n\nPR1 of the org-directory track (spec + tasks in docs/specs/). No schema,\nroutes, or UI yet — those land in follow-up PRs per the tasks file.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(db): add org_employees + org_directory_sync_runs tables, wire gdpr erasure\n\nNew tenant-scoped tables for the org-directory tree (docs/specs/org-directory.md\nT3): org_employees (self-referential parent_id tree, nullable user_id for the\nsynthetic per-tenant root card) and org_directory_sync_runs (sync status;\na partial unique index on (tenant_id) WHERE status=''running'' doubles as the\nper-tenant sync concurrency lock at the DB level). Plain Drizzle tables, not\nan entity-engine module -- same reasoning as packages/teams (ADR-016\nDecision 1): tree traversal is a hot path, not a JSONB walk.\n\nWires both tables into the platform''s GDPR erasure paths (#635, added to\ndb-conventions.md after this spec was drafted): tenant-purge.ts deletes them\non tenant deletion; user-erasure.ts reparents an erased employee''s direct\nreports one hop up (falling back to the tenant root if needed) then deletes\ntheir row, and redacts org_directory_sync_runs.triggered_by like other\ncreated_by-style columns. Fixture and DB-level isolation tests included.\n\nPR2 of the org-directory track, stacked on PR1. No routes/query API/UI yet.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(auth): address pr711 review feedback -- vitest deps.inline, dead param\n\n- packages/org-directory/vitest.config.ts: add server.deps.inline for\n  @platform/* workspace deps, matching the existing packages/workflow-engine\n  convention -- without it, vitest''s per-package module isolation can break\n  instanceof checks across the @platform/* boundary.\n- zitadel-management.ts: remove parseOrgMetadataEntries''s unused _userId\n  param rather than keep it for a hypothetical future logging path.\n- zitadel-management.test.ts: tighten the malformed-base64 test to assert\n  the exact best-effort-decoded value (the function does not skip malformed\n  entries, despite the old test''s name implying it did); add a test proving\n  the no-token path evicts its cache entry instead of permanently caching\n  an empty result.\n\nAddresses PrabhuVijit''s review on PR #711.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(db): address pr712 review feedback -- renumber migration, fix erasure null-fallback\n\n- Renumber packages/db/migrations/0128_org_directory_tables.sql to\n  0129_org_directory_tables.sql -- 0128 collides with an already-merged\n  security advisory PR''s own migration (verified against upstream/main).\n  Updates the header comment and one sibling code comment in\n  packages/db/src/schema/org-directory.ts to match.\n- apps/api/src/services/user-erasure.ts: when reparenting an erased\n  employee''s direct reports (docs/specs/org-directory.md T12), throw\n  instead of silently writing parent_id = NULL when no root row exists for\n  the tenant. The prior fallback (root?.id ?? null) would detach reports\n  from the tree entirely on a corrupt/never-synced tenant instead of\n  surfacing the inconsistency. New isolation test proves both the throw\n  and that nothing gets detached when it fires.\n- Migration comment corrected: the partial unique index on\n  org_directory_sync_runs is a secondary DB-level backstop, not the\n  primary sync-concurrency lock -- that''s the Postgres advisory lock\n  (acquireTenantAdvisoryLock, landing in PR #713).\n\nAddresses PrabhuVijit''s review on PR #712.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(db): register 0129_org_directory_tables in the migration journal\n\nmigrations/meta/_journal.json was missing this migration''s entry, so a\nfresh db:migrate (including CI''s isolation-test job) never actually created\norg_employees/org_directory_sync_runs -- causing PR712''s CI to fail with\n\"relation org_employees does not exist\" across 6 isolation tests. Same fix\nalready applied on the stacked feat/org-directory-04 branch; backported\nhere since PR712''s own CI checks out this branch in isolation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(db): invalid uuid literals + missing root row in shared erasure fixture\n\norg-directory.isolation.test.ts used uuid literals with non-hex segments\n(org1 contains o/r/g), which Postgres now correctly rejects once the tables\nactually exist to test against.\n\nseed-every-tenant-table.sql seeded an org_employees row directly without\never creating the required synthetic root (R3: exactly one root per\ntenant) -- a state that can never occur in real operation, but tripped\neraseUserFromTenant''s no-root guard (PR712''s own review fix) in every\ngeneric per-user-erasure coverage test that uses this shared fixture.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"31dd96b7f3e0900146519168bb6be6f21b5c5ee7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/trees/31dd96b7f3e0900146519168bb6be6f21b5c5ee7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/commits/6599d79a5e80c4df8c6e72350feca038a418971a","verification":{"payload":"tree 31dd96b7f3e0900146519168bb6be6f21b5c5ee7\nparent b1415639c6c94ef8400bffd436b535995aafdc65\nauthor TusharSharma991 <67047397+TusharSharma991@users.noreply.github.com> 1790765570 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790765570 +0530\n\nfeat(db): org-directory PR2 — org_employees/org_directory_sync_runs schema + GDPR erasure wiring (#712)\n\n* feat(auth): add zitadel manager_id/department metadata read + org-directory scaffold\n\nNew @platform/org-directory package (docs/specs/org-directory.md) with the\nOrgSourceImporter/OrgNode/OrgTree contract that keeps the org-chart tree\nswappable across identity providers. Adds getOrgMetadataForUser to\npackages/auth/src/zitadel-management.ts, reading exactly the manager_id/\ndepartment metadata keys via the existing service-account token path,\nwith the same cache/single-flight pattern as the file''s other lookups.\n\nPR1 of the org-directory track (spec + tasks in docs/specs/). No schema,\nroutes, or UI yet — those land in follow-up PRs per the tasks file.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(db): add org_employees + org_directory_sync_runs tables, wire gdpr erasure\n\nNew tenant-scoped tables for the org-directory tree (docs/specs/org-directory.md\nT3): org_employees (self-referential parent_id tree, nullable user_id for the\nsynthetic per-tenant root card) and org_directory_sync_runs (sync status;\na partial unique index on (tenant_id) WHERE status=''running'' doubles as the\nper-tenant sync concurrency lock at the DB level). Plain Drizzle tables, not\nan entity-engine module -- same reasoning as packages/teams (ADR-016\nDecision 1): tree traversal is a hot path, not a JSONB walk.\n\nWires both tables into the platform''s GDPR erasure paths (#635, added to\ndb-conventions.md after this spec was drafted): tenant-purge.ts deletes them\non tenant deletion; user-erasure.ts reparents an erased employee''s direct\nreports one hop up (falling back to the tenant root if needed) then deletes\ntheir row, and redacts org_directory_sync_runs.triggered_by like other\ncreated_by-style columns. Fixture and DB-level isolation tests included.\n\nPR2 of the org-directory track, stacked on PR1. No routes/query API/UI yet.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(auth): address pr711 review feedback -- vitest deps.inline, dead param\n\n- packages/org-directory/vitest.config.ts: add server.deps.inline for\n  @platform/* workspace deps, matching the existing packages/workflow-engine\n  convention -- without it, vitest''s per-package module isolation can break\n  instanceof checks across the @platform/* boundary.\n- zitadel-management.ts: remove parseOrgMetadataEntries''s unused _userId\n  param rather than keep it for a hypothetical future logging path.\n- zitadel-management.test.ts: tighten the malformed-base64 test to assert\n  the exact best-effort-decoded value (the function does not skip malformed\n  entries, despite the old test''s name implying it did); add a test proving\n  the no-token path evicts its cache entry instead of permanently caching\n  an empty result.\n\nAddresses PrabhuVijit''s review on PR #711.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(db): address pr712 review feedback -- renumber migration, fix erasure null-fallback\n\n- Renumber packages/db/migrations/0128_org_directory_tables.sql to\n  0129_org_directory_tables.sql -- 0128 collides with an already-merged\n  security advisory PR''s own migration (verified against upstream/main).\n  Updates the header comment and one sibling code comment in\n  packages/db/src/schema/org-directory.ts to match.\n- apps/api/src/services/user-erasure.ts: when reparenting an erased\n  employee''s direct reports (docs/specs/org-directory.md T12), throw\n  instead of silently writing parent_id = NULL when no root row exists for\n  the tenant. The prior fallback (root?.id ?? null) would detach reports\n  from the tree entirely on a corrupt/never-synced tenant instead of\n  surfacing the inconsistency. New isolation test proves both the throw\n  and that nothing gets detached when it fires.\n- Migration comment corrected: the partial unique index on\n  org_directory_sync_runs is a secondary DB-level backstop, not the\n  primary sync-concurrency lock -- that''s the Postgres advisory lock\n  (acquireTenantAdvisoryLock, landing in PR #713).\n\nAddresses PrabhuVijit''s review on PR #712.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(db): register 0129_org_directory_tables in the migration journal\n\nmigrations/meta/_journal.json was missing this migration''s entry, so a\nfresh db:migrate (including CI''s isolation-test job) never actually created\norg_employees/org_directory_sync_runs -- causing PR712''s CI to fail with\n\"relation org_employees does not exist\" across 6 isolation tests. Same fix\nalready applied on the stacked feat/org-directory-04 branch; backported\nhere since PR712''s own CI checks out this branch in isolation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(db): invalid uuid literals + missing root row in shared erasure fixture\n\norg-directory.isolation.test.ts used uuid literals with non-hex segments\n(org1 contains o/r/g), which Postgres now correctly rejects once the tables\nactually exist to test against.\n\nseed-every-tenant-table.sql seeded an org_employees row directly without\never creating the required synthetic root (R3: exactly one root per\ntenant) -- a state that can never occur in real operation, but tripped\neraseUserFromTenant''s no-root guard (PR712''s own review fix) in every\ngeneric per-user-erasure coverage test that uses this shared fixture.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"---