ich a session can\nchange. A Stage 2 SQL Lab user could therefore re-point its tenant or widen its\nown-rows scope. Advisory: GHSA-28jx-36cp-g34h.\n\nMigration 0128 adds a key table that only a SECURITY DEFINER function can read.\nreporting_bound_tenant() verifies HMAC-SHA256(key, tenant|scope|user_id) against\napp.reporting_binding_sig using the current settings, and a restrictive policy on\nanalytics_user''s six readable tables requires the verified tenant.\nrecord_reporting_audit now requires it too. Any mismatch fails closed.\n\nSuperset''s mutator signs the binding and disables the chart-data cache when SSO\nis on. run-migrations syncs REPORTING_BINDING_SECRET into the database (turbo\npassthrough added), and compose/env are wired. The init script stops granting\nanalytics_user BYPASSRLS or default SELECT. New isolation suite covers each\nbypass and fail-closed case.\n\n* fix(security): refuse production migrations without a binding secret (ghsa-28jx)\n\nIn production, the migration runner now fails when\nREPORTING_BINDING_SECRET is unset instead of warning and leaving\nreporting empty. Also documents the rotation order, lists every\nrollback statement, covers the reporting_instances view in the binding\ntests and explains why the chart cache is off rather than keyed per\ntenant.\n\nAdvisory: GHSA-28jx-36cp-g34h.","tree":{"sha":"28cb85d1e748e113252d3e905832d94330b576fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/trees/28cb85d1e748e113252d3e905832d94330b576fc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/commits/1047f0324b1db4910f3dab4a4ed2597b9d9e3329","verification":{"payload":"tree 28cb85d1e748e113252d3e905832d94330b576fc\nparent 32f09ecd5bd3575fafa58cdba2f0b1ca20000b76\nauthor Abhinav Mishra <needabhinav@gmail.com> 1790742580 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790742580 +0530\n\nMerge commit from fork\n\n* fix(security): bind reporting sessions to their tenant with a signature (ghsa-28jx)\n\nReporting sessions were scoped only by custom settings stamped at connect time\n(app.tenant_id, app.reporting_scope, app.reporting_user_id), which a session can\nchange. A Stage 2 SQL Lab user could therefore re-point its tenant or widen its\nown-rows scope. Advisory: GHSA-28jx-36cp-g34h.\n\nMigration 0128 adds a key table that only a SECURITY DEFINER function can read.\nreporting_bound_tenant() verifies HMAC-SHA256(key, tenant|scope|user_id) against\napp.reporting_binding_sig using the current settings, and a restrictive policy on\nanalytics_user''s six readable tables requires the verified tenant.\nrecord_reporting_audit now requires it too. Any mismatch fails closed.\n\nSuperset''s mutator signs the binding and disables the chart-data cache when SSO\nis on. run-migrations syncs REPORTING_BINDING_SECRET into the database (turbo\npassthrough added), and compose/env are wired. The init script stops granting\nanalytics_user BYPASSRLS or default SELECT. New isolation suite covers each\nbypass and fail-closed case.\n\n* fix(security): refuse production migrations without a binding secret (ghsa-28jx)\n\nIn production, the migration runner now fails when\nREPORTING_BINDING_SECRET is unset instead of warning and leaving\nreporting empty. Also documents the rotation order, lists every\nrollback statement, covers the reporting_instances view in the binding\ntests and explains why the chart cache is off rather than keyed per\ntenant.\n\nAdvisory: GHSA-28jx-36cp-g34h.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvJA0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9l8QAHeUyKBDsdMMv/0vBf9bVOsH\nkXdjxeTt9iFehg9iS4QDuIVTFYe62GEF90j+hw7E9rSRWA+8QGmDoGNYhXmdE/rx\ntmc7kcfw7fQb2RCIzu4NAimD7uBO04PPhXzm3/H9ID7gHHRGzJ4RnDVEWdXmWcfv\n/05mnj95bhe7JmyAq7BnwIeO7XQEHoZdtX8g+LcZv/eHKDtPwvzWv8X85lKGpJA/\nWhxo/JMGWABgipfilzVLyjIjPyrCVcjU6bfHapBMy7Imz6MEKJshylwJRwOxLXGI\ns8kLvF9F4lempN5rdqKlCCIa8pC3k8aI9PW+HdLokO3NY8kiGAfm18+elU95NEB/\n5/GeEf8Rdh6xsPtEwfNJhUxZGHqPrLCUoZnZnZB+KLG/Ik7YzGblLl3wGrNuEBjQ\nr/4HBh0IL6EDIJXtVogU