/eab1110cb2486eeb312759119b05b282220f60df","sha":"eab1110cb2486eeb312759119b05b282220f60df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/eab1110cb2486eeb312759119b05b282220f60df"}],"sha":"439c5d67b57294b80b7d090772caa93b1906aac8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/439c5d67b57294b80b7d090772caa93b1906aac8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3049693?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/abmish","id":3049693,"login":"abmish","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNDk2OTM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/eab1110cb2486eeb312759119b05b282220f60df/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T05:02:40Z","email":"needabhinav@gmail.com","name":"Abhinav Mishra"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T05:02:40Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(dx): stop guardrail hooks treating large diffs as empty (#698) (#699)\n\nsh()/shBuf() in .claude/hooks/lib/context.js, and write-docs-marker.sh''s inline\nsh(), called execSync without maxBuffer, so Node''s 1 MiB default applied. A larger\ngit diff threw ENOBUFS and came back as an empty result, and every gate reported\nnothing to review or stage. Pass a shared 256 MiB MAX_BUFFER, and add hook tests\nthat push 2 MiB through both helpers (both returned 0 before the fix).","tree":{"sha":"8970f57484ccded3290f7da6bcafab9cd393ae50","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/trees/8970f57484ccded3290f7da6bcafab9cd393ae50"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/commits/eab1110cb2486eeb312759119b05b282220f60df","verification":{"payload":"tree 8970f57484ccded3290f7da6bcafab9cd393ae50\nparent 01c849eae92d54662220467ecf4ff857e711eb3c\nauthor Abhinav Mishra <needabhinav@gmail.com> 1790571760 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790571760 +0530\n\nfix(dx): stop guardrail hooks treating large diffs as empty (#698) (#699)\n\nsh()/shBuf() in .claude/hooks/lib/context.js, and write-docs-marker.sh''s inline\nsh(), called execSync without maxBuffer, so Node''s 1 MiB default applied. A larger\ngit diff threw ENOBUFS and came back as an empty result, and every gate reported\nnothing to review or stage. Pass a shared 256 MiB MAX_BUFFER, and add hook tests\nthat push 2 MiB through both helpers (both returned 0 before the fix).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqufTwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5C8QAKWWWUFcsPLW1a4KF5DQPPVO\ng7JTLDsONiH4vNHcvEI7KvdvjJ3eocvBNmkfCA+MUMrEsX2t9GvmXnioXrUFvztb\ncOiKVvcFArA/DIJzKtM9kN6G70a7yBssc0CIzV3nwa9c9CqL5jVjciainFUnF4Bi\nS1FRX+T3034jyQlwWu7eJuTJKf+N5awGNHjtsdYSpCWLaiMIEYslv9q/9eE+fsnE\ng3sLr0broAFiOaTqIRLAzLJIRrQhAPQPtL3MNg18kgrZ8AAi7JHYQNt5jnIY+8Mo\ngkd5/+FbL/N++o3N7y0zYLc6hQLqd0t80CBs32wBy2Vz2qOHSanDEzIdusA0sHfe\nKOAcoxf65yjg79J152q+UiSH2272pX++38QF8HP3Tjkf83ejfSOsrGRX5nuKfero\nfOHyn/J1HUpBZjgJmOzg0IJVHyiY3bQlS0z9V1pVfbYaT7JYsDe6cXTd4i+5XBID\neTqR3LGhUvO2wRl6HZiM+nlmfvBZUKmVnMRcF5JvnbKNZR99w4/hQElrYoJVy62u\nA2g83TILMLlNzoPijg6RRW2ANV+m4ox7sSyAWAKDzNKD1T8BYPoJ6WeYaEUi9zxD\n3BgYtf/3kOAOUmPmLCVIsdCm6V00/xhFc64eKGkkiufAgS8/Ly1qfwNNWVSjS413\nBLiAfmQbiRZUbASpcMO8\n=tpyP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T05:02:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commit/eab1110cb2486eeb312759119b05b282220f60df","node_id":"C_kwDOScMdh9oAKGVhYjExMTBjYjI0ODZlZWIzMTI3NTkxMTliMDViMjgyMjIwZjYwZGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commit/01c849eae92d54662220467ecf4ff857e711eb3c","sha":"01c849eae92d54662220467ecf4ff857e711eb3c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/01c849eae92d54662220467ecf4ff857e711eb3c"}],"sha":"eab1110cb2486eeb312759119b05b282220f60df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/eab1110cb2486eeb312759119b05b282220f60df"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3049693?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/abmish","id":3049693,"login":"abmish","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNDk2OTM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/01c849eae92d54662220467ecf4ff857e711eb3c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T05:00:37Z","email":"needabhinav@gmail.com","name":"Abhinav Mishra"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T05:00:37Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(api): anonymize instead of delete in per-user erasure, and scrub ids in payloads (#688) (#690)\n\n* fix(worker): make tenant purge and per-user erasure complete and cover every table (#635)\n\nTenant purge failed outright for most tenants (attachments -> files and\nseveral other NO ACTION/RESTRICT FKs rolled back the whole transaction), and\nper-user erasure failed on every call (app_user had no DELETE on\nticket_alerts/access_requests). saved_views were silently kept, 15 tenant\ntables were never purged and ~15 user-reference columns never scrubbed.\n\n- tenant-purge.ts: FK-safe order covering every tenant table; privileged\n  pre-step archives schedule rules, then deletes append-only\n  schedule_executions and user-scoped saved_views; exports\n  PURGED_TENANT_TABLES and ERASURE_EXEMPT_TABLES.\n- Per-user erasure moved to apps/api/src/services/user-erasure.ts and\n  extended to every user-reference column (legacy and map __accessUsers,\n  api_keys rotated_from, on-call primary shifts deleted).\n- Migration 0125: DELETE on ticket_alerts/access_requests, column-level\n  UPDATE (created_by) on entity_instance_tags.\n- information_schema-driven guards fail CI on any uncovered tenant table or\n  user-id column; db-conventions.md states the same-PR rule.\n\nCloses #635\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(api): scope the erasure app.user_id switch to a savepoint (#681 review)\n\nIf the saved_views delete throws, ROLLBACK TO SAVEPOINT now also reverts\napp.user_id, so a caller that catches and continues never keeps the erased\nuser''s id as the transaction''s user. Adds a test that the caller''s\napp.user_id is restored.\n\ndb-conventions.md: policies reading app.* GUCs must NULLIF(..., '''') before a\ncast, because an unset custom GUC reads as '''' on pooled connections. The\nuser_ref / mention erasure gap is tracked as #688.\n\nRefs #635\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(api): anonymize instead of delete in per-user erasure, and scrub ids in payloads (#688)\n\nPer-user erasure now keeps business records with the identity removed, and\nreaches user ids and names inside JSON payloads and comment text.\n\n- Newly scrubbed: user_ref custom fields (optional removed, required\n  redacted), comment mentions, @<display name> in comments that recorded the\n  mention (word-boundary match), actorName, actingPersonId and field-change\n  history in workflow_events.metadata.\n- Kept, anonymized: API keys the user created stay active on a forced\n  rotation window (expires_at at most 30 days out, one audit entry per key);\n  resolved access requests; every on-call shift (primary redacted, so the\n  resolver still pages backup and escalation). Pending access requests are\n  still deleted.\n- USER_ID_FIELD_TYPES classifies every field type exhaustively, so a new\n  type fails typecheck until handled.\n\nChanges #681''s delete-vs-redact choices for api_keys, access_requests and\non_call_schedules. Stacked on #681.\n\nCloses #688\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(api): restore app.user_id to null and delete membership last in erasure (#681 review)\n\n- The saved_views GUC restore passes null (\"back to nothing\") and its\n  comment now matches; observable value is unchanged.\n- tenant_users and idempotency_keys deletes move to the end of\n  eraseUserFromTenant, after every other footprint is scrubbed.\n- Spec records the retrospective check: saved_views is the only policy\n  reading app.user_id, and it never casts it to uuid.\n\nRefs #635\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(api): drop dead triggered_by rewrite from per-user erasure (#690 review)\n\nworkflow_events.triggered_by holds the trigger type (user, automation, api,\nsystem), never a user id, so the UPDATE matching it against the erased user''s id\nnever ran, and would have corrupted the type if it had. The author is already\nanonymized by the actor_id UPDATE (actorId + metadata.actorName). Move\ntriggered_by from the handled list to USER_REFERENCE_COLUMNS_EXEMPT, since the\ncoverage guard only picked it up by name. Assert that the target''s comment keeps\ntriggered_by = ''user'' with actor_id redacted, and note that on-call schedule\nuser columns have no FK to tenant_users (migration 0094).","tree":{"sha":"6077605dd8b893d630150b4017a0cefdbbde3d18","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/trees/6077605dd8b893d630150b4017a0cefdbbde3d18"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/commits/01c849eae92d54662220467ecf4ff857e711eb3c","verification":{"payload":"tree 6077605dd8b893d630150b4017a0cefdbbde3d18\nparent f3349ca2aa71e0cada6b64380144e81ee22cf94b\nauthor Abhinav Mishra <needabhinav@gmail.com> 1790571637 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790571637 +0530\n\nfix(api): anonymize instead of delete in per-user erasure, and scrub ids in payloads (#688) (#690)\n\n* fix(worker): make tenant purge and per-user erasure complete and cover every table (#635)\n\nTenant purge failed outright for most tenants (attachments -> files and\nseveral other NO ACTION/RESTRICT FKs rolled back the whole transaction), and\nper-user erasure failed on every call (app_user had no DELETE on\nticket_alerts/access_requests). saved_views were silently kept, 15 tenant\ntables were never purged and ~15 user-reference columns never scrubbed.\n\n- tenant-purge.ts: FK-safe order covering every tenant table; privileged\n  pre-step archives schedule rules, then deletes append-only\n  schedule_executions and user-scoped saved_views; exports\n  PURGED_TENANT_TABLES and ERASURE_EXEMPT_TABLES.\n- Per-user erasure moved to apps/api/src/services/user-erasure.ts and\n  extended to every user-reference column (legacy and map __accessUsers,\n  api_keys rotated_from, on-call primary shifts deleted).\n- Migration 0125: DELETE on ticket_alerts/access_requests, column-level\n  UPDATE (created_by) on entity_instance_tags.\n- information_schema-driven guards fail CI on any uncovered tenant table or\n  user-id column; db-conventions.md states the same-PR rule.\n\nCloses #635\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(api): scope the erasure app.user_id switch to a savepoint (#681 review)\n\nIf the saved_views delete throws, ROLLBACK TO SAVEPOINT now also reverts\napp.user_id, so a caller that catches and continues never keeps the erased\nuser''s id as the transaction''s user. Adds a test that the caller''s\napp.user_id is restored.\n\ndb-conventions.md: policies reading app.* GUCs must NULLIF(..., '''') before a\ncast, because an unset custom GUC reads as '''' on pooled connections. The\nuser_ref / mention erasure gap is tracked as #688.\n\nRefs #635\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(api): anonymize instead of delete in per-user erasure, and scrub ids in payloads (#688)\n\nPer-user erasure now keeps business records with the identity removed, and\nreaches user ids and names inside JSON payloads and comment text.\n\n- Newly scrubbed: user_ref custom fields (optional removed, required\n  redacted), comment mentions, @<display name> in comments that recorded the\n  mention (word-boundary match), actorName, actingPersonId and field-change\n  history in workflow_events.metadata.\n- Kept, anonymized: API keys the user created stay active on a forced\n  rotation window (expires_at at most 30 days out, one audit entry per key);\n  resolved access requests; every on-call shift (primary redacted, so the\n  resolver still pages backup and escalation). Pending access requests are\n  still deleted.\n- USER_ID_FIELD_TYPES classifies every field type exhaustively, so a new\n  type fails typecheck until handled.\n\nChanges #681''s delete-vs-redact choices for api_keys, access_requests and\non_call_schedules. Stacked on #681.\n\nCloses #688\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(api): restore app.user_id to null and delete membership last in erasure (#681 review)\n\n- The saved_views GUC restore passes null (\"back to nothing\") and its\n  comment now matches; observable value is unchanged.\n- tenant_users and idempotency_keys deletes move to the end of\n  eraseUserFromTenant, after every other footprint is scrubbed.\n- Spec records the retrospective check: saved_views is the only policy\n  reading app.user_id, and it never casts it to uuid.\n\nRefs #635\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(api): drop dead triggered_by rewrite from per-user erasure (#690 review)\n\nworkflow_events.triggered_by holds the trigger type (user, automation, api,\nsystem), never a user id, so the UPDATE matching it against the erased user''s id\nnever ran, and would have corrupted the type if it had. The author is already\nanonymized by the actor_id UPDATE (actorId + metadata.actorName). Move\ntriggered_by from the handled list to USER_REFERENCE_COLUMNS_EXEMPT, since the\ncoverage guard only picked it up by name. Assert that the target''s comment keeps\ntriggered_by = ''user'' with actor_id redacted, and note that on-call schedule\nuser columns have no FK to tenant_users (migration 0094).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqufR1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOPoQAKgQBEflgeLZ2gQYtQ8h322c\nlnh66pohjmjMc8AYxpRr4WIkDmo/4W1KaQXyC6TGFAoKem757ujG2uVanfyYziOr\nh+Jz63TeGm+SpwC9URMJad2dugdHp4cN459bO3PKGJN+9LQw9lMk7W1gHhQ7qJXU\nqCAyHle1c1GwGUNJbkDyvNKyRydqz5GCOJfytw2Hjq/WvpEAFoqx8wn1sH/sDs9x\nEyQPgFcT81veE7mCSQh6IHTuGwx1T2pU3GlKAipwXoDWyt4PBDoJLtBZYJXsHofk\n88VLT5F+hl1eLP05e7dTy5+UMQGrFUEedAZJ950R3WkhnOd/bRvGlcExqU6pNQAy\n7VlaSXhRYA7D15JjbDSS2StDFvkLY44tLmUmVDaQAVaUppL2IHilFkbGpNO9UUV9\n3L7piK5xbjw8b20YWrozsFpHEY41j0mqrldRTWm6LFsXb8xLzRZnFcF1ZEl390Go\ngH9DvZtM8ktAguHCmEGhiQ2rwCxe8mmPw5/oSU6YY66KXbK8I5N+fZYqfbudNYbc\n3KM3gzZLl4LfchKJvrB5sArTXq6lf2wj/R3M3GOajnYtXPnTFdsTKNSSYa4SF38D\nk2Nb242BLQs+0q7rnx7B3/vsDctqsI/EQpilLn+S7U2No2vmx02405DUAWivTetb\nagzpEqo6adQlwqKjbZjg\n=ybD+\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T05:00:38Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commit/01c849eae92d54662220467ecf4ff857e711eb3c","node_id":"C_kwDOScMdh9oAKDAxYzg0OWVhZTkyZDU0NjYyMjIwNDY3ZWNmNGZmODU3ZTcxMWViM2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commit/f3349ca2aa71e0cada6b64380144e81ee22cf94b","sha":"f3349ca2aa71e0cada6b64380144e81ee22cf94b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/f3349ca2aa71e0cada6b64380144e81ee22cf94b"}],"sha":"01c849eae92d54662220467ecf4ff857e711eb3c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/01c849eae92d54662220467ecf4ff857e711eb3c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3049693?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/abmish","id":3049693,"login":"abmish","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNDk2OTM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/f3349ca2aa71e0cada6b64380144e81ee22cf94b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T04:44:37Z","email":"needabhinav@gmail.com","name":"Abhinav Mishra"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T04:44:37Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(api): add optional vendor-approval module with role-gated approval chain (#606) (#680)\n\n* feat(api): add optional vendor-approval module with role-gated approval chain (#606)\n\n@modules/vendor-approval (category optional, seed SQL only): Vendor entity,\nsix-state workflow, 48h SLA on review states, comment-required rejection.\nReview stages are gated by new Zitadel project roles it_security, legal and\nfinance_approver (plus admin); approvers also hold agent.\n\nThree notify rules ship disabled with no recipient, since NotifyConfig has no\nrole-based recipient (deferred to #607). Each is pinned to the vendor entity\ntype because the automation executor ignores trigger_config.\n\nbootstrap.ts adds the department roles and three demo approver users.\napps/api/src/scripts/vendor-approval-demo.ts sets up demo vendors through a\nsingle payload-to-fields mapping (the swap seam for #634); it is idempotent\nand resumable. Includes integration, isolation and unit tests, spec, module\nREADME, tracker row, week-log and two filed platform findings.\n\nRefs #606, #613\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(docs): link #678 and #679 in pending review findings\n\nMove the two findings from #606 out of the untracked section into the\ntracked-issue table now that both have GitHub issues.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(api): address vendor-approval review feedback (#680)\n\n- Drop the vendor-approval module''s unused runtime dependencies (M1).\n- Test rejection at legal review and final approval, and that each review\n  state schedules a 48h SLA (S1, M2 partial).\n- Spec lists annual_spend_estimate as currency (G1); README warns against\n  re-seeding a tenant with live vendors and notes the demo only rejects at\n  IT Security (G2, S3).\n\nRefs #606\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(api): reject demo vendors at the stage they have reached (#680 review)\n\nA fixture with advanceTo \"rejected\" only rejected from it_security_review,\nso a vendor resumed at a later review stage walked on to Approved. The demo\nscript now rejects at the fixture''s rejectAt stage, or at the current review\nstage if the vendor is already past it, using that stage''s department role.\n\n- Rejection decision extracted to vendor-approval-rejection.ts, unit-tested.\n- Fixtures gain optional rejectAt; demo-vendor-007 is rejected at Legal.\n- Script seeds the module registry before installing, so it works before\n  the API has ever booted.\n\nRefs #606\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(docs): record the live walk-through risk acceptance for vendor-approval (#680 review)\n\nThe live admin-ui/Zitadel/worker walk-through (T12) is deferred by explicit\nowner decision and tracked in #691. The spec records what is unverified live,\nwhy the risk is bounded, and what closes it.\n\nRefs #606","tree":{"sha":"d929eb1195dbec7b34e4fe0f31413ec527513a41","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/trees/d929eb1195dbec7b34e4fe0f31413ec527513a41"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/commits/f3349ca2aa71e0cada6b64380144e81ee22cf94b","verification":{"payload":"tree d929eb1195dbec7b34e4fe0f31413ec527513a41\nparent 30082ce1c14974068edfdbbdaf7ee9814f436184\nauthor Abhinav Mishra <needabhinav@gmail.com> 1790570677 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790570677 +0530\n\nfeat(api): add optional vendor-approval module with role-gated approval chain (#606) (#680)\n\n* feat(api): add optional vendor-approval module with role-gated approval chain (#606)\n\n@modules/vendor-approval (category optional, seed SQL only): Vendor entity,\nsix-state workflow, 48h SLA on review states, comment-required rejection.\nReview stages are gated by new Zitadel project roles it_security, legal and\nfinance_approver (plus admin); approvers also hold agent.\n\nThree notify rules ship disabled with no recipient, since NotifyConfig has no\nrole-based recipient (deferred to #607). Each is pinned to the vendor entity\ntype because the automation executor ignores trigger_config.\n\nbootstrap.ts adds the department roles and three demo approver users.\napps/api/src/scripts/vendor-approval-demo.ts sets up demo vendors through a\nsingle payload-to-fields mapping (the swap seam for #634); it is idempotent\nand resumable. Includes integration, isolation and unit tests, spec, module\nREADME, tracker row, week-log and two filed platform findings.\n\nRefs #606, #613\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(docs): link #678 and #679 in pending review findings\n\nMove the two findings from #606 out of the untracked section into the\ntracked-issue table now that both have GitHub issues.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(api): address vendor-approval review feedback (#680)\n\n- Drop the vendor-approval module''s unused runtime dependencies (M1).\n- Test rejection at legal review and final approval, and that each review\n  state schedules a 48h SLA (S1, M2 partial).\n- Spec lists annual_spend_estimate as currency (G1); README warns against\n  re-seeding a tenant with live vendors and notes the demo only rejects at\n  IT Security (G2, S3).\n\nRefs #606\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(api): reject demo vendors at the stage they have reached (#680 review)\n\nA fixture with advanceTo \"rejected\" only rejected from it_security_review,\nso a vendor resumed at a later review stage walked on to Approved. The demo\nscript now rejects at the fixture''s rejectAt stage, or at the current review\nstage if the vendor is already past it, using that stage''s department role.\n\n- Rejection decision extracted to vendor-approval-rejection.ts, unit-tested.\n- Fixtures gain optional rejectAt; demo-vendor-007 is rejected at Legal.\n- Script seeds the module registry before installing, so it works before\n  the API has ever booted.\n\nRefs #606\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(docs): record the live walk-through risk acceptance for vendor-approval (#680 review)\n\nThe live admin-ui/Zitadel/worker walk-through (T12) is deferred by explicit\nowner decision and tracked in #691. The spec records what is unverified live,\nwhy the risk is bounded, and what closes it.\n\nRefs #606","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqufC1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAW/0QAE6g7Gu3MkkyhbKYK9VasJgA\nVlndYA8FqGNCoY00XcOAQtO9ERUEH5NtUNum4LBpN6IF+sepnAN1FohJ4DRPUtTe\nQAlXnhVQVVIEJSMAaauSEfcef1nPzGPTB1bTEusY4oYJ0zrdwoRjkmSbZ8/G19bT\n0UyWxbvY50kqm9I0Dzx/UTD7V1IoZtd067yxZcDMNkToAVpNfFYLkn1yolpb2u9M\n2ip+8J5qzum0kiGI7t4FZKrDnIp6r3XIrETX5k7lMtqH13b95rL39j3/KX3mmNc9\nnxB1H00m3e0SsqBDvK6/NKI30LiytEuDiuJ68gO4aWmhTEkpmd6YNTigeju+9xFs\n6XUXWyO4sngI+DrTPNe00eh6nNUcirgiwwgJAPcVcCQd7hftqiz7OQTIGxkS0Hfu\nEcirb58+7wMHQ5jqoAMIOCV5cq1+OKBJVRrPzsSnxaavcdIAtyOYMUnuP4/xWCA+\nnNbsBmynKwlmlYprtCrHXLiavV5nz9MAwHtjLugYd6eTAiP99Yo1nmXIS9uGn+r0\nrrSgEpbRxE4IW72v/U20F00/Qu+8LP/d0jjXBoNAFlXE2JyEyUgCNGoP1mlUZXsV\n1WlMeudsOJTxMfC0NveGPjLqddtqfLeIRhV55tVXhsV50JkykCMXobDR+NBXat55\na9YS4TfpI5L9zKDqJorS\n=JFPm\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T04:44:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commit/f3349ca2aa71e0cada6b64380144e81ee22cf94b","node_id":"C_kwDOScMdh9oAKGYzMzQ5Y2EyYWE3MWUwY2FkYTZiNjQzODAxNDRlODFlZTIyY2Y5NGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commit/30082ce1c14974068edfdbbdaf7ee9814f436184","sha":"30082ce1c14974068edfdbbdaf7ee9814f436184","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/30082ce1c14974068edfdbbdaf7ee9814f436184"}],"sha":"f3349ca2aa71e0cada6b64380144e81ee22cf94b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/f3349ca2aa71e0cada6b64380144e81ee22cf94b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3049693?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/abmish","id":3049693,"login":"abmish","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNDk2OTM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/30082ce1c14974068edfdbbdaf7ee9814f436184/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T04:43:32Z","email":"needabhinav@gmail.com","name":"Abhinav Mishra"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T04:43:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(api): audit every entity-list export, sync and async (#638) (#687)\n\n* fix(worker): make tenant purge and per-user erasure complete and cover every table (#635)\n\nTenant purge failed outright for most tenants (attachments -> files and\nseveral other NO ACTION/RESTRICT FKs rolled back the whole transaction), and\nper-user erasure failed on every call (app_user had no DELETE on\nticket_alerts/access_requests). saved_views were silently kept, 15 tenant\ntables were never purged and ~15 user-reference columns never scrubbed.\n\n- tenant-purge.ts: FK-safe order covering every tenant table; privileged\n  pre-step archives schedule rules, then deletes append-only\n  schedule_executions and user-scoped saved_views; exports\n  PURGED_TENANT_TABLES and ERASURE_EXEMPT_TABLES.\n- Per-user erasure moved to apps/api/src/services/user-erasure.ts and\n  extended to every user-reference column (legacy and map __accessUsers,\n  api_keys rotated_from, on-call primary shifts deleted).\n- Migration 0125: DELETE on ticket_alerts/access_requests, column-level\n  UPDATE (created_by) on entity_instance_tags.\n- information_schema-driven guards fail CI on any uncovered tenant table or\n  user-id column; db-conventions.md states the same-PR rule.\n\nCloses #635\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(api): audit every entity-list export, sync and async (#638)\n\nEntity-list exports (up to 10,000 rows, including PII/financial fields for\nPII_EXPORT_ROLES) left no audit trail.\n\n- Migration 0126 adds export.requested / export.completed / export.failed to\n  audit_log_action_check; AuditAction and audit''s exhaustive outcome and\n  request-kind maps gain the same three.\n- entity-types/export.ts writes export.requested before any data leaves on\n  both paths (fail-closed), export.completed / export.failed on the sync\n  path, and pre-generates the async job id so the request entry names it.\n- export-worker.ts: processExportJob writes export.completed or\n  export.failed (throw or deactivated tenant), then rethrows.\n- Entries record format, row count, mode, job id and includePii; no row\n  values, and assignee filters are recorded as a flag, not a user id. The\n  state filter is bounded.\n\nDepends on #681 (migration 0125 must apply before 0126).\n\nCloses #638\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(api): scope the erasure app.user_id switch to a savepoint (#681 review)\n\nIf the saved_views delete throws, ROLLBACK TO SAVEPOINT now also reverts\napp.user_id, so a caller that catches and continues never keeps the erased\nuser''s id as the transaction''s user. Adds a test that the caller''s\napp.user_id is restored.\n\ndb-conventions.md: policies reading app.* GUCs must NULLIF(..., '''') before a\ncast, because an unset custom GUC reads as '''' on pooled connections. The\nuser_ref / mention erasure gap is tracked as #688.\n\nRefs #635\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(api): restore app.user_id to null and delete membership last in erasure (#681 review)\n\n- The saved_views GUC restore passes null (\"back to nothing\") and its\n  comment now matches; observable value is unchanged.\n- tenant_users and idempotency_keys deletes move to the end of\n  eraseUserFromTenant, after every other footprint is scrubbed.\n- Spec records the retrospective check: saved_views is the only policy\n  reading app.user_id, and it never casts it to uuid.\n\nRefs #635\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a9bb187fcb384e4425121048801f81cc37c53a77","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/trees/a9bb187fcb384e4425121048801f81cc37c53a77"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/commits/30082ce1c14974068edfdbbdaf7ee9814f436184","verification":{"payload":"tree a9bb187fcb384e4425121048801f81cc37c53a77\nparent 5a42152ca1ca786a0c5dfe69e3891e04246c897f\nauthor Abhinav Mishra <needabhinav@gmail.com> 1790570612 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790570612 +0530\n\nfix(api): audit every entity-list export, sync and async (#638) (#687)\n\n* fix(worker): make tenant purge and per-user erasure complete and cover every table (#635)\n\nTenant purge failed outright for most tenants (attachments -> files and\nseveral other NO ACTION/RESTRICT FKs rolled back the whole transaction), and\nper-user erasure failed on every call (app_user had no DELETE on\nticket_alerts/access_requests). saved_views were silently kept, 15 tenant\ntables were never purged and ~15 user-reference columns never scrubbed.\n\n- tenant-purge.ts: FK-safe order covering every tenant table; privileged\n  pre-step archives schedule rules, then deletes append-only\n  schedule_executions and user-scoped saved_views; exports\n  PURGED_TENANT_TABLES and ERASURE_EXEMPT_TABLES.\n- Per-user erasure moved to apps/api/src/services/user-erasure.ts and\n  extended to every user-reference column (legacy and map __accessUsers,\n  api_keys rotated_from, on-call primary shifts deleted).\n- Migration 0125: DELETE on ticket_alerts/access_requests, column-level\n  UPDATE (created_by) on entity_instance_tags.\n- information_schema-driven guards fail CI on any uncovered tenant table or\n  user-id column; db-conventions.md states the same-PR rule.\n\nCloses #635\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(api): audit every entity-list export, sync and async (#638)\n\nEntity-list exports (up to 10,000 rows, including PII/financial fields for\nPII_EXPORT_ROLES) left no audit trail.\n\n- Migration 0126 adds export.requested / export.completed / export.failed to\n  audit_log_action_check; AuditAction and audit''s exhaustive outcome and\n  request-kind maps gain the same three.\n- entity-types/export.ts writes export.requested before any data leaves on\n  both paths (fail-closed), export.completed / export.failed on the sync\n  path, and pre-generates the async job id so the request entry names it.\n- export-worker.ts: processExportJob writes export.completed or\n  export.failed (throw or deactivated tenant), then rethrows.\n- Entries record format, row count, mode, job id and includePii; no row\n  values, and assignee filters are recorded as a flag, not a user id. The\n  state filter is bounded.\n\nDepends on #681 (migration 0125 must apply before 0126).\n\nCloses #638\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(api): scope the erasure app.user_id switch to a savepoint (#681 review)\n\nIf the saved_views delete throws, ROLLBACK TO SAVEPOINT now also reverts\napp.user_id, so a caller that catches and continues never keeps the erased\nuser''s id as the transaction''s user. Adds a test that the caller''s\napp.user_id is restored.\n\ndb-conventions.md: policies reading app.* GUCs must NULLIF(..., '''') before a\ncast, because an unset custom GUC reads as '''' on pooled connections. The\nuser_ref / mention erasure gap is tracked as #688.\n\nRefs #635\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(api): restore app.user_id to null and delete membership last in erasure (#681 review)\n\n- The saved_views GUC restore passes null (\"back to nothing\") and its\n  comment now matches; observable value is unchanged.\n- tenant_users and idempotency_keys deletes move to the end of\n  eraseUserFromTenant, after every other footprint is scrubbed.\n- Spec records the retrospective check: saved_views is the only policy\n  reading app.user_id, and it never casts it to uuid.\n\nRefs #635\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqufB0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmLQQAEiSn0/A5AOTu2FK061rVczE\nh3RMDesrDn3LO6pfQN2h9kKSnLr+UM+R0cRkhK8bzgs9IimOnxwVaYevuY5UsWUL\ngQ66GUXflSdYt+GAZtqXtRuR1KxqLXB5/GTaUYudQw0cGv6DAOdor+WAY7Cp4cO+\nx+puA0mV9NWxyBYGdXNEcSisCewpzC8CF3yosuZ+tue5zE2y48nQ75i2B46Nwhpc\nKYV8Zucpp5f7jFR8Tu7yTh1qDY8aLOAWSkKegUmCTiezqgsrljTbEz6vv0ajRStV\nXC15lOexvqSDIiwd871ZscIi22hMdcYm5ijQIh99LHAz+jPwP+I7VxxSRgINlHZP\nNyCITL/NebxAdRbtzvzlNSA1mvyp