ithubusercontent.com/u/3049693?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/abmish","id":3049693,"login":"abmish","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNDk2OTM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/5a42152ca1ca786a0c5dfe69e3891e04246c897f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T03:52:57Z","email":"needabhinav@gmail.com","name":"Abhinav Mishra"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T03:52:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(worker): make tenant purge and per-user erasure complete and cover every table (#635) (#681)\n\n* fix(worker): make tenant purge and per-user erasure complete and cover every table (#635)\n\nTenant purge failed outright for most tenants (attachments -> files and\nseveral other NO ACTION/RESTRICT FKs rolled back the whole transaction), and\nper-user erasure failed on every call (app_user had no DELETE on\nticket_alerts/access_requests). saved_views were silently kept, 15 tenant\ntables were never purged and ~15 user-reference columns never scrubbed.\n\n- tenant-purge.ts: FK-safe order covering every tenant table; privileged\n  pre-step archives schedule rules, then deletes append-only\n  schedule_executions and user-scoped saved_views; exports\n  PURGED_TENANT_TABLES and ERASURE_EXEMPT_TABLES.\n- Per-user erasure moved to apps/api/src/services/user-erasure.ts and\n  extended to every user-reference column (legacy and map __accessUsers,\n  api_keys rotated_from, on-call primary shifts deleted).\n- Migration 0125: DELETE on ticket_alerts/access_requests, column-level\n  UPDATE (created_by) on entity_instance_tags.\n- information_schema-driven guards fail CI on any uncovered tenant table or\n  user-id column; db-conventions.md states the same-PR rule.\n\nCloses #635\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(api): scope the erasure app.user_id switch to a savepoint (#681 review)\n\nIf the saved_views delete throws, ROLLBACK TO SAVEPOINT now also reverts\napp.user_id, so a caller that catches and continues never keeps the erased\nuser''s id as the transaction''s user. Adds a test that the caller''s\napp.user_id is restored.\n\ndb-conventions.md: policies reading app.* GUCs must NULLIF(..., '''') before a\ncast, because an unset custom GUC reads as '''' on pooled connections. The\nuser_ref / mention erasure gap is tracked as #688.\n\nRefs #635\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(api): restore app.user_id to null and delete membership last in erasure (#681 review)\n\n- The saved_views GUC restore passes null (\"back to nothing\") and its\n  comment now matches; observable value is unchanged.\n- tenant_users and idempotency_keys deletes move to the end of\n  eraseUserFromTenant, after every other footprint is scrubbed.\n- Spec records the retrospective check: saved_views is the only policy\n  reading app.user_id, and it never casts it to uuid.\n\nRefs #635\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"405ad0f12bb7cd53cf4704af05fed5fdf431750f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/trees/405ad0f12bb7cd53cf4704af05fed5fdf431750f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/commits/5a42152ca1ca786a0c5dfe69e3891e04246c897f","verification":{"payload":"tree 405ad0f12bb7cd53cf4704af05fed5fdf431750f\nparent d10562908d13d9a0ac28a05c75aff108552e46de\nauthor Abhinav Mishra <needabhinav@gmail.com> 1790567577 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790567577 +0530\n\nfix(worker): make tenant purge and per-user erasure complete and cover every table (#635) (#681)\n\n* fix(worker): make tenant purge and per-user erasure complete and cover every table (#635)\n\nTenant purge failed outright for most tenants (attachments -> files and\nseveral other NO ACTION/RESTRICT FKs rolled back the whole transaction), and\nper-user erasure failed on every call (app_user had no DELETE on\nticket_alerts/access_requests). saved_views were silently kept, 15 tenant\ntables were never purged and ~15 user-reference columns never scrubbed.\n\n- tenant-purge.ts: FK-safe order covering every tenant table; privileged\n  pre-step archives schedule rules, then deletes append-only\n  schedule_executions and user-scoped saved_views; exports\n  PURGED_TENANT_TABLES and ERASURE_EXEMPT_TABLES.\n- Per-user erasure moved to apps/api/src/services/user-erasure.ts and\n  extended to every user-reference column (legacy and map __accessUsers,\n  api_keys rotated_from, on-call primary shifts deleted).\n- Migration 0125: DELETE on ticket_alerts/access_requests, column-level\n  UPDATE (created_by) on entity_instance_tags.\n- information_schema-driven guards fail CI on any uncovered tenant table or\n  user-id column; db-conventions.md states the same-PR rule.\n\nCloses #635\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(api): scope the erasure app.user_id switch to a savepoint (#681 review)\n\nIf the saved_views delete throws, ROLLBACK TO SAVEPOINT now also reverts\napp.user_id, so a caller that catches and continues never keeps the erased\nuser''s id as the transaction''s user. Adds a test that the caller''s\napp.user_id is restored.\n\ndb-conventions.md: policies reading app.* GUCs must NULLIF(..., '''') before a\ncast, because an unset custom GUC reads as '''' on pooled connections. The\nuser_ref / mention erasure gap is tracked as #688.\n\nRefs #635\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(api): restore app.user_id to null and delete membership last in erasure (#681 review)\n\n- The saved_views GUC restore passes null (\"back to nothing\") and its\n  comment now matches; observable value is unchanged.\n- tenant_users and idempotency_keys deletes move to the end of\n  eraseUserFromTenant, after every other footprint is scrubbed.\n- Spec records the retrospective check: saved_views is the only policy\n  reading app.user_id, and it never casts it to uuid.\n\nRefs #635\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqueSZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA24AQAB/aycbTBHWfhLReOkl5TADR\nvuCeemnop1oYiISyGTShLAxNn6e7NvIhi89ZVxuqaNtJFDGXMvEFBdkxxujXzlYg\nN7FXXE+lEXAF2BF6M2JDsGeGndesGZvpHWwQpOVn2DLUiiA7NmFrfpjWzy+J3mKV\nZBQASFzqE/CFPAXe6ldBoFTBko3dsjm2gX72t0KJuxbNWmcSbNQI5kne1yCmz/mS\nzQ7Qirs5s8Xp8o1DGVb4LQuPT1mt5XfJTXbuNbgbpQg4hu2PfK19KNQDIjK89Jom\n2LjC2xq70cpn4NvtpWH+hJROOVjhhcaUvGfgGwJ7E/8DcjeW31YGmpevRarAGQYA\nX63tQwq/bYWu4qz17O5dgGHQmatPtc89kFLwSQf0D8rYWoSw6Pawyz9BGzd7AyYy\nexKvEU6DxHVxufbmL41YQaiRvt/zXF7oSV8r5IQaYEwTRHhQgSAjEDGdBGuSsNFt\nxRiv2YuCddnDvolPPoMOoFMx9LrEiA3KMtWlkqVJa3AOOwTSWQEfDOlmQBMR4Tsr\nIX/Uvpk5wwAAPIFmehIKekBf4Ju0bISEukUl8eJcmeEliqiHGTE/XorYPYjAsBjc\nN3E8fIFGi2CxvBG4n43S/UEr8OctCl7J1jJVCsGXiTANidPieOhMcA6FMQDGOfw0\nwzkhY8sJ2NmBhj/PQxQG\n=MMcs\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T03:52:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commit/5a42152ca1ca786a0c5dfe69e3891e04246c897f","node_id":"C_kwDOScMdh9oAKDVhNDIxNTJjYTFjYTc4NmEwYzVkZmU2OWUzODkxZTA0MjQ2Yzg5N2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commit/d10562908d13d9a0ac28a05c75aff108552e46de","sha":"d10562908d13d9a0ac28a05c75aff108552e46de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/d10562908d13d9a0ac28a05c75aff108552e46de"}],"sha":"5a42152ca1ca786a0c5dfe69e3891e04246c897f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/5a42152ca1ca786a0c5dfe69e3891e04246c897f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3049693?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/abmish","id":3049693,"login":"abmish","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNDk2OTM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/d10562908d13d9a0ac28a05c75aff108552e46de/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T16:12:34Z","email":"needabhinav@gmail.com","name":"Abhinav Mishra"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T16:12:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(automation-engine): honour trigger_config when matching rules (#678) (#686)\n\n* fix(automation-engine): honour trigger_config when matching rules (#678)\n\nThe executor matched rules on tenant, trigger_type and conditions only, so\nevery wizard-built rule (which scopes by workflow, state or entity type in\ntrigger_config) fired on every event of its trigger type in the tenant,\nincluding webhook, transition and set_field actions.\n\n- trigger-scope.ts: ruleInScope checks workflowId/fromState/toState for\n  transitions, workflowId/state for SLA breaches, entityTypeId for entity\n  events, and the legacy seed {entityType: name} by the event''s type name.\n  Empty values match anything; ids compare case-insensitively.\n- executor.ts: scope is checked before conditions and before any execution\n  row; entity-type name lookups are memoised and tenant-filtered.\n- actions/transition.ts: follow-up events carry the transitioned instance''s\n  real entityTypeId instead of the triggering event''s or the instance id.\n\nCloses #678\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(automation-engine): address trigger_config scoping review (#686)\n\n- Log instead of silently skipping follow-up rules when the transitioned\n  instance can''t be found.\n- Match the legacy entityType name case-insensitively, since entity type\n  names have no casing constraint.\n- Warn when a non-empty trigger_config meets an event type with no scope\n  keys, so a new emitter without scoping support is visible.\n- Scoping isolation test runs under withTenantContext, like production.\n\nRefs #678","tree":{"sha":"fb19c88f34ba6a4394b92449bb7d7498a123c7ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/trees/fb19c88f34ba6a4394b92449bb7d7498a123c7ac"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/commits/d10562908d13d9a0ac28a05c75aff108552e46de","verification":{"payload":"tree fb19c88f34ba6a4394b92449bb7d7498a123c7ac\nparent 4902f5d947a5108923d7d4df4d0d3c340f381857\nauthor Abhinav Mishra <needabhinav@gmail.com> 1790525554 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790525554 +0530\n\nfix(automation-engine): honour trigger_config when matching rules (#678) (#686)\n\n* fix(automation-engine): honour trigger_config when matching rules (#678)\n\nThe executor matched rules on tenant, trigger_type and conditions only, so\nevery wizard-built rule (which scopes by workflow, state or entity type in\ntrigger_config) fired on every event of its trigger type in the tenant,\nincluding webhook, transition and set_field actions.\n\n- trigger-scope.ts: ruleInScope checks workflowId/fromState/toState for\n  transitions, workflowId/state for SLA breaches, entityTypeId for entity\n  events, and the legacy seed {entityType: name} by the event''s type name.\n  Empty values match anything; ids compare case-insensitively.\n- executor.ts: scope is checked before conditions and before any execution\n  row; entity-type name lookups are memoised and tenant-filtered.\n- actions/transition.ts: follow-up events carry the transitioned instance''s\n  real entityTypeId instead of the triggering event''s or the instance id.\n\nCloses #678\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(automation-engine): address trigger_config scoping review (#686)\n\n- Log instead of silently skipping follow-up rules when the transitioned\n  instance can''t be found.\n- Match the legacy entityType name case-insensitively, since entity type\n  names have no casing constraint.\n- Warn when a non-empty trigger_config meets an event type with no scope\n  keys, so a new emitter without scoping support is visible.\n- Scoping isolation test runs under withTenantContext, like production.\n\nRefs #678","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquUByCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbgAQAJl5ozrQi6F6z/lDZtzjR21M\nMTj6+qmmRPDFQcXc/Gh2CQBs0TxK4a0XeAC/njRlVKNoRpF0AioFPmchv9BNbYgM\nmYaA3Oph3cPTREHAIMsQ1wcWx0kW0XKiRO7zMYcc9IfrgsgoRdyTvzEDCUwaJKPD\nuse19v89HNEGUSewJNcUE7i1K+bRv56hnBM4ZG4yBMW1zepHZWt9ZrISwjPj2Niq\nh2fLEPSkA1ZhYSJk9/Z4raYOz6N69NlbGN8mi7No34kJaI6+IQhd61i1XMUAJGap\nEjBl29kU+snsMpVREmPw04uNVGrlGRKQzBIOYm9iOoTljIMSd4lYvGjYW5YKCTV3\n5kD31eZo9UzNuP7Q3u2U15/BpHdAb0Q8FHo8J0dVNoHBdXeskw1L4ZFvkEDJdwAf\nTi7qfQHyk9POSDgXhfymwb/DvisuVWLXlWBk5XiwT24RK672oK6+DqlV1JethZcS\nF7+PiKGMhOydPNYRoWwzwnaQrbPCGQIKAEIXnm/UkDTRjScNRA5CBl9E2g8N/Nq0\nBfAIz9WaJd3tqXkqVFzxbsJPreJKVTWWNOLPL+s9arBAHTn1bUEvbb/xQk8WkLD6\ng2J/LrJAfaKl/iMcLA9ej+5mNdwFqpSuKE2nnQ+YKvM60XsbSSll0+fQM+RwTs7b\nYsLRI6fBEmR/Q2Tx+iAW\n=sfGK\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T16:12:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github