HWlqeBLOFH349aubasqj2ZDvyO+ORI4D\nogAS6VpezeT21zryob8/P2XrCIURUIxcxlvnkhtGv56l23Jgc2Rw8R44d9/WD+Vh\n+3La0NodoG1EGtNDYLc9\n=OvsM\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T07:18:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commit/43f61a0595628110e34f9333c5e4f41954a01ebb","node_id":"C_kwDOScMdh9oAKDQzZjYxYTA1OTU2MjgxMTBlMzRmOTMzM2M1ZTRmNDE5NTRhMDFlYmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commit/1a16f0ba4865b883d74d138745409ffcc017813b","sha":"1a16f0ba4865b883d74d138745409ffcc017813b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/1a16f0ba4865b883d74d138745409ffcc017813b"}],"sha":"43f61a0595628110e34f9333c5e4f41954a01ebb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/43f61a0595628110e34f9333c5e4f41954a01ebb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/184391486?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bikash-barnwal","id":184391486,"login":"bikash-barnwal","node_id":"U_kgDOCv2XPg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/1a16f0ba4865b883d74d138745409ffcc017813b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T16:44:32Z","email":"bikashprasadbarnwal@gmail.com","name":"Bikash"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T16:44:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(db): reporting role with tenant isolation and pii withheld (#663)\n\n* feat(db): reporting role with tenant isolation and pii withheld\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(db): reporting audit allowlist matches its writers\n\nThe in-app query builder and its /reporting/query endpoint were removed\n(review feedback). That endpoint was the only writer of\nreporting.query_failed, so migration 0115 no longer admits it, neither in\nadmin_audit_log''s CHECK constraint nor in record_reporting_audit()''s\nown action check.\n\nThe allowlist is now exactly what Superset writes through\nrecord_reporting_audit(): reporting.query_executed and reporting.exported.\nIt matches the TypeScript list in @platform/audit (audit PR).\n\nAlso reworded the 0121 comment that pointed at\napps/api/src/routes/reporting/query.ts, which no longer exists. The\ndecision it records (exact mirrors, no friendlier fallback title) is\nunchanged.\n\nVerified on a fresh CI-equivalent database: all 125 migrations apply,\nthe constraint lists only the two reporting actions, and the reporting\ngrants isolation suite plus the admin_audit_log constraint tests pass\n(30/30). check-analytics-annotations: 125/125.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(db): bind reporting audit rows to the session tenant\n\nReview on #663.\n\nM1: record_reporting_audit() is SECURITY DEFINER and took p_tenant_id\nfrom the caller, so any reporting connection could write an audit row\nthat appears to come from another tenant. It now refuses unless\np_tenant_id equals the connection''s app.tenant_id; an unstamped\nconnection is refused too. Superset''s audit path runs on the same\nreporting connection its connection mutator stamps, with the same tenant,\nso legitimate calls are unaffected; only a forged call mismatches.\n\nM2: ADR-001''s per-table grant list still showed tables that migration\n0113''s least-privilege pass revoked. Corrected against 0113''s actual\nre-grant list: entity_fields, entity_relations, automation_rules and\nautomation_executions (the four in the review), plus tenants (org to\ntenant is answered by tenant_for_org(), 0114) and workflow_transitions,\nare now marked excluded, so nobody re-adds them believing they were\nreviewed grants. Edited at @bikash-barnwal''s direction; ADRs are\nhuman-authored, so please review the wording.\n\nAlso: the audit allowlist admits reporting.guest_token_issued and\nreporting.guest_token_denied, which the reporting API now records for\nevery embedded pass it mints or refuses (#670 review M1). They are\nwritten by the API through the normal audit writer, not through\nrecord_reporting_audit(), whose own action list is unchanged.\n\nTests (reporting-grants isolation suite): a record claiming another\ntenant is refused; one from an unstamped connection is refused; one\nmatching the session tenant is written with that tenant. 33/33 with the\nadmin_audit_log constraint tests, on a fresh CI-equivalent database.\ncheck-analytics-annotations 125/125.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(db): refuse a missing session tenant in the reporting audit function\n\nRe-review on #663.\n\nB1: the tenant guard compared p_tenant_id with the session tenant using\nIS DISTINCT FROM, which treats two NULLs as equal. A NULL parameter from\nan unstamped connection therefore passed the guard (and was stopped only\nby admin_audit_log.tenant_id''s NOT NULL, with a generic constraint error\nrather than a refusal).\n\nBoth suggested fixes are applied:\n- The session tenant is read once and checked on its own first: no\n  session tenant raises \"no session tenant\".\n- The row is written with the session tenant, never the caller''s\n  parameter. After the checks they are equal, and this keeps the\n  parameter from being the source of the stored tenant at all.\nThe mismatch check stays for a parameter that disagrees with the session.\n\nG2: the own-rows policy''s second block (events scoped by their ticket) had\nno test. The fixture now adds one workflow event per ticket; a non-staff\nsession sees only the event on its own ticket, and a staff session sees\nboth.\n\nG1 (index for the own-rows EXISTS): no change needed. workflow_events\nalready has indexes leading on instance_id ((instance_id,\nidempotency_key)) and (tenant_id, instance_id), and the subquery looks up\nentity_instances by primary key.\n\nTests: NULL tenant on an unstamped connection is refused with \"no session\ntenant\"; NULL tenant on a stamped connection is refused as a mismatch;\nthe unstamped-connection case now reports \"no session tenant\". 37/37 with\nthe admin_audit_log constraint tests, on a fresh CI-equivalent database.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3eacb93c0eef6b8e6a96af5e52d1c9cfea33cb7c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/trees/3eacb93c0eef6b8e6a96af5e52d1c9cfea33cb7c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/commits/1a16f0ba4865b883d74d138745409ffcc017813b","verification":{"payload":"tree 3eacb93c0eef6b8e6a96af5e52d1c9cfea33cb7c\nparent 276b7515e690b9371d730b957147c927835764c8\nauthor Bikash <bikashprasadbarnwal@gmail.com> 1790354672 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790354672 +0530\n\nfeat(db): reporting role with tenant isolation and pii withheld (#663)\n\n* feat(db): reporting role with tenant isolation and pii withheld\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(db): reporting audit allowlist matches its writers\n\nThe in-app query builder and its /reporting/query endpoint were removed\n(review feedback). That endpoint was the only writer of\nreporting.query_failed, so migration 0115 no longer admits it, neither in\nadmin_audit_log''s CHECK constraint nor in record_reporting_audit()''s\nown action check.\n\nThe allowlist is now exactly what Superset writes through\nrecord_reporting_audit(): reporting.query_executed and reporting.exported.\nIt matches the TypeScript list in @platform/audit (audit PR).\n\nAlso reworded the 0121 comment that pointed at\napps/api/src/routes/reporting/query.ts, which no longer exists. The\ndecision it records (exact mirrors, no friendlier fallback title) is\nunchanged.\n\nVerified on a fresh CI-equivalent database: all 125 migrations apply,\nthe constraint lists only the two reporting actions, and the reporting\ngrants isolation suite plus the admin_audit_log constraint tests pass\n(30/30). check-analytics-annotations: 125/125.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(db): bind reporting audit rows to the session tenant\n\nReview on #663.\n\nM1: record_reporting_audit() is SECURITY DEFINER and took p_tenant_id\nfrom the caller, so any reporting connection could write an audit row\nthat appears to come from another tenant. It now refuses unless\np_tenant_id equals the connection''s app.tenant_id; an unstamped\nconnection is refused too. Superset''s audit path runs on the same\nreporting connection its connection mutator stamps, with the same tenant,\nso legitimate calls are unaffected; only a forged call mismatches.\n\nM2: ADR-001''s per-table grant list still showed tables that migration\n0113''s least-privilege pass revoked. Corrected against 0113''s actual\nre-grant list: entity_fields, entity_relations, automation_rules and\nautomation_executions (the four in the review), plus tenants (org to\ntenant is answered by tenant_for_org(), 0114) and workflow_transitions,\nare now marked excluded, so nobody re-adds them believing they were\nreviewed grants. Edited at @bikash-barnwal''s direction; ADRs are\nhuman-authored, so please review the wording.\n\nAlso: the audit allowlist admits reporting.guest_token_issued and\nreporting.guest_token_denied, which the reporting API now records for\nevery embedded pass it mints or refuses (#670 review M1). They are\nwritten by the API through the normal audit writer, not through\nrecord_reporting_audit(), whose own action list is unchanged.\n\nTests (reporting-grants isolation suite): a record claiming another\ntenant is refused; one from an unstamped connection is refused; one\nmatching the session tenant is written with that tenant. 33/33 with the\nadmin_audit_log constraint tests, on a fresh CI-equivalent database.\ncheck-analytics-annotations 125/125.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(db): refuse a missing session tenant in the reporting audit function\n\nRe-review on #663.\n\nB1: the tenant guard compared p_tenant_id with the session tenant using\nIS DISTINCT FROM, which treats two NULLs as equal. A NULL parameter from\nan unstamped connection therefore passed the guard (and was stopped only\nby admin_audit_log.tenant_id''s NOT NULL, with a generic constraint error\nrather than a refusal).\n\nBoth suggested fixes are applied:\n- The session tenant is read once and checked on its own first: no\n  session tenant raises \"no session tenant\".\n- The row is written with the session tenant, never the caller''s\n  parameter. After the checks they are equal, and this keeps the\n  parameter from being the source of the stored tenant at all.\nThe mismatch check stays for a parameter that disagrees with the session.\n\nG2: the own-rows policy''s second block (events scoped by their ticket) had\nno test. The fixture now adds one workflow event per ticket; a non-staff\nsession sees only the event on its own ticket, and a staff session sees\nboth.\n\nG1 (index for the own-rows EXISTS): no change needed. workflow_events\nalready has indexes leading on instance_id ((instance_id,\nidempotency_key)) and (tenant_id, instance_id), and the subquery looks up\nentity_instances by primary key.\n\nTests: NULL tenant on an unstamped connection is refused with \"no session\ntenant\"; NULL tenant on a stamped connection is refused as a mismatch;\nthe unstamped-connection case now reports \"no session tenant\". 37/37 with\nthe admin_audit_log constraint tests, on a fresh CI-equivalent database.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtqTwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVsAQAJkVWFlqsint3VU2T+SwY9v6\nVoYLkpgiNV0laJZ56N3dPuwNkTwjVaw2W01QrgjJb3rdaUpWKvVScMiINTff7Uud\nIuM+BTPxvnMDU4FpNj5aP8tv8BPW5HeQoB5pUmQDfkkxuHDfXHCqnppIWiBfl+d4\nobabXCGzQADzJkmaFMi5FshdviLeOr2g7EKFARH42/3kj27/8jbVddc5pRHmRXAK\nu07LbvIAPIoXkp4M+hVspJpiEctLc0DieLP6u+8VYy3EJ1wKuN4ErnCBTJVYyJ5y\njI/HZQsBMefPVeYe1/s/o78PXwnT7K+Izj8bUv7L3kzWD1tgeA7mZDaRVsJ3iEhU\nn993r15htE++Owfho+P4abVEbSV7WQVuoyHOkoDjNHeYYCwSTWesiM1bqFaU