?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bikash-barnwal","id":184391486,"login":"bikash-barnwal","node_id":"U_kgDOCv2XPg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/276b7515e690b9371d730b957147c927835764c8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T16:43:56Z","email":"bikashprasadbarnwal@gmail.com","name":"Bikash"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T16:43:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(api): superset guest token endpoint (#670)\n\n* feat(audit): add reporting query audit actions\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(audit): point comments at the renumbered audit migration\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(audit): match reporting actions to what is actually written\n\nWith the in-app query builder and its /reporting/query endpoint removed\n(review feedback), the reporting audit actions were re-checked against\ntheir real writers.\n\n- reporting.query_failed removed: only that endpoint ever wrote it, so\n  nothing can produce it any more.\n- reporting.exported added: Superset (standalone, Stage 2) writes it\n  through record_reporting_audit() whenever an analyst exports, but the\n  audit package had no classification for it.\n- reporting.query_executed kept: Superset writes it for every query run.\n\nThe TypeScript list now equals the set migration 0115''s CHECK constraint\nadmits (updated to match in the reporting DB PR), so every reporting row\nthat can reach admin_audit_log is classified when it is read back by the\nthird-party access-log route and the retention rollup.\n\nBoth classify as outcome \"allowed\" and request kind \"read\". Comments no\nlonger refer to the removed BYOQ spec.\n\naudit suite 103/103; typecheck and lint clean across every package that\ndepends on @platform/audit.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(audit): add guest-token audit actions for embedded reporting\n\nReview M1 on #670 (and the cross-PR gap noted on #665): issuing an\nembedded-dashboard guest pass was logged only to the application log,\nwhich is ephemeral and not queryable, so \"who viewed which reporting\ndashboards, and when\" (data-subject access requests, incident windows)\nhad no durable answer.\n\n- reporting.guest_token_issued: a pass was minted for a dashboard.\n  Outcome allowed, request kind read.\n- reporting.guest_token_denied: a dashboard the caller''s role does not\n  entitle them to was refused (a customer asking for the tenant-wide\n  dashboard). Outcome denied, request kind read.\n\nThe reviewer suggested a \"failed\" action; a Superset outage is an\noperational failure rather than an access decision, so it stays in the\napplication log, and the security-relevant refusal is audited instead.\nThe API writes these (#670); migration 0115 admits them (#663).\n\nTests: reporting-actions.test.ts covers both (issued with the other\nallowed reporting actions; denied classifies as denied/read), and the\ndenied list in outcome.test.ts includes the new denial. Audit suite\n111/111; typecheck and lint clean across every dependent package.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(config): validate superset environment\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(api): superset guest token and reporting query endpoints\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(api): isolation tests for the reporting query endpoint\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(api): remove the reporting query endpoint\n\nReview feedback removed the in-app query-builder sidebar, and\nPOST /reporting/query existed only to serve it. With no caller left it\nis dead code, so it goes with everything that existed only for it.\n\nRemoved\n- apps/api/src/routes/reporting/query.ts (the endpoint: query building,\n  own-rows scoping, statement timeout, audit writes) and query.test.ts.\n- tests/isolation/reporting-query.isolation.test.ts, which tested only\n  that endpoint.\n- The router''s POST /query route, and the second mount of the reporting\n  router at /reporting. Nothing calls /reporting/*; the embed page uses\n  /superset/guest-token, which is unchanged.\n\nAdded\n- tests/isolation/reporting-guest-token.isolation.test.ts (5 tests)\n  for the one remaining route. It runs the real handler and inspects the\n  row filters handed to Superset: Tenant A''s pass names only Tenant A\n  and Tenant B''s only Tenant B; the tenant clause is unscoped, so it\n  covers every dataset; a customer is refused the tenant dashboard; and a\n  customer''s personal pass is narrowed to their own id on every dataset.\n  Only the Superset HTTP call is stubbed. Checked that it fails when the\n  customer 403 is removed.\n\nThe audit actions the endpoint wrote are handled in the audit PR\n(reporting.query_failed removed, reporting.exported added).\n\nAPI suite on a fresh CI-equivalent database: 1577/1577. Typecheck and\nlint clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(config): reject empty and short superset secrets\n\nReview M1 (#666): an empty SUPERSET_SECRET_KEY passed every production\nguard, since \"\" is not the dev default, and would hand Superset an empty\nsigning key.\n\n- All four Superset secrets (SUPERSET_SECRET_KEY,\n  SUPERSET_GUEST_TOKEN_SECRET, SUPERSET_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_PASSWORD,\n  SUPERSET_ADMIN_PASSWORD) are now min(1): never empty, in any\n  environment.\n- In production, the two signing keys must be at least 32 characters, each\n  with its own refine so the error names the variable.\n\nThe 32-character floor is production-only rather than on the field itself:\nthe guest-token dev default is 29 characters, and a field-level min(32)\nwould stop a fresh clone from starting. Dev defaults remain rejected in\nproduction as before.\n\nTests: an empty value for each secret throws in production and in dev; a\n31-character signing key throws in production and a 32-character one\npasses. The production fixture''s two keys were lengthened to 32+\ncharacters (they were 17 and 25). Config suite 28/28; typecheck and lint\nclean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(api): audit guest passes and refuse long-lived ones\n\nReview on #670.\n\nM1 (HIGH): minting an embedded-dashboard guest pass was recorded only in\nthe application log, which rotates and is not queryable. The handler now\nwrites a durable row to the platform audit store:\n- reporting.guest_token_issued when a pass is minted: resource is the\n  embedded dashboard''s id; metadata carries the dashboard key and slug.\n- reporting.guest_token_denied when a customer asks for the tenant-wide\n  dashboard and gets 403 (nothing is minted).\nWritten inside the caller''s tenant context through the normal audit\nwriter. Best-effort by design: a failed audit write is logged at error\nlevel and does not fail the request, since the SDK re-mints every ~55s\nper open dashboard and an audit-store hiccup should not blank it. A\nSuperset outage is an operational failure, not an access decision, and\nstays in the application log.\n\nG1: the pass lifetime is set only in Superset''s config (60s), and\nSuperset''s guest-token API takes no per-request expiry. mintGuestToken\nnow reads the minted pass''s exp and refuses one that outlives\nMAX_GUEST_TOKEN_LIFETIME_SECONDS (90 = 60 plus 30s clock tolerance), so a\nlost or reverted Superset setting (default 300s) fails closed instead of\nsilently widening the revocation window. Checked against a live\nSuperset: its passes carry exp, 60s after issue.\n\nM2 (dual mount) and S2 (LIKE escaping) were already resolved: the\n/reporting mount and the query endpoint were removed with the sidebar.\n\nTests: an issued pass writes the issued row with the dashboard id and\nslug; a refused request writes a denied row and mints nothing; an\naudit-write failure still returns the pass; a 300s pass is refused;\nisGuestTokenLifetimeAcceptable accepts 60s and refuses beyond the limit,\na missing exp, and a non-JWT. API suite on a fresh CI-equivalent\ndatabase: 1583/1583. Typecheck and lint clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(config): move superset dev defaults out of env.ts\n\nRe-review suggestion on #670: DEV_SUPERSET_DEFAULTS was exported from the\nruntime env module only so the tests could import it.\n\nThe four development defaults now live in packages/config/src/dev-defaults.ts.\nenv.ts imports them for the schema defaults and the production guards;\nenv.test.ts imports them for the guard tests. env.ts no longer exports\nthem, and they are not part of the package''s public exports.\n\nThe values still ship with the config module, necessarily: they are the\ndefaults, and the production guard compares against them. What changes is\nthat they are no longer part of the runtime module''s API.\n\nNo behaviour change. Config suite 28/28; typecheck and lint clean across\nevery package that depends on @platform/config.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(api): stable audit resource id per reporting dashboard\n\nRe-review G1 on #670: refused guest-pass requests were audited with a\nrandom resource id, so the refused rows for a dashboard could not be\nfound by target without reading metadata.\n\nEvery guest-pass audit row, issued or refused, now uses a deterministic\nRFC 4122 v5 UUID derived from the dashboard slug\n(dashboardResourceId). The same dashboard always has the same id, across\nissued and denied rows and across deployments. The embedded dashboard id,\nwhich Superset regenerates per install, moves into metadata.embeddedId\nwhen there is one.\n\nv5 is computed with node:crypto (no new dependency).\n\nTests: uuidV5 matches the RFC reference value (Python\nuuid5(NAMESPACE_URL, \"http://example.com\")); the id is stable per\ndashboard and differs between dashboards; an issued and a refused row for\nthe same dashboard share it. API suite 1586/1586 on a fresh\nCI-equivalent database; typecheck and lint clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"17a3c322c06151ff276a06d6324738e4bba84cee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/trees/17a3c322c06151ff276a06d6324738e4bba84cee"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/commits/276b7515e690b9371d730b957147c927835764c8","verification":{"payload":"tree 17a3c322c06151ff276a06d6324738e4bba84cee\nparent 76aae1b790309bde7a4d0e00a45952ebd7dcaddd\nauthor Bikash <bikashprasadbarnwal@gmail.com> 1790354636 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790354636 +0530\n\nfeat(api): superset guest token endpoint (#670)\n\n* feat(audit): add reporting query audit actions\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(audit): point comments at the renumbered audit migration\n\nCo