ddd"}],"sha":"276b7515e690b9371d730b957147c927835764c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/276b7515e690b9371d730b957147c927835764c8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/184391486?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bikash-barnwal","id":184391486,"login":"bikash-barnwal","node_id":"U_kgDOCv2XPg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/76aae1b790309bde7a4d0e00a45952ebd7dcaddd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T16:43:40Z","email":"bikashprasadbarnwal@gmail.com","name":"Bikash"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T16:43:40Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(entity-engine): reject a due date earlier than creation (#672)\n\n* fix(entity-engine): reject a due date earlier than creation\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(api): use relative due dates in ticket-create isolation tests\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(entity-engine): allow clock skew on create, clearer due-date errors\n\nReview on #672.\n\nB1: the create path compared dueDate against this process''s clock at\nvalidation time, which runs after auth, pool wait and tenant setup and\nmay be skewed from the caller''s clock, so a dueDate meant as \"a few\nseconds from now\" could arrive already past and be refused. Create now\nhas its own check, validateDueDateOnCreate, which refuses only a dueDate\nmore than 60 seconds in the past (CREATE_DUE_DATE_GRACE_MS). The edit\npaths are unchanged: they still compare against the stored createdAt,\nwhich the review confirmed is correct.\n\nS1: the create path said \"must be after the entity''s created date\" when\nthere is no created date yet. Create now says \"dueDate must not be in the\npast\"; edit keeps \"must be after the entity''s created date\".\n\nTests\n- Create: a past dueDate is refused with the new message; one 30s in the\n  past is accepted; one 2 minutes in the past is still refused.\n- G2: bulkCreateEntities reports a past dueDate against that item''s index\n  and still creates the valid item, instead of failing the batch.\n- G1 (clearing with dueDate: null) is already covered by the existing\n  \"supersedes the pending schedule but writes no new one when dueDate is\n  cleared\" test, which would fail if the null gate were changed.\n\nentity-engine 250/250; API suite 1547/1547 on a fresh CI-equivalent\ndatabase; typecheck and lint clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(entity-engine): explicit due-date clear test; narrow create grace\n\nRe-review on #672.\n\nG1: an explicit test for clearing a due date. updateEntity with\ndueDate: null returns dueDate null, and the row update sets dueDate to\nNULL. Checked that it fails if the gate is changed to\n`input.dueDate !== undefined` (null would then be validated and refused);\nthe existing schedule-supersede test fails too.\n\nG1-new: the create-path grace window goes from 60s to 15s. NTP-synced skew\nis typically well under 5s; 15s covers that plus request latency without\nletting a ticket start with its SLA clock visibly in the past. The\nboundary tests move with it: 10s in the past is accepted, 30s is refused.\n\nNot changed:\n- G2-new (configurable window): a fixed, documented tolerance is easier\n  to reason about in SLA reports than a per-deployment value; happy to\n  add a setting if ops needs one.\n- G3-new (repeated block in updateEntity/bulkUpdateEntities): each pair\n  sits in two separate branches (fields changed vs not), so each path\n  runs the check once; left as is rather than restructure those\n  functions in this PR.\n\nentity-engine 251/251; typecheck and lint clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d778ee7264588ffc1e90feed644a59fba208500b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/trees/d778ee7264588ffc1e90feed644a59fba208500b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/commits/76aae1b790309bde7a4d0e00a45952ebd7dcaddd","verification":{"payload":"tree d778ee7264588ffc1e90feed644a59fba208500b\nparent 5e9da4261ccb34c4fd24e7fc2262cb0454adfe3b\nauthor Bikash <bikashprasadbarnwal@gmail.com> 1790354620 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790354620 +0530\n\nfix(entity-engine): reject a due date earlier than creation (#672)\n\n* fix(entity-engine): reject a due date earlier than creation\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(api): use relative due dates in ticket-create isolation tests\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(entity-engine): allow clock skew on create, clearer due-date errors\n\nReview on #672.\n\nB1: the create path compared dueDate against this process''s clock at\nvalidation time, which runs after auth, pool wait and tenant setup and\nmay be skewed from the caller''s clock, so a dueDate meant as \"a few\nseconds from now\" could arrive already past and be refused. Create now\nhas its own check, validateDueDateOnCreate, which refuses only a dueDate\nmore than 60 seconds in the past (CREATE_DUE_DATE_GRACE_MS). The edit\npaths are unchanged: they still compare against the stored createdAt,\nwhich the review confirmed is correct.\n\nS1: the create path said \"must be after the entity''s created date\" when\nthere is no created date yet. Create now says \"dueDate must not be in the\npast\"; edit keeps \"must be after the entity''s created date\".\n\nTests\n- Create: a past dueDate is refused with the new message; one 30s in the\n  past is accepted; one 2 minutes in the past is still refused.\n- G2: bulkCreateEntities reports a past dueDate against that item''s index\n  and still creates the valid item, instead of failing the batch.\n- G1 (clearing with dueDate: null) is already covered by the existing\n  \"supersedes the pending schedule but writes no new one when dueDate is\n  cleared\" test, which would fail if the null gate were changed.\n\nentity-engine 250/250; API suite 1547/1547 on a fresh CI-equivalent\ndatabase; typecheck and lint clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(entity-engine): explicit due-date clear test; narrow create grace\n\nRe-review on #672.\n\nG1: an explicit test for clearing a due date. updateEntity with\ndueDate: null returns dueDate null, and the row update sets dueDate to\nNULL. Checked that it fails if the gate is changed to\n`input.dueDate !== undefined` (null would then be validated and refused);\nthe existing schedule-supersede test fails too.\n\nG1-new: the create-path grace window goes from 60s to 15s. NTP-synced skew\nis typically well under 5s; 15s covers that plus request latency without\nletting a ticket start with its SLA clock visibly in the past. The\nboundary tests move with it: 10s in the past is accepted, 30s is refused.\n\nNot changed:\n- G2-new (configurable window): a fixed, documented tolerance is easier\n  to reason about in SLA reports than a per-deployment value; happy to\n  add a setting if ops needs one.\n- G3-new (repeated block in updateEntity/bulkUpdateEntities): each pair\n  sits in two separate branches (fields changed vs not), so each path\n  runs the check once; left as is rather than restructure those\n  functions in this PR.\n\nentity-engine 251/251; typecheck and lint clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtqS8CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArSkQAIOa2ES4jojiB7vWgsPBbLBs\nznJ8Ffn+ihsWTECnyJR4ZxKElijZD1nlpCL+n5S/xoZOyJsgn2kXh5g+C9XBeSNr\nu+WpownaUUyvpKSxSQFb4dJw6SuQ4tTYIadoxzaNwH1AnPwbiq/zE31b0yIoew6e\nsKlV+/XELju2hALVOfBf4YCDylFURmkgyT+JaDFMDq5O9stuYrn/wByeNZ/V1zlK\nMvsynCPjnlmQpEVRuyrsTcF3x/b5QEVvznq3d8G3VgW0JGVlXBmJOb2sCwIYKAjK\n5cFwpG986K2/JUDWSloXZJuy8StLtgiPjf8+AWdkFmPsrI4QE6R/tYSueqSMnL2b\nThsZ7hee5en3TLdK2ZTaL1K5ABmI0w+lwYGbsWwC+3VwFORwL9T8C8ou2vybktLF\n6r0hOXQ3+4qdYl9xihlXHqBlzDCnjDVXNKHKSIvf5sUuluD/ulP5xBrxvjtfNsUm\nnog+0UcRur5UcAjR4W2Vyq2Julur4sngAr4loykiQ4MCSb2oWzWgu733ItJ4ggfE\nFKYEbGDMH3K5iZxjNDHfU/+7KeGv+iFmjLCHEbSwMYb12ecSjxMqcw/5b2qH6Q+0\ndwu/tNDbp04R+GgOx3JbofzIR3ZMT48vfmmX9azRzpwYx6u0A1V8+CwzEX4emRt0\ny0Fb9VvxGJDsjk2q7zhm\n=zV80\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-25T16:43:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commit/76aae1b790309bde7a4d0e00a45952ebd7dcaddd","node_id":"C_kwDOScMdh9oAKDc2YWFlMWI3OTAzMDliZGU3YTRkMGUwMGE0NTk1MmViZDdkY2FkZGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commit/5e9da4261ccb34c4fd24e7fc2262cb0454adfe3b","sha":"5e9da4261ccb34c4fd24e7fc2262cb0454adfe3b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/5e9da4261ccb34c4fd24e7fc2262cb0454adfe3b"}],"sha":"76aae1b790309bde7a4d0e00a45952ebd7dcaddd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/76aae1b790309bde7a4d0e00a45952ebd7dcaddd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/184391486?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bikash-barnwal","id":184391486,"login":"bikash-barnwal","node_id":"U_kgDOCv2XPg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/5e9da4261ccb34c4fd24e7fc2262cb0454adfe3b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T16:10:23Z","email":"bikashprasadbarnwal@gmail.com","name":"Bikash"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T16:10:23Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: reporting specs and changelog (#671)\n\n* docs: reporting specs and changelog\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: point reporting specs at the renumbered migrations\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: bring the reporting changelog entry up to date\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: drop the query-builder spec and update reporting docs\n\nFollows the review feedback that removed the in-app query-builder sidebar\nand its POST /reporting/query endpoint.\n\n- docs/specs/byoq-hardening.md deleted: it specified only the removed\n  endpoint (measures, parameterised filters, role scoping, cost bounds).\n  Nothing links to it.\n- CHANGELOG: the \"Query builder on the Reporting page\" entry is gone. The\n  embedded-reporting entry now describes the filter bar led by the date\n  range, the SLA watch table directly under the KPI numbers, and ticket\n  rows linking to the ticket. The Stage 2 entry records what Superset\n  audits (reporting.query_executed / reporting.exported).\n- reporting-metadata-masking-repair.md: the \"unaffected by design\" row no\n  longer describes the in-app sidebar as a live path; task T16 notes the\n  endpoint it touched was later removed. Historical entries are otherwise\n  unchanged.\n- superset-embedded-dashboarding.md: the nav row now says where Reporting\n  actually sits (workspace nav after Dashboard; customers'' own link).\n\n\"BYOQ\" is kept where it refers to standalone Superset (Stage 2), which is\nunchanged. Prettier clean on every changed file.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: mark the stage 2 audit trail task done, note its one gap\n\nRe-review note on #671: the CHANGELOG says every Stage 2 query and\nexport is recorded in the platform audit log, while the standalone\nspec''s T11 (query/export audit trail) still said \"todo\".\n\nThe CHANGELOG is right; the spec had lagged. T11 is now marked done,\npointing at what implements it: PlatformAuditEventLogger in\ndocker/superset/superset_config.py writes every SQL Lab query and export\nto admin_audit_log through record_reporting_audit() (migration 0115),\nwith the query text, row count and duration, bound to the session\ntenant.\n\nOne gap is stated rather than hidden: the recorded actor is the Zitadel\nlogin name (falling back to the subject id), not always the subject id\nT11 asks for.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"636401475604ae8b6147a6407dc4f126e1fc6a27","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/trees/636401475604ae8b6147a6407dc4f126e1fc6a27"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/commits/5e9da4261ccb34c4fd24e7fc2262cb0454adfe3b","verification":{"payload":"tree 636401475604ae8b6147a6407dc4f126e1fc6a27\nparent 8b3a2cf8557cc4d6834ff344f0ba403929f642c8\nauthor Bikash <bikashprasadbarnwal@gmail.com> 1790352623 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790352623 +0530\n\ndocs: reporting specs and changelog (#671)\n\n* docs: reporting specs and changelog\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: point reporting specs at the renumbered migrations\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: bring the reporting changelog entry up to date\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: drop the query-builder spec and update reporting docs\n\nFollows the review feedback that removed the in-app query-builder sidebar\nand its POST /reporting/query endpoint.\n\n- docs/specs/byoq-hardening.md deleted: it specified only the removed\n  endpoint (measures, parameterised filters, role scoping, cost bounds).\n  Nothing links to it.\n- CHANGELOG: the \"Query builder on the Reporting page\" entry is gone. The\n  embedded-reporting entry now describes the filter bar led by the date\n  range, the SLA watch table directly under the KPI numbers, and ticket\n  rows linking to the ticket. The Stage 2 entry records what Superset\n  audits (reporting.query_executed / reporting.exported).\n- reporting-metadata-masking-repair.md: the \"unaffected by design\" row no\n  longer describes the in-app sidebar as a live path; task T16 notes the\n  endpoint it touched was later removed. Historical entries are otherwise\n  unchanged.\n- superset-embedded-dashboarding.md: the nav row now says where Reporting\n  actually sits (workspace nav after Dashboard; customers'' own link).\n\n\"BYOQ\" is kept where it refers to standalone Superset (Stage 2), which is\nunchanged. Prettier clean on every changed file.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: mark the stage 2 audit trail task done, note its one gap\n\nRe-review note on #671: the CHANGELOG says every Stage 2 query and\nexport is recorded in the platform audit log, while the standalone\nspec''s T11 (query/export audit trail) still said \"todo\".\n\nThe CHANGELOG is right; the spec had lagged. T11 is now marked done,\npointing at what implements it: PlatformAuditEventLogger in\ndocker/superset/superset_config.py writes every SQL Lab query and export\nto admin_audit_log through record_reporting_audit() (migration 0115),\nwith the query text, row count and duration, bound to the session\ntenant.\n\nOne gap is stated rather than hidden: the recorded actor is the Zitadel\nlogin name (falling back to the subject id), not always the subject id\nT11 asks for.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtpzvCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAheEQAJ87n3cPAGTwuXMCN0KN0c0e\nUVi7rjNHxgKoTPYqYopZIk2Z7i4+uuiKHF/ASdkizvUwVTPJybvdxZCZasD8iSFH\nWtpdzoDk8iqr5mqbmlAHC0elgo3zltC2QFQVjndSvTtzLM25Wsw7DBnmIK84C7KK\nrwTd+ZweYIYWbUZNJSCmK6z6ULP3SQLA67vPJidlfMVmiR9qv1uj7fSmoPyWtNfy\nksGjPqWuHB8lW9+BueNPe3/iyFTUX1uU5K/QS1wtNbwWYWaaztjElc6nodf2KclW\nZlmBI1Acm944hDnOagwCAJxdINFvrigpeoBtGr6x8MFjrPWqD6ZG0T9eX83YLAwZ\nHvtQIAae1shI7yv25KkTNMopLwsRDLlBV6xvb13ksrx5fMlcpDIHgYu80Uaubq4D\n012R0jG35Q9oChlX6uJXAoJvo/KMc4VcfeleJLFJBm5n2ipjQcqwDpNZUPo3EBaY\nydKwnqU+rY46dy0vhp/HXpV5qandGydZlm8uxEbe/J4bs/zm3HQ8BPaOQVhKttSN\nrHOfroditV3YYv12gDokkNI/G9mB4E0zbw+ndXWavmZRWSZHJV/Xw8x4YqknEdvy\nvHfS1IPEBHniStJRDMehczOMiZJk+UbK5J7KJNrDBbp71w/0e8aZKLbRXnFge8Ae\neSXAmZhwBMiI4CSkdswW\n=CYP7\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-25T16:10:24Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commit/5e9da4261ccb34c4fd24e7fc2262cb0454adfe3b","node_id":"C_kwDOScMdh9oAKDVlOWRhNDI2MWNjYjM0YzRmZDI0ZTdmYzIyNjJjYjA0NTRhZGZlM2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commit/8b3a2cf8557cc4d6834ff344f0ba403929f642c8","sha":"8b3a2cf8557cc4d6834ff344f0ba403929f642c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/8b3a2cf8557cc4d6834ff344f0ba403929f642c8"}],"sha":"5e9da4261ccb34c4fd24e7fc2262cb0454adfe3b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/5e9da4261ccb34c4fd24e7fc2262cb0454adfe3b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/184391486?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bikash-barnwal","id":184391486,"login":"bikash-barnwal","node_id":"U_kgDOCv2XPg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/8b3a2cf8557cc4d6834ff344f0ba403929f642c8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T16:09:29Z","email":"bikashprasadbarnwal@gmail.com","name":"Bikash"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T16:09:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(admin-ui): surface login failures instead of swallowing them (#669)\n\n* fix(admin-ui): surface login failures instead of swallowing them\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(admin-ui): cover the logged sign-in failure path\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(admin-ui): show a sign-in failure on the login page\n\nReview M1 on #669: logging the failure to the console fixed the silent\nswallow, but the user still saw only a button that reset, and would retry\nand then raise a support ticket.\n\n- A failed redirect to the identity provider now shows a fixed message\n  under the button: \"Sign-in failed. If this continues, please contact\n  support.\" (role=\"alert\", translated via login.signInFailed). The raw\n  error is deliberately not shown: it can name hosts or endpoints. It\n  still goes to the console for whoever is debugging.\n- The handoff sign-in path (handleHandoffLogin) had the same empty catch;\n  it now logs and shows the same message.\n- The message clears when sign-in is retried.\n\nRouting to a server-side logger (review \"recommended\"): admin-ui has no\nfrontend error-reporting client today, so there is nothing to send this\nto. Left for a follow-up rather than adding an event nothing listens to.\n\nTests: the failure test asserts the alert text, that the raw error text is\nabsent from the page, and that the button re-enables; it now uses\nfireEvent.click (review S1). New test: a failed handoff sign-in shows the\nsame message. admin-ui suite green (one known-flaky upstream records test\npasses on re-run). Typecheck and lint clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2430414468e0b25e8ca9e5e5a1848672d5ec23c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/trees/2430414468e0b25e8ca9e5e5a1848672d5ec23c0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/commits/8b3a2cf8557cc4d6834ff344f0ba403929f642c8","verification":{"payload":"tree 2430414468e0b25e8ca9e5e5a1848672d5ec23c0\nparent fa1a2ca5028f280feacc657bfae16abb02e7af86\nauthor Bikash <bikashprasadbarnwal@gmail.com> 1790352569 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790352569 +0530\n\nfix(admin-ui): surface login failures instead of swallowing them (#669)\n\n* fix(admin-ui): surface login failures instead of swallowing them\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(admin-ui): cover the logged sign-in failure path\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(admin-ui): show a sign-in failure on the login page\n\nReview M1 on #669: logging the failure to the console fixed the silent\nswallow, but the user still saw only a button that reset, and would retry\nand then raise a support ticket.\n\n- A failed redirect to the identity provider now shows a fixed message\n  under the button: \"Sign-in failed. If this continues, please contact\n  support.\" (role=\"alert\", translated via login.signInFailed). The raw\n  error is deliberately not shown: it can name hosts or endpoints. It\n  still goes to the console for whoever is debugging.\n- The handoff sign-in path (handleHandoffLogin) had the same empty catch;\n  it now logs and shows the same message.\n- The message clears when sign-in is retried.\n\nRouting to a server-side logger (review \"recommended\"): admin-ui has no\nfrontend error-reporting client today, so there is nothing to send this\nto. Left for a follow-up rather than adding an event nothing listens to.\n\nTests: the failure test asserts the alert text, that the raw error text is\nabsent from the page, and that the button re-enables; it now uses\nfireEvent.click (review S1). New test: a failed handoff sign-in shows the\nsame message. admin-ui suite green (one known-flaky upstream records test\npasses on re-run). Typecheck and lint clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtpy5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAASLUQAIJbnHqd7ssnZGEp4Uz2GchU\nqFRpwRyyXFHLG1HCVw0m+Vg4bG1+d+jd20zx4Zj6EYDRAyOyxjKQi38/bOG7YvZD\n1Gcn5Fv6EohoZ4ZkU4iuMju+dsJvx/krFtqir4XCSK8+xT9k8IQDlXdQkdrpR8i5\nPr482yv8+jg+DNq8zN+KRKKGOpmanMs9PK2BlReqJwd9H+5ZiPilUXxyl0ZWdKiC\nKEucR/IflLN+/f7c2xDHgkvVv9pa4DtlGuWRVJKc+GW2Pv+gS0L7uvDwO0O7XFLS\nFb5YO5ditEVxossER+cWQ48mFGUx5jjNObNZMuTE0LOUPyByZ8+84P22ity3do1r\nowHMGrEdtllTIkNXSw/KZBdPjx4ewrHbT1rEJrozE9tGsSzeIPhI4XpYCxYdm62F\nZB8UhmqyXYTd2d8ZDxLo+ebRmOmPIOK9X/GlrBKJBe0VCCF/QbKCasT4wDbPf6MW\ngnq9IgqFhWUx028ngQYviJ1etmw0g/8iCe/roQQD2owlEYYOWH0l/S2fGP7/pc08\nLnTGB5p9BPhLe1k0HJJ32rArZ1et58zcUjiLFOIPtB3c4WI01EsBbTgmWYOVpWJg\nYP9vKd6fxOJYBvN+feanXtuxeF00CDugf3WxIE6vTnXbMvSmnlNepVaaTKzPZz5S\njtiu69Wdn6PS9xAlTVIA\n=78u1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-25T16:09:29Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commit/8b3a2cf8557cc4d6834ff344f0ba403929f642c8","node_id":"C_kwDOScMdh9oAKDhiM2EyY2Y4NTU3Y2M0ZDY4MzRmZjM0NGYwYmE0MDM5MjlmNjQyYzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commit/fa1a2ca5028f280feacc657bfae16abb02e7af86","sha":"fa1a2ca5028f280feacc657bfae16abb02e7af86","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/fa1a2ca5028f280feacc657bfae16abb02e7af86"}],"sha":"8b3a2cf8557cc4d6834ff344f0ba403929f642c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/8b3a2cf8557cc4d6834ff344f0ba403929f642c8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/184391486?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bikash-barnwal","id":184391486,"login":"bikash-barnwal","node_id":"U_kgDOCv2XPg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/fa1a2ca5028f280feacc657bfae16abb02e7af86/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T16:09:05Z","email":"bikashprasadbarnwal@gmail.com","name":"Bikash"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T16:09:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(dx): superset service, provisioning and dashboards (#668)\n\n* chore(dx): superset service, provisioning and dashboards\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(dx): correct a stale reporting-role comment in superset provisioning\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(dx): remove hint text from the org overview kpi tiles\n\nReview feedback: the four big numbers on My Organisation Overview should\nshow only the number and its title, without the line of text under it.\n\nRemoved the `subheader` (and its now-unused `subheader_font_size`) from:\n- Total Tickets (\"All Tickets to be respond\")\n- Overdue Now (\"Tickets past due date and not yet closed.\")\n- Unassigned Tickets (\"Tickets with no assignee yet.\")\n- Median Time to First Response (\"Median Response Time(24hrs), ...\")\n\nProvisioning writes each chart''s params in full on every run, so the text\nis cleared from existing charts too, not only from fresh installs.\nVerified on a running instance: after superset-init, the four slices carry\nno subheader. The My Performance tiles (Raised by Me, Assigned to Me) are\nunchanged.\n\nAlso reworded the two bootstrap.py comments that said the KPI tiles'' hint\nlives in `subheader`, so they no longer describe text that is gone.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(dx): reporting layout, filter order and the table''s open link\n\nReview feedback on the embedded dashboards, plus a broken link found while\nchecking it.\n\nOpen link in the ticket tables\n- The link pointed at /records/record/<id>, but admin-ui serves tickets at\n  /records/<type slug>/<id>. It now uses the same slug expression as the\n  dataset''s record_type_slug column, e.g. /records/tickets/<id>.\n- The comments claimed the new tab needs no extra iframe permission. It\n  does: the SDK''s allow-popups opens the tab but keeps it inside the\n  dashboard iframe''s sandbox. The embed page now adds\n  allow-popups-to-escape-sandbox (reporting page PR); comments corrected.\n\nMy Organisation Overview layout\n- \"Ticket SLA Watch\" moves from the 11th tile to directly under the four\n  KPI numbers. It is full width, so it is row 2 on its own.\n- Retitled to \"Ticket SLA Watch (Upcoming & Overdue)\". A new optional\n  `renamed_from` key renames the provisioned chart in place, so the\n  chart keeps its id, nothing is left stranded, and copies users saved\n  under the old title are not touched.\n\nFilter bar order (both dashboards)\n- Date Range now leads the row; Priority moves after the other dropdowns,\n  so on a typical screen it sits in Superset''s \"More filters\" menu.\n\nDead config\n- VITE_REPORTING_TIMEZONE removed from .env and .env.example: nothing\n  reads it.\n\nVerified on a running instance after superset-init: row 1 is the four\nKPIs, row 2 is the SLA table (chart id unchanged), the filter order is\nDate Range, Status, Department, Assignee, Priority, and the dataset emits\n<a href=\".../records/tickets/<id>\" target=\"_blank\">.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(dx): halve the height of the org overview kpi row\n\nReview feedback: the first row of My Organisation Overview (Total\nTickets, Overdue Now, Unassigned Tickets, Median Time to First Response)\ntakes too much vertical space. Their height goes from 50 to 25 grid\nunits, half the previous size. The big-number font scales with the tile,\nso no font setting changes.\n\nVerified after superset-init: row 1 is the four KPI tiles at height 25,\nand row 2 (Ticket SLA Watch) is unchanged at 80.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(dx): show the hours unit on the median first-response tile\n\nReview feedback: the fourth KPI on My Organisation Overview (Median Time\nto First Response) showed a bare number. It now shows \"hrs\" under the\nvalue.\n\nSuperset''s number formats are numeric only and cannot append text to the\nvalue, so the unit uses the big-number tile''s own subheader, the one\ntext mechanism confirmed to render on a tile. It carries only the unit,\nnot the hint text removed earlier. The two bootstrap.py comments that\nsaid the KPI tiles carry no subheader are updated to match.\n\nVerified after superset-init: chart 11 carries subheader \"hrs\"; the\nother three KPI tiles carry none.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(dx): superset review fixes: persistence, secrets, headers, cors\n\nReview on #668.\n\nB1 (critical): in ensure_service_account the commit and log after\n`return created` were unreachable, so on a first-ever run the new service\naccount could go unsaved, depending on whether Flask-AppBuilder''s\nadd_user commits on its own. The commit now runs before the return. A\nscan of bootstrap.py found no other statements after a return.\n\nB2: SUPERSET_DB_PASSWORD and ANALYTICS_USER_PASSWORD fell back silently\nto well-known dev strings in docker-compose.yml and were undocumented.\nBoth are now required (:?, compose refuses to start without them), with\nthe dev values in .env and documented in .env.example, including the\nALTER ROLE needed to change them on the database roles too. The API does\nnot read these, so they are guarded at compose level rather than in\n@platform/config.\n\nH1: TALISMAN_ENABLED was False, which dropped every Flask security\nheader. Talisman is on again with Superset''s own default policy (read\nfrom superset.config, so it follows Superset upgrades), changed in only\nthe two places embedding needs: frame_options None (X-Frame-Options can\nonly say DENY/SAMEORIGIN) and CSP frame-ancestors ''self'' plus the\nadmin-ui origin. TALISMAN_DEV_CONFIG gets the same, for debug instances.\nVerified on a running instance: X-Content-Type-Options, Referrer-Policy\nand the nonce-based CSP are back, frame-ancestors is\n''self'' http://localhost:3001, and there is no X-Frame-Options.\n\nH2: CORS allow_headers was \"*\" with credentials. Now Authorization,\nContent-Type, X-CSRFToken, X-GuestToken and X-Requested-With.\n\nG1: the superset service gets a 2GB memory limit (~400MB at rest with 2\nworkers), so a runaway query cannot take the host down.\n\nG3: the demo seed script built four UPDATE statements by string\ninterpolation. They now use drizzle''s sql template with bound\nparameters; dates go as ISO strings with ::timestamptz (drizzle''s raw\ntemplate does not serialise a Date object, checked against a database).\n\nG2 (pip --require-hashes) is left for a follow-up: it needs hashes for\nevery transitive wheel of the pinned packages, and is better done as its\nown change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a17fe2951b3f05405ddde7f3dfc62880ca4f69aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/trees/a17fe2951b3f05405ddde7f3dfc62880ca4f69aa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/commits/fa1a2ca5028f280feacc657bfae16abb02e7af86","verification":{"payload":"tree a17fe2951b3f05405ddde7f3dfc62880ca4f69aa\nparent d78fcceda182774aa66499be1bd2caf4293c0868\nauthor Bikash <bikashprasadbarnwal@gmail.com> 1790352545 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790352545 +0530\n\nchore(dx): superset service, provisioning and dashboards (#668)\n\n* chore(dx): superset service, provisioning and dashboards\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(dx): correct a stale reporting-role comment in superset provisioning\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(dx): remove hint text from the org overview kpi tiles\n\nReview feedback: the four big numbers on My Organisation Overview should\nshow only the number and its title, without the line of text under it.\n\nRemoved the `subheader` (and its now-unused `subheader_font_size`) from:\n- Total Tickets (\"All Tickets to be respond\")\n- Overdue Now (\"Tickets past due date and not yet closed.\")\n- Unassigned Tickets (\"Tickets with no assignee yet.\")\n- Median Time to First Response (\"Median Response Time(24hrs), ...\")\n\nProvisioning writes each chart''s params in full on every run, so the text\nis cleared from existing charts too, not only from fresh installs.\nVerified on a running instance: after superset-init, the four slices carry\nno subheader. The My Performance tiles (Raised by Me, Assigned to Me) are\nunchanged.\n\nAlso reworded the two bootstrap.py comments that said the KPI tiles'' hint\nlives in `subheader`, so they no longer describe text that is gone.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(dx): reporting layout, filter order and the table''s open link\n\nReview feedback on the embedded dashboards, plus a broken link found while\nchecking it.\n\nOpen link in the ticket tables\n- The link pointed at /records/record/<id>, but admin-ui serves tickets at\n  /records/<type slug>/<id>. It now uses the same slug expression as the\n  dataset''s record_type_slug column, e.g. /records/tickets/<id>.\n- The comments claimed the new tab needs no extra iframe permission. It\n  does: the SDK''s allow-popups opens the tab but keeps it inside the\n  dashboard iframe''s sandbox. The embed page now adds\n  allow-popups-to-escape-sandbox (reporting page PR); comments corrected.\n\nMy Organisation Overview layout\n- \"Ticket SLA Watch\" moves from the 11th tile to directly under the four\n  KPI numbers. It is full width, so it is row 2 on its own.\n- Retitled to \"Ticket SLA Watch (Upcoming & Overdue)\". A new optional\n  `renamed_from` key renames the provisioned chart in place, so the\n  chart keeps its id, nothing is left stranded, and copies users saved\n  under the old title are not touched.\n\nFilter bar order (both dashboards)\n- Date Range now leads the row; Priority moves after the other dropdowns,\n  so on a typical screen it sits in Superset''s \"More filters\" menu.\n\nDead config\n- VITE_REPORTING_TIMEZONE removed from .env and .env.example: nothing\n  reads it.\n\nVerified on a running instance after superset-init: row 1 is the four\nKPIs, row 2 is the SLA table (chart id unchanged), the filter order is\nDate Range, Status, Department, Assignee, Priority, and the dataset emits\n<a href=\".../records/tickets/<id>\" target=\"_blank\">.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(dx): halve the height of the org overview kpi row\n\nReview feedback: the first row of My Organisation Overview (Total\nTickets, Overdue Now, Unassigned Tickets, Median Time to First Response)\ntakes too much vertical space. Their height goes from 50 to 25 grid\nunits, half the previous size. The big-number font scales with the tile,\nso no font setting changes.\n\nVerified after superset-init: row 1 is the four KPI tiles at height 25,\nand row 2 (Ticket SLA Watch) is unchanged at 80.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(dx): show the hours unit on the median first-response tile\n\nReview feedback: the fourth KPI on My Organisation Overview (Median Time\nto First Response) showed a bare number. It now shows \"hrs\" under the\nvalue.\n\nSuperset''s number formats are numeric only and cannot append text to the\nvalue, so the unit uses the big-number tile''s own subheader, the one\ntext mechanism confirmed to render on a tile. It carries only the unit,\nnot the hint text removed earlier. The two bootstrap.py comments that\nsaid the KPI tiles carry no subheader are updated to match.\n\nVerified after superset-init: chart 11 carries subheader \"hrs\"; the\nother three KPI tiles carry none.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(dx): superset review fixes: persistence, secrets, headers, cors\n\nReview on #668.\n\nB1 (critical): in ensure_service_account the commit and log after\n`return created` were unreachable, so on a first-ever run the new service\naccount could go unsaved, depending on whether Flask-AppBuilder''s\nadd_user commits on its own. The commit now runs before the return. A\nscan of bootstrap.py found no other statements after a return.\n\nB2: SUPERSET_DB_PASSWORD and ANALYTICS_USER_PASSWORD fell back silently\nto well-known dev strings in docker-compose.yml and were undocumented.\nBoth are now required (:?, compose refuses to start without them), with\nthe dev values in .env and documented in .env.example, including the\nALTER ROLE needed to change them on the database roles too. The API does\nnot read these, so they are guarded at compose level rather than in\n@platform/config.\n\nH1: TALISMAN_ENABLED was False, which dropped every Flask security\nheader. Talisman is on again with Superset''s own default policy (read\nfrom superset.config, so it follows Superset upgrades), changed in only\nthe two places embedding needs: frame_options None (X-Frame-Options can\nonly say DENY/SAMEORIGIN) and CSP frame-ancestors ''self'' plus the\nadmin-ui origin. TALISMAN_DEV_CONFIG gets the same, for debug instances.\nVerified on a running instance: X-Content-Type-Options, Referrer-Policy\nand the nonce-based CSP are back, frame-ancestors is\n''self'' http://localhost:3001, and there is no X-Frame-Options.\n\nH2: CORS allow_headers was \"*\" with credentials. Now Authorization,\nContent-Type, X-CSRFToken, X-GuestToken and X-Requested-With.\n\nG1: the superset service gets a 2GB memory limit (~400MB at rest with 2\nworkers), so a runaway query cannot take the host down.\n\nG3: the demo seed script built four UPDATE statements by string\ninterpolation. They now use drizzle''s sql template with bound\nparameters; dates go as ISO strings with ::timestamptz (drizzle''s raw\ntemplate does not serialise a Date object, checked against a database).\n\nG2 (pip --require-hashes) is left for a follow-up: it needs hashes for\nevery transitive wheel of the pinned packages, and is better done as its\nown change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtpyhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQa0QADRHHCY/dGxBv3YT28rM03mT\nyoxsNbGDRebgpOfcs3mWN5aQChOIdOZgCSd2waZZDv8BtlBkoIP2eY1ItB+49Fd6\nTnzf5nD3dsyeodcB5/+Wddx5DkF4BnH/C8mMoJkeGEK2syji7rNRTfrjD56WciPf\nd9CxNVBnPppjENm7Ez+0Gx9C4YV45ItkJ7Wy9zFs7PDLdVE2Fb4JVlHo32MremMe\neNDadRgPbsQf6DXfq0kU5UsRVhc/OPGTH5/jkodzboIzWlG9MFUl9yo+Yuu8muuR\nJekVe4xSwN5p5ITMtImT19z/YJFLRTtzFGdGrTodsXMQ6s/t4BXdfz8HEzy1wDiy\nCHMSYlz+n3aAxVZmw1FPHVBjViSV7PCQGCtNmrkgS6z/BG5kVx8LJ20o4ZDgH1zp\nsSOpQS1GPjB8Gd5B01Xba2UcZ9gzLaGZ3koDTkIi40puJwX4vTTQ1T0ABjI0V7HO\nt0q9mhe/8YHsHU7GB9yBBb8pkGfxQRvfkR96jYF0sBpVPuGqD0ZVfffsyi+Fm0JT\nUVQ++3yzh6RO7Az3RCc5HGM7u/n6GhHEMXw5oyMthjzQ90/1yxCEyqv0vlAWJNQj\nZNqjiwTeBSUxCmof+/k/OjdR2oTVD769ojodrkpmV1NaZjM9xSeCsg6605LfBxWs\ncuLfBlEQkZ9wH/ceKODv\n=bf+t\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-25T16:09:06Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commit/fa1a2ca5028f280feacc657bfae16abb02e7af86","node_id":"C_kwDOScMdh9oAKGZhMWEyY2E1MDI4ZjI4MGZlYWNjNjU3YmZhZTE2YWJiMDJlN2FmODY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commit/d78fcceda182774aa66499be1bd2caf4293c0868","sha":"d78fcceda182774aa66499be1bd2caf4293c0868","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/d78fcceda182774aa66499be1bd2caf4293c0868"}],"sha":"fa1a2ca5028f280feacc657bfae16abb02e7af86","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/fa1a2ca5028f280feacc657bfae16abb02e7af86"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/184391486?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bikash-barnwal","id":184391486,"login":"bikash-barnwal","node_id":"U_kgDOCv2XPg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/d78fcceda182774aa66499be1bd2caf4293c0868/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T10:35:25Z","email":"bikashprasadbarnwal@gmail.com","name":"Bikash"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T10:35:25Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(config): validate superset environment (#666)\n\n* feat(config): validate superset environment\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(config): reject empty and short superset secrets\n\nReview M1 (#666): an empty SUPERSET_SECRET_KEY passed every production\nguard, since \"\" is not the dev default, and would hand Superset an empty\nsigning key.\n\n- All four Superset secrets (SUPERSET_SECRET_KEY,\n  SUPERSET_GUEST_TOKEN_SECRET, SUPERSET_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_PASSWORD,\n  SUPERSET_ADMIN_PASSWORD) are now min(1): never empty, in any\n  environment.\n- In production, the two signing keys must be at least 32 characters, each\n  with its own refine so the error names the variable.\n\nThe 32-character floor is production-only rather than on the field itself:\nthe guest-token dev default is 29 characters, and a field-level min(32)\nwould stop a fresh clone from starting. Dev defaults remain rejected in\nproduction as before.\n\nTests: an empty value for each secret throws in production and in dev; a\n31-character signing key throws in production and a 32-character one\npasses. The production fixture''s two keys were lengthened to 32+\ncharacters (they were 17 and 25). Config suite 28/28; typecheck and lint\nclean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(config): move superset dev defaults out of env.ts\n\nRe-review suggestion on #670: DEV_SUPERSET_DEFAULTS was exported from the\nruntime env module only so the tests could import it.\n\nThe four development defaults now live in packages/config/src/dev-defaults.ts.\nenv.ts imports them for the schema defaults and the production guards;\nenv.test.ts imports them for the guard tests. env.ts no longer exports\nthem, and they are not part of the package''s public exports.\n\nThe values still ship with the config module, necessarily: they are the\ndefaults, and the production guard compares against them. What changes is\nthat they are no longer part of the runtime module''s API.\n\nNo behaviour change. Config suite 28/28; typecheck and lint clean across\nevery package that depends on @platform/config.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"797101a84212bbf8d48be98b6cf5be0e5cd9d8cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/trees/797101a84212bbf8d48be98b6cf5be0e5cd9d8cb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/commits/d78fcceda182774aa66499be1bd2caf4293c0868","verification":{"payload":"tree 797101a84212bbf8d48be98b6cf5be0e5cd9d8cb\nparent 93e907e1f934b1b4c7cb0579fd0c83c1b608a861\nauthor Bikash <bikashprasadbarnwal@gmail.com> 1790332525 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790332525 +0530\n\nfeat(config): validate superset environment (#666)\n\n* feat(config): validate superset environment\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(config): reject empty and short superset secrets\n\nReview M1 (#666): an empty SUPERSET_SECRET_KEY passed every production\nguard, since \"\" is not the dev default, and would hand Superset an empty\nsigning key.\n\n- All four Superset secrets (SUPERSET_SECRET_KEY,\n  SUPERSET_GUEST_TOKEN_SECRET, SUPERSET_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_PASSWORD,\n  SUPERSET_ADMIN_PASSWORD) are now min(1): never empty, in any\n  environment.\n- In production, the two signing keys must be at least 32 characters, each\n  with its own refine so the error names the variable.\n\nThe 32-character floor is production-only rather than on the field itself:\nthe guest-token dev default is 29 characters, and a field-level min(32)\nwould stop a fresh clone from starting. Dev defaults remain rejected in\nproduction as before.\n\nTests: an empty value for each secret throws in production and in dev; a\n31-character signing key throws in production and a 32-character one\npasses. The production fixture''s two keys were lengthened to 32+\ncharacters (they were 17 and 25). Config suite 28/28; typecheck and lint\nclean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(config): move superset dev defaults out of env.ts\n\nRe-review suggestion on #670: DEV_SUPERSET_DEFAULTS was exported from the\nruntime env module only so the tests could import it.\n\nThe four development defaults now live in packages/config/src/dev-defaults.ts.\nenv.ts imports them for the schema defaults and the production guards;\nenv.test.ts imports them for the guard tests. env.ts no longer exports\nthem, and they are not part of the package''s public exports.\n\nThe values still ship with the config module, necessarily: they are the\ndefaults, and the production guard compares against them. What changes is\nthat they are no longer part of the runtime module''s API.\n\nNo behaviour change. Config suite 28/28; typecheck and lint clean across\nevery package that depends on @platform/config.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtk5tCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAq0IQAHZ0VY6hfiu1hfpGbmf3eytQ\nlDPj7FRa1k/2dvTeyR8Dohdyv5LPrYUwFGaCitqUf/n1c14PJPVvYFjkEglnNKl2\n8mo1RQxf0Q/jXoFLr8fWmRA2ekf0tqHWYiD7VF4jD4Okiha1Lxe4yumIe1H5uOew\nffk8vHwPgmeyNNm8toZWJaLZHZxG9+GiXdl4isrcnRh6LqjgBX/O8lKb+Ofttnly\n2rC61dDOFAY7biROzK5bTtFGkHazKUQml+DBuh6Q7LA/cceeK5Vqzu1sAMttvCmy\nGHwJz17bAyRCSEPpH8swSy8KmN9McQU+1hfI/p3L1Nr3svnU1uF0fp2yr/GjWboA\nzEsV4fSnxaLI8cOGem/0MykAxrIsxsIfTNtTpRIqGeq+WjyOtVCKlTxFfcNk2PB0\nJAwoyTPzoK5t+EDB7qv5c1xiyiuQMSCFmQFmzSKorCDY/SEubn7eBVvzBPPdmQBV\nwF3m9iXqBao9FjmA3ZJkw7cFTD/K47NSVyaS5xLzvDQlRQxzRqzQA1eQKIDud4E6\nrRIomo6mQqOqoIhAZmpfQwkZJZlf7GuWzqi61iKzx85vif6Km+B7mQek3pL3/L08\nuJ8IchegOHduZ25X7ghXKx57z87VtJr20IIMWj/WvLo1iZR5etppGUQRC4wcXaRX\nSBb6F4kVPLglqPCz+GGG\n=a9yz\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-25T10:35:26Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commit/d78fcceda182774aa66499be1bd2caf4293c0868","node_id":"C_kwDOScMdh9oAKGQ3OGZjY2VkYTE4Mjc3NGFhNjY0OTliZTFiZDJjYWY0MjkzYzA4Njg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commit/93e907e1f934b1b4c7cb0579fd0c83c1b608a861","sha":"93e907e1f934b1b4c7cb0579fd0c83c1b608a861","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/93e907e1f934b1b4c7cb0579fd0c83c1b608a861"}],"sha":"d78fcceda182774aa66499be1bd2caf4293c0868","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/d78fcceda182774aa66499be1bd2caf4293c0868"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/184391486?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bikash-barnwal","id":184391486,"login":"bikash-barnwal","node_id":"U_kgDOCv2XPg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bikash-barnwal","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/93e907e1f934b1b4c7cb0579fd0c83c1b608a861/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T10:24:45Z","email":"bikashprasadbarnwal@gmail.com","name":"Bikash"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T10:24:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(admin-ui): reporting page with embedded dashboards (#667)\n\n* feat(admin-ui): reporting page with query builder panel\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(admin-ui): remove the reporting query-builder sidebar\n\nReview feedback: the embedded Reporting page does not need the \"BYOQ\"\nsidebar. Removed it and everything that existed only for it.\n\nRemoved\n- apps/admin-ui/src/pages/reporting-byoq.tsx (the sidebar component).\n- The sidebar toggle, its open/closed state and the layout gap it used\n  in reporting.tsx.\n- The REPORTING_TIMEZONE entry this PR had added to vite.config.ts:\n  nothing read it, so the file is back to upstream.\n- Test mocks that only served the sidebar: the /users and\n  /reporting/query responses and the useHoverStyle stub.\n\nChanged\n- The info tooltip no longer mentions BYOQ.\n- embedDashboard now passes iframeSandboxExtras:\n  [\"allow-popups-to-escape-sandbox\"]. The ticket tables'' \"Open\" link\n  opens a new tab; the SDK''s allow-popups lets it open but keeps it inside\n  the dashboard iframe''s sandbox, where OpenWind fails to load. This\n  gives the new tab a normal browsing context and widens nothing for the\n  iframe itself.\n\nTests\n- Sidebar tests removed; tab and customer tests keep their role checks\n  without the sidebar assertions.\n- New: the page renders no query-builder remnant and calls only the\n  guest-token endpoint.\n- New: the embed receives allow-popups-to-escape-sandbox.\n- admin-ui suite: 343/343. Typecheck and lint clean.\n\nEmbedded dashboards are unaffected: they use /superset/guest-token,\nwhich is unchanged. The /reporting/query endpoint the sidebar called is\nremoved in the reporting API PR.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(admin-ui): no superset link until its real address is known\n\nReview on #667.\n\nM2: the \"Explore Detailed Report\" link''s address started as a hardcoded\nhttp://localhost:8088 and was replaced only when the guest-token response\narrived, so a staff user clicking during load was sent to localhost, the\nwrong place in any real deployment. The address now starts unset, and\nthe link is not rendered until the API has returned Superset''s actual\naddress.\n\nS1: the customer nav''s Reporting link is deliberately not behind the\n!isPlainUser guard that the Templates link uses, since plain users are\nexactly who the personal dashboard is for. The comment now says so, so\nnobody adds the guard and removes their reporting. It also now describes\nthe scope correctly (tickets raised or assigned, not only raised).\n\nM1, M3 and G1 targeted the query-builder sidebar, which was removed on\nreview feedback, so there is no sidebar error handling, CSV export or\nfree-text filter left to fix.\n\nTest: the link is absent while the pass is pending and appears with the\naddress the API returned once it resolves. Reporting page 15/15;\ntypecheck and lint clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8e3c2a587715d622b17ee0b1ebecd4f231551d24","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/trees/8e3c2a587715d622b17ee0b1ebecd4f231551d24"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/commits/93e907e1f934b1b4c7cb0579fd0c83c1b608a861","verification":{"payload":"tree 8e3c2a587715d622b17ee0b1ebecd4f231551d24\nparent 38e45371bb6285df2ab2f9abab64a94610212103\nauthor Bikash <bikashprasadbarnwal@gmail.com> 1790331885 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790331885 +0530\n\nfeat(admin-ui): reporting page with embedded dashboards (#667)\n\n* feat(admin-ui): reporting page with query builder panel\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(admin-ui): remove the reporting query-builder sidebar\n\nReview feedback: the embedded Reporting page does not need the \"BYOQ\"\nsidebar. Removed it and everything that existed only for it.\n\nRemoved\n- apps/admin-ui/src/pages/reporting-byoq.tsx (the sidebar component).\n- The sidebar toggle, its open/closed state and the layout gap it used\n  in reporting.tsx.\n- The REPORTING_TIMEZONE entry this PR had added to vite.config.ts:\n  nothing read it, so the file is back to upstream.\n- Test mocks that only served the sidebar: the /users and\n  /reporting/query responses and the useHoverStyle stub.\n\nChanged\n- The info tooltip no longer mentions BYOQ.\n- embedDashboard now passes iframeSandboxExtras:\n  [\"allow-popups-to-escape-sandbox\"]. The ticket tables'' \"Open\" link\n  opens a new tab; the SDK''s allow-popups lets it open but keeps it inside\n  the dashboard iframe''s sandbox, where OpenWind fails to load. This\n  gives the new tab a normal browsing context and widens nothing for the\n  iframe itself.\n\nTests\n- Sidebar tests removed; tab and customer tests keep their role checks\n  without the sidebar assertions.\n- New: the page renders no query-builder remnant and calls only the\n  guest-token endpoint.\n- New: the embed receives allow-popups-to-escape-sandbox.\n- admin-ui suite: 343/343. Typecheck and lint clean.\n\nEmbedded dashboards are unaffected: they use /superset/guest-token,\nwhich is unchanged. The /reporting/query endpoint the sidebar called is\nremoved in the reporting API PR.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(admin-ui): no superset link until its real address is known\n\nReview on #667.\n\nM2: the \"Explore Detailed Report\" link''s address started as a hardcoded\nhttp://localhost:8088 and was replaced only when the guest-token response\narrived, so a staff user clicking during load was sent to localhost, the\nwrong place in any real deployment. The address now starts unset, and\nthe link is not rendered until the API has returned Superset''s actual\naddress.\n\nS1: the customer nav''s Reporting link is deliberately not behind the\n!isPlainUser guard that the Templates link uses, since plain users are\nexactly who the personal dashboard is for. The comment now says so, so\nnobody adds the guard and removes their reporting. It also now describes\nthe scope correctly (tickets raised or assigned, not only raised).\n\nM1, M3 and G1 targeted the query-builder sidebar, which was removed on\nreview feedback, so there is no sidebar error handling, CSV export or\nfree-text filter left to fix.\n\nTest: the link is absent while the pass is pending and appears with the\naddress the API returned once it resolves. Reporting page 15/15;\ntypecheck and lint clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtkvtCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAaioQADzZe1eO0SXhMBAMvCZWGJck\nmBpLWYB2ZN+5dWazRkdCEi2ylGew0BZ7Em9iGONXm6CrdS3dHMgU5e41yMxfoAWw\njTGnmOcpRD6ZI4uH16NnVKbgTXU4ovdUzaC73jjN0HGCaCNO/GhMksHs34KLyFmB\n1FgrzGoYFHhZz6edNz5VE1J1YmPnDk8IsQ+h7epi