enWind/commits/bbf1840d967982f75a4b1003a6b0d3ce8dc7f3de"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3049693?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/abmish","id":3049693,"login":"abmish","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNDk2OTM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/05bfd340860c6b686666481f5e22b4e1e34b023d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T19:40:21Z","email":"needabhinav@gmail.com","name":"Abhinav Mishra"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T19:40:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci: add CLA Assistant workflow [skip-tests-check] (#655)\n\n* ci: add cla assistant workflow\n\nAdds .github/workflows/cla.yml running contributor-assistant/github-action\nto require a signed CLA (or DCO-style acknowledgement) before a first-time\ncontributor''s PR can merge, per CLA.md / CONTRIBUTING.md''s Contribution Terms\n(PR #654). Config verified directly against the action''s current action.yml\nand README (upstream repo is archived/no-longer-maintained, but the pinned\nv2.6.1 release still functions).\n\nTwo known follow-ups, deliberately not blocking this PR:\n- path-to-document currently points at the legal/cla-draft branch (where\n  CLA.md lives today) — needs updating to main once PR #654 merges.\n- Untested against a real PR yet — repo/org Actions permission settings can\n  override the explicit `permissions:` block here, so this needs a live\n  throwaway-PR test before being trusted for a real contributor.\n\nHuman-directed addition — .github/workflows/ edits are off-limits to\nautonomous changes per CLAUDE.md; added on explicit instruction, SHIP_BYPASS\n(logged) since this is a config-only diff with nothing for typecheck/lint/\ntest to cover.\n\n* ci: point cla assistant at main now that cla.md has merged\n\nPR #654 (CLA.md, CONTRIBUTING.md Contribution Terms) merged into main.\nUpdates the two remaining legal/cla-draft references in cla.yml to main,\nper this PR''s own test plan item 1.","tree":{"sha":"ce8ab8f8d49e5ee5db9e697198e3e23d538a8e1e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/trees/ce8ab8f8d49e5ee5db9e697198e3e23d538a8e1e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/commits/05bfd340860c6b686666481f5e22b4e1e34b023d","verification":{"payload":"tree ce8ab8f8d49e5ee5db9e697198e3e23d538a8e1e\nparent ab3b0c2a45057a67135f8df786aca28e58af624a\nauthor Abhinav Mishra <needabhinav@gmail.com> 1789760421 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789760421 +0530\n\nci: add CLA Assistant workflow [skip-tests-check] (#655)\n\n* ci: add cla assistant workflow\n\nAdds .github/workflows/cla.yml running contributor-assistant/github-action\nto require a signed CLA (or DCO-style acknowledgement) before a first-time\ncontributor''s PR can merge, per CLA.md / CONTRIBUTING.md''s Contribution Terms\n(PR #654). Config verified directly against the action''s current action.yml\nand README (upstream repo is archived/no-longer-maintained, but the pinned\nv2.6.1 release still functions).\n\nTwo known follow-ups, deliberately not blocking this PR:\n- path-to-document currently points at the legal/cla-draft branch (where\n  CLA.md lives today) — needs updating to main once PR #654 merges.\n- Untested against a real PR yet — repo/org Actions permission settings can\n  override the explicit `permissions:` block here, so this needs a live\n  throwaway-PR test before being trusted for a real contributor.\n\nHuman-directed addition — .github/workflows/ edits are off-limits to\nautonomous changes per CLAUDE.md; added on explicit instruction, SHIP_BYPASS\n(logged) since this is a config-only diff with nothing for typecheck/lint/\ntest to cover.\n\n* ci: point cla assistant at main now that cla.md has merged\n\nPR #654 (CLA.md, CONTRIBUTING.md Contribution Terms) merged into main.\nUpdates the two remaining legal/cla-draft references in cla.yml to main,\nper this PR''s own test plan item 1.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrZOlCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACg0QAEKOwnYdqiBNdAUZZyfiEq83\nPS32hJSIp+sY42qpjEHk6lYZLcK0DDxh6pAz7vn11PHOlCpC5txoYSQUPiz+VMzl\nRTuOVoSXznM3ZUeQB8aSTdkUwcVHglkxLUA/XwvMRVKn3h6hebFNziu9UXC4foRe\nl7vLRB0jhcz71Czf8gMoJzCFRJdCykx/w9GNlOykw4SoKD0zKZlS3D9K5x3MF4+t\nSX8fV2OkM0uz65ymcrboikaXh++8wQWXVWR6k3yZr9vqIrKHcefdNFPWy5pconYE\neq4UqnKrgi4vXBMvt+q8JxSxFNkW9+v5/Ny/Q7knMAa7NOMVoK7McQnVVbR/MxFU\nExENPadIHQHevmeRBJF8R0RsElXokxDCEoaNgIRyXl70Gx31VRDENSa7iOXMNHjj\njX5cZB/o2TG8ebdx4mHogUqjVWgcz/jdnWXcPTN+ZUcmTZtfAz/zkfz9tPjGbPI8\n/Jk7JAcY/r1Eu2WpyQ1MaBhKXjpUbXmT/ZbR9VmZrsWF6BtXPz1AtfwUtdErhgwB\nwyoW0NsfTlrTpG9hVniPqpMG7T5nxLDnnpfSLch53f1b9yXsvE5n0dbEtcqli8WU\npd7PUnmInuQDttvR8EGb8T+S3NGHvNW70nLqK58sCuKbROSWfL4oY4XSrvIHtIMU\nnzzJbHwCN2Nh90+8f8d9\n=Yzk+\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T19:40:21Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commit/05bfd340860c6b686666481f5e22b4e1e34b023d","node_id":"C_kwDOScMdh9oAKDA1YmZkMzQwODYwYzZiNjg2NjY2NDgxZjVlMjJiNGUxZTM0YjAyM2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commit/ab3b0c2a45057a67135f8df786aca28e58af624a","sha":"ab3b0c2a45057a67135f8df786aca28e58af624a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/ab3b0c2a45057a67135f8df786aca28e58af624a"}],"sha":"05bfd340860c6b686666481f5e22b4e1e34b023d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/05bfd340860c6b686666481f5e22b4e1e34b023d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3049693?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/abmish","id":3049693,"login":"abmish","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNDk2OTM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/ab3b0c2a45057a67135f8df786aca28e58af624a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T19:29:40Z","email":"needabhinav@gmail.com","name":"Abhinav Mishra"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T19:29:40Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: add contributor assignment agreement (CLA) [skip-tests-check] (#654)\n\n* docs: add contributor assignment agreement and contribution terms\n\nAdds CLA.md (a draft Contributor Assignment Agreement — contributors assign\ncopyright and patent rights to Abhinav Mishra, current owner of the TinyPhi\norg and OpenWind project, in exchange for a license back to their own\ncontribution), a matching lightweight \"Contribution Terms\" section in\nCONTRIBUTING.md, and a PR template.\n\nThis closes a real gap: the project''s commercial dual-license offer (README)\nrequires clean rights over every contribution, and at least 4 people have\ncommitted code with no CLA or assignment on file today.\n\nStill open, deliberately not blocking this commit:\n- CLA.md is explicitly marked draft/unreviewed by counsel — not for real\n  signature yet.\n- The Section 19(4), Indian Copyright Act, 1957 citation needs verification\n  against current post-amendment numbering before reliance.\n- No automated enforcement yet (cla-assistant.io planned) — until then, new\n  contributors need to be pointed at CLA.md manually, not assumed to have\n  agreed by merely opening a PR.\n\nNo application code touched. SHIP_BYPASS (logged) — legal/docs diff, not a\nplan-lock/review candidate per this repo''s own guidance to scale process to\ndiff size and risk.\n\n* fix: resolve prettier non-idempotence in cla.md signature table\n\npnpm format:check failed in CI on PR #654 (Quality gates job). Root cause:\nraw underscore runs in the signature table''s blank-line placeholders hit a\nnon-idempotent path in prettier''s markdown printer — `--write` produced\noutput that `--check` itself still flagged, an infinite-oscillation bug\nrather than a one-time miss. Fixed by wrapping the placeholders in inline\ncode spans (backticks), which prettier passes through verbatim instead of\nescaping. Verified convergent across repeated write+check cycles locally.","tree":{"sha":"722b20a61a10e0f2d690d97a21a68fadfed3542f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/trees/722b20a61a10e0f2d690d97a21a68fadfed3542f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/commits/ab3b0c2a45057a67135f8df786aca28e58af624a","verification":{"payload":"tree 722b20a61a10e0f2d690d97a21a68fadfed3542f\nparent 1bf6ee00123aa0aa30014c40f810c489b70522ca\nauthor Abhinav Mishra <needabhinav@gmail.com> 1789759780 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789759780 +0530\n\ndocs: add contributor assignment agreement (CLA) [skip-tests-check] (#654)\n\n* docs: add contributor assignment agreement and contribution terms\n\nAdds CLA.md (a draft Contributor Assignment Agreement — contributors assign\ncopyright and patent rights to Abhinav Mishra, current owner of the TinyPhi\norg and OpenWind project, in exchange for a license back to their own\ncontribution), a matching lightweight \"Contribution Terms\" section in\nCONTRIBUTING.md, and a PR template.\n\nThis closes a real gap: the project''s commercial dual-license offer (README)\nrequires clean rights over every contribution, and at least 4 people have\ncommitted code with no CLA or assignment on file today.\n\nStill open, deliberately not blocking this commit:\n- CLA.md is explicitly marked draft/unreviewed by counsel — not for real\n  signature yet.\n- The Section 19(4), Indian Copyright Act, 1957 citation needs verification\n  against current post-amendment numbering before reliance.\n- No automated enforcement yet (cla-assistant.io planned) — until then, new\n  contributors need to be pointed at CLA.md manually, not assumed to have\n  agreed by merely opening a PR.\n\nNo application code touched. SHIP_BYPASS (logged) — legal/docs diff, not a\nplan-lock/review candidate per this repo''s own guidance to scale process to\ndiff size and risk.\n\n* fix: resolve prettier non-idempotence in cla.md signature table\n\npnpm format:check failed in CI on PR #654 (Quality gates job). Root cause:\nraw underscore runs in the signature table''s blank-line placeholders hit a\nnon-idempotent path in prettier''s markdown printer — `--write` produced\noutput that `--check` itself still flagged, an infinite-oscillation bug\nrather than a one-time miss. Fixed by wrapping the placeholders in inline\ncode spans (backticks), which prettier passes through verbatim instead of\nescaping. Verified convergent across repeated write+check cycles locally.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrZEkCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIuYQADgPEYzf9dgloFrpZQyw85I4\nIMfykZU5lrN8LsXTMvlhrWztZpmxTW9jU3PRXlrYBj1G7jO6RhzV3MZ/59Vu5Xpz\nC5GqXJiRvyBtCaGn175Xlr/SH07aAuKMdIiPeYTwtuL1XxWjDAbagb81MHTjaK+v\neWnAJ+E46KvhPiJzxtbFph4cQcOaDRXvtr5IR6aAju6fKFO1dAYQMLhjwVb1Vb01\nWFpX3Xe1qYsaiMVLmSVzBrPUyI/3x2wnCBGZMi82F8cB33/tu43a6+xDj9q05RFt\nlomfz1SoVSqLU6TAChzpLdfG05RKrjC3ZKmI+XnzLpO1qafpXc4TgFHoe6WlpmUh\n7KIf9t6AieDPDM0THIiqVTdElZhoOYJPOZPNyPsF9PpiLMxqM5IDsl8qQF1c63Pl\nuKzHnjXI4dStwE15Po9nO8VgOurWY7JN8nBCEo+7DN0TVSobN4op+psZTM+mO/VX\nFvFlLuEuFXKRxSEY6FBKVSH4R4RrQSjbFqehQqOCo6Mdy0s+ajeq76YNCw58zw+J\nKZuqNfcYbqNIsKudeDCl2yUPW1UcPZK4fa+Wm18C8tMp2oRSnXIi8cf1MF/oBPij\nu8DqEjEaQCP6XPPtLryTEa29ZWUh3+mvCXoDZO1SirswCDGxrLjPOQtEGLp8XOAJ\nktdHjdRUVzw6oZYw5E3X\n=96qa\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T19:29:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commit/ab3b0c2a45057a67135f8df786aca28e58af624a","node_id":"C_kwDOScMdh9oAKGFiM2IwYzJhNDUwNTdhNjcxMzVmOGRmNzg2YWNhMjhlNThhZjYyNGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commit/1bf6ee00123aa0aa30014c40f810c489b70522ca","sha":"1bf6ee00123aa0aa30014c40f810c489b70522ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/1bf6ee00123aa0aa30014c40f810c489b70522ca"}],"sha":"ab3b0c2a45057a67135f8df786aca28e58af624a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/ab3b0c2a45057a67135f8df786aca28e58af624a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/67047397?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TusharSharma991","id":67047397,"login":"TusharSharma991","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3MDQ3Mzk3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/1bf6ee00123aa0aa30014c40f810c489b70522ca/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T16:02:41Z","email":"67047397+TusharSharma991@users.noreply.github.com","name":"TusharSharma991"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T16:02:41Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(worker): temporal scheduler never fires under RLS; friendly recurrence UI (#646)\n\n* fix(worker): temporal scheduler never fires under rls; friendly recurrence ui\n\nThe scheduler''s cross-tenant poll (schedulerTick/claimRule) ran under RLS\nwith no app.tenant_id set, so schedule_rules matched zero rows always --\nno schedule rule has ever fired on any RLS-enforced environment. Fixes it\nwith a schedule_sweeper BYPASSRLS role, mirroring the existing\noutbox_sweeper pattern (0064_outbox_sweeper_role.sql).\n\nAlso:\n- isValidTimezone rejected valid IANA aliases (e.g. Asia/Kolkata, which\n  this ICU build canonicalizes as Asia/Calcutta) via strict Set membership\n  against Intl.supportedValuesOf(''timeZone''); now validates via\n  Intl.DateTimeFormat construction, which accepts any valid zone/alias.\n- entity-type-context.tsx silently truncated to page 1 of /entity-types\n  (100/page) instead of paging through every cursor -- any tenant with\n  100+ entity types could have a real type simply missing from the\n  app-wide entityTypes list with no error at all.\n- Schedule-rule admin UI: replaced raw cron-expression input with a\n  plain-language recurrence picker (daily/weekly/monthly/quarterly + time\n  + day), timezone dropdown (Asia/Kolkata first), and a ticket template\n  trimmed to Title/Remark/Due-after-days/Severity to match the fields\n  agents actually use -- the Entity Type picker is hidden and hardcoded to\n  \"ticket\" rather than exposed as a confusing generic concept.\n- fireRule now: defaults assignee to the rule''s creator when the template\n  doesn''t set one, defaults priority/category (required fields with no\n  DB default) so auto-created tickets don''t fail FIELD_VALIDATION_FAILED,\n  computes dueDate from the new template.due_after_days offset, and posts\n  the template''s remark as the ticket''s first comment authored by the\n  rule''s creator.\n\nVerified against a live rule end-to-end (manual QA): fires on schedule,\ncorrect workflow/assignee/due-date/comment.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(worker): add isolation tests for schedule_sweeper role\n\nVerifies the RLS fix from the previous commit against a real Postgres\ninstance: schedule_rules matches zero rows under plain app_user with no\ntenant context (the bug), and schedule_sweeper has exactly SELECT/UPDATE\n(BYPASSRLS, no login, no superuser) with app_user able to assume it.\nMirrors outbox-sweeper-role.isolation.test.ts''s existing pattern.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d678dfb574c9c8fac78dc2c2d173361968a47578","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/trees/d678dfb574c9c8fac78dc2c2d173361968a47578"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/commits/1bf6ee00123aa0aa30014c40f810c489b70522ca","verification":{"payload":"tree d678dfb574c9c8fac78dc2c2d173361968a47578\nparent 66ba6f0292da9a84736d897c216bf8a0020a36b5\nauthor TusharSharma991 <67047397+TusharSharma991@users.noreply.github.com> 1789747361 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789747361 +0530\n\nfix(worker): temporal scheduler never fires under RLS; friendly recurrence UI (#646)\n\n* fix(worker): temporal scheduler never fires under rls; friendly recurrence ui\n\nThe scheduler''s cross-tenant poll (schedulerTick/claimRule) ran under RLS\nwith no app.tenant_id set, so schedule_rules matched zero rows always --\nno schedule rule has ever fired on any RLS-enforced environment. Fixes it\nwith a schedule_sweeper BYPASSRLS role, mirroring the existing\noutbox_sweeper pattern (0064_outbox_sweeper_role.sql).\n\nAlso:\n- isValidTimezone rejected valid IANA aliases (e.g. Asia/Kolkata, which\n  this ICU build canonicalizes as Asia/Calcutta) via strict Set membership\n  against Intl.supportedValuesOf(''timeZone''); now validates via\n  Intl.DateTimeFormat construction, which accepts any valid zone/alias.\n- entity-type-context.tsx silently truncated to page 1 of /entity-types\n  (100/page) instead of paging through every cursor -- any tenant with\n  100+ entity types could have a real type simply missing from the\n  app-wide entityTypes list with no error at all.\n- Schedule-rule admin UI: replaced raw cron-expression input with a\n  plain-language recurrence picker (daily/weekly/monthly/quarterly + time\n  + day), timezone dropdown (Asia/Kolkata first), and a ticket template\n  trimmed to Title/Remark/Due-after-days/Severity to match the fields\n  agents actually use -- the Entity Type picker is hidden and hardcoded to\n  \"ticket\" rather than exposed as a confusing generic concept.\n- fireRule now: defaults assignee to the rule''s creator when the template\n  doesn''t set one, defaults priority/category (required fields with no\n  DB default) so auto-created tickets don''t fail FIELD_VALIDATION_FAILED,\n  computes dueDate from the new template.due_after_days offset, and posts\n  the template''s remark as the ticket''s first comment authored by the\n  rule''s creator.\n\nVerified against a live rule end-to-end (manual QA): fires on schedule,\ncorrect workflow/assignee/due-date/comment.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(worker): add isolation tests for schedule_sweeper role\n\nVerifies the RLS fix from the previous commit against a real Postgres\ninstance: schedule_rules matches zero rows under plain app_user with no\ntenant context (the bug), and schedule_sweeper has exactly SELECT/UPDATE\n(BYPASSRLS, no login, no superuser) with app_user able to assume it.\nMirrors outbox-sweeper-role.isolation.test.ts''s existing pattern.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrWChCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA158QACYjOlvHckrXH2CNCSxy7oRR\nYJDG386WgulMqb532XcDErnzssYa//k+Ow8N6OgzUkp/r30tlY35mwUlugqV82M5\n1uQnRZaFEDeL4VuBmI9V6cHGwwChKCMzoOJg0Yy/vQKQILFNSHPBQNOEmuNVO5gH\nOdHeRxSYwGs4huAKIpINg/tS6phEHBixxuXYw10ThDiTOX8jSIOzGuaZyQ00w9Ia\nxLRPuVBCBagQL5nrDP0JYtllegJan9h8X3JxWUktC1VUJx0M1oQZlfQ9h6f99o4I\n4pkYcwlEIed6u5Xw+IJhgllhpfPNrtlZGIIltnVdmB1I0BbG+iEpWnFuAe3Ym0ji\ncwmQjc5iPOsLd/DxOsFguTzn9uKTiJHrpcW7gpPoLSTP5HivLti/O8uWn1lqvt9o\njjR+uuhMXyl7cNzg2zjkpLPjyKLDy9/840EAOnTv5cpe+2od5+JfWaC2OWojzUdr\nVJhtWJriH3L2senNjzgt2tsvfJYr17MM1a6QGwMNsJgjoaPbCfzo0lD4FykWAcqO\nlRRWZ619Uz+6jACy0z11y656mqsj00JUGM7ZnbhdEC2npCmH3yeemjk8SjY6/z7S\n/J9qE1x0x5rkHv7ID4bcYyeBRo499L7zQso5/RpBCPUO8aRSWo4Hw1gzhy+PNC+2\n7OGvzVeaU/9Oh2rbxQPm\n=zayO\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T16:02:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commit/1bf6ee00123aa0aa30014c40f810c489b70522ca","node_id":"C_kwDOScMdh9oAKDFiZjZlZTAwMTIzYWEwYWEzMDAxNGM0MGY4MTBjNDg5YjcwNTIyY2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commit/66ba6f0292da9a84736d897c216bf8a0020a36b5","sha":"66ba6f0292da9a84736d897c216bf8a0020a36b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/66ba6f0292da9a84736d897c216bf8a0020a36b5"}],"sha":"1bf6ee00123aa0aa30014c40f810c489b70522ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/1bf6ee00123aa0aa30014c40f810c489b70522ca"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3049693?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/abmish","id":3049693,"login":"abmish","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNDk2OTM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/66ba6f0292da9a84736d897c216bf8a0020a36b5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T15:42:50Z","email":"needabhinav@gmail.com","name":"Abhinav Mishra"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T15:42:50Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: correct stale architecture and phase claims in contributor-facing docs (#645)\n\nREADME.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, docs/architecture-brief.md, and docs/local-setup.md\ndescribed a project state that hasn''t been true for months: Phase 1 \"in progress\"\n(actually done since 2026-05-21, with Phase 2 also done since 2026-06-18), S3/MinIO\nfile storage (replaced by local-disk + ClamAV scanning in PR #340), a portal app\nthat no longer has source code (removed in PR #211), and a docker-compose stack\ndescription (MinIO/MailHog, pnpm 9+) that no longer matches docker-compose.yml.\ndocs/local-setup.md''s services table was internally self-contradictory — it still\nlisted MinIO/ow-storage as auto-starting while its own Backup section correctly\nsaid MinIO was decommissioned.\n\nCorrected against the actual current state (roadmap-tracker.md, docker-compose.yml,\npackage.json) rather than assumed: connector/AI feature claims scaled back to what''s\nactually shipped vs. in progress, ADR list extended from 3 to all 17, missing default\ncontainers (ow-worker, ow-clamav) added to the services reference.\n\nNo application code touched — pure documentation accuracy fixes, hence no plan-lock/\nreview pass for this diff (SHIP_BYPASS, logged) per this repo''s own guidance to scale\nprocess to diff size and risk.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6c2c47a98bb311bfa10e1213e9df8cc0ac644ccc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/trees/6c2c47a98bb311bfa10e1213e9df8cc0ac644ccc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/commits/66ba6f0292da9a84736d897c216bf8a0020a36b5","verification":{"payload":"tree 6c2c47a98bb311bfa10e1213e9df8cc0ac644ccc\nparent 0bee19493f8b0e58c29e723c63dbde3a8d82f22d\nauthor Abhinav Mishra <needabhinav@gmail.com> 1789746170 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789746170 +0530\n\ndocs: correct stale architecture and phase claims in contributor-facing docs (#645)\n\nREADME.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, docs/architecture-brief.md, and docs/local-setup.md\ndescribed a project state that hasn''t been true for months: Phase 1 \"in progress\"\n(actually done since 2026-05-21, with Phase 2 also done since 2026-06-18), S3/MinIO\nfile storage (replaced by local-disk + ClamAV scanning in PR #340), a portal app\nthat no longer has source code (removed in PR #211), and a docker-compose stack\ndescription (MinIO/MailHog, pnpm 9+) that no longer matches docker-compose.yml.\ndocs/local-setup.md''s services table was internally self-contradictory — it still\nlisted MinIO/ow-storage as auto-starting while its own Backup section correctly\nsaid MinIO was decommissioned.\n\nCorrected against the actual current state (roadmap-tracker.md, docker-compose.yml,\npackage.json) rather than assumed: connector/AI feature claims scaled back to what''s\nactually shipped vs. in progress, ADR list extended from 3 to all 17, missing default\ncontainers (ow-worker, ow-clamav) added to the services reference.\n\nNo application code touched — pure documentation accuracy fixes, hence no plan-lock/\nreview pass for this diff (SHIP_BYPASS, logged) per this repo''s own guidance to scale\nprocess to diff size and risk.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrVv6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAba4QAFmg9jI9d3FyeFzHcpY094I3\numltA+LsvcZ/pleu+q8ZlrxyEeAU9hP3rrjsJeh51UgN9vKP35SS/KBJohTV/YCY\npnhlP+v2TQESIFWfBsGu/cVLGbftWcqAQqObtZAoBMJ00b6/KPVqRd/NicVGO59y\nqG06QaKp5yA0MIqs4Hueh3bI6y/GNT4smoe6VqTOiN6DUt0OOToij1zhjshWeUh6\naWJCxsRzHccw6wOoSr2WOHQvKKjOzlWYAHgAY5kgB8uDMyOxOx38UAw5ubdLM16y\n+PC++Y2Xs6IzeIZ4aOy9k2eFPPid1mFZJoZYX6Xc8A2Nf4IxxrdDSrDb5pOnFZqm\npHEbPVKeYUJQkj/Ej0Os4TST9CPPObgcO+4qhKlsCdfqmZGPTkUXK0vw8a8PPZKa\nqSh8Bh69goRJhxODZ/hdXKFcwVjxC2rnVFCNC0VMu/ZgJBXKad2xRNkNW60eGrAr\nLG9poLwSOVlY90xYRJbpAOHGvHFUyr2k9vUU4dkfCK8yEMs5x+NgcQnT254bCvFG\nVQSbHX7E297+0Zuz9ZmpWCQvuPKJVIYapE6SF33eI3oCx5LL8bviqc7FYWSJMPqc\nUEW8ZVdbYPyoDcudSIXBDAV7TnowVupMk9W/8zmqXrLkYO6j4L9iBqbGJJF0A8sE\nhp+L1+2eg0+hBtZufODo\n=vhmW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T15:42:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commit/66ba6f0292da9a84736d897c216bf8a0020a36b5","node_id":"C_kwDOScMdh9oAKDY2YmE2ZjAyOTJkYTlhODQ3MzZkODk3YzIxNmJmOGEwMDIwYTM2YjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commit/0bee19493f8b0e58c29e723c63dbde3a8d82f22d","sha":"0bee19493f8b0e58c29e723c63dbde3a8d82f22d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/0bee19493f8b0e58c29e723c63dbde3a8d82f22d"}],"sha":"66ba6f0292da9a84736d897c216bf8a0020a36b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/66ba6f0292da9a84736d897c216bf8a0020a36b5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/67047397?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TusharSharma991","id":67047397,"login":"TusharSharma991","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3MDQ3Mzk3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/0bee19493f8b0e58c29e723c63dbde3a8d82f22d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T09:42:05Z","email":"67047397+TusharSharma991@users.noreply.github.com","name":"TusharSharma991"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T09:42:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(admin-ui): schedule rules admin UI (#624)\n\n* feat(db): add teams, services & on-call schedule data model\n\nLays the data-model foundation for 3E on-call routing: teams, services,\nand on_call_schedules tables (RLS + analytics annotations), the first\nGIST exclusion constraint in this repo (no-overlap invariant on\non_call_schedules windows), and the admin_audit_log CHECK extension for\noncall.* action strings. Adds a new packages/teams package with the\ngeneric, table-agnostic cross-tenant FK validation helper (R1d/T44)\nshared by both the on-call routing and temporal-scheduler tracks, so\nneither reimplements this check separately.\n\ndocs/specs/oncall-routing.md T1-T4, T44 (R1d).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(db): insert real tenant rows in new isolation tests to satisfy fk constraint\n\nteams/services/on_call_schedules.tenant_id all carry a real FK to\ntenants(id) (unlike admin_audit_log''s tenant_id, which has none) -- the\nisolation tests need actual tenant rows inserted before inserting rows\nthat reference them, or the insert fails with a 23503 FK violation.\nCI caught this on PR #583''s Tenant isolation job.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(db): address review blockers on services fk, soft-delete filtering, any type\n\nAddresses PrabhuVijit''s review on PR #583 (4 blockers, several\nnon-blocking improvements):\n\n- services.team_id had a FK contradicting its own migration comment --\n  removed, matching the documented app-layer-only design intent and\n  on_call_schedules'' identical treatment (also resolves the FK asymmetry\n  concern -- both tables now consistently have no DB FK)\n- lookupValidIdsInTable silently validated soft-deleted rows as\n  accessible -- added a required softDeleteColumn param, isNull-filtered\n  when present\n- replaced the any-typed table param with AnyPgTable, removing the\n  eslint-disable\n- added the missing cross-tenant WRITE isolation test for\n  on_call_schedules\n- added created_by NOT NULL to teams/services, matching every other\n  admin-managed resource in the platform\n- added @platform/teams to apps/api''s vitest resolve.alias ahead of\n  Phase 2 need\n- deduped refIds before the batch lookup + added a test\n- explained the write-classification of oncall.no_schedule/\n  skipped_explicit_assignee in the test itself, not just the source\n\nInvestigated and did not apply the reviewer''s suggested vitest.config.ts\nenv-var trim: @platform/config''s schema validates required vars eagerly\non import regardless of whether the importing package uses them --\napps/api/vitest.config.ts already documents this exact constraint for\nits own env block.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(db): use text not uuid for zitadel user-reference columns\n\ncreated_by/primary_user_id/backup_user_id/escalation_manager_user_id\nwere typed uuid, but every other user-reference column in this schema\n(entityInstances.createdBy, tenantUsers.userId, etc.) is text, since\nZitadel JWT sub claims are not guaranteed to be uuid-shaped. Self-caught\nwhile researching PR 2 (ticket_labels.assigned_by needed the same\ncolumn and the inconsistency showed up immediately) -- not a reviewer\nfinding. CI passed on the wrong type only because the test fixtures\nhappened to use uuid-shaped strings, which are also valid text values.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(db): add ticket severity field and labels data model\n\nAdds the second slice of 3E on-call routing''s Phase 1 data model:\n\n- severity system field seeded on the ticket entity type (select,\n  critical/high/medium/low, optional)\n- labels table -- GitHub-style tenant-managed label vocabulary\n  (ADR-016 Decision 3), RLS, unique-per-tenant name, created_by\n- ticket_labels junction table -- composite PK, denormalized tenant_id,\n  hard-delete on removal per spec (history lives in the audit log, not\n  a deleted_at column here)\n- admin_audit_log CHECK extended for label.assigned/label.removed\n\nteam_id/service_id were originally planned for this PR but are\ndeliberately NOT seeded: seeding them as entity_ref fields would be an\nimmediately-reachable bug, not a Phase-2-deferred one -- the existing\ngeneric entity create/update route already accepts arbitrary fields,\nand entity-engine''s validateEntityRefs only resolves refs against\nentity_instances, not plain tables like teams/services. Fixing this\nproperly also hits a real dependency-rule blocker (entity-engine ->\ndb only, per CLAUDE.md -- it cannot import packages/teams as\nstructured). Deferred to a follow-up PR; full writeup in the project''s\nworking docs (open-questions.md).\n\ndocs/specs/oncall-routing.md T5 (severity only), T34-T36.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(db): add notification policies and schedule rules data model\n\nAdds the final Phase 1 data-model slice, covering the last piece of 3E\nplus all of 3F''s schema:\n\n3E half:\n- notification_policies -- severity x team x workflow-type -> channel\n  list, 4 partial unique indexes (one per specificity level, since a\n  composite UNIQUE can''t handle nullable dimension columns). team_id/\n  workflow_type_id have no FK -- app-layer cross-tenant validation only,\n  matching services.team_id (fixed an inconsistency in the design doc,\n  which had kept a FK on team_id here)\n- admin_audit_log extended for notification.dispatched/\n  notification.channel_failed\n\n3F half (temporal scheduler):\n- schedule_rules -- entity_type_id/workflow_id keep a real FK (existence)\n  plus an app-layer tenant check (FK bypasses RLS); the template JSONB''s\n  team_id/assignee_id/service_id are purely app-layer validated (can''t FK\n  into JSONB) -- matches docs/temporal-scheduler-design.md exactly, and\n  resolves an open question from the planning phase since this table\n  isn''t an entity-engine type (no dependency-rule conflict like the\n  ticket fields had)\n- schedule_executions -- append-only, no soft-delete, no UPDATE/DELETE\n  grant to app_user\n- admin_audit_log extended for all 6 schedule.* action strings\n\ndocs/specs/oncall-routing.md T21-T22, docs/specs/temporal-scheduler.md T1-T3.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(db): add channel/cron/template validation constraints + cross-tenant test\n\nAddresses PrabhuVijit''s PR #586 review:\n- B1: notification_policies.channels DB CHECK now validates against the\n  canonical channel set (email/sms/whatsapp/call, R14/R15) instead of only\n  checking non-empty\n- B2: schedule_rules.cron_expr gets a cheap DB-layer field-count CHECK as a\n  backstop; full semantic validation stays at the route layer via\n  cron-parser per the design doc\n- B3: added an isolation test documenting that RLS alone does not catch a\n  cross-tenant team_id smuggled under the caller''s own tenant_id on\n  notification_policies -- app-layer validateCrossTenantRefs is the only\n  guard (tracked in #592)\n- G1: documented that entity_type_id''s FK doesn''t guarantee tenant-module\n  access; tracked in #593 for the Phase 2 route\n- G2: added a template-has-title DB CHECK as a cheap backstop\n- S2: documented why schedule_executions.rule_id uses ON DELETE RESTRICT\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(api): schedule-rules routes (3f phase 2 pr 6)\n\nadds packages/scheduler (cron validation, IANA timezone validation,\nnext_fire_at calculator, {{variable}} whitelist template renderer, shared\ncross-tenant ref validation) and the admin schedule-rules routes.\n\n- packages/scheduler: cron-parser v5-based validateCronExpr/\n  computeNextFireAt/getNextFires (verified against the installed package''s\n  own .d.ts -- v5 replaced v4''s parseExpression function export with\n  CronExpressionParser.parse), cronstrue-based describeCronExpr,\n  Intl.supportedValuesOf-based isValidTimezone (special-cased \"UTC\", which\n  the column''s own DB default uses but supportedValuesOf doesn''t always\n  include depending on ICU/tzdata version), TemplateSchema + renderTemplate\n  (snake_case fields to match the documented cross-system JSON contract),\n  validateScheduleRuleRefs (entity_type_id must resolve to name=''ticket''\n  and tenant-accessible, workflow_id + template team_id/service_id/\n  assignee_id cross-tenant validated via the shared FK helper)\n- GET/POST/PATCH/DELETE /admin/schedule-rules -- admin-only, 422 on invalid\n  cron/timezone/refs, 409 on duplicate active name, status transitions\n  (paused/active/archived) with schedule.rule_paused/resumed/archived audit\n  actions, archived is terminal (409 on un-archive)\n- GET /admin/schedule-rules/:id/executions -- paginated execution history\n- GET /admin/schedule-rules/:id/next-fires?count=N -- dry-run, no DB write\n\nSecurity review caught and fixed one gap before shipping: PATCH''s UPDATE\nstatement was missing an explicit tenant_id filter (relied only on the\nprior SELECT existence check + RLS) -- added, matching the DELETE\nhandler''s existing pattern.\n\ntemplate.fields deep validation against the entity type''s field schema is\ndeferred to the Phase 3 worker''s createEntity call (no public standalone\nvalidateFields export in entity-engine) -- documented in the route file;\nnot reachable through this routes-only PR since no fire-time execution\npath exists yet.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(admin-ui): schedule rules admin ui\n\n- New Schedule Rules list + create/edit form: cron expression with friendly\n  presets, timezone input, entity-type/workflow pickers, ticket template\n  fields (title/description/severity), catchUp toggle, pause/resume/delete.\n- New per-rule detail page: next-fires preview (next 5 fires in the rule''s\n  timezone) and execution history table (status, fired-at, linked ticket,\n  error code).\n- Nav + routing wired, admin-only (matches this router''s all-admin-only\n  surface, including reads).\n\nBranched off feat/PLAT-606-tagsev-3f-schedule-routes (PR #595, unmerged) since\nthat''s where the /admin/schedule-rules API this UI consumes actually lives.\n\ndocs/specs/temporal-scheduler.md T15/T16/T17\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(admin-ui,api): fix next-fires invalid date and schedule-rules patch soft-delete race\n\nVijit review, PR #604:\n\nB1 -- the next-fires preview assumed fires: string[], but the real\nresponse from getNextFires() is { utc, local }[]. Every row rendered\n''Invalid Date'' in production while the test''s mock supplied the wrong\nshape and passed CI regardless. Now reads fireData.fires[].utc, and the\ntest mock matches the real shape with an explicit assertion that no\n''Invalid Date'' text renders.\n\nG1 -- same isNull(deletedAt) gap as PR #595''s PATCH UPDATE WHERE (this\nbranch carries its own copy of schedule-rules.ts, predating that fix):\nthe pre-fetch SELECT guarded against a soft-deleted rule but the UPDATE\ndid not, letting a concurrent soft-delete race let PATCH silently mutate\nan already-deleted row. Same regression test added here as in #595.\n\nG2 -- investigated, does not reproduce against current code: this\ncodebase has no separate super_admin tier. isAdmin is exactly\nroles.includes(''admin''), and SUPER_ADMIN_NAV_EXTRA (SCHEDULE_RULES_NAV''s\narray) is gated on that same isAdmin check -- identical to the backend''s\nrequireRole(''admin''). No nav-visibility mismatch exists to fix.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: PrabhuVijit <prabhu.vijit@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"807a9a00cdc8e3e6b2bf3d7135fde88fc2264ef6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/trees/807a9a00cdc8e3e6b2bf3d7135fde88fc2264ef6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/commits/0bee19493f8b0e58c29e723c63dbde3a8d82f22d","verification":{"payload":"tree 807a9a00cdc8e3e6b2bf3d7135fde88fc2264ef6\nparent b36cc8d4cc21b8f6d0d6c380e10187cb9cda3764\nauthor TusharSharma991 <67047397+TusharSharma991@users.noreply.github.com> 1789724525 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789724525 +0530\n\nfeat(admin-ui): schedule rules admin UI (#624)\n\n* feat(db): add teams, services & on-call schedule data model\n\nLays the data-model foundation for 3E on-call routing: teams, services,\nand on_call_schedules tables (RLS + analytics annotations), the first\nGIST exclusion constraint in this repo (no-overlap invariant on\non_call_schedules windows), and the admin_audit_log CHECK extension for\noncall.* action strings. Adds a new packages/teams package with the\ngeneric, table-agnostic cross-tenant FK validation helper (R1d/T44)\nshared by both the on-call routing and temporal-scheduler tracks, so\nneither reimplements this check separately.\n\ndocs/specs/oncall-routing.md T1-T4, T44 (R1d).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(db): insert real tenant rows in new isolation tests to satisfy fk constraint\n\nteams/services/on_call_schedules.tenant_id all carry a real FK to\ntenants(id) (unlike admin_audit_log''s tenant_id, which has none) -- the\nisolation tests need actual tenant rows inserted before inserting rows\nthat reference them, or the insert fails with a 23503 FK violation.\nCI caught this on PR #583''s Tenant isolation job.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(db): address review blockers on services fk, soft-delete filtering, any type\n\nAddresses PrabhuVijit''s review on PR #583 (4 blockers, several\nnon-blocking improvements):\n\n- services.team_id had a FK contradicting its own migration comment --\n  removed, matching the documented app-layer-only design intent and\n  on_call_schedules'' identical treatment (also resolves the FK asymmetry\n  concern -- both tables now consistently have no DB FK)\n- lookupValidIdsInTable silently validated soft-deleted rows as\n  accessible -- added a required softDeleteColumn param, isNull-filtered\n  when present\n- replaced the any-typed table param with AnyPgTable, removing the\n  eslint-disable\n- added the missing cross-tenant WRITE isolation test for\n  on_call_schedules\n- added created_by NOT NULL to teams/services, matching every other\n  admin-managed resource in the platform\n- added @platform/teams to apps/api''s vitest resolve.alias ahead of\n  Phase 2 need\n- deduped refIds before the batch lookup + added a test\n- explained the write-classification of oncall.no_schedule/\n  skipped_explicit_assignee in the test itself, not just the source\n\nInvestigated and did not apply the reviewer''s suggested vitest.config.ts\nenv-var trim: @platform/config''s schema validates required vars eagerly\non import regardless of whether the importing package uses them --\napps/api/vitest.config.ts already documents this exact constraint for\nits own env block.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(db): use text not uuid for zitadel user-reference columns\n\ncreated_by/primary_user_id/backup_user_id/escalation_manager_user_id\nwere typed uuid, but every other user-reference column in this schema\n(entityInstances.createdBy, tenantUsers.userId, etc.) is text, since\nZitadel JWT sub claims are not guaranteed to be uuid-shaped. Self-caught\nwhile researching PR 2 (ticket_labels.assigned_by needed the same\ncolumn and the inconsistency showed up immediately) -- not a reviewer\nfinding. CI passed on the wrong type only because the test fixtures\nhappened to use uuid-shaped strings, which are also valid text values.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(db): add ticket severity field and labels data model\n\nAdds the second slice of 3E on-call routing''s Phase 1 data model:\n\n- severity system field seeded on the ticket entity type (select,\n  critical/high/medium/low, optional)\n- labels table -- GitHub-style tenant-managed label vocabulary\n  (ADR-016 Decision 3), RLS, unique-per-tenant name, created_by\n- ticket_labels junction table -- composite PK, denormalized tenant_id,\n  hard-delete on removal per spec (history lives in the audit log, not\n  a deleted_at column here)\n- admin_audit_log CHECK extended for label.assigned/label.removed\n\nteam_id/service_id were originally planned for this PR but are\ndeliberately NOT seeded: seeding them as entity_ref fields would be an\nimmediately-reachable bug, not a Phase-2-deferred one -- the existing\ngeneric entity create/update route already accepts arbitrary fields,\nand entity-engine''s validateEntityRefs only resolves refs against\nentity_instances, not plain tables like teams/services. Fixing this\nproperly also hits a real dependency-rule blocker (entity-engine ->\ndb only, per CLAUDE.md -- it cannot import packages/teams as\nstructured). Deferred to a follow-up PR; full writeup in the project''s\nworking docs (open-questions.md).\n\ndocs/specs/oncall-routing.md T5 (severity only), T34-T36.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(db): add notification policies and schedule rules data model\n\nAdds the final Phase 1 data-model slice, covering the last piece of 3E\nplus all of 3F''s schema:\n\n3E half:\n- notification_policies -- severity x team x workflow-type -> channel\n  list, 4 partial unique indexes (one per specificity level, since a\n  composite UNIQUE can''t handle nullable dimension columns). team_id/\n  workflow_type_id have no FK -- app-layer cross-tenant validation only,\n  matching services.team_id (fixed an inconsistency in the design doc,\n  which had kept a FK on team_id here)\n- admin_audit_log extended for notification.dispatched/\n  notification.channel_failed\n\n3F half (temporal scheduler):\n- schedule_rules -- entity_type_id/workflow_id keep a real FK (existence)\n  plus an app-layer tenant check (FK bypasses RLS); the template JSONB''s\n  team_id/assignee_id/service_id are purely app-layer validated (can''t FK\n  into JSONB) -- matches docs/temporal-scheduler-design.md exactly, and\n  resolves an open question from the planning phase since this table\n  isn''t an entity-engine type (no dependency-rule conflict like the\n  ticket fields had)\n- schedule_executions -- append-only, no soft-delete, no UPDATE/DELETE\n  grant to app_user\n- admin_audit_log extended for all 6 schedule.* action strings\n\ndocs/specs/oncall-routing.md T21-T22, docs/specs/temporal-scheduler.md T1-T3.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(db): add channel/cron/template validation constraints + cross-tenant test\n\nAddresses PrabhuVijit''s PR #586 review:\n- B1: notification_policies.channels DB CHECK now validates against the\n  canonical channel set (email/sms/whatsapp/call, R14/R15) instead of only\n  checking non-empty\n- B2: schedule_rules.cron_expr gets a cheap DB-layer field-count CHECK as a\n  backstop; full semantic validation stays at the route layer via\n  cron-parser per the design doc\n- B3: added an isolation test documenting that RLS alone does not catch a\n  cross-tenant team_id smuggled under the caller''s own tenant_id on\n  notification_policies -- app-layer validateCrossTenantRefs is the only\n  guard (tracked in #592)\n- G1: documented that entity_type_id''s FK doesn''t guarantee tenant-module\n  access; tracked in #593 for the Phase 2 route\n- G2: added a template-has-title DB CHECK as a cheap backstop\n- S2: documented why schedule_executions.rule_id uses ON DELETE RESTRICT\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(api): schedule-rules routes (3f phase 2 pr 6)\n\nadds packages/scheduler (cron validation, IANA timezone validation,\nnext_fire_at calculator, {{variable}} whitelist template renderer, shared\ncross-tenant ref validation) and the admin schedule-rules routes.\n\n- packages/scheduler: cron-parser v5-based validateCronExpr/\n  computeNextFireAt/getNextFires (verified against the installed package''s\n  own .d.ts -- v5 replaced v4''s parseExpression function export with\n  CronExpressionParser.parse), cronstrue-based describeCronExpr,\n  Intl.supportedValuesOf-based isValidTimezone (special-cased \"UTC\", which\n  the column''s own DB default uses but supportedValuesOf doesn''t always\n  include depending on ICU/tzdata version), TemplateSchema + renderTemplate\n  (snake_case fields to match the documented cross-system JSON contract),\n  validateScheduleRuleRefs (entity_type_id must resolve to name=''ticket''\n  and tenant-accessible, workflow_id + template team_id/service_id/\n  assignee_id cross-tenant validated via the shared FK helper)\n- GET/POST/PATCH/DELETE /admin/schedule-rules -- admin-only, 422 on invalid\n  cron/timezone/refs, 409 on duplicate active name, status transitions\n  (paused/active/archived) with schedule.rule_paused/resumed/archived audit\n  actions, archived is terminal (409 on un-archive)\n- GET /admin/schedule-rules/:id/executions -- paginated execution history\n- GET /admin/schedule-rules/:id/next-fires?count=N -- dry-run, no DB write\n\nSecurity review caught and fixed one gap before shipping: PATCH''s UPDATE\nstatement was missing an explicit tenant_id filter (relied only on the\nprior SELECT existence check + RLS) -- added, matching the DELETE\nhandler''s existing pattern.\n\ntemplate.fields deep validation against the entity type''s field schema is\ndeferred to the Phase 3 worker''s createEntity call (no public standalone\nvalidateFields export in entity-engine) -- documented in the route file;\nnot reachable through this routes-only PR since no fire-time execution\npath exists yet.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(admin-ui): schedule rules admin ui\n\n- New Schedule Rules list + create/edit form: cron expression with friendly\n  presets, timezone input, entity-type/workflow pickers, ticket template\n  fields (title/description/severity), catchUp toggle, pause/resume/delete.\n- New per-rule detail page: next-fires preview (next 5 fires in the rule''s\n  timezone) and execution history table (status, fired-at, linked ticket,\n  error code).\n- Nav + routing wired, admin-only (matches this router''s all-admin-only\n  surface, including reads).\n\nBranched off feat/PLAT-606-tagsev-3f-schedule-routes (PR #595, unmerged) since\nthat''s where the /admin/schedule-rules API this UI consumes actually lives.\n\ndocs/specs/temporal-scheduler.md T15/T16/T17\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(admin-ui,api): fix next-fires invalid date and schedule-rules patch soft-delete race\n\nVijit review, PR #604:\n\nB1 -- the next-fires preview assumed fires: string[], but the real\nresponse from getNextFires() is { utc, local }[]. Every row rendered\n''Invalid Date'' in production while the test''s mock supplied the wrong\nshape and passed CI regardless. Now reads fireData.fires[].utc, and the\ntest mock matches the real shape with an explicit assertion that no\n''Invalid Date'' text renders.\n\nG1 -- same isNull(deletedAt) gap as PR #595''s PATCH UPDATE WHERE (this\nbranch carries its own copy of schedule-rules.ts, predating that fix):\nthe pre-fetch SELECT guarded against a soft-deleted rule but the UPDATE\ndid not, letting a concurrent soft-delete race let PATCH silently mutate\nan already-deleted row. Same regression test added here as in #595.\n\nG2 -- investigated, does not reproduce against current code: this\ncodebase has no separate super_admin tier. isAdmin is exactly\nroles.includes(''admin''), and SUPER_ADMIN_NAV_EXTRA (SCHEDULE_RULES_NAV''s\narray) is gated on that same isAdmin check -- identical to the backend''s\nrequireRole(''admin''). No nav-visibility mismatch exists to fix.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: PrabhuVijit <prabhu.vijit@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrQdtCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVhYQAI9G7u3DaCcbrwYXu9Q6Q6I+\nb2d4bJHl4jCWl33tvcf6o0t3nmpylly1EIuvWFM1T5+ARELe/OuMIcYvwEXl1zyl\njUuJ+zIw5r3IX42haBSKSs/RJ0f31PtKKzicc6CbWPlMb8kzvMRq6LwtSXbTljKv\nFiiJ8vhvoO/TJ10BCVcl6lZILK7T5kEl+ME44Kw3IiHOU4tsWKtTMt5iu16tlF++\ntJmSzP136znRrAUEeVEEVd/SE526gWLkasigAv/APjMXKn/Iy6nc/L4wV5/8OvEa\nt7mhccPvMB7clAVL+5I+ohVwG5F2TMkV3FwrzS1/iD5S3uPbegC4xT467X8emt+c\ns7wCrE9oLYqetnYjUAr6WqOmR2jwIk7ClQia6kGzaqQvV/c4NsaEdAk6J82ybsnT\n1DBIRWPqMXz6cOKXwLGXgb7BjAUENQGHIC1vIgDLIp3fGyNGng/uLBwOM3WePwSF\nVQCdB6TP+NBLS4dv2NquHtE5tRntY1O2ZrN6McsjnTOAaiVLtNebNDpxtohnsT+A\noB+GGsmu03zAGwpKo+82c8abCAJJIKMiIrQnr7AkU5o8T/s5g6jYCZlMHzDMIzew\n6Shpp8EqBAHrMS5Oir7NkgEVsKgCxJ5H3Ba0qFp0cCIv6XrlLPiuJIhRzogwlsig\ndnhPZKxGRPqs0l2vCJBt\n=9r2Q\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T09:42:06Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commit/0bee19493f8b0e58c29e723c63dbde3a8d82f22d","node_id":"C_kwDOScMdh9oAKDBiZWUxOTQ5M2Y4YjBlNThjMjllNzIzYzYzZGJkZTNhOGQ4MmYyMmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commit/b36cc8d4cc21b8f6d0d6c380e10187cb9cda3764","sha":"b36cc8d4cc21b8f6d0d6c380e10187cb9cda3764","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/b36cc8d4cc21b8f6d0d6c380e10187cb9cda3764"}],"sha":"0bee19493f8b0e58c29e723c63dbde3a8d82f22d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/0bee19493f8b0e58c29e723c63dbde3a8d82f22d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","id":49699333,"login":"dependabot[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/b36cc8d4cc21b8f6d0d6c380e10187cb9cda3764/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T08:45:56Z","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"dependabot[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T08:45:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(deps): bump hono from 4.12.34 to 4.13.5 (#625)\n\nBumps [hono](https://github.com/honojs/hono) from 4.12.34 to 4.13.5.\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/honojs/hono/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/honojs/hono/compare/v4.12.34...v4.13.5)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: hono\n  dependency-version: 4.13.5\n  dependency-type: direct:production\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"50b75193d938d9dcf0aaa1f2ec6931bcfcc52ab3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/trees/50b75193d938d9dcf0aaa1f2ec6931bcfcc52ab3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/commits/b36cc8d4cc21b8f6d0d6c380e10187cb9cda3764","verification":{"payload":"tree 50b75193d938d9dcf0aaa1f2ec6931bcfcc52ab3\nparent ce3cf494901c82f44cb16df1a9ae13df3b7a7a0e\nauthor dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1789721156 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789721156 +0530\n\nchore(deps): bump hono from 4.12.34 to 4.13.5 (#625)\n\nBumps [hono](https://github.com/honojs/hono) from 4.12.34 to 4.13.5.\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/honojs/hono/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/honojs/hono/compare/v4.12.34...v4.13.5)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: hono\n  dependency-version: 4.13.5\n  dependency-type: direct:production\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrPpECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQHMQABYH8jvX7y5hMwnXp8QmnR5/\n5MF8OC2F10NLABSkmEIzRwHN+9cuE983uWPz6w7kp92e/eroipGQU11TnVNNtWG9\nKimOpDIKZd1hnomjlVeXzxJzjXy/wow0NH7Fx/CTkVv+3kEKfHUSZohXrDIYg3sQ\nS1qHBum3/crR+OtdHXfYtVBZKV1ZTEaTcNgXGlCEhLg6+voF2atnMnX8bgs6F34C\nqR6ssmdJXEIxUzjUFbulHQsPv6ymFuYP0H38OZoATHMk1b4CMS+sTYIuXp02aNbb\nxahpoZ7MObplrQWNXXOX6RWDm9Dcmaxkc943Y0wFv4mpZjtbrsypsk70a+f/Ss6g\nFNyrIEUhK+bkCnjxCqsPfBFmg6FVB3rYBerRgHmLkvw6KDEk7i/MsCpM9s+j4XZi\nb97/A04ttf+RAcxh5nHRFxCj4vieFuDS+w80/4dc0eOjkSfNduz3Ee/lCOjmuda4\nYQPVnPAQkqwCh2U6zgBH6fh4n0zjHpi8e8axkePEVZKBXerpV/mUXgsB/UU3jXAG\n/kOEeVl7GEbvSfeW0DbNVXWfl6BfnU7FRJdXzoA1Dmo3lhl8lxgCn5q1B4zFjsBG\nSah6YVxpYR8wgY3iUKdQK1LLR9bjuYDDzqN/qXLsml95eMHaqhchF9zgXRRRV+SY\nUoUhfvfzSmuky8ZT309h\n=vrzO\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T08:45:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commit/b36cc8d4cc21b8f6d0d6c380e10187cb9cda3764","node_id":"C_kwDOScMdh9oAKGIzNmNjOGQ0Y2MyMWI4ZjZkMGQ2YzM4MGUxMDE4N2NiOWNkYTM3NjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commit/ce3cf494901c82f44cb16df1a9ae13df3b7a7a0e","sha":"ce3cf494901c82f44cb16df1a9ae13df3b7a7a0e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/ce3cf494901c82f44cb16df1a9ae13df3b7a7a0e"}],"sha":"b36cc8d4cc21b8f6d0d6c380e10187cb9cda3764","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/b36cc8d4cc21b8f6d0d6c380e10187cb9cda3764"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/67047397?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/TusharSharma991","id":67047397,"login":"TusharSharma991","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3MDQ3Mzk3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TusharSharma991","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/ce3cf494901c82f44cb16df1a9ae13df3b7a7a0e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T02:03:33Z","email":"67047397+TusharSharma991@users.noreply.github.com","name":"TusharSharma991"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T02:03:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(dx): on-call routing Grafana dashboard + Prometheus alerts (#605)\n\n* feat(db): add teams, services & on-call schedule data model\n\nLays the data-model foundation for 3E on-call routing: teams, services,\nand on_call_schedules tables (RLS + analytics annotations), the first\nGIST exclusion constraint in this repo (no-overlap invariant on\non_call_schedules windows), and the admin_audit_log CHECK extension for\noncall.* action strings. Adds a new packages/teams package with the\ngeneric, table-agnostic cross-tenant FK validation helper (R1d/T44)\nshared by both the on-call routing and temporal-scheduler tracks, so\nneither reimplements this check separately.\n\ndocs/specs/oncall-routing.md T1-T4, T44 (R1d).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(db): insert real tenant rows in new isolation tests to satisfy fk constraint\n\nteams/services/on_call_schedules.tenant_id all carry a real FK to\ntenants(id) (unlike admin_audit_log''s tenant_id, which has none) -- the\nisolation tests need actual tenant rows inserted before inserting rows\nthat reference them, or the insert fails with a 23503 FK violation.\nCI caught this on PR #583''s Tenant isolation job.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(db): address review blockers on services fk, soft-delete filtering, any type\n\nAddresses PrabhuVijit''s review on PR #583 (4 blockers, several\nnon-blocking improvements):\n\n- services.team_id had a FK contradicting its own migration comment --\n  removed, matching the documented app-layer-only design intent and\n  on_call_schedules'' identical treatment (also resolves the FK asymmetry\n  concern -- both tables now consistently have no DB FK)\n- lookupValidIdsInTable silently validated soft-deleted rows as\n  accessible -- added a required softDeleteColumn param, isNull-filtered\n  when present\n- replaced the any-typed table param with AnyPgTable, removing the\n  eslint-disable\n- added the missing cross-tenant WRITE isolation test for\n  on_call_schedules\n- added created_by NOT NULL to teams/services, matching every other\n  admin-managed resource in the platform\n- added @platform/teams to apps/api''s vitest resolve.alias ahead of\n  Phase 2 need\n- deduped refIds before the batch lookup + added a test\n- explained the write-classification of oncall.no_schedule/\n  skipped_explicit_assignee in the test itself, not just the source\n\nInvestigated and did not apply the reviewer''s suggested vitest.config.ts\nenv-var trim: @platform/config''s schema validates required vars eagerly\non import regardless of whether the importing package uses them --\napps/api/vitest.config.ts already documents this exact constraint for\nits own env block.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(db): use text not uuid for zitadel user-reference columns\n\ncreated_by/primary_user_id/backup_user_id/escalation_manager_user_id\nwere typed uuid, but every other user-reference column in this schema\n(entityInstances.createdBy, tenantUsers.userId, etc.) is text, since\nZitadel JWT sub claims are not guaranteed to be uuid-shaped. Self-caught\nwhile researching PR 2 (ticket_labels.assigned_by needed the same\ncolumn and the inconsistency showed up immediately) -- not a reviewer\nfinding. CI passed on the wrong type only because the test fixtures\nhappened to use uuid-shaped strings, which are also valid text values.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(db): add ticket severity field and labels data model\n\nAdds the second slice of 3E on-call routing''s Phase 1 data model:\n\n- severity system field seeded on the ticket entity type (select,\n  critical/high/medium/low, optional)\n- labels table -- GitHub-style tenant-managed label vocabulary\n  (ADR-016 Decision 3), RLS, unique-per-tenant name, created_by\n- ticket_labels junction table -- composite PK, denormalized tenant_id,\n  hard-delete on removal per spec (history lives in the audit log, not\n  a deleted_at column here)\n- admin_audit_log CHECK extended for label.assigned/label.removed\n\nteam_id/service_id were originally planned for this PR but are\ndeliberately NOT seeded: seeding them as entity_ref fields would be an\nimmediately-reachable bug, not a Phase-2-deferred one -- the existing\ngeneric entity create/update route already accepts arbitrary fields,\nand entity-engine''s validateEntityRefs only resolves refs against\nentity_instances, not plain tables like teams/services. Fixing this\nproperly also hits a real dependency-rule blocker (entity-engine ->\ndb only, per CLAUDE.md -- it cannot import packages/teams as\nstructured). Deferred to a follow-up PR; full writeup in the project''s\nworking docs (open-questions.md).\n\ndocs/specs/oncall-routing.md T5 (severity only), T34-T36.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(db): add notification policies and schedule rules data model\n\nAdds the final Phase 1 data-model slice, covering the last piece of 3E\nplus all of 3F''s schema:\n\n3E half:\n- notification_policies -- severity x team x workflow-type -> channel\n  list, 4 partial unique indexes (one per specificity level, since a\n  composite UNIQUE can''t handle nullable dimension columns). team_id/\n  workflow_type_id have no FK -- app-layer cross-tenant validation only,\n  matching services.team_id (fixed an inconsistency in the design doc,\n  which had kept a FK on team_id here)\n- admin_audit_log extended for notification.dispatched/\n  notification.channel_failed\n\n3F half (temporal scheduler):\n- schedule_rules -- entity_type_id/workflow_id keep a real FK (existence)\n  plus an app-layer tenant check (FK bypasses RLS); the template JSONB''s\n  team_id/assignee_id/service_id are purely app-layer validated (can''t FK\n  into JSONB) -- matches docs/temporal-scheduler-design.md exactly, and\n  resolves an open question from the planning phase since this table\n  isn''t an entity-engine type (no dependency-rule conflict like the\n  ticket fields had)\n- schedule_executions -- append-only, no soft-delete, no UPDATE/DELETE\n  grant to app_user\n- admin_audit_log extended for all 6 schedule.* action strings\n\ndocs/specs/oncall-routing.md T21-T22, docs/specs/temporal-scheduler.md T1-T3.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(api): add teams, services and on-call-schedules admin routes\n\nPhase 2 API layer for 3E on-call routing:\n\n- GET/POST/PATCH/DELETE /admin/teams -- cursor pagination, admin-only\n  write, agent+admin read, 409 on duplicate name\n- GET/POST/PATCH/DELETE /admin/services -- same shape, team_id\n  cross-tenant validated via packages/teams'' shared helper (422 on\n  invalid ref)\n- GET/POST/PATCH/DELETE /admin/on-call-schedules -- overlap validation\n  (409 via the GIST exclusion constraint), PATCH blocked on\n  already-started windows (422 per R5), team_id/primary_user_id/\n  backup_user_id/escalation_manager_user_id validated cross-tenant\n- GET /admin/on-call-schedules/current -- active on-call snapshot per\n  team, LEFT JOIN semantics (uncovered teams show oncall: null, not\n  omitted), soft-deleted teams excluded, soft-deleted/unresolvable user\n  references surfaced with reason: referenced_user_deleted\n\nRan through /security-review before landing -- 2 findings, both fixed:\ncross-tenant ref validation was running against the raw db client\n(bypassing RLS as a second defense layer, relying solely on the\nexplicit tenantId filter already inside lookupValidIdsInTable); moved\nvalidation inside withTenantContext so it runs under the same\nRLS-enforcing transaction as the write it guards. Cursor-pagination\nsub-queries looked up the cursor row by id alone with no tenant_id\nfilter -- added it to all three list endpoints.\n\n@platform/teams added as an apps/api dependency; packages/teams built\nso tsc can resolve its published types.\n\ndocs/specs/oncall-routing.md T6-T11.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(api): add patch /admin/teams rename-conflict test\n\nCloses a CodeQL \"useless conditional\" finding on teams.test.ts —\nupdateShouldConflict was declared and checked but never set to true.\nAdds the missing PATCH-rename-to-duplicate-name coverage (R3) instead\nof just deleting the dead flag.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(api): audit trail, cursor pagination tiebreaker, n+1 fix on admin routes\n\nAddresses PrabhuVijit''s PR #590 review (B1 answered with evidence, not\nimplemented -- see PR comment: no per-handler OTel span pattern exists\nanywhere in this codebase; these routes already get the same global\ntelemetry() middleware + OTel auto-instrumentation as every other route):\n\n- B2: all 12 mutating handlers across teams/services/on-call-schedules now\n  write an audit entry inside the same withTenantContext transaction as the\n  mutation, reusing the existing created/updated/deleted actions\n- B3: cursor pagination now uses id as an explicit tiebreaker alongside\n  createdAt/startsAt in both ORDER BY and the cursor condition -- same-\n  instant inserts could otherwise be silently skipped\n- B4: validateScheduleRefs'' user-ref check now goes through\n  lookupValidIdsInTable (scoped to the specific ids being validated)\n  instead of scanning the entire tenant_users table\n- G1: added GET /:id for teams, services, and on-call-schedules\n- G2: /current''s user lookup now filters by inArray(...) instead of\n  scanning the whole tenant\n- S2: teams.ts''s POST now guards against an empty .returning() the same\n  way PATCH/DELETE already did\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(api): resolve_oncall automation action (on-call auto-assign + cascade)\n\nImplements PR 7 of the 3E on-call routing track: a new resolve_oncall\nautomation-engine action that auto-assigns tickets via the primary ->\nbackup -> escalation cascade (R8b), skipping any tier whose user is\nunresolvable, with explicit-assignee-wins (R10), idempotent re-delivery\n(R11), fail-open coverage-gap parity for both \"no schedule\" and\n\"cascade exhausted\" (R9/R8b), a backup on-call notification, full\naudit trail with assignedTier metadata, and openwind_oncall_* metrics.\n\nRequired wiring entity.updated into the automation engine for the first\ntime (new trigger type, event schema with a field-diff `changed` map,\noutbox-poller allowlist entry) since no prior action needed to react to\n\"which field changed\". Also extends automation-engine''s allowed\ndependencies to packages/teams and packages/audit (CLAUDE.md) so the\ncascade can reuse the same schedule-resolution helper as the\non-call-schedules /current route, and write oncall.* audit entries\ndirectly -- both confirmed with the user as deliberate DAG extensions,\nnot violations (teams and audit each depend only on db).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(docs): prettier formatting fix in oncall-routing.md task table\n\nCI''s Quality gates job failed prettier --check on the T39 task-table row\nadded in the resolve_oncall PR (escaped-underscore spacing). No content\nchange, formatting only.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(api): insert tenant_users rows in resolve_oncall isolation test\n\nCI caught the real failure the isolation test itself was written to\ncatch: without a tenant_users row for USER_A/USER_B, isUserResolvable\ncorrectly treats both as unresolvable, so the cascade exhausts (R8b\nfail-open) instead of assigning -- the test asserted the assignment\nhappened, but its own fixture never made that possible.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(db): extend notifications_type_check for oncall.backup_tagged\n\nFound via live manual testing against a real (non-mocked) Postgres\ndatabase, not CI: packages/automation-engine/src/actions/\nresolve-oncall.ts inserts a notifications row with\ntype = ''oncall.backup_tagged'' for the backup on-call notification, but\nthe CHECK constraint was never extended for it. Same lesson migration\n0066 already documents -- a CHECK constraint enum is invisible to a\nmocked-DB unit test (resolve-oncall.test.ts mocks @platform/db\nentirely) -- but worse here: the notification insert runs inside the\nSAME transaction as the ticket assignment, so the constraint violation\nrolled back the entire rule execution, silently undoing the\nauto-assignment and its audit entry too, every time a backup\nnotification was attempted.\n\nVerified against an isolated scratch database (not the shared local\ndev DB): cascade fallback to backup, cascade fallback to escalation\nwith the backup notification actually landing in the table, and\nexplicit-assignee-wins all now pass end-to-end.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(automation-engine): dispatch_severity_notification action for ticket severity changes\n\nResolves the matching notification policy (specificity-scored: team+workflow\n> team > workflow > global > hardcoded email-only default) and dispatches to\nthe assignee, backup, and escalation manager (per-policy flags, or always for\ncritical severity). One notifications row per (channel, recipient) pair so\nper-channel dispatch failures are isolated and independently auditable.\n\n- packages/automation-engine: new action, wired into executor/types\n- packages/db: migration 0105 adds notifications.channel + the\n  ticket.severity_notification type\n- modules/helpdesk: automation rule seed (entity.created + entity.updated)\n- packages/telemetry: openwind_notification_dispatch_total counter\n- docs/local-setup.md: Novu per-channel wiring notes (email wired today;\n  sms/whatsapp/call pending the outbound worker''s provider contract)\n- isolation test verifies Tenant B''s policy/schedule never affects Tenant A''s\n  dispatch\n\n* feat(dx): on-call routing grafana dashboard + prometheus alerts\n\n- 3 new Grafana panels (On-Call Resolution Rate, Notification Channel Success\n  Rate, Coverage Gaps live), scoped to the 3 of 6 design-doc metrics that are\n  actually registered on any branch today (T39 partially done).\n- 2 new Prometheus alerts (OncallCoverageGapsDetected,\n  NotificationChannelHighFailureRate) added to the existing openwind-alerts\n  group; fixed two PromQL bugs found in review (unaggregated ratio division,\n  cross-tenant sum masking per-tenant gaps).\n- Extended observability-config.test.ts to cover the new panels/alerts.\n\nThe remaining 3 design-doc panels + 1 alert (needing 2 histograms + a\npolicy-match counter that were never registered) are documented as follow-up\nin the week-log entry, not silently dropped.\n\nBranched off feat/PLAT-608-tagsev-3e-dispatch-severity-notification (PR #600,\nunmerged) since that branch has the most complete metric set available.\n\ndocs/oncall-routing-design.md T42/T43\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(dx): correct label names in oncall/notification alerts and dashboard\n\nalert.rules.yml and openwind-dashboard.json queried result=/tenant_hash\nlabels that no metric emits (packages/telemetry/src/metrics.ts uses\noutcome/tenant_id) -- NotificationChannelHighFailureRate could never fire\nand the success-rate/resolution-rate/coverage-gap panels always showed\n0%/blank regardless of real data (Vijit review, PR #605 B1/B2/G1/G2).\n\n* fix(automation-engine): guard optional event.changed in severity dispatch\n\nEntityUpdatedV1Schema''s changed field became optional in PR #597 (B1) --\napply the same missing-changed no-op guard to\ndispatch-severity-notification.ts that resolve-oncall.ts already carries,\nsince both actions consume the same entity.updated event shape.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Vijit Prabhu <prabhu.vijit@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"d19af885f51d31a3c8cc1d26fd68188503625176","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/trees/d19af885f51d31a3c8cc1d26fd68188503625176"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/commits/ce3cf494901c82f44cb16df1a9ae13df3b7a7a0e","verification":{"payload":"tree d19af885f51d31a3c8cc1d26fd68188503625176\nparent 94fbaa210416535b8c2fe62b75799538bab5398a\nauthor TusharSharma991 <67047397+TusharSharma991@users.noreply.github.com> 1789697013 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789697013 +0530\n\nfeat(dx): on-call routing Grafana dashboard + Prometheus alerts (#605)\n\n* feat(db): add teams, services & on-call schedule data model\n\nLays the data-model foundation for 3E on-call routing: teams, services,\nand on_call_schedules tables (RLS + analytics annotations), the first\nGIST exclusion constraint in this repo (no-overlap invariant on\non_call_schedules windows), and the admin_audit_log CHECK extension for\noncall.* action strings. Adds a new packages/teams package with the\ngeneric, table-agnostic cross-tenant FK validation helper (R1d/T44)\nshared by both the on-call routing and temporal-scheduler tracks, so\nneither reimplements this check separately.\n\ndocs/specs/oncall-routing.md T1-T4, T44 (R1d).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(db): insert real tenant rows in new isolation tests to satisfy fk constraint\n\nteams/services/on_call_schedules.tenant_id all carry a real FK to\ntenants(id) (unlike admin_audit_log''s tenant_id, which has none) -- the\nisolation tests need actual tenant rows inserted before inserting rows\nthat reference them, or the insert fails with a 23503 FK violation.\nCI caught this on PR #583''s Tenant isolation job.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(db): address review blockers on services fk, soft-delete filtering, any type\n\nAddresses PrabhuVijit''s review on PR #583 (4 blockers, several\nnon-blocking improvements):\n\n- services.team_id had a FK contradicting its own migration comment --\n  removed, matching the documented app-layer-only design intent and\n  on_call_schedules'' identical treatment (also resolves the FK asymmetry\n  concern -- both tables now consistently have no DB FK)\n- lookupValidIdsInTable silently validated soft-deleted rows as\n  accessible -- added a required softDeleteColumn param, isNull-filtered\n  when present\n- replaced the any-typed table param with AnyPgTable, removing the\n  eslint-disable\n- added the missing cross-tenant WRITE isolation test for\n  on_call_schedules\n- added created_by NOT NULL to teams/services, matching every other\n  admin-managed resource in the platform\n- added @platform/teams to apps/api''s vitest resolve.alias ahead of\n  Phase 2 need\n- deduped refIds before the batch lookup + added a test\n- explained the write-classification of oncall.no_schedule/\n  skipped_explicit_assignee in the test itself, not just the source\n\nInvestigated and did not apply the reviewer''s suggested vitest.config.ts\nenv-var trim: @platform/config''s schema validates required vars eagerly\non import regardless of whether the importing package uses them --\napps/api/vitest.config.ts already documents this exact constraint for\nits own env block.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(db): use text not uuid for zitadel user-reference columns\n\ncreated_by/primary_user_id/backup_user_id/escalation_manager_user_id\nwere typed uuid, but every other user-reference column in this schema\n(entityInstances.createdBy, tenantUsers.userId, etc.) is text, since\nZitadel JWT sub claims are not guaranteed to be uuid-shaped. Self-caught\nwhile researching PR 2 (ticket_labels.assigned_by needed the same\ncolumn and the inconsistency showed up immediately) -- not a reviewer\nfinding. CI passed on the wrong type only because the test fixtures\nhappened to use uuid-shaped strings, which are also valid text values.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(db): add ticket severity field and labels data model\n\nAdds the second slice of 3E on-call routing''s Phase 1 data model:\n\n- severity system field seeded on the ticket entity type (select,\n  critical/high/medium/low, optional)\n- labels table -- GitHub-style tenant-managed label vocabulary\n  (ADR-016 Decision 3), RLS, unique-per-tenant name, created_by\n- ticket_labels junction table -- composite PK, denormalized tenant_id,\n  hard-delete on removal per spec (history lives in the audit log, not\n  a deleted_at column here)\n- admin_audit_log CHECK extended for label.assigned/label.removed\n\nteam_id/service_id were originally planned for this PR but are\ndeliberately NOT seeded: seeding them as entity_ref fields would be an\nimmediately-reachable bug, not a Phase-2-deferred one -- the existing\ngeneric entity create/update route already accepts arbitrary fields,\nand entity-engine''s validateEntityRefs only resolves refs against\nentity_instances, not plain tables like teams/services. Fixing this\nproperly also hits a real dependency-rule blocker (entity-engine ->\ndb only, per CLAUDE.md -- it cannot import packages/teams as\nstructured). Deferred to a follow-up PR; full writeup in the project''s\nworking docs (open-questions.md).\n\ndocs/specs/oncall-routing.md T5 (severity only), T34-T36.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(db): add notification policies and schedule rules data model\n\nAdds the final Phase 1 data-model slice, covering the last piece of 3E\nplus all of 3F''s schema:\n\n3E half:\n- notification_policies -- severity x team x workflow-type -> channel\n  list, 4 partial unique indexes (one per specificity level, since a\n  composite UNIQUE can''t handle nullable dimension columns). team_id/\n  workflow_type_id have no FK -- app-layer cross-tenant validation only,\n  matching services.team_id (fixed an inconsistency in the design doc,\n  which had kept a FK on team_id here)\n- admin_audit_log extended for notification.dispatched/\n  notification.channel_failed\n\n3F half (temporal scheduler):\n- schedule_rules -- entity_type_id/workflow_id keep a real FK (existence)\n  plus an app-layer tenant check (FK bypasses RLS); the template JSONB''s\n  team_id/assignee_id/service_id are purely app-layer validated (can''t FK\n  into JSONB) -- matches docs/temporal-scheduler-design.md exactly, and\n  resolves an open question from the planning phase since this table\n  isn''t an entity-engine type (no dependency-rule conflict like the\n  ticket fields had)\n- schedule_executions -- append-only, no soft-delete, no UPDATE/DELETE\n  grant to app_user\n- admin_audit_log extended for all 6 schedule.* action strings\n\ndocs/specs/oncall-routing.md T21-T22, docs/specs/temporal-scheduler.md T1-T3.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(api): add teams, services and on-call-schedules admin routes\n\nPhase 2 API layer for 3E on-call routing:\n\n- GET/POST/PATCH/DELETE /admin/teams -- cursor pagination, admin-only\n  write, agent+admin read, 409 on duplicate name\n- GET/POST/PATCH/DELETE /admin/services -- same shape, team_id\n  cross-tenant validated via packages/teams'' shared helper (422 on\n  invalid ref)\n- GET/POST/PATCH/DELETE /admin/on-call-schedules -- overlap validation\n  (409 via the GIST exclusion constraint), PATCH blocked on\n  already-started windows (422 per R5), team_id/primary_user_id/\n  backup_user_id/escalation_manager_user_id validated cross-tenant\n- GET /admin/on-call-schedules/current -- active on-call snapshot per\n  team, LEFT JOIN semantics (uncovered teams show oncall: null, not\n  omitted), soft-deleted teams excluded, soft-deleted/unresolvable user\n  references surfaced with reason: referenced_user_deleted\n\nRan through /security-review before landing -- 2 findings, both fixed:\ncross-tenant ref validation was running against the raw db client\n(bypassing RLS as a second defense layer, relying solely on the\nexplicit tenantId filter already inside lookupValidIdsInTable); moved\nvalidation inside withTenantContext so it runs under the same\nRLS-enforcing transaction as the write it guards. Cursor-pagination\nsub-queries looked up the cursor row by id alone with no tenant_id\nfilter -- added it to all three list endpoints.\n\n@platform/teams added as an apps/api dependency; packages/teams built\nso tsc can resolve its published types.\n\ndocs/specs/oncall-routing.md T6-T11.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(api): add patch /admin/teams rename-conflict test\n\nCloses a CodeQL \"useless conditional\" finding on teams.test.ts —\nupdateShouldConflict was declared and checked but never set to true.\nAdds the missing PATCH-rename-to-duplicate-name coverage (R3) instead\nof just deleting the dead flag.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(api): audit trail, cursor pagination tiebreaker, n+1 fix on admin routes\n\nAddresses PrabhuVijit''s PR #590 review (B1 answered with evidence, not\nimplemented -- see PR comment: no per-handler OTel span pattern exists\nanywhere in this codebase; these routes already get the same global\ntelemetry() middleware + OTel auto-instrumentation as every other route):\n\n- B2: all 12 mutating handlers across teams/services/on-call-schedules now\n  write an audit entry inside the same withTenantContext transaction as the\n  mutation, reusing the existing created/updated/deleted actions\n- B3: cursor pagination now uses id as an explicit tiebreaker alongside\n  createdAt/startsAt in both ORDER BY and the cursor condition -- same-\n  instant inserts could otherwise be silently skipped\n- B4: validateScheduleRefs'' user-ref check now goes through\n  lookupValidIdsInTable (scoped to the specific ids being validated)\n  instead of scanning the entire tenant_users table\n- G1: added GET /:id for teams, services, and on-call-schedules\n- G2: /current''s user lookup now filters by inArray(...) instead of\n  scanning the whole tenant\n- S2: teams.ts''s POST now guards against an empty .returning() the same\n  way PATCH/DELETE already did\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(api): resolve_oncall automation action (on-call auto-assign + cascade)\n\nImplements PR 7 of the 3E on-call routing track: a new resolve_oncall\nautomation-engine action that auto-assigns tickets via the primary ->\nbackup -> escalation cascade (R8b), skipping any tier whose user is\nunresolvable, with explicit-assignee-wins (R10), idempotent re-delivery\n(R11), fail-open coverage-gap parity for both \"no schedule\" and\n\"cascade exhausted\" (R9/R8b), a backup on-call notification, full\naudit trail with assignedTier metadata, and openwind_oncall_* metrics.\n\nRequired wiring entity.updated into the automation engine for the first\ntime (new trigger type, event schema with a field-diff `changed` map,\noutbox-poller allowlist entry) since no prior action needed to react to\n\"which field changed\". Also extends automation-engine''s allowed\ndependencies to packages/teams and packages/audit (CLAUDE.md) so the\ncascade can reuse the same schedule-resolution helper as the\non-call-schedules /current route, and write oncall.* audit entries\ndirectly -- both confirmed with the user as deliberate DAG extensions,\nnot violations (teams and audit each depend only on db).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(docs): prettier formatting fix in oncall-routing.md task table\n\nCI''s Quality gates job failed prettier --check on the T39 task-table row\nadded in the resolve_oncall PR (escaped-underscore spacing). No content\nchange, formatting only.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(api): insert tenant_users rows in resolve_oncall isolation test\n\nCI caught the real failure the isolation test itself was written to\ncatch: without a tenant_users row for USER_A/USER_B, isUserResolvable\ncorrectly treats both as unresolvable, so the cascade exhausts (R8b\nfail-open) instead of assigning -- the test asserted the assignment\nhappened, but its own fixture never made that possible.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(db): extend notifications_type_check for oncall.backup_tagged\n\nFound via live manual testing against a real (non-mocked) Postgres\ndatabase, not CI: packages/automation-engine/src/actions/\nresolve-oncall.ts inserts a notifications row with\ntype = ''oncall.backup_tagged'' for the backup on-call notification, but\nthe CHECK constraint was never extended for it. Same lesson migration\n0066 already documents -- a CHECK constraint enum is invisible to a\nmocked-DB unit test (resolve-oncall.test.ts mocks @platform/db\nentirely) -- but worse here: the notification insert runs inside the\nSAME transaction as the ticket assignment, so the constraint violation\nrolled back the entire rule execution, silently undoing the\nauto-assignment and its audit entry too, every time a backup\nnotification was attempted.\n\nVerified against an isolated scratch database (not the shared local\ndev DB): cascade fallback to backup, cascade fallback to escalation\nwith the backup notification actually landing in the table, and\nexplicit-assignee-wins all now pass end-to-end.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(automation-engine): dispatch_severity_notification action for ticket severity changes\n\nResolves the matching notification policy (specificity-scored: team+workflow\n> team > workflow > global > hardcoded email-only default) and dispatches to\nthe assignee, backup, and escalation manager (per-policy flags, or always for\ncritical severity). One notifications row per (channel, recipient) pair so\nper-channel dispatch failures are isolated and independently auditable.\n\n- packages/automation-engine: new action, wired into executor/types\n- packages/db: migration 0105 adds notifications.channel + the\n  ticket.severity_notification type\n- modules/helpdesk: automation rule seed (entity.created + entity.updated)\n- packages/telemetry: openwind_notification_dispatch_total counter\n- docs/local-setup.md: Novu per-channel wiring notes (email wired today;\n  sms/whatsapp/call pending the outbound worker''s provider contract)\n- isolation test verifies Tenant B''s policy/schedule never affects Tenant A''s\n  dispatch\n\n* feat(dx): on-call routing grafana dashboard + prometheus alerts\n\n- 3 new Grafana panels (On-Call Resolution Rate, Notification Channel Success\n  Rate, Coverage Gaps live), scoped to the 3 of 6 design-doc metrics that are\n  actually registered on any branch today (T39 partially done).\n- 2 new Prometheus alerts (OncallCoverageGapsDetected,\n  NotificationChannelHighFailureRate) added to the existing openwind-alerts\n  group; fixed two PromQL bugs found in review (unaggregated ratio division,\n  cross-tenant sum masking per-tenant gaps).\n- Extended observability-config.test.ts to cover the new panels/alerts.\n\nThe remaining 3 design-doc panels + 1 alert (needing 2 histograms + a\npolicy-match counter that were never registered) are documented as follow-up\nin the week-log entry, not silently dropped.\n\nBranched off feat/PLAT-608-tagsev-3e-dispatch-severity-notification (PR #600,\nunmerged) since that branch has the most complete metric set available.\n\ndocs/oncall-routing-design.md T42/T43\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(dx): correct label names in oncall/notification alerts and dashboard\n\nalert.rules.yml and openwind-dashboard.json queried result=/tenant_hash\nlabels that no metric emits (packages/telemetry/src/metrics.ts uses\noutcome/tenant_id) -- NotificationChannelHighFailureRate could never fire\nand the success-rate/resolution-rate/coverage-gap panels always showed\n0%/blank regardless of real data (Vijit review, PR #605 B1/B2/G1/G2).\n\n* fix(automation-engine): guard optional event.changed in severity dispatch\n\nEntityUpdatedV1Schema''s changed field became optional in PR #597 (B1) --\napply the same missing-changed no-op guard to\ndispatch-severity-notification.ts that resolve-oncall.ts already carries,\nsince both actions consume the same entity.updated event shape.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Vijit Prabhu <prabhu.vijit@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrJv1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAxqAQAEPgEUWPhDMT2fcKWiyxpmVs\nPamvaGwUKA60M49rclRHQfDOwT9O8foY7AVRs/dbvNcejgArCCFSAhccLLpH7piq\nGKiYsW0RUqTLQuFOiI1JM/RihE3PE0y3C9O37/aFlpmPFlt1FVfgeEr2zm9m8y7k\nV1xM1GztKi/7FUKEFHtYbU54PDM0PheTBTQEV8rKLzSn3G37Ec0uuU5l/bmWAAoF\nKb8b8wyRrOz9ajLSt26viQNPKCi8OWWF4Bed6Nqqb2jzvpPcnsb4g2+T8WD7qsfc\nQxRIWfcH9d3Az6AhnANMflfc2yp9B0YV8QPJBdp92U0fejSdc91a5cAUqP5WMqhP\nbbYH8y58WqXRkcV8lCdbYv9ARp8+fbxMFVO2xev5RhFFAqySMM6FbGkrjqJKCwa2\nV1jcnA5oxXWuqOn75c3WjRMNq6PDMX6ogceI0VeIs8WE+cge6/n7Y3hHEDv42VaN\nXL+9I/hWAitP+bb5jmNQPT9/wkTv94JTccjwbA6a6ClW/fzEvIyShxeOk5picBSq\nzxmp2+AJsg9njKXEEH69Add5UqeU8PRdbkJ/YOgWvk2BCKFdTQsBCm2crrEJFbmJ\nMQdOtC+wR0fdRWLJS3sj8GhSkk5YnIDIBaB1ZmvAoo3WVz7eX3XFGX/DoALxXwCo\nJCkSrQJF1s00KgfKWhdG\n=C6T2\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T02:03:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commit/ce3cf494901c82f44cb16df1a9ae13df3b7a7a0e","node_id":"C_kwDOScMdh9oAKGNlM2NmNDk0OTAxYzgyZjQ0Y2IxNmRmMWE5YWUxM2RmM2I3YTdhMGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commit/94fbaa210416535b8c2fe62b75799538bab5398a","sha":"94fbaa210416535b8c2fe62b75799538bab5398a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/94fbaa210416535b8c2fe62b75799538bab5398a"}],"sha":"ce3cf494901c82f44cb16df1a9ae13df3b7a7a0e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/ce3cf494901c82f44cb16df1a9ae13df3b7a7a0e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3049693?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/abmish","id":3049693,"login":"abmish","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNDk2OTM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/abmish","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/commits/94fbaa210416535b8c2fe62b75799538bab5398a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T19:37:22Z","email":"needabhinav@gmail.com","name":"Abhinav Mishra"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T19:37:22Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"3E Phase 1 (teams/services/on-call schema+API) + docs restructure: tracker/sup-docs split, spec cleanup, roadmap consolidation (#619)\n\n* docs(docs): mark 3e phase 1 merged, update week log\n\nPR #583 merged 2026-09-09 — teams/services/on_call_schedules DB layer.\nUpdates roadmap-tracker 3E row (0%→10%, red→yellow) and adds week-log entry.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(docs): prune shipped/stale spec drafts\n\nRemoves docs/specs/*.md and *-tasks.md files for features confirmed\nfully shipped and closed out (verified against closed GitHub issues,\nroadmap-tracker.md, and actual code, not just the files'' own often-stale\nstatus headers) and the ADR-015 review-draft staging file, whose\nproposed diff has already been applied verbatim to the accepted ADR.\nNo open track, accepted ADR, or in-code citation depends on any of these\n59 files.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(docs): add revised phase-wise management-os product roadmap\n\nAdds docs/management-os-roadmap.md — a proposed, not-yet-ratified\nreprioritization of the Phase 3 build sequence around the \"leadership\ncockpit\" pivot (org-wide operational visibility + one-click action,\nnot a single-department point tool). Stages 1-4 map onto what ships\nand why, explicitly flagging the scope/architecture decisions (module\nboundary, license-gate model, 3A/3E/3F re-sequencing) that still need\nhuman sign-off rather than assuming them. Companion to the\nimplementation timeline and GTM notes drafted alongside it this\nsession.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(docs): split shared tracking docs into docs/tracker/, gitignore docs/sup-docs/\n\nMoves roadmap-tracker.md, phase-timeline.md, week-log.md, and week-log/\nout of docs/sup-docs/ into a new docs/tracker/ directory, preserving\nhistory via git mv. docs/sup-docs/ is now entirely gitignored — reserved\nfor strategy/pricing/GTM/competitive-positioning material shared offline\nwith a select few, never via the repo (previously only\nopen-issues-tracker.md had this treatment; everything else in that\ndirectory was inadvertently shareable with every collaborator).\n\nUpdates every cross-reference to the moved files across CLAUDE.md,\nVISION.md, .claude/rules, .claude/context, .claude/references,\n.claude/skills, .claude/hooks/session-start.sh, and the docs tree.\nLeft unfixed, on purpose: three references inside accepted ADRs\n(ADR-008, ADR-009, ADR-011) and one inside the frozen\ndocs/tracker/week-log.md (do-not-edit historical record) — both are\noff-limits to touch per CLAUDE.md.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(docs): move management-os-roadmap.md into gitignored sup-docs\n\nThe owner moved this file into docs/sup-docs/ directly (private,\noffline-shared strategy content) rather than keeping it in the tracked\ndocs tree. This commit removes it from git tracking to match.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(docs): retire docs/roadmap.md, consolidate into roadmap-tracker.md\n\ndocs/roadmap.md was a 2026-05-vintage build plan that had drifted from\nCLAUDE.md/roadmap-tracker.md''s phase lettering and was largely\nsuperseded by accepted ADRs (3A by ADR-008/009/010, 3B by ADR-011).\nIts two still-useful, non-duplicated tables (feature-request triage,\ndeliberately-deferred capabilities) move into roadmap-tracker.md as a\nnew reference section; the rest (per-phase component classification,\ndependency map) is either stale or already captured in accepted ADRs.\n\nRepoints README.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, .claude/context/phase-3-primer.md,\ndocs/architecture-brief.md, and docs/specs/plugin-system.md at the\ntracker or the relevant ADR instead. Left as-is: two references inside\ndocs/decisions/ADR-009 (off-limits, human-authored) now point at a\nretired file — historical citations, not live pointers.","tree":{"sha":"1fcca370318f1e4d5201a9aa14d546d7032bc10f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/trees/1fcca370318f1e4d5201a9aa14d546d7032bc10f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/TinyPhi/OpenWind/git/commits/94fbaa210416535b8c2fe62b75799538bab5398a","verification":{"payload":"tree 1fcca370318f1e4d5201a9aa14d546d7032bc10f\nparent dd807cf4023b7032b71ddd860de4d8bdfed634a5\nauthor Abhinav Mishra <needabhinav@gmail.com> 1789673842 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789673842 +0530\n\n3E Phase 1 (teams/services/on-call schema+API) + docs restructure: tracker/sup-docs split, spec cleanup, roadmap consolidation (#619)\n\n* docs(docs): mark 3e phase 1 merged, update week log\n\nPR #583 merged 2026-09-09 — teams/services/on_call_schedules DB layer.\nUpdates roadmap-tracker 3E row (0%→10%, red→yellow) and adds week-log entry.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore(docs): prune shipped/stale spec drafts\n\nRemoves docs/specs/*.md and *-tasks.md files for features confirmed\nfully shipped and closed out (verified against closed GitHub issues,\nroadmap-tracker.md, and actual code, not just the files'' own often-stale\nstatus headers) and the ADR-015 review-draft staging file, whose\nproposed diff has already been applied verbatim to the accepted ADR.\nNo open track, accepted ADR, or in-code citation depends on any of these\n59 files.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(docs): add revised phase-wise management-os product roadmap\n\nAdds docs/management-os-roadmap.md — a proposed, not-yet-ratified\nreprioritization of the Phase 3 build sequence around the \"leadership\