i.github.com/users/wdunn001/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdunn001/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdunn001","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wdunn001/Unstable-legion/commits/81fa812ce330dd2b12fd8fbd0099099b3970a4f6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-19T12:56:59Z","email":"wdunn001@gmail.com","name":"wdunn001"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-19T12:56:59Z","email":"wdunn001@gmail.com","name":"wdunn001"},"message":"fix(chat): retire the PWA via a self-destroying service worker\n\nThe app-shell service worker made field testing unreproducible: a deployed\nfix could not be observed because the SW kept serving its precached bundle\nand legion-stage.wasm, so \"still broken\" was indistinguishable from\n\"stale cache\". Removing the plugin would not help — already-registered\nservice workers survive removal and keep serving their cache indefinitely.\nselfDestroying ships a SW that unregisters itself and deletes its caches on\nactivation, which is the only way to retire a deployed PWA. The rest of the\nconfig is left intact so re-enabling is a one-line change.","tree":{"sha":"d31c159bef5fe1a2fc9166683cbde4a5b2b70610","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wdunn001/Unstable-legion/git/trees/d31c159bef5fe1a2fc9166683cbde4a5b2b70610"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wdunn001/Unstable-legion/git/commits/81fa812ce330dd2b12fd8fbd0099099b3970a4f6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4011100?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdunn001/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdunn001/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdunn001/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdunn001/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"htt