os","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdunn001/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdunn001/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdunn001","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wdunn001/Unstable-legion/commits/9ef85731d5b820e3c98da1d16bfb64591430e786/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-18T13:25:23Z","email":"wdunn001@gmail.com","name":"wdunn001"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-18T13:25:23Z","email":"wdunn001@gmail.com","name":"wdunn001"},"message":"fix(chat): IndexedDB DB-name collision broke the thread store\n\nuseModelFolder opened an IndexedDB DB named ''unstable-legion-chat'' (v1, store\n''model-folder'') — the SAME name the thread store uses (v1, store ''threads'').\nSame name + same version + different stores is a collision: whichever opens\nfirst creates the DB with only its store, and the other''s transaction() then\nthrows ''object store not found'' (putThread crashed after loading 14B). Fix:\nuseModelFolder gets its OWN DB (''unstable-legion-model-folder''); threadStore\nbumps to v2 so onupgradeneeded recreates ''threads'' on any DB the collision\nleft without it (healthy DBs no-op). Existing folder handle re-picked once.","tree":{"sha":"597e572a0d6ce28958daf2a34ed81231b84a2e04","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wdunn001/Unstable-legion/git/trees/597e572a0d6ce28958daf2a34ed81231b84a2e04"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wdunn001/Unstable-legion/git/commits/9ef85731d5b820e3c98da1d16bfb64591430e786","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4011100?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdunn001/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdunn001/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdunn001/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdunn001/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/wdunn001","id":4011100,"login":"wdunn001","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwMTExMDA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdunn001/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdunn001/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdunn001/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdunn001/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdunn001/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdunn001","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/wdunn001/Unstable-legion/commit/9ef85731d5b820e3c98da1d16bfb64591430e786","node_id":"C_kwDOSckSltoAKDllZjg1NzMxZDViODIwZTNjOThkYTFkMTZiZmI2NDU5MTQzMGU3ODY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/wdunn001/Unstable-legion/commit/b7db6c7bca9ce45a80aafe63afccdda5d54db21a","sha":"b7db6c7bca9ce45a80aafe63afccdda5d54db21a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wdunn001/Unstable-legion/commits/b7db6c7bca9ce45a80aafe63afccdda5d54db21a"}],"sha":"9ef85731d5b820e3c98da1d16bfb64591430e786","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wdunn001/Unstable-legion/commits/9ef85731d5b820e3c98da1d16bfb64591430e786"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4011100?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdunn001/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdunn001/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdunn001/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdunn001/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/wdunn001","id":4011100,"login":"wdunn001","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwMTExMDA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdunn001/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdunn001/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdunn001/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdunn001/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdunn001/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdunn001","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wdunn001/Unstable-legion/commits/b7db6c7bca9ce45a80aafe63afccdda5d54db21a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-18T13:01:39Z","email":"wdunn001@gmail.com","name":"wdunn001"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-18T13:01:39Z","email":"wdunn001@gmail.com","name":"wdunn001"},"message":"fix(chat): pause loading when a remembered folder needs re-grant (no silent download)\n\nA local folder''s read permission doesn''t survive the channel-switch reload\n(File System Access API needs a fresh user gesture), so useModelFolder set\nneedsPermission + left handle undefined — and the host/serve loads silently\nfell back to DOWNLOADING the whole model (the 14B solo test hit the network +\nOPFS quota instead of reading the picked folder). Now hosting + serve are\ngated on !needsPermission, so a pending folder pauses the load instead of\nquietly downloading GBs. ModelFolderPanel surfaces it as a prominent warning\nwith an explicit choice — ''Re-grant folder'' (re-picks, restores read access)\nor ''Download instead'' (clears the folder) — and a clear ''Local folder active ✓''\nwhen granted. Resolving either way clears needsPermission and resumes.","tree":{"sha":"38c0f38fe7f2c6d6e977f798a86f8458e03d278a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wdunn001/Unstable-legion/git/trees/38c0f38fe7f2c6d6e977f798a86f8458e03d278a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wdunn001/Unstable-legion/git/commits/b7db6c7bca9ce45a80aafe63afccdda5d54db21a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4011100?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdunn001/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdunn001/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdunn001/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdunn001/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/wdunn001","id":4011100,"login":"wdunn001","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwMTExMDA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdunn001/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdunn001/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdunn001/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdunn001/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdunn001/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdunn001","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/wdunn001/Unstable-legion/commit/b7db6c7bca9ce45a80aafe63afccdda5d54db21a","node_id":"C_kwDOSckSltoAKGI3ZGI2YzdiY2E5Y2U0NWE4MGFhZmU2M2FmY2NkZGE1ZDU0ZGIyMWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/wdunn001/Unstable-legion/commit/bd374dd6fc380d0a766635c45292b533cdffc0e8","sha":"bd374dd6fc380d0a766635c45292b533cdffc0e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wdunn001/Unstable-legion/commits/bd374dd6fc380d0a766635c45292b533cdffc0e8"}],"sha":"b7db6c7bca9ce45a80aafe63afccdda5d54db21a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wdunn001/Unstable-legion/commits/b7db6c7bca9ce45a80aafe63afccdda5d54db21a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4011100?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdunn001/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdunn001/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdunn001/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdunn001/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/wdunn001","id":4011100,"login":"wdunn001","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwMTExMDA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdunn001/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdunn001/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdunn001/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdunn001/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdunn001/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wdunn001","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wdunn001/Unstable-legion/commits/bd374dd6fc380d0a766635c45292b533cdffc0e8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-18T12:41:28Z","email":"wdunn001@gmail.com","name":"wdunn001"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-18T12:41:28Z","email":"wdunn001@gmail.com","name":"wdunn001"},"message":"fix(chat): local-folder loads skip OPFS cache (avoid QuotaExceededError)\n\nA local-folder load was still caching the read bytes into OPFS, duplicating\nthe on-disk copy and burning the origin storage quota — the same failure\nmode a folder load exists to avoid (14B hit ''exceed its storage quota'' at\n~6GB, stacked on top of a previously-cached 8B). Add createNullShardStore\n(get always misses, put discards) and use it for local-folder loads: the\nfolder is the durable copy, so nothing is written to OPFS. SHA-256 verify\nstill runs on every fragment (fetchAndCacheFragment hashes regardless of the\nstore) — tampered layers still rejected; tests cover both.\n\nNOTE: the DOWNLOAD path still stacks multiple models'' shards in OPFS across\nchannel switches (8B + 14B) and can hit the quota — separate follow-up\n(evict other-model shards / handle QuotaExceededError). Workaround: clear\nsite storage, or use a local folder (now quota-free).","tree":{"sha":"f9f997474f732ddcbe26310e81bdf1bc0ffd6262","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wdunn001/Unstable-legion/git/trees/f9f997474f732ddcbe26310e81bdf1bc0ffd6262"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wdunn001/Unstable-legion/git/commits/bd374dd6fc380d0a766635c45292b533cdffc0e8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verifi