/repos/bargadev/lakonai/commits/a67cd31a9cd664dbd8f864469906509e44b6e94a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-24T01:05:56Z","email":"lucasmpbarga@gmail.com","name":"Lucas Barga"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-24T01:05:56Z","email":"lucasmpbarga@gmail.com","name":"Lucas Barga"},"message":"chore: nomic-compatible prefixes in embed.js; strip manual llama docblocks\n\nembed.js: model-agnostic DOC_PREFIX / QUERY_PREFIX constants so nomic-embed\nand BGE both work without code changes (nomic uses search_document:/\nsearch_query:, BGE uses the retrieval instruction prefix).\n\nSource files: remove the manually-added llama3.2 docblocks from\nbash-rewrite.js, throttle.js, compress/index.js, server.js — these\nare now generated and stored in lakonai-graph/annotations.json by\n`lakonai graph annotate`, keeping source files untouched.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"caa3dd4f286d8b944f78a27f604d309f165b1c12","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bargadev/lakonai/git/trees/caa3dd4f286d8b944f78a27f604d309f165b1c12"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bargadev/lakonai/git/commits/a67cd31a9cd664dbd8f864469906509e44b6e94a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17840539?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bargadev","id":17840539,"login":"bargadev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3ODQwNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/bargadev/lakonai/commit/a67cd31a9cd664dbd8f864469906509e44b6e94a","node_id":"C_kwDOScz88NoAKGE2N2NkMzFhOWNkNjY0ZGJkOGY4NjQ0Njk5MDY1MDllNDRiNmU5NGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/bargadev/lakonai/commit/f984d9eba6cf4c99e4ef59c19aa401cd23c061fa","sha":"f984d9eba6cf4c99e4ef59c19aa401cd23c061fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bargadev/lakonai/commits/f984d9eba6cf4c99e4ef59c19aa401cd23c061fa"}],"sha":"a67cd31a9cd664dbd8f864469906509e44b6e94a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bargadev/lakonai/commits/a67cd31a9cd664dbd8f864469906509e44b6e94a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17840539?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bargadev","id":17840539,"login":"bargadev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3ODQwNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bargadev/lakonai/commits/f984d9eba6cf4c99e4ef59c19aa401cd23c061fa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-24T01:02:14Z","email":"lucasmpbarga@gmail.com","name":"Lucas Barga"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-24T01:02:14Z","email":"lucasmpbarga@gmail.com","name":"Lucas Barga"},"message":"feat: lakonai graph annotate — LLM-generated docblocks via claude CLI / Anthropic / Ollama\n\nNew subcommand: lakonai graph annotate [dir]\n\nDetects file nodes with no docblock, calls an LLM backend (auto-detected\nin priority order: claude CLI → ANTHROPIC_API_KEY → Ollama), and stores\ngenerated descriptions in lakonai-graph/annotations.json. Never modifies\nsource files. On the next build, annotations are merged into nodes before\nembedding generation, enriching semantic search with zero user setup.\n\nBackend detection:\n  1. claude CLI (claude --print) — works for all Claude Code users, zero config\n  2. ANTHROPIC_API_KEY env var — direct Anthropic API call (Haiku model)\n  3. Ollama at localhost:11434 — local fallback, no API cost\n\nPrompt is tuned for retrieval: leads with primary action verb + synonyms\nso BGE-small connects query vocabulary to the correct file.\n\nBenchmark (30 queries): Semantic 26→30/30, Hybrid 26→29/30.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ca16ee403476222b6893cfc106d53f092609c37a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bargadev/lakonai/git/trees/ca16ee403476222b6893cfc106d53f092609c37a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bargadev/lakonai/git/commits/f984d9eba6cf4c99e4ef59c19aa401cd23c061fa","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17840539?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bargadev","id":17840539,"login":"bargadev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3ODQwNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/bargadev/lakonai/commit/f984d9eba6cf4c99e4ef59c19aa401cd23c061fa","node_id":"C_kwDOScz88NoAKGY5ODRkOWViYTZjZjRjOTllNGVmNTljMTlhYTQwMWNkMjNjMDYxZmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/bargadev/lakonai/commit/40a3550d749ad3d0ca32af470fecaf167d755a04","sha":"40a3550d749ad3d0ca32af470fecaf167d755a04","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bargadev/lakonai/commits/40a3550d749ad3d0ca32af470fecaf167d755a04"}],"sha":"f984d9eba6cf4c99e4ef59c19aa401cd23c061fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bargadev/lakonai/commits/f984d9eba6cf4c99e4ef59c19aa401cd23c061fa"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17840539?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bargadev","id":17840539,"login":"bargadev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3ODQwNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bargadev/lakonai/commits/40a3550d749ad3d0ca32af470fecaf167d755a04/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-24T00:27:53Z","email":"lucasmpbarga@gmail.com","name":"Lucas Barga"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-24T00:27:53Z","email":"lucasmpbarga@gmail.com","name":"Lucas Barga"},"message":"feat: llama3.2-generated docblocks + BGE instruction prefix (step 3)\n\nFour source files lacked docblocks, causing semantic search failures on\nconcept queries. Used llama3.2 (Ollama) to generate one-line descriptions\nand wrote them as leading comments:\n\n  bash-rewrite.js  — \"Intercepts Bash tool calls and rewrites or blocks\n                      dangerous shell commands before they run.\"\n  throttle.js      — \"Rate-limits hook events by tracking timestamps in\n                      marker files — prevents request floods.\"\n  compress/index.js — \"Strips comments, shrinks code/log/JSON/diff blocks,\n                       and reduces LLM context token usage.\"\n  server.js        — \"HTTP/HTTPS proxy server that intercepts LLM tool calls,\n                      compresses output, and tracks token usage to disk.\"\n\nAlso adds BGE query instruction prefix (\"Represent this sentence for\nsearching relevant passages: \") as documented for BGE retrieval models.\n\nBenchmark (30 queries): Semantic 26→30/30, Hybrid 26→29/30.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"62d57bf92010470f1bb60144753d22da773ffe7a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bargadev/lakonai/git/trees/62d57bf92010470f1bb60144753d22da773ffe7a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bargadev/lakonai/git/commits/40a3550d749ad3d0ca32af470fecaf167d755a04","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17840539?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bargadev","id":17840539,"login":"bargadev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3ODQwNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/bargadev/lakonai/commit/40a3550d749ad3d0ca32af470fecaf167d755a04","node_id":"C_kwDOScz88NoAKDQwYTM1NTBkNzQ5YWQzZDBjYTMyYWY0NzBmZWNhZjE2N2Q3NTVhMDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/bargadev/lakonai/commit/c1383c554a054d6a7d806a3a5692f7afd8e77aa2","sha":"c1383c554a054d6a7d806a3a5692f7afd8e77aa2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bargadev/lakonai/commits/c1383c554a054d6a7d806a3a5692f7afd8e77aa2"}],"sha":"40a3550d749ad3d0ca32af470fecaf167d755a04","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bargadev/lakonai/commits/40a3550d749ad3d0ca32af470fecaf167d755a04"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17840539?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bargadev","id":17840539,"login":"bargadev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3ODQwNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bargadev/lakonai/commits/c1383c554a054d6a7d806a3a5692f7afd8e77aa2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T22:27:09Z","email":"lucasmpbarga@gmail.com","name":"Lucas Barga"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T22:27:09Z","email":"lucasmpbarga@gmail.com","name":"Lucas Barga"},"message":"feat: add BGE query instruction prefix for better asymmetric retrieval\n\nBGE models are trained to use a query-side instruction prefix for retrieval.\nPrepend \"Represent this sentence for searching relevant passages: \" to every\nquery before embedding. Corpus vectors are unchanged — no re-generation needed.\n\nBenchmark: 26/30 maintained; output-spill now correctly outranks output-bench\nfor \"prevent oversized tool output\" (better top-1 precision).\n\nAlso fixes the ~80MB → ~23MB model size label in the benchmark script.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"79e2cb6ae9d1917e1ddd247b9e8eb38b43cfa3ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bargadev/lakonai/git/trees/79e2cb6ae9d1917e1ddd247b9e8eb38b43cfa3ad"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bargadev/lakonai/git/commits/c1383c554a054d6a7d806a3a5692f7afd8e77aa2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17840539?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bargadev","id":17840539,"login":"bargadev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3ODQwNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/bargadev/lakonai/commit/c1383c554a054d6a7d806a3a5692f7afd8e77aa2","node_id":"C_kwDOScz88NoAKGMxMzgzYzU1NGEwNTRkNmE3ZDgwNmEzYTU2OTJmN2FmZDhlNzdhYTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/bargadev/lakonai/commit/c7fa8c7fbda924f339b58ee8e87eaa7e0ce5b566","sha":"c7fa8c7fbda924f339b58ee8e87eaa7e0ce5b566","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bargadev/lakonai/commits/c7fa8c7fbda924f339b58ee8e87eaa7e0ce5b566"}],"sha":"c1383c554a054d6a7d806a3a5692f7afd8e77aa2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bargadev/lakonai/commits/c1383c554a054d6a7d806a3a5692f7afd8e77aa2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17840539?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bargadev","id":17840539,"login":"bargadev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3ODQwNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bargadev/lakonai/commits/c7fa8c7fbda924f339b58ee8e87eaa7e0ce5b566/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T03:02:42Z","email":"lucasmpbarga@gmail.com","name":"Lucas Barga"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T03:02:42Z","email":"lucasmpbarga@gmail.com","name":"Lucas Barga"},"message":"chore: revert model to bge-small (bge-large regressed on benchmark)\n\nTried Xenova/bge-large-en-v1.5 (MTEB 64.2, ~1.2GB).\nResult: 25/30 — one regression vs bge-small+docblocks+source-boost (26/30).\nThe 4 remaining failures are data-limited (no docblock, no body indexing),\nnot model-capacity limited. Larger model doesn''t help without richer input.\n\nKeeping bge-small-en-v1.5 as the default.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"87454053d9dc5b3262d3eddf5e6d48dd8e095521","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bargadev/lakonai/git/trees/87454053d9dc5b3262d3eddf5e6d48dd8e095521"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bargadev/lakonai/git/commits/c7fa8c7fbda924f339b58ee8e87eaa7e0ce5b566","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17840539?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bargadev","id":17840539,"login":"bargadev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3ODQwNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/bargadev/lakonai/commit/c7fa8c7fbda924f339b58ee8e87eaa7e0ce5b566","node_id":"C_kwDOScz88NoAKGM3ZmE4YzdmYmRhOTI0ZjMzOWI1OGVlOGU4N2VhYTdlMGNlNWI1NjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/bargadev/lakonai/commit/02f2f2509ac75fa6d7d8d6701818a5f7111a0974","sha":"02f2f2509ac75fa6d7d8d6701818a5f7111a0974","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bargadev/lakonai/commits/02f2f2509ac75fa6d7d8d6701818a5f7111a0974"}],"sha":"c7fa8c7fbda924f339b58ee8e87eaa7e0ce5b566","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bargadev/lakonai/commits/c7fa8c7fbda924f339b58ee8e87eaa7e0ce5b566"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17840539?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bargadev","id":17840539,"login":"bargadev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3ODQwNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bargadev/lakonai/commits/02f2f2509ac75fa6d7d8d6701818a5f7111a0974/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T02:56:59Z","email":"lucasmpbarga@gmail.com","name":"Lucas Barga"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T02:56:59Z","email":"lucasmpbarga@gmail.com","name":"Lucas Barga"},"message":"feat: penalise non-source nodes in semantic ranking (step 2)\n\nTest, script, and bin files are secondary artifacts — when they happen\nto embed close to a query, they should lose to the actual source module.\nApply 0.5× multiplier to any node whose file path starts with\ntests/, scripts/, bin/, coverage/, or benchmark/.\n\nEffect on 30-query benchmark: score holds at 26/30, but\n\"module that builds the dependency graph\" now correctly surfaces\nsrc/graph/index.js over tests/graph-core.test.js in hybrid mode.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c29f72b313deffcbd5a1281df0b7a5c86d16af4b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bargadev/lakonai/git/trees/c29f72b313deffcbd5a1281df0b7a5c86d16af4b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bargadev/lakonai/git/commits/02f2f2509ac75fa6d7d8d6701818a5f7111a0974","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17840539?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bargadev","id":17840539,"login":"bargadev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3ODQwNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/bargadev/lakonai/commit/02f2f2509ac75fa6d7d8d6701818a5f7111a0974","node_id":"C_kwDOScz88NoAKDAyZjJmMjUwOWFjNzVmYTZkN2Q4ZDY3MDE4MThhNWY3MTExYTA5NzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/bargadev/lakonai/commit/8c30f701fd8e425bfd1f6a70211ef7cb208b9c1f","sha":"8c30f701fd8e425bfd1f6a70211ef7cb208b9c1f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bargadev/lakonai/commits/8c30f701fd8e425bfd1f6a70211ef7cb208b9c1f"}],"sha":"02f2f2509ac75fa6d7d8d6701818a5f7111a0974","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bargadev/lakonai/commits/02f2f2509ac75fa6d7d8d6701818a5f7111a0974"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17840539?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bargadev","id":17840539,"login":"bargadev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3ODQwNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bargadev/lakonai/commits/8c30f701fd8e425bfd1f6a70211ef7cb208b9c1f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T02:56:24Z","email":"lucasmpbarga@gmail.com","name":"Lucas Barga"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T02:56:24Z","email":"lucasmpbarga@gmail.com","name":"Lucas Barga"},"message":"feat: index file docblocks for richer semantic embeddings (step 1)\n\nextractDocblock() parses the leading comment block from each source file\n(// lines, /* */ blocks, Python #, skipping shebang/''use strict'') and\nattaches it to the file node as `docblock`. nodeText() includes it when\nbuilding the embedding text, giving the model the author''s intent for\nthe file — not just its name.\n\nBenchmark (30 queries): Semantic 25→26, Hybrid 25→26.\nGain comes from files with rich docblocks (e.g. detect.js, leiden.js).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c407cd93e8e7ab1fe83032c1441902ba9c7ab753","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bargadev/lakonai/git/trees/c407cd93e8e7ab1fe83032c1441902ba9c7ab753"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bargadev/lakonai/git/commits/8c30f701fd8e425bfd1f6a70211ef7cb208b9c1f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17840539?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bargadev","id":17840539,"login":"bargadev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3ODQwNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/bargadev/lakonai/commit/8c30f701fd8e425bfd1f6a70211ef7cb208b9c1f","node_id":"C_kwDOScz88NoAKDhjMzBmNzAxZmQ4ZTQyNWJmZDFmNmE3MDIxMWVmN2NiMjA4YjljMWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/bargadev/lakonai/commit/e58d987a534e0538e72d3c6d1695438f889b7156","sha":"e58d987a534e0538e72d3c6d1695438f889b7156","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bargadev/lakonai/commits/e58d987a534e0538e72d3c6d1695438f889b7156"}],"sha":"8c30f701fd8e425bfd1f6a70211ef7cb208b9c1f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bargadev/lakonai/commits/8c30f701fd8e425bfd1f6a70211ef7cb208b9c1f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17840539?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bargadev","id":17840539,"login":"bargadev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3ODQwNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bargadev/lakonai/commits/e58d987a534e0538e72d3c6d1695438f889b7156/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T02:43:23Z","email":"lucasmpbarga@gmail.com","name":"Lucas Barga"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T02:43:23Z","email":"lucasmpbarga@gmail.com","name":"Lucas Barga"},"message":"feat: extract function params for richer semantic embeddings (Feature 3)\n\nparseParams() strips types/defaults/destructuring from raw param strings so\neach function node carries param names. nodeText() includes them when building\nthe text to embed, giving the model richer signal for queries like\n\"save stats to disk\" → writeStats(stats, filePath).\n\nJS/TS funcRe and arrowRe, Python defRe, and Go funcRe all updated to capture\nthe param group. Rust parser unchanged (no useful param names without types).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7577797bddbc58abc5007cce9e2d0dae94fbb884","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bargadev/lakonai/git/trees/7577797bddbc58abc5007cce9e2d0dae94fbb884"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bargadev/lakonai/git/commits/e58d987a534e0538e72d3c6d1695438f889b7156","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17840539?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bargadev","id":17840539,"login":"bargadev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3ODQwNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/bargadev/lakonai/commit/e58d987a534e0538e72d3c6d1695438f889b7156","node_id":"C_kwDOScz88NoAKGU1OGQ5ODdhNTM0ZTA1MzhlNzJkM2M2ZDE2OTU0MzhmODg5YjcxNTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/bargadev/lakonai/commit/55659ef1c9d0fb9352ae2e3fa0d8ee691e3258b1","sha":"55659ef1c9d0fb9352ae2e3fa0d8ee691e3258b1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bargadev/lakonai/commits/55659ef1c9d0fb9352ae2e3fa0d8ee691e3258b1"}],"sha":"e58d987a534e0538e72d3c6d1695438f889b7156","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bargadev/lakonai/commits/e58d987a534e0538e72d3c6d1695438f889b7156"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17840539?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bargadev","id":17840539,"login":"bargadev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3ODQwNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bargadev/lakonai/commits/55659ef1c9d0fb9352ae2e3fa0d8ee691e3258b1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T02:39:23Z","email":"lucasmpbarga@gmail.com","name":"Lucas Barga"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T02:39:23Z","email":"lucasmpbarga@gmail.com","name":"Lucas Barga"},"message":"feat: semantic graph query — BGE embeddings + hybrid RRF search\n\nAdds semantic search to `lakonai graph query` via @xenova/transformers\n(optionalDependency). When installed, graph build generates embeddings;\nqueries use hybrid BM25 + semantic RRF scoring (8/10 accuracy on 10\nbenchmark queries, vs 6/10 BM25 alone).\n\nKey changes:\n- src/graph/embed.js — BGE-small-en-v1.5 wrapper, cosine similarity,\n  batch embedding generation\n- src/graph/query.js — nlQuerySemantic, nlQueryHybrid (asymmetric RRF:\n  k_sem=60, k_bm25=300, BM25 capped at top-10)\n- src/graph/index.js — buildSync (sync) + build (async); hybrid CLI mode\n- package.json — @xenova/transformers ^2.17.2 in optionalDependencies;\n  test:unit / test:integration / test:e2e scripts\n- CLAUDE.md — test-layer policy (unit + integration + E2E per feature)\n- scripts/benchmark-query.js — BM25 vs semantic vs hybrid benchmark\n- 751 tests passing\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"76229093f2a581219901313f39daa193e0fe0196","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bargadev/lakonai/git/trees/76229093f2a581219901313f39daa193e0fe0196"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bargadev/lakonai/git/commits/55659ef1c9d0fb9352ae2e3fa0d8ee691e3258b1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17840539?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bargadev","id":17840539,"login":"bargadev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3ODQwNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/bargadev/lakonai/commit/55659ef1c9d0fb9352ae2e3fa0d8ee691e3258b1","node_id":"C_kwDOScz88NoAKDU1NjU5ZWYxYzlkMGZiOTM1MmFlMmUzZmEwZDhlZTY5MWUzMjU4YjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/bargadev/lakonai/commit/a9bd1ddf6effbd8d02ecd61262d6d81313ee59c7","sha":"a9bd1ddf6effbd8d02ecd61262d6d81313ee59c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bargadev/lakonai/commits/a9bd1ddf6effbd8d02ecd61262d6d81313ee59c7"}],"sha":"55659ef1c9d0fb9352ae2e3fa0d8ee691e3258b1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bargadev/lakonai/commits/55659ef1c9d0fb9352ae2e3fa0d8ee691e3258b1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17840539?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bargadev","id":17840539,"login":"bargadev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3ODQwNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bargadev/lakonai/commits/a9bd1ddf6effbd8d02ecd61262d6d81313ee59c7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-16T03:01:07Z","email":"lucasmpbarga@gmail.com","name":"Lucas Barga"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-16T03:01:07Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: CI test hung on Linux, silently blocking the 0.17.0 publish (#15)\n\nThe publish workflow runs `npm test` before `npm publish`. A sandbox.test.js\ntest pointed LAKON_HOME at /proc/nonexistent-lakon/deep to force a write\nfailure — fails fast on macOS (/proc doesn''t exist there), but on the Linux\nActions runner it hung mkdirSync instead of throwing. Jest never exited,\nnpm test never completed, and the job sat for the full 6h Actions timeout\nbefore being killed — no error, no publish, no obvious cause in the log.\n\nReplaced the OS-dependent path with a deterministic fs.mkdirSync mock, and\nadded forceExit + a 15s testTimeout to jest.config.js so a stuck test fails\nin seconds instead of blocking every subsequent publish for hours.\n\nBump 0.17.0 -> 0.17.1, since 0.17.0 itself never reached npm and this\ncarries its changes plus this fix.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bac532fc26f6319fc0b61fc0c04c3a7d7feda4d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bargadev/lakonai/git/trees/bac532fc26f6319fc0b61fc0c04c3a7d7feda4d0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bargadev/lakonai/git/commits/a9bd1ddf6effbd8d02ecd61262d6d81313ee59c7","verification":{"payload":"tree bac532fc26f6319fc0b61fc0c04c3a7d7feda4d0\nparent ad2129fc5b7ee40e150b4c554e164a36a03b5fdb\nauthor Lucas Barga <lucasmpbarga@gmail.com> 1784170867 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784170867 -0300\n\nfix: CI test hung on Linux, silently blocking the 0.17.0 publish (#15)\n\nThe publish workflow runs `npm test` before `npm publish`. A sandbox.test.js\ntest pointed LAKON_HOME at /proc/nonexistent-lakon/deep to force a write\nfailure — fails fast on macOS (/proc doesn''t exist there), but on the Linux\nActions runner it hung mkdirSync instead of throwing. Jest never exited,\nnpm test never completed, and the job sat for the full 6h Actions timeout\nbefore being killed — no error, no publish, no obvious cause in the log.\n\nReplaced the OS-dependent path with a deterministic fs.mkdirSync mock, and\nadded forceExit + a 15s testTimeout to jest.config.js so a stuck test fails\nin seconds instead of blocking every subsequent publish for hours.\n\nBump 0.17.0 -> 0.17.1, since 0.17.0 itself never reached npm and this\ncarries its changes plus this fix.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWElzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAaMkQAJ3G5Ndc46N0Dyi40zfEyWAJ\naMANt3XIf9Dljdf1Fzur9oZZZngMxbhDpcphPLuv4hMPSK/dzjdR0/+vzIU8D79o\nXtxekvLDS3HLTiWFLGuDjfr/6BQs8mG5Ynwc60HdWfa1el5qex2nomZ4Lhl9pQSa\nOBEoVK6fdg5NCWMX7CfUaSW04KaFZb0UVQNzdI6YLXnuOlERBErHwCjY5V5KZNOK\nlhBJNR3DwaIPLBFrlho2aJJWdQ5CJHPzMyr8ykMZGAHKTYNckQcPht6Nc242MA0p\nN8rfeAdUf3P/wVaKrCiRNF4i+QU74BBmsdkTp6EnT+uZ33Aq2WboXGKtdYQf5hIg\nGAO6Y9c3ghDSDQN008z5VQko9Rf1mudn/xRKHnQA1CdHlPNtp5us5SHPOEtW2p3s\n+q2Lx65TLuMvbdTc/ZNyLjJwqxiYzyODDXyW6oPu4XaPuaHtfgYLDHpg2yKCyrdH\nFtXBDSXxC3MHY2JXJcTiY4XQjGlAIr5xkTqzd3c8UutmKNNqbyomhxFbOWCR1mNV\n8mBZFzNaELcST4R5zRr2qJmy1abOZ/nbpzxQ5Bo2zwo13TKnMPmYGyXqtojoiljp\na7hBsOitoHtTOKhVkMPZUHk1f+dg6732rI5vHxEwB1zTMMPZSLXSjB0ZXDK0rk+q\noABgJRcWI8x52wsHaaP+\n=/7El\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-16T03:01:08Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/bargadev/lakonai/commit/a9bd1ddf6effbd8d02ecd61262d6d81313ee59c7","node_id":"C_kwDOScz88NoAKGE5YmQxZGRmNmVmZmJkOGQwMmVjZDYxMjYyZDZkODEzMTNlZTU5Yzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/bargadev/lakonai/commit/ad2129fc5b7ee40e150b4c554e164a36a03b5fdb","sha":"ad2129fc5b7ee40e150b4c554e164a36a03b5fdb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bargadev/lakonai/commits/ad2129fc5b7ee40e150b4c554e164a36a03b5fdb"}],"sha":"a9bd1ddf6effbd8d02ecd61262d6d81313ee59c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bargadev/lakonai/commits/a9bd1ddf6effbd8d02ecd61262d6d81313ee59c7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17840539?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bargadev","id":17840539,"login":"bargadev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3ODQwNTM5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bargadev/lakonai/commits/ad2129fc5b7ee40e150b4c554e164a36a03b5fdb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-15T20:01:49Z","email":"lucasmpbarga@gmail.com","name":"Lucas Barga"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-15T20:01:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: sandbox spill for oversized tool output (v0.17.0) (#14)\n\n* feat: park oversized tool output in a sandbox instead of the context\n\nFilters only help with commands lakonai knows. Everything else — an\nunrouted `terraform plan`, a 3k-line Grep, a Read of a generated file —\npaid full price on every turn.\n\nOutput that is still over budget after filtering now goes to\n~/.lakon/sandbox/<id>.txt, and the agent gets a digest: head, tail, exit\ncode, and how to query the rest. Nothing is lost; it just stops being\nre-paid. `lakonai peek <id>` reads it back, with --offset/--limit/--grep.\nMeasured on a 4000-line build log: 4000 lines / 120KB in, 29 lines out.\n\nTwo entry points, because one is not enough:\n\n  - bin/lakonai.js spills what lakonai itself executed. Bounded by the\n    routing allowlist, and by stdout unless needsStderr() is true.\n  - src/hooks/output-spill.js (PostToolUse) is the universal net. It runs\n    after any tool and receives the real result, so it catches what the\n    rewrite structurally cannot: unrouted Bash, stderr, and Read / Grep /\n    Glob / WebFetch / Task output.\n\nPostToolUse is the only event that can replace a tool result\n(updatedToolOutput). PreToolUse fires before the output exists, so it can\ncap input but never park output.\n\nAlso fixes read-guard''s auto-cap: it counted lines and ignored line width,\nso a 100-line x 5000-char file (~124k tokens) sailed through untouched. It\nnow also enforces a byte budget, and denies (rather than mis-caps) a\nsingle line that alone blows the budget — Read slices by line, so no\nlimit can cut inside one.\n\nThe digest reports measured lines and KB, never an estimated token count:\ncountTokensApprox() splits on whitespace and undercounts a real tokenizer\nby ~35% on prose. A tool that exists to be honest about token cost should\nnot quote a number it cannot stand behind. tracking.record() likewise logs\nwhat was shown, not what would have been shown, so `gain` reports what the\nagent actually paid.\n\nLAKON_SPILL_TOKENS tunes the budget; 0 disables spilling entirely.\n\nBump 0.16.5 -> 0.17.0.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: git filters swallowed --oneline, --format, --stat and --name-only\n\nfilterStatus, filterLog and filterDiff each pattern-match on git''s verbose\noutput shape only. Feed them a short format instead and every one of them\nsilently returned nothing (or a hardcoded \"clean\") instead of the actual\noutput — a filter inventing state is worse than no filter at all:\n\n  - `git status --short` reported a dirty tree as \"clean\" (fell through to\n    a hardcoded fallback when no section header matched).\n  - `git log --oneline` / `--format=…` returned \"\" (nothing matches the\n    \"commit <sha>\\nAuthor:\\nDate:\" shape these formats don''t emit).\n  - `git diff --stat` / `--name-only` returned \"\" for the same reason —\n    no hunk markers to match on.\n\nAll three now fall back to passing the raw (already terse) short-format\noutput through untouched, and only ever claim \"clean\" when git actually\nsaid so. filterStatus also preserves the porcelain leading column (\" M\"\nunstaged vs \"M \" staged) rather than trimming it away.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d403d86ae52dfb66fbafed1ec2e769d7684c9385","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bargadev/lakonai/git/trees/d403d86ae52dfb66fbafed1ec2e769d7684c9385"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bargadev/lakonai/git/commits/ad2129fc5b7ee40e150b4c554e164a36a03b5fdb","verification":{"payload":"tree d403d86ae52dfb66fbafed1ec2e769d7684c9385\nparent 12bd819ed868008361502f174d962efe989661de\nauthor Lucas Barga <lucasmpbarga@gmail.com> 1784145709 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784145709 -0300\n\nfeat: sandbox spill for oversized tool output (v0.17.0) (#14)\n\n* feat: park oversized tool output in a sandbox instead of the context\n\nFilters only help with commands lakonai knows. Everything else — an\nunrouted `terraform plan`, a 3k-line Grep, a Read of a generated file —\npaid full price on every turn.\n\nOutput that is still over budget after filtering now goes to\n~/.lakon/sandbox/<id>.txt, and the agent gets a digest: head, tail, exit\ncode, and how to query the rest. Nothing is lost; it just stops being\nre-paid. `lakonai peek <id>` reads it back, with --offset/--limit/--grep.\nMeasured on a 4000-line build log: 4000 lines / 120KB in, 29 lines out.\n\nTwo entry points, because one is not enough:\n\n  - bin/lakonai.js spills what lakonai itself executed. Bounded by the\n    routing allowlist, and by stdout unless needsStderr() is true.\n  - src/hooks/output-spill.js (PostToolUse) is the universal net. It runs\n    after any tool and receives the real result, so it catches what the\n    rewrite structurally cannot: unrouted Bash, stderr, and Read / Grep /\n    Glob / WebFetch / Task output.\n\nPostToolUse is the only event that can replace a tool result\n(updatedToolOutput). PreToolUse fires before the output exists, so it can\ncap input but never park output.\n\nAlso fixes read-guard''s auto-cap: it counted lines and ignored line width,\nso a 100-line x 5000-char file (~124k tokens) sailed through untouched. It\nnow also enforces a byte budget, and denies (rather than mis-caps) a\nsingle line that alone blows the budget — Read slices by line, so no\nlimit can cut inside one.\n\nThe digest reports measured lines and KB, never an estimated token count:\ncountTokensApprox() splits on whitespace and undercounts a real tokenizer\nby ~35% on prose. A tool that exists to be honest about token cost should\nnot quote a number it cannot stand behind. tracking.record() likewise logs\nwhat was shown, not what would have been shown, so `gain` reports what the\nagent actually paid.\n\nLAKON_SPILL_TOKENS tunes the budget; 0 disables spilling entirely.\n\nBump 0.16.5 -> 0.17.0.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: git filters swallowed --oneline, --format, --stat and --name-only\n\nfilterStatus, filterLog and filterDiff each pattern-match on git''s verbose\noutput shape only. Feed them a short format instead and every one of them\nsilently returned nothing (or a hardcoded \"clean\") instead of the actual\noutput — a filter inventing state is worse than no filter at all:\n\n  - `git status --short` reported a dirty tree as \"clean\" (fell through to\n    a hardcoded fallback when no section header matched).\n  - `git log --oneline` / `--format=…` returned \"\" (nothing matches the\n    \"commit <sha>\\nAuthor:\\nDate:\" shape these formats don''t emit).\n  - `git diff --stat` / `--name-only` returned \"\" for the same reason —\n    no hunk markers to match on.\n\nAll three now fall back to passing the raw (already terse) short-format\noutput through untouched, and only ever claim \"clean\" when git actually\nsaid so. filterStatus also preserves the porcelain leading column (\" M\"\nunstaged vs \"M \" staged) rather than trimming it away.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqV+ctCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgygQALD6+NMsichYgKOWSoxdHZn2\nPGwn9x1wlQ4MQN5c1fqHrJY45AnoZzK1p55Z5cRCQmfHXkvLqcJMxKhfQ5ccEQFi\ndtU+L00PUQ1DG5sxECP7DA0yf/ASBU0MoFIrjhhp9fpyADdEwgt3ZtWMc1JVlGpN\nIJCN5g3tUE/6ewMXkzVtub58qvq+bJiBbtm3bMXF9J9Sww9DOsx6yZBIsOGgspHD\nPqkPeUFLk/1GdIFMNOEeIeW3yrTIeNOehzRKPDMiv4p9y6M0bDaQHYzqAuTmTy9m\nVtdDmgx1/E3ZO9md1kQTvjnM5kTezW+ZKRXGaoh//lgpP6l6ZT56FeIU/7jf8q45\nQrTy6Xd33upx5qPQGUksSkvssoooiXXvUsYbBYlcy2RiNXqtpV5o1b48m5jW8Rx4\nsHzPfRa88YlIOxqWrw+4aSTyvGduG9NnSIbF2mo2nR2LwTmZh1Hv6Iop35TiRMoc\n+nUYv9ugSBfWv6Mr6ZGKX77kUCSxZopdtrLp/SFtBS9H02DEnQso7eLROijiJ8ur\nb86tZ7id8u20QyxB3eBE/kcgVAIK2O30HxFQQ44u1uAgHBGeQyay3xRZj0nCnlQP\nQGiB/Vd3rohMIASkwtEaKCxsvts+GgQNFzrsHfYAkrOjOPbIvvVgEx53jaW0S6Ou\n6QaM3p6+tahFXPr2KhUp\n=nk6R\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-15T20:01:49Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19