i.github.com/users/bargadev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bargadev/lakonai/commits/73753caed83d9a86bde122b4ac3368b00bddea46/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-02T21:32:01Z","email":"lucasmpbarga@gmail.com","name":"Lucas Barga"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-02T21:32:01Z","email":"lucasmpbarga@gmail.com","name":"Lucas Barga"},"message":"docs: sync README output-savings with the fixed bench (~52%, honestly framed)\n\n0.16.1 fixed the output bench, so `lakonai gain` now reports the rule''s effect\nagainst a rule-free Claude baseline (~52% on prose prompts) instead of the old\n\"~10% marginal vs an already-concise agent\" framing — headless `claude --print`\nis verbose without the rule, not concise-by-design.\n\nRewrite the section to match reality and stay honest: ~52% is labelled a\nbest-case on prose turns; the real workload sits between the deterministic input\nsavings (~46%) and that ceiling. Refresh the example block to the current format.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c529958bd8f4a296c8a009e184a3573af8cec6b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bargadev/lakonai/git/trees/c529958bd8f4a296c8a009e184a3573af8cec6b7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bargadev/lakonai/git/commits/73753caed83d9a86bde122b4ac3368b00bddea46","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17840539?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/followers","following_url":