os","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bargadev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bargadev/lakonai/commits/b38d9130b9144a14803c8fc95916f4605895f8fc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-30T21:42:49Z","email":"lucasmpbarga@gmail.com","name":"Lucas Barga"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-30T21:42:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: automatic filtering on every agent (shim + universal read-guard + auto-learning) — 0.12.0→0.15.0 (#6)\n\n* feat: memory-file compression via local AI CLI (0.12.x)\n\nAdd `lakonai compress-memory <file>` (+ `revert-memory`): manual, opt-in\ncompression of authored memory (CLAUDE.md, notes) using whichever local AI CLI\nthe user already has — claude/gemini/codex/cursor-agent, auto-detected on PATH\n(LAKONAI_MEM_CLI / LAKONAI_MEM_MODEL overrides). No API key.\n\nSafety harness (src/mem-compress.js): always writes a <name>.original.md backup\nfirst, validates every fenced/inline code span and URL survives byte-for-byte\n(one fix pass, else aborts untouched), refuses sensitive filenames. Provider\nregistry + prompts in src/mem-llm.js. `install` offers a one-time opt-in prompt.\nUnlike MCP catalog shrink, never automatic — it rewrites authored prose.\n\nTwo engines by domain: regex for machine/high-frequency (shell output, MCP\ncatalogs), LLM only for authored prose (memory). Lands together with the\npreviously-unreleased MCP auto-compression + command-surface simplification.\n\nREADME: sellable marketing pass (four-fronts framing, surfaced MCP + memory).\nCLAUDE.md: rule to keep the npm About page in sync (republish on README change).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: universal PATH shim — automatic shell filtering on every agent (0.13.0)\n\n`lakonai shim` makes shell-output filtering automatic on agents without a\ncall-rewriting hook (Codex/Cursor/Windsurf/Cline/Gemini), not just Claude Code.\nDrops executable wrappers for ls/grep/rg/ag/find/cat/tree/head into\n~/.lakon/shim/ and prepends it to PATH via a managed block in the shell rc, so\nany agent that runs those commands through a shell routes them through lakonai —\nno hook API, no model cooperation.\n\ngit/tail excluded (editors/streaming). Recursion prevented: runAndFilter spawns\nthe real binary with pathWithoutShim(PATH) so the shim dir is excluded\n(end-to-end tested). Opt-in (edits shell rc); reaches agents that inherit the\nshell PATH.\n\nREADME capability matrix updated: shell filtering now automatic on all six\nagents via the shim. Read/Grep guard + auto-learning stay Claude-only — they act\non the agent''s own tool calls, which needs a call-rewriting hook (today only\nClaude Code''s; Codex blocked upstream, openai/codex#18491).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: universal Read-guard on the shell path (0.14.0)\n\n`lakonai cat`/`head`/`tail`/`less`/`more`/`bat` now refuse junk reads (lockfiles,\nnode_modules, build artifacts) using the same deny rules as the Claude Read hook\n(src/shim-guard.js, reusing read-guard.isDeniedPath). Checked in runAndFilter\nbefore spawning: a denied path is skipped with a one-line reason + 0-token track.\n\nCombined with the PATH shim, junk-read protection is now automatic on EVERY\nagent for shell-mediated reads (`cat pnpm-lock.yaml` -> skipped), not just Claude\nCode''s Read tool. The agent''s own non-shell Read tool still needs a hook (Claude\nonly). Auto-learning stays Claude-only (it needs the agent''s full command stream)\nand is largely moot elsewhere since the shim already filters the standard set.\n\nMatrix updated honestly: shell filter + shell-read guard automatic on all six;\ninternal-tool guard + auto-learning Claude-only, with sourced upstream reasons.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: platform-agnostic auto-learning + cleaner install output (0.15.0)\n\nAuto-learning now also runs off ~/.lakon/log.jsonl (appended by every lakonai\ncall — shim wrappers + rule-prefixed commands — on ANY agent), not just the\nClaude transcript. learn.analyzeLog / maybeLearnFromLog (throttled hourly) are\ncalled from runAndFilter, so heavy non-builtin commands get promoted to the\nfiltered set automatically on every agent. With the shim, all four input-side\nfeatures now run automatically everywhere for shell-mediated work; only guarding\nthe agent''s own non-shell Read tool stays Claude-only (needs a rewriting hook).\n\nAlso: Claude Code install line shows \"+ N slash commands\" instead of the full\nlist. CLAUDE.md: rule that releases publish via CI only (never manual npm\npublish) — assistant scope is commit/PR/merge at most.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"dc533c7ca3d90a716e946964177ae5f40af690da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bargadev/lakonai/git/trees/dc533c7ca3d90a716e946964177ae5f40af690da"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bargadev/lakonai/git/commits/b38d9130b9144a14803c8fc95916f4605895f8fc","verification":{"payload":"tree dc533c7ca3d90a716e946964177ae5f40af690da\nparent 6cf2f876d27cc78d586daf00915079971a2019da\nauthor Lucas Barga <lucasmpbarga@gmail.com> 1780177369 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780177369 -0300\n\nfeat: automatic filtering on every agent (shim + universal read-guard + auto-learning) — 0.12.0→0.15.0 (#6)\n\n* feat: memory-file compression via local AI CLI (0.12.x)\n\nAdd `lakonai compress-memory <file>` (+ `revert-memory`): manual, opt-in\ncompression of authored memory (CLAUDE.md, notes) using whichever local AI CLI\nthe user already has — claude/gemini/codex/cursor-agent, auto-detected on PATH\n(LAKONAI_MEM_CLI / LAKONAI_MEM_MODEL overrides). No API key.\n\nSafety harness (src/mem-compress.js): always writes a <name>.original.md backup\nfirst, validates every fenced/inline code span and URL survives byte-for-byte\n(one fix pass, else aborts untouched), refuses sensitive filenames. Provider\nregistry + prompts in src/mem-llm.js. `install` offers a one-time opt-in prompt.\nUnlike MCP catalog shrink, never automatic — it rewrites authored prose.\n\nTwo engines by domain: regex for machine/high-frequency (shell output, MCP\ncatalogs), LLM only for authored prose (memory). Lands together with the\npreviously-unreleased MCP auto-compression + command-surface simplification.\n\nREADME: sellable marketing pass (four-fronts framing, surfaced MCP + memory).\nCLAUDE.md: rule to keep the npm About page in sync (republish on README change).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: universal PATH shim — automatic shell filtering on every agent (0.13.0)\n\n`lakonai shim` makes shell-output filtering automatic on agents without a\ncall-rewriting hook (Codex/Cursor/Windsurf/Cline/Gemini), not just Claude Code.\nDrops executable wrappers for ls/grep/rg/ag/find/cat/tree/head into\n~/.lakon/shim/ and prepends it to PATH via a managed block in the shell rc, so\nany agent that runs those commands through a shell routes them through lakonai —\nno hook API, no model cooperation.\n\ngit/tail excluded (editors/streaming). Recursion prevented: runAndFilter spawns\nthe real binary with pathWithoutShim(PATH) so the shim dir is excluded\n(end-to-end tested). Opt-in (edits shell rc); reaches agents that inherit the\nshell PATH.\n\nREADME capability matrix updated: shell filtering now automatic on all six\nagents via the shim. Read/Grep guard + auto-learning stay Claude-only — they act\non the agent''s own tool calls, which needs a call-rewriting hook (today only\nClaude Code''s; Codex blocked upstream, openai/codex#18491).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: universal Read-guard on the shell path (0.14.0)\n\n`lakonai cat`/`head`/`tail`/`less`/`more`/`bat` now refuse junk reads (lockfiles,\nnode_modules, build artifacts) using the same deny rules as the Claude Read hook\n(src/shim-guard.js, reusing read-guard.isDeniedPath). Checked in runAndFilter\nbefore spawning: a denied path is skipped with a one-line reason + 0-token track.\n\nCombined with the PATH shim, junk-read protection is now automatic on EVERY\nagent for shell-mediated reads (`cat pnpm-lock.yaml` -> skipped), not just Claude\nCode''s Read tool. The agent''s own non-shell Read tool still needs a hook (Claude\nonly). Auto-learning stays Claude-only (it needs the agent''s full command stream)\nand is largely moot elsewhere since the shim already filters the standard set.\n\nMatrix updated honestly: shell filter + shell-read guard automatic on all six;\ninternal-tool guard + auto-learning Claude-only, with sourced upstream reasons.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: platform-agnostic auto-learning + cleaner install output (0.15.0)\n\nAuto-learning now also runs off ~/.lakon/log.jsonl (appended by every lakonai\ncall — shim wrappers + rule-prefixed commands — on ANY agent), not just the\nClaude transcript. learn.analyzeLog / maybeLearnFromLog (throttled hourly) are\ncalled from runAndFilter, so heavy non-builtin commands get promoted to the\nfiltered set automatically on every agent. With the shim, all four input-side\nfeatures now run automatically everywhere for shell-mediated work; only guarding\nthe agent''s own non-shell Read tool stays Claude-only (needs a rewriting hook).\n\nAlso: Claude Code install line shows \"+ N slash commands\" instead of the full\nlist. CLAUDE.md: rule that releases publish via CI only (never manual npm\npublish) — assistant scope is commit/PR/merge at most.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","si