es OUTPUT savings via the user''s claude CLI\n  (3 arms, honest delta vs concise); scripts/bench-measure.js aggregates a\n  committed snapshot offline (CI-safe). npm run bench / bench:output / bench:measure.\n\nmcp-shrink: shipped as a SEPARATE sibling package `lakonai-shrink` (not in this repo).\n\n294 tests, 100% coverage.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"439de1b213990eb908dd3624ca8ed90f17375c87","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bargadev/lakonai/git/trees/439de1b213990eb908dd3624ca8ed90f17375c87"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bargadev/lakonai/git/commits/e2cca294c460f11dd16fd6480d4dedc1939a8fe1","verification":{"payload":"tree 439de1b213990eb908dd3624ca8ed90f17375c87\nparent f3e0c4c8d06c757366780be047c557c6f5d81e42\nauthor Lucas Barga <lucasmpbarga@gmail.com> 1780152586 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780152586 -0300\n\nfeat: implement the 5 plans — doctor, capability matrix, shell wrapper, subagents, output bench (0.10.0) (#4)\n\nsix-platforms:\n- `lakonai doctor` (src/doctor.js): per-platform CLI/rule/hooks health.\n- Honest capability matrix in README (hooks are Claude-Code-only).\n- platforms get rulePath() for doctor.\n\ncross-platform:\n- `lakonai shell-init`/`shell-uninit` (src/shell.js): opt-in shell wrapper that\n  auto-filters read-only commands when LAKON_SHELL=1.\n\ncavecrew:\n- terse subagents installed on Claude Code (investigator/builder/reviewer) via\n  src/install/claude-agents.js.\n\nbench-e2e:\n- scripts/bench-output.js measures OUTPUT savings via the user''s claude CLI\n  (3 arms, honest delta vs concise); scripts/bench-measure.js aggregates a\n  committed snapshot offline (CI-safe). npm run bench / bench:output / bench:measure.\n\nmcp-shrink: shipped as a SEPARATE sibling package `lakonai-shrink` (not in this repo).\n\n294 tests, 100% coverage.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQB