r"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T23:01:17.206Z","repositoryId":1238266408,"sha":"4b7576493030bbadba2d6af0eaddc1c9b3317174"}],"observedAt":"2026-10-08T23:01:17.206Z","raw":[{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63979266?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Elesiann","id":63979266,"login":"Elesiann","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzOTc5MjY2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commits/42494e77ece3327ef7c2ff375bdfc6bcb1e93fea/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T14:55:04Z","email":"giovanimcorrea18@gmail.com","name":"Giovani"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T14:55:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(presets): enable paged LDAP search in the ldapOrg ingestion blocks (#202)\n\nWithout RFC 2696 paging, LdapClient.search issues a single unpaged search.\nAny directory whose server-side size limit is smaller than the result set\n(AD caps at MaxPageSize=1000 by default; OpenLDAP at 500) fails the search\nwith SizeLimitExceededError, and LdapOrgEntityProvider aborts the WHOLE\nrefresh run — the catalog ends up with zero User entities, and every login\n404s with \"User not found\" even though the LDAP bind itself succeeds.\nThis is the default posture for the exact target of `ldap-ad`: a corporate\nActive Directory with >1000 users.\n\nReproduced against veecode/devportal:2.2.2 + OpenLDAP with an AD-like\nlimits profile (size.hard=2, size.pr=100, size.prtotal=unlimited):\nstock preset → ingestion aborts, login 404 \"User not found\" (141-byte\nbody, byte-identical to the field report); with `paged: true` → ingestion\ncompletes and the same login returns 200.\n\n`ldap-ad` must carry its own `paged` since arrays replace on config merge.\nPreset versions: ldap 1.1.0 → 1.2.0, ldap-ad 2.1.0 → 2.2.0.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011qk5FVbw3akXQfqUXVzmbd\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"eb6024cf26cd4211cdd8af6ab9fbefd609bd927c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/git/trees/eb6024cf26cd4211cdd8af6ab9fbefd609bd927c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/git/commits/42494e77ece3327ef7c2ff375bdfc6bcb1e93fea","verification":{"payload":"tree eb6024cf26cd4211cdd8af6ab9fbefd609bd927c\nparent fe976221622812786dee9784e9a231750d7ba958\nauthor Giovani <giovanimcorrea18@gmail.com> 1788447304 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788447304 -0300\n\nfix(presets): enable paged LDAP search in the ldapOrg ingestion blocks (#202)\n\nWithout RFC 2696 paging, LdapClient.search issues a single unpaged search.\nAny directory whose server-side size limit is smaller than the result set\n(AD caps at MaxPageSize=1000 by default; OpenLDAP at 500) fails the search\nwith SizeLimitExceededError, and LdapOrgEntityProvider aborts the WHOLE\nrefresh run — the catalog ends up with zero User entities, and every login\n404s with \"User not found\" even though the LDAP bind itself succeeds.\nThis is the default posture for the exact target of `ldap-ad`: a corporate\nActive Directory with >1000 users.\n\nReproduced against veecode/devportal:2.2.2 + OpenLDAP with an AD-like\nlimits profile (size.hard=2, size.pr=100, size.prtotal=unlimited):\nstock preset → ingestion aborts, login 404 \"User not found\" (141-byte\nbody, byte-identical to the field report); with `paged: true` → ingestion\ncompletes and the same login returns 200.\n\n`ldap-ad` must carry its own `paged` since arrays replace on config merge.\nPreset versions: ldap 1.1.0 → 1.2.0, ldap-ad 2.1.0 → 2.2.0.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011qk5FVbw3akXQfqUXVzmbd\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmYpICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqYMQAD1HkkoZs6sC+HtHnDynRzj2\nA9Yq4CmHODSZSNXoZTD56L9oRv5P+Yk2YPYGuyN4DcSHOyLkjJhOWUR/StFoDrxy\nY6gB6eQ+gC9V8Q3N6kDYB50o8CriZ9ZVkUuuiLJv6ibvXq9T4cyvc1yLNRNSZnoY\n2ke2/YjbV1/k0EdojoV7t7AkVR1XLrzEy+NuG8mmf8xVVtaswaGIf344Yykt9DWi\ndZwu6aCCBsiWIcbT3N7vTi76YucN43IZkvx+MoHrxRFvjXUdLggku0t5ttj/hSNI\ncg5Swa6vpjTyHj5wmbuD0QUGU3fiopWVbRMZW0e0RX7b8Bxb+vsq9DNQ3zT0poAV\n81Ytc9XlidBstQd/qeeq9FqDRLudbjmJ6yDqP8MqdFfX047n49SOq4DXHThcHPeQ\nyq34fOowl+/2Urwsf/bbHqayYOIuCQ6f3uCwcqjpyqgM6ruQTbfqcpbLS3TWSGES\nIqlkVhoeXnYhDE9vAoDG9C1VmVpYzrc3Xsk3/gGBUaEEpJeDyhFwBXBbzg0WbUKD\ndazDQZ71ZxpWp8ANy9eAz04KI+QbRjxqNg4Hx/BdKeQ1HQYMxFKIiISNmwAdhb4C\nevhx5LrI+RJz0L9Tle6XAh1MZRKVpBwK5mzL2nUch+e0Q5eyvI0IvecrhQJYqlay\nJNpQQ6fXDsl2EEPFnbiX\n=r5Fy\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-03T14:55:05Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commit/42494e77ece3327ef7c2ff375bdfc6bcb1e93fea","node_id":"C_kwDOSc5yKNoAKDQyNDk0ZTc3ZWNlMzMyN2VmN2MyZmYzNzViZGZjNmJjYjFlOTNmZWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commit/fe976221622812786dee9784e9a231750d7ba958","sha":"fe976221622812786dee9784e9a231750d7ba958","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commits/fe976221622812786dee9784e9a231750d7ba958"}],"sha":"42494e77ece3327ef7c2ff375bdfc6bcb1e93fea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commits/42494e77ece3327ef7c2ff375bdfc6bcb1e93fea"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63979266?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Elesiann","id":63979266,"login":"Elesiann","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzOTc5MjY2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commits/fe976221622812786dee9784e9a231750d7ba958/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T18:21:36Z","email":"giovanimcorrea18@gmail.com","name":"Giovani"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T18:21:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(presets): declare the LDAP auth block on both NODE_ENV ramps (#195)\n\nThe ldap auth plugin resolves its config sub-key from process.env.NODE_ENV — a\nprocess variable, not config:\n\n  // @veecode-platform/backstage-plugin-ldap-auth-backend, dist/provider.cjs.js\n  const cnf = config.get(process.env.NODE_ENV || ''development'')\n\nIt cannot honour the `auth.environment: production` this preset already sets,\nthe way this platform''s own authProvidersModule.ts does, because\nplugin-auth-backend hands a provider factory only the `auth.providers.<id>`\nsubtree (providers/router.cjs.js: `providersConfig.getConfig(providerId)`).\n\nBoth presets declared only the `production` ramp, so a pod whose NODE_ENV is\n`development` resolves a ramp that does not exist. plugin-auth-backend then\ntakes its lenient path (the throw is guarded by `NODE_ENV !== \"development\"`),\nlogs a WARN and installs a stub route:\n\n  auth warn Skipping ldap auth provider, Missing required config value at\n            ''auth.providers.ldap.development'' in ''app-config.preset-ldap-ad.yaml''\n\nThe pod stays healthy, /healthcheck returns 200, the ldapOrg catalog sync runs\nnormally — and every login 404s with \"Auth provider registered for ''ldap'' is\nmisconfigured\", which reads as a credential failure and is not. Reported from\nthe field on 2.2.1.\n\nDeclare the block on both ramps via a YAML anchor rather than a copy: two copies\ndrifting is the same class of bug. ldap-ad mirrors the ramps too — overriding\nonly `production` leaves a development pod authenticating against `uid` instead\nof `sAMAccountName`, which registers the provider and then fails against a real\nAD (harder to diagnose than the provider going missing).\n\nThe smoke harness could not have caught this: for identity presets it stopped at\n/healthcheck 200, and every combo ran under the image''s default\nNODE_ENV=production, where the old presets register fine. Two changes, neither\nsufficient alone: identity combos now assert the boot log carries no\n`Skipping <id> auth provider` / `Failed to initialize <id> auth provider`; and a\n`+devenv` modifier (mirroring `+mount`) boots with NODE_ENV=development, plus the\n`ldap,ldap-ad+devenv` combo. dev-run.sh forwards env by allowlist, so NODE_ENV\nwas added there.\n\nVerified against a real OpenLDAP with veecode/devportal:2.2.1: NODE_ENV=development\nplus the old presets reproduces the field log byte-for-byte and the same 404 body;\nwith these presets the same boot logs in a 200 login. Red/green of the new gate\nagainst 2.3.1-rc.1: pre-fix presets report FAIL_AUTH_PROVIDER_DROPPED, fixed\npresets pass. All eight identity combos still pass.\n\nThe `development` ramp can be dropped once the plugin stops keying off NODE_ENV\n(devportal-plugins#90) and that release is pinned in yarn.lock here.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0127jXKT4Mkhqn7jaLp9E4QE","tree":{"sha":"8203ef8a50617d7fedae81d9cc8e954088f57cfe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/git/trees/8203ef8a50617d7fedae81d9cc8e954088f57cfe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/git/commits/fe976221622812786dee9784e9a231750d7ba958","verification":{"payload":"tree 8203ef8a50617d7fedae81d9cc8e954088f57cfe\nparent ee38a31e9c3706a63c49c09da1075c701d0e6971\nauthor Giovani <giovanimcorrea18@gmail.com> 1788200496 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788200496 -0300\n\nfix(presets): declare the LDAP auth block on both NODE_ENV ramps (#195)\n\nThe ldap auth plugin resolves its config sub-key from process.env.NODE_ENV — a\nprocess variable, not config:\n\n  // @veecode-platform/backstage-plugin-ldap-auth-backend, dist/provider.cjs.js\n  const cnf = config.get(process.env.NODE_ENV || ''development'')\n\nIt cannot honour the `auth.environment: production` this preset already sets,\nthe way this platform''s own authProvidersModule.ts does, because\nplugin-auth-backend hands a provider factory only the `auth.providers.<id>`\nsubtree (providers/router.cjs.js: `providersConfig.getConfig(providerId)`).\n\nBoth presets declared only the `production` ramp, so a pod whose NODE_ENV is\n`development` resolves a ramp that does not exist. plugin-auth-backend then\ntakes its lenient path (the throw is guarded by `NODE_ENV !== \"development\"`),\nlogs a WARN and installs a stub route:\n\n  auth warn Skipping ldap auth provider, Missing required config value at\n            ''auth.providers.ldap.development'' in ''app-config.preset-ldap-ad.yaml''\n\nThe pod stays healthy, /healthcheck returns 200, the ldapOrg catalog sync runs\nnormally — and every login 404s with \"Auth provider registered for ''ldap'' is\nmisconfigured\", which reads as a credential failure and is not. Reported from\nthe field on 2.2.1.\n\nDeclare the block on both ramps via a YAML anchor rather than a copy: two copies\ndrifting is the same class of bug. ldap-ad mirrors the ramps too — overriding\nonly `production` leaves a development pod authenticating against `uid` instead\nof `sAMAccountName`, which registers the provider and then fails against a real\nAD (harder to diagnose than the provider going missing).\n\nThe smoke harness could not have caught this: for identity presets it stopped at\n/healthcheck 200, and every combo ran under the image''s default\nNODE_ENV=production, where the old presets register fine. Two changes, neither\nsufficient alone: identity combos now assert the boot log carries no\n`Skipping <id> auth provider` / `Failed to initialize <id> auth provider`; and a\n`+devenv` modifier (mirroring `+mount`) boots with NODE_ENV=development, plus the\n`ldap,ldap-ad+devenv` combo. dev-run.sh forwards env by allowlist, so NODE_ENV\nwas added there.\n\nVerified against a real OpenLDAP with veecode/devportal:2.2.1: NODE_ENV=development\nplus the old presets reproduces the field log byte-for-byte and the same 404 body;\nwith these presets the same boot logs in a 200 login. Red/green of the new gate\nagainst 2.3.1-rc.1: pre-fix presets report FAIL_AUTH_PROVIDER_DROPPED, fixed\npresets pass. All eight identity combos still pass.\n\nThe `development` ramp can be dropped once the plugin stops keying off NODE_ENV\n(devportal-plugins#90) and that release is pinned in yarn.lock here.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0127jXKT4Mkhqn7jaLp9E4QE","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlcYwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAiQEQAEEQtlRfAD18J/nNTxoSusHW\n6JBQIV/rYiJqbCe3FHuR/MLFAm5IHpoB2rz0Ks28qRNx1maF2SoaP9KL1xu70EAg\nf01fsRaAIsVa2YYChP40Mh+uJikJXge2kMnAdGm9R/+qNJM8viHxD9DDKepHYKRa\nnUHsRZW0kJrH7VPIt1oD9Vs9nZfrErc+QZz2zyC46+6z/Z7z22ZU0d1SMB1RL7mE\nGy2l3w9zNyaoyFz3rA0ds+EYidhrQya4v+zk/unIvz6pHLatX6KySIb3q5wHKYWe\nHwwCc7m7IsQ/VOeePc6686x7W9NoxQcTyLfqiuwo/+jQ66QqyKmLWe+Z87yh56eR\nW3QQ3CeueryakTSM/eCErHXIDWz+7B5saD3yQQ73297OIlDrq7BbybXauqyHmvV3\nelRWKGqsrQAcWeoiWF67FLVEKDi1g+fSeiZv8u7ZgFhhRx4wFVUQdjE90dK1aOLG\nPJK0Nh15y1nn9poFWRVA8jMREc8HGZdVrWFMKtU+iz2Zenj5y5euszcZKlkU8wfv\natCqa6QOmJnLGknSdOan5r4u4XN0vRdRA5+5qU9dKTZs8mT2P99iCQmJhy7jRx38\n5bmalMF942aS36wuMQyyQZEbZ9oXrC9dAruH7Oxs3ilduBaF4YGfpYpDykeBkMFG\n56sL94sXeDWDY15kQhlK\n=H3eD\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-31T18:21:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commit/fe976221622812786dee9784e9a231750d7ba958","node_id":"C_kwDOSc5yKNoAKGZlOTc2MjIxNjIyODEyNzg2ZGVlOTc4NGU5YTIzMTc1MGQ3YmE5NTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commit/ee38a31e9c3706a63c49c09da1075c701d0e6971","sha":"ee38a31e9c3706a63c49c09da1075c701d0e6971","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commits/ee38a31e9c3706a63c49c09da1075c701d0e6971"}],"sha":"fe976221622812786dee9784e9a231750d7ba958","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commits/fe976221622812786dee9784e9a231750d7ba958"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63979266?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Elesiann","id":63979266,"login":"Elesiann","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzOTc5MjY2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commits/ee38a31e9c3706a63c49c09da1075c701d0e6971/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-24T20:05:39Z","email":"giovanimcorrea18@gmail.com","name":"Giovani"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-24T20:05:39Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: support {{inherit}} tags and bare per-plugin OCI refs in installer (#186)\n\n* fix: support {{inherit}} tags and bare per-plugin OCI refs in installer\n\nADR-008 phase 3: the vendorized install-dynamic-plugins.py required a\n`!<selector>` suffix on every OCI ref (package.split(''!'') crashes with\nValueError otherwise), with no support for the new one-image-per-plugin\nformat or the `{{inherit}}` tag placeholder. Backporting upstream RHDH''s\nTS rewrite was assessed and rejected (no Python original to diff\nagainst, ~40-file port, would drop this fork''s own hardening); this\nships a minimal, targeted patch instead: parse_oci_package() +\nresolve_inherit_refs() + manifest-annotation auto-detection for bare\nrefs (falls back to the image''s own repo name when absent).\n\npresets/mcp.yaml moves to pinned per-plugin refs (verified via skopeo),\nnot {{inherit}} — entrypoint.sh''s includes: chain only carries\nextensions-install.yaml + preset fragments (dynamic-plugins.default.yaml\nis documentation-only, never included), so there is no pinned base for\na preset ref to inherit from yet. Losing ${BACKSTAGE_VERSION} templating\non these 4 refs and the includes-chain gap for the rest of the preset\ncatalog are both documented in docs/OCI_PLUGINS.md as follow-up work.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01A27F3Wt2ShmWyVkvcy4Q1S\n\n* docs: hedge unverified tenant/Helm-chart installer claim\n\nThe tenant-runs-upstream-TS-installer detail came from the requesting\nteammate''s message, not from anything checked in this repo or its\nsibling — flag it as such instead of stating it as verified fact.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01A27F3Wt2ShmWyVkvcy4Q1S\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"77596bee6e4367aaeec08bb9f6c651fd10870144","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/git/trees/77596bee6e4367aaeec08bb9f6c651fd10870144"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/git/commits/ee38a31e9c3706a63c49c09da1075c701d0e6971","verification":{"payload":"tree 77596bee6e4367aaeec08bb9f6c651fd10870144\nparent 1354fe92932f21fb65620ffe10ccd914a5a7bf5b\nauthor Giovani <giovanimcorrea18@gmail.com> 1787601939 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787601939 -0300\n\nfix: support {{inherit}} tags and bare per-plugin OCI refs in installer (#186)\n\n* fix: support {{inherit}} tags and bare per-plugin OCI refs in installer\n\nADR-008 phase 3: the vendorized install-dynamic-plugins.py required a\n`!<selector>` suffix on every OCI ref (package.split(''!'') crashes with\nValueError otherwise), with no support for the new one-image-per-plugin\nformat or the `{{inherit}}` tag placeholder. Backporting upstream RHDH''s\nTS rewrite was assessed and rejected (no Python original to diff\nagainst, ~40-file port, would drop this fork''s own hardening); this\nships a minimal, targeted patch instead: parse_oci_package() +\nresolve_inherit_refs() + manifest-annotation auto-detection for bare\nrefs (falls back to the image''s own repo name when absent).\n\npresets/mcp.yaml moves to pinned per-plugin refs (verified via skopeo),\nnot {{inherit}} — entrypoint.sh''s includes: chain only carries\nextensions-install.yaml + preset fragments (dynamic-plugins.default.yaml\nis documentation-only, never included), so there is no pinned base for\na preset ref to inherit from yet. Losing ${BACKSTAGE_VERSION} templating\non these 4 refs and the includes-chain gap for the rest of the preset\ncatalog are both documented in docs/OCI_PLUGINS.md as follow-up work.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01A27F3Wt2ShmWyVkvcy4Q1S\n\n* docs: hedge unverified tenant/Helm-chart installer claim\n\nThe tenant-runs-upstream-TS-installer detail came from the requesting\nteammate''s message, not from anything checked in this repo or its\nsibling — flag it as such instead of stating it as verified fact.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01A27F3Wt2ShmWyVkvcy4Q1S\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjKQTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAzL8QAKDjtbfTfcqHbYeDuN3EZcTZ\nIVMgNTY0oOXrnFETq+JyuUFZUFDO2ZDajcrjkxLN9Y/VTfjJ/WMc+3yDGOdI16TP\nJmaFvK27/roucmYYJ9E9uj80uBaVfaKfh2Q/vHAdN3Mou+vHrQYW6/yEnQmUqFot\nxoKNMMiFhD3zx1RURySbbx831vi/CevPoL0fhnAOJtRmBEhpr7ENE7GYHw94ZnHn\nupnpzPjrMjeMAO3UZd5Onbl6ya+s0LvhKvjUxtjQ4kfmLS4mn/FwtlqshOoNkQLL\nw/8zdZ1EnNnCLOplJ+2bt0+VnapJLYWn2bfsUxR8c+dAZt4HW/0RZUopFe0s5VEu\nQnXF4iPiAcIg5sGEv+zMeaRvQuJeRrvXbwbRIN29YU/jW176AakDAdH9PHRs1iB8\nC9ReUZN0Nn6c058bLOlPe4O0e5WY0ztxIdzJhYxr4RQdIC9vFdKKVmowXjwp0D/4\nFrDapNLVNMoFdHflQ7Xt1BSgwU/aCE3EGBiXdR7PRyyYp3ThIJNaSXhuLtlC6NuK\nA2kSx1BiMIIHBHl1F5PYfK6v45mGhdRYBXr9jQKFStB/jgxZi5KiSNmcKXtFYeii\nV1fz1a47lVu8l2Ee5JCoQFZxaca+mXVm427o+XT/CdLYKnWk/6qBEsYC+hdEWNpa\nhHcEzbRmxS2UleKme+ay\n=sXiW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-24T20:05:40Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commit/ee38a31e9c3706a63c49c09da1075c701d0e6971","node_id":"C_kwDOSc5yKNoAKGVlMzhhMzFlOWMzNzA2YTYzYzQ5YzA5ZGExMDc1YzcwMWQwZTY5NzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commit/1354fe92932f21fb65620ffe10ccd914a5a7bf5b","sha":"1354fe92932f21fb65620ffe10ccd914a5a7bf5b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commits/1354fe92932f21fb65620ffe10ccd914a5a7bf5b"}],"sha":"ee38a31e9c3706a63c49c09da1075c701d0e6971","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commits/ee38a31e9c3706a63c49c09da1075c701d0e6971"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63979266?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Elesiann","id":63979266,"login":"Elesiann","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzOTc5MjY2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commits/1354fe92932f21fb65620ffe10ccd914a5a7bf5b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-06T18:58:52Z","email":"giovanimcorrea18@gmail.com","name":"Giovani"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-06T18:58:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci(nfs): register the nfs/next publish channel on the default branch (#161)\n\nworkflow_dispatch only exists for a workflow file present on the default\nbranch, so this channel was undispatchable — gh workflow run returned 404 and\nthe publish=false dry run could not be reached at all. A dispatch still runs\nthe definition from the ref you select, so nfs/next stays the branch that\nbuilds; this copy exists to make the trigger appear.\n\nmain carries Dockerfile.nfs and packages/app-next as well, which is the hazard\nthat registration introduces: dispatched on the default ref this would build\nmain''s older app-next and, with publish=true, point :next at it. So this copy\nadds a ref guard that fails before the first build step. The nfs/next copy\nneeds no guard — its ref always matches — and the divergence is that one\nguarded step, documented in the file header.\n\nNothing else about main changes. No NFS application code, no touch to\npublish.yml or the OFS Dockerfile.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e4a75e30b129c9559bf61bfdecc0edbcf948bb96","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/git/trees/e4a75e30b129c9559bf61bfdecc0edbcf948bb96"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/git/commits/1354fe92932f21fb65620ffe10ccd914a5a7bf5b","verification":{"payload":"tree e4a75e30b129c9559bf61bfdecc0edbcf948bb96\nparent 4894fce66fec88a55b6f258d374bfeed96ed53e8\nauthor Giovani <giovanimcorrea18@gmail.com> 1786042732 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786042732 -0300\n\nci(nfs): register the nfs/next publish channel on the default branch (#161)\n\nworkflow_dispatch only exists for a workflow file present on the default\nbranch, so this channel was undispatchable — gh workflow run returned 404 and\nthe publish=false dry run could not be reached at all. A dispatch still runs\nthe definition from the ref you select, so nfs/next stays the branch that\nbuilds; this copy exists to make the trigger appear.\n\nmain carries Dockerfile.nfs and packages/app-next as well, which is the hazard\nthat registration introduces: dispatched on the default ref this would build\nmain''s older app-next and, with publish=true, point :next at it. So this copy\nadds a ref guard that fails before the first build step. The nfs/next copy\nneeds no guard — its ref always matches — and the divergence is that one\nguarded step, documented in the file header.\n\nNothing else about main changes. No NFS application code, no touch to\npublish.yml or the OFS Dockerfile.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqdNlsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAREgQAC8tucijjZHp+GB9tsAH8uTN\nD4EsrxqF54B2rjmh2lEm47E3yE6liZxm/T3MSU+osQeUcZJjPqIdI/Qz6Ndt1YsR\nNNwYgDqc14bPi2u7bQW0Yr0XI9RU8Yom2WI74PA3cicF6Dpea/tPmGme4ifLQBAT\nGbNR3JvPymMoKCpDXTdiGfMgg8dw+sIb56Oo+bVzm4xDycPTNaC74kazw2HrP/cV\n5gLqLfl9ArhxXQaf9F91ML1b92UIl41qk2iYZwZHVTRwhRv9YFvbBtTq26SRPXKb\nJEWR/DAlUx73onq27WcuRbOBj4iKXEbpka1bxmBb8ib0KUq3cn/nUvhusP1k0EM0\nHdGfrB0DPr