,"html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","id":41898282,"login":"github-actions[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commits/a46fbf97700ff4fbeb5e8b3706b9ed92e914f412/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-27T20:18:27Z","email":"41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"github-actions[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-27T20:18:27Z","email":"41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"github-actions[bot]"},"message":"chore: release 2.3.0-rc.2","tree":{"sha":"ee84e8c0f29cc4a9debe325bd8051c5da772481a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/git/trees/ee84e8c0f29cc4a9debe325bd8051c5da772481a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/git/commits/a46fbf97700ff4fbeb5e8b3706b9ed92e914f412","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","id":41898282,"login":"github-actions[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commit/a46fbf97700ff4fbeb5e8b3706b9ed92e914f412","node_id":"C_kwDOSc5yKNoAKGE0NmZiZjk3NzAwZmY0ZmJlYjVlOGIzNzA2YjllZDkyZTkxNGY0MTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commit/983738ca184d2d57956c6fc93cfabb15dfb79145","sha":"983738ca184d2d57956c6fc93cfabb15dfb79145","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commits/983738ca184d2d57956c6fc93cfabb15dfb79145"}],"sha":"a46fbf97700ff4fbeb5e8b3706b9ed92e914f412","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commits/a46fbf97700ff4fbeb5e8b3706b9ed92e914f412"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63979266?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Elesiann","id":63979266,"login":"Elesiann","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzOTc5MjY2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commits/983738ca184d2d57956c6fc93cfabb15dfb79145/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-27T19:19:00Z","email":"giovanimcorrea18@gmail.com","name":"Giovani"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-27T19:19:00Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(publish): label the image and announce it to Drydock (#138)\n\nThe image carried no VeeCode provenance: every label on the config blob was\ninherited from ubi10/nodejs-22-minimal, including a misleading version=10.1.\nNothing in the artefact said which Backstage it was built against, so Drydock\ncould verify a fleet against the wrong runtime and still reach\nREADY_FOR_PROMOTION (veecode-drydock issue #26).\n\nThree labels now come from source, not literals — backstage.json is the single\nsource of truth for io.veecode.devportal.backstage-version. The manifest job\nexports the manifest-list digest, and a new leaf job hands both to Drydock so a\nBumpRun anchors on an exact digest instead of an operator pasting one by hand.\n\nnotify-drydock is separate from notify-downstream on purpose. It must fire for\npre-releases, which notify-downstream deliberately skips, because the Factory''s\ntarget images are RCs. It also uses workflow_dispatch rather than\nrepository_dispatch: for a fine-grained token the former needs only\nActions:write on drydock, while the latter needs Contents:write — a token able\nto push code into the repo it is merely notifying.\n\nBoth notifiers stay leaf jobs that cannot fail a release: a missing secret,\nan unavailable digest, or a failed call warns and exits 0.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"365eb2d62ac83021466aa6994a1dcb89869ed600","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/git/trees/365eb2d62ac83021466aa6994a1dcb89869ed600"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/git/commits/983738ca184d2d57956c6fc93cfabb15dfb79145","verification":{"payload":"tree 365eb2d62ac83021466aa6994a1dcb89869ed600\nparent 074ad8b09465f0d3fc71acdaa566b2670c3ce8be\nauthor Giovani <giovanimcorrea18@gmail.com> 1785179940 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785179940 -0300\n\nfeat(publish): label the image and announce it to Drydock (#138)\n\nThe image carried no VeeCode provenance: every label on the config blob was\ninherited from ubi10/nodejs-22-minimal, including a misleading version=10.1.\nNothing in the artefact said which Backstage it was built against, so Drydock\ncould verify a fleet against the wrong runtime and still reach\nREADY_FOR_PROMOTION (veecode-drydock issue #26).\n\nThree labels now come from source, not literals — backstage.json is the single\nsource of truth for io.veecode.devportal.backstage-version. The manifest job\nexports the manifest-list digest, and a new leaf job hands both to Drydock so a\nBumpRun anchors on an exact digest instead of an operator pasting one by hand.\n\nnotify-drydock is separate from notify-downstream on purpose. It must fire for\npre-releases, which notify-downstream deliberately skips, because the Factory''s\ntarget images are RCs. It also uses workflow_dispatch rather than\nrepository_dispatch: for a fine-grained token the former needs only\nActions:write on drydock, while the latter needs Contents:write — a token able\nto push code into the repo it is merely notifying.\n\nBoth notifiers stay leaf jobs that cannot fail a release: a missing secret,\nan unavailable digest, or a failed call warns and exits 0.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"--