lowing_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Elesiann","id":63979266,"login":"Elesiann","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzOTc5MjY2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commits/aa792bd6a8439b7efcf7deb79227f4d892c8b03c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-17T18:40:51Z","email":"giovanimcorrea18@gmail.com","name":"Giovani"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-17T18:40:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(presets): drop dynamic scaffolder-backend-module-sonarqube (static collision) (#119)\n\nThe sonarqube preset enabled the OCI dynamic plugin for\n@backstage-community/plugin-scaffolder-backend-module-sonarqube, but that\nmodule is already compiled statically into the backend\n(packages/backend/src/index.ts). Loading both makes Backstage''s module\nregistry throw \"Module ''scaffolder-backend-sonarqube'' for plugin\n''scaffolder'' is already registered\" and the boot crashes — any deploy\nwith VEECODE_PRESETS including ''sonarqube'' hits this.\n\nThe static module already provides the sonarqube:create-project action\nand reads the preset''s appConfig.sonarqube block, so the dynamic entry\nwas pure redundancy. Same convention azure.yaml already uses for its two\nstatic-only modules (documented with a comment in place of the entry).\n\nEvidence: veecode-drydock fleet baseline, findings/12 + findings/15.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"82b9c8c2d61279dc4a301230c80fb58172dabd90","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/git/trees/82b9c8c2d61279dc4a301230c80fb58172dabd90"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/git/commits/aa792bd6a8439b7efcf7deb79227f4d892c8b03c","verification":{"payload":"tree 82b9c8c2d61279dc4a301230c80fb58172dabd90\nparent 60227dc8091c8700d4520fcd6ff6f09d689f6687\nauthor Giovani <giovanimcorrea18@gmail.com> 1784313651 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784313651 -0300\n\nfix(presets): drop dynamic scaffolder-backend-module-sonarqube (static collision) (#119)\n\nThe sonarqube preset enabled the OCI dynamic plugin for\n@backstage-community/plugin-scaffolder-backend-module-sonarqube, but that\nmodule is already compiled statically into the backend\n(packages/backend/src/index.ts). Loading both makes Backstage''s module\nregistry throw \"Module ''scaffolder-backend-sonarqube'' for plugin\n''scaffolder'' is already registered\" and the boot crashes — any deploy\nwith VEECODE_PRESETS including ''sonarqube'' hits this.\n\nThe static module already provides the sonarqube:create-project action\nand reads the preset''s appConfig.sonarqube block, so the dynamic entry\nwas pure redundancy. Same convention azure.yaml already uses for its two\nstatic-only modules (documented with a comment in place of the entry).\n\nEvidence: veecode-drydock fleet baseline, findings/12 + findings/15.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqWnczCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAm/AQABLyJvLJG53QLxLzkvhd+LLX\n/nUMA1SZ6Q98gRqJyiu8Gg+FpuItWeja/Iis1R1eLPlOZPBlVv7UkebkdJrgIFFY\n78n8WkjXQjn+k5wEptm/XWKqqbMJSQ5wT3X6ou6HMJkj0qWzdaegj3HP211cSajt\noOnQIxGvvAOvtrmbqDPQoairSF4Vkwe78x5Vf34bjWp9MRFuWAvTAsISUcL+9f6g\nDWgaRhDPrY58tay2fiFFNNKocpfs64zr6rJHu8m5gUiS5KiBpxsJFKyzPas/qNe4\nfeJ83vWXtJQprDVq