r":{"date":"2026-06-22T17:56:58Z","email":"41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"github-actions[bot]"},"message":"chore: release 2.2.0","tree":{"sha":"cf7909e4267dfb3f6e0b2035bab2cbb98cc5922c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/git/trees/cf7909e4267dfb3f6e0b2035bab2cbb98cc5922c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/git/commits/827965c40b77f53867edd4f3970473bf1e9b75cd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","id":41898282,"login":"github-actions[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commit/827965c40b77f53867edd4f3970473bf1e9b75cd","node_id":"C_kwDOSc5yKNoAKDgyNzk2NWM0MGI3N2Y1Mzg2N2VkZDRmMzk3MDQ3M2JmMWU5Yjc1Y2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commit/75baf075574dd50b06d8048861de91df7a2ec60e","sha":"75baf075574dd50b06d8048861de91df7a2ec60e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commits/75baf075574dd50b06d8048861de91df7a2ec60e"}],"sha":"827965c40b77f53867edd4f3970473bf1e9b75cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commits/827965c40b77f53867edd4f3970473bf1e9b75cd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63979266?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Elesiann","id":63979266,"login":"Elesiann","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzOTc5MjY2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commits/75baf075574dd50b06d8048861de91df7a2ec60e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-22T17:52:54Z","email":"giovanimcorrea18@gmail.com","name":"Giovani"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-22T17:52:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(boot): stateless persistence — regenerate extensions-install.yaml from external DB (ADR-014) (#78)\n\n* feat(boot): regenerate extensions-install.yaml from external DB before installer (ADR-014)\n\nWS1 of ADR-014: make a DB-backed DevPortal pod fully stateless. When\nbackend.database.client is pg, the operator''s marketplace selections live in\nPostgres (table marketplace_installations), not on /app/data — so a fresh /app/data\nwould boot with no plugins. A new boot pre-step rebuilds extensions-install.yaml\nfrom the DB before install-dynamic-plugins.py reads it (the Python installer runs\nbefore the Node backend, so it cannot read the DB itself).\n\n- docker/regenerate-extensions-install.js: standalone Node pre-step. Node, not\n  Python — the runtime image has no psycopg2 and no build toolchain, while pg and\n  yaml are already baked. Resolves backend.database via the baked\n  @backstage/config-loader over the same --config chain the backend gets (there is\n  no assembled app-config on disk). Discovers the owning schema via\n  information_schema so pluginDivisionMode database and schema both work without\n  hardcoding a name. Bounded connectionTimeoutMillis/statement_timeout so an\n  unreachable DB degrades instead of hanging the boot; on any error it leaves the\n  entrypoint-guaranteed file in place and exits 0.\n- entrypoint.sh: invoke the pre-step after the SaaS/preset config files are\n  assembled and before the ${BACKSTAGE_VERSION}/${PLUGIN_REGISTRY} substitution.\n  No-op for SQLite/file deployments (gates on client: pg) — fully backward compatible.\n- Dockerfile: COPY the pre-step to /app/.\n- docker/test_regenerate_extensions_install.js: node:test unit coverage for the\n  pure transforms (11 tests). End-to-end behavior validated against a live Postgres\n  per the WS1 spike rig (database/schema modes, no-op, degrade, idempotency).\n- docs/adr/014: status Accepted + implementation notes and the pinned schema contract.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(boot): harden extensions-install pre-step per PR review\n\nAddresses /ecc:review-pr findings (no critical/high; one Important + advisories):\n\n- rowsToPlugins: a single corrupt config_yaml row no longer drops every\n  selection. YAML.parse is now per-row try/catch — on bad YAML it warns with the\n  package name and falls through to {package, disabled}. Also backfills `package`\n  from the package_name PK and skips a row only if no usable package exists.\n  (Raised independently by pr-test, silent-failure, and type-design reviewers.)\n- main(): read all backend.database.* values, then call config.close() exactly\n  once before any early return (previously skipped on the connection-missing path).\n- main(): build the pg client config (pgClientConfig can throw on a malformed\n  connection URL) OUTSIDE the DB try, so a config error reads as a config error\n  instead of \"could not read marketplace_installations\".\n- Merge findSchema + queryInstallations into loadInstallations — one connection\n  (one TCP+TLS+auth handshake) instead of two at boot.\n- Quote the table identifier (\"${TABLE}\") and backfilled `disabled` via !! for\n  consistency; clarify the db-name and ssl comments.\n- Tests: add coverage for malformed-YAML fallback and package backfill (13 total).\n\nRe-verified: 13/13 unit tests, plus the full spike rig vs live Postgres\n(database/schema modes incl. a corrupt row, SQLite no-op, unreachable degrade\nin 5s, idempotency).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: regenerate docs index for ADR-014\n\nscripts/build-docs-index.py --check (CI: ''Docs frontmatter + index check'')\nflagged llms.txt/docs/README.md as stale after adding ADR-014. Regenerated.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"99bfd85905e4c38802810cc46b2d56e97879f5d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/git/trees/99bfd85905e4c38802810cc46b2d56e97879f5d5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/git/commits/75baf075574dd50b06d8048861de91df7a2ec60e","verification":{"payload":"tree 99bfd85905e4c38802810cc46b2d56e97879f5d5\nparent 181c80dd40d2b068d2bfd28fd00b5bc04f562119\nauthor Giovani <giovanimcorrea18@gmail.com> 1782150774 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782150774 -0300\n\nfeat(boot): stateless persistence — regenerate extensions-install.yaml from external DB (ADR-014) (#78)\n\n* feat(boot): regenerate extensions-install.yaml from external DB before installer (ADR-014)\n\nWS1 of ADR-014: make a DB-backed DevPortal pod fully stateless. When\nbackend.database.client is pg, the operator''s marketplace selections live in\nPostgres (table marketplace_installations), not on /app/data — so a fresh /app/data\nwould boot with no plugins. A new boot pre-step rebuilds extensions-install.yaml\nfrom the DB before install-dynamic-plugins.py reads it (the Python installer runs\nbefore the Node backend, so it cannot read the DB itself).\n\n- docker/regenerate-extensions-install.js: standalone Node pre-step. Node, not\n  Python — the runtime image has no psycopg2 and no build toolchain, while pg and\n  yaml are already baked. Resolves backend.database via the baked\n  @backstage/config-loader over the same --config chain the backend gets (there is\n  no assembled app-config on disk). Discovers the owning schema via\n  information_schema so pluginDivisionMode database and schema both work without\n  hardcoding a name. Bounded connectionTimeoutMillis/statement_timeout so an\n  unreachable DB degrades instead of hanging the boot; on any error it leaves the\n  entrypoint-guaranteed file in place and exits 0.\n- entrypoint.sh: invoke the pre-step after the SaaS/preset config files are\n  assembled and before the ${BACKSTAGE_VERSION}/${PLUGIN_REGISTRY} substitution.\n  No-op for SQLite/file deployments (gates on client: pg) — fully backward compatible.\n- Dockerfile: COPY the pre-step to /app/.\n- docker/test_regenerate_extensions_install.js: node:test unit coverage for the\n  pure transforms (11 tests). End-to-end behavior validated against a live Postgres\n  per the WS1 spike rig (database/schema modes, no-op, degrade, idempotency).\n- docs/adr/014: status Accepted + implementation notes and the pinned schema contract.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(boot): harden extensions-install pre-step per PR review\n\nAddresses /ecc:review-pr findings (no critical/high; one Important + advisories):\n\n- rowsToPlugins: a single corrupt config_yaml row no longer drops every\n  selection. YAML.parse is now per-row try/catch — on bad YAML it warns with the\n  package name and falls through to {package, disabled}. Also backfills `package`\n  from the package_name PK and skips a row only if no usable package exists.\n  (Raised independently by pr-test, silent-failure, and type-design reviewers.)\n- main(): read all backend.database.* values, then call config.close() exactly\n  once before any early return (previously skipped on the connection-missing path).\n- main(): build the pg client config (pgClientConfig can throw on a malformed\n  connection URL) OUTSIDE the DB try, so a config error reads as a config error\n  instead of \"could not read marketplace_installations\".\n- Merge findSchema + queryInstallations into loadInstallations — one connection\n  (one TCP+TLS+auth handshake) instead of two at boot.\n- Quote the table identifier (\"${TABLE}\") and backfilled `disabled` via !! for\n  consistency; clarify the db-name and ssl comments.\n- Tests: add coverage for malformed-YAML fallback and package backfill (13 total).\n\nRe-verified: 13/13 unit tests, plus the full spike rig vs live Postgres\n(database/schema modes incl. a corrupt row, SQLite no-op, unreachable degrade\nin 5s, idempotency).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: regenerate docs index for ADR-014\n\nscripts/build-docs-index.py --check (CI: ''Docs frontmatter + index check'')\nflagged llms.txt/docs/README.md as stale after adding ADR-014. Regenerated.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOXZ2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAlF8QAGfDxc3J8rJuiQcZTduRXCwI\n2i0d6O68UusME1/Avu+cj974NDIk5AURobcedWggr255iD7O/1i1AYyJNMSDCK+v\nTVP0Z/GMF1wgjRaUNJunp78tVcJ0gTSBkz7kKeFkCWs3a6ESkIuW5R3AOoJsSyPv\n4xu0seQyJB9OZzfUX1gwQ1sYhah3P6Eopsb/1rjbcGswV2n0k0u0Q2bzvPKRjQxl\nmkhKX1eVbFzD+uQG/5EXL04yhAG1/KYThRs91p6P6TTZRE9fGqHzPAa6xZQV3uyI\ne9jCwYCk66B1+qwZ6FrwNNXYca3PoRsjQW2ZYpBUbO/EQWwYEhc3LPHCd2i+iy7B\nj8b13oWQWnYvs/WQnlZUePuOEkVSbwpScF63yF/eGJZbFtsBTUqF34myYDgS/W8I\nntFoZ1ykZRgN3WjCuJCe3267HzEmOq/Tg5xBDkYSzJL8CizhXj3DenFaXR6b5VCs\neQpMfZHhXe/l0zE2GitZv4czoWGvV/RBxkjgh8fHYbuMhkXm/nFt91H8uU4qKrkj\ntIIUa+Gw0s3ukuyOEdQs9QB80eGZ8rVYwp/IKObYWkJdWFxnoqhUgHSwJn0qHY5C\nX55xLJmaQrOfvShHNCPuV1MLdP2+9DH4uxeerC9unQvJmbyV9VuGI240Yd6SFCjs\n0dDJ8Z0RRWp/Cux4aGyr\n=eX6h\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-22T17:52:55Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commit/75baf075574dd50b06d8048861de91df7a2ec60e","node_id":"C_kwDOSc5yKNoAKDc1YmFmMDc1NTc0ZGQ1MGIwNmQ4MDQ4ODYxZGU5MWRmN2EyZWM2MGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commit/181c80dd40d2b068d2bfd28fd00b5bc04f562119","sha":"181c80dd40d2b068d2bfd28fd00b5bc04f562119","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commits/181c80dd40d2b068d2bfd28fd00b5bc04f562119"}],"sha":"75baf075574dd50b06d8048861de91df7a2ec60e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commits/75baf075574dd50b06d8048861de91df7a2ec60e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63979266?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Elesiann","id":63979266,"login":"Elesiann","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzOTc5MjY2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commits/181c80dd40d2b068d2bfd28fd00b5bc04f562119/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-16T18:45:31Z","email":"giovanimcorrea18@gmail.com","name":"Giovani"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-16T18:45:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(docker): slim runtime image 2.49GB→1.59GB (-36%) (#71)\n\n* chore(docker): slim runtime image 2.49GB->1.59GB (-36%)\n\nStrip non-runtime cruft in the SAME RUN that creates the files (a later RUN\nonly whiteouts): sourcemaps (*.map), markdown, test dirs from node_modules,\nthe frontend bundle, and baked dynamic plugins; plus *.d.ts EXCEPT config.d.ts\nand typescript/ (which @backstage/config-loader needs at runtime - stripping\nthem breaks boot with \"Cannot find global type ''Array''\"). Remove unused git\n(scaffolder uses isomorphic-git) and kubectl (k8s plugin talks HTTP). Add npm\ncache mount to the baked-plugins step.\n\nVerified: full boot + guest auth + catalog ingestion + dynamic-plugin (scalprum)\nparity vs baseline across before/after; Trivy 78->67 vulns (-8 HIGH, 0 CRITICAL).\n\ndeck (Kong) kept. TechDocs/mkdocs (-175MB) and integration-SDK->dynamic (-130MB+)\ndeferred as ADR decisions (rollout risk / arch trade-off), not done here.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(docker): drop kubectl from DOCKER_DEVELOPMENT — removed from runtime image\n\nThe slim commit removed the kubectl binary and the KUBECTL_VERSION build arg.\nNothing in the image spawns kubectl (the k8s plugin talks HTTP; the\nlocalKubectlProxy locator just targets localhost:8001 and never launched it),\nso the runtime-binary list and build-arg list are updated to match.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"72bb47d72a4788e1eeec474f5172e230bcf2ee8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/git/trees/72bb47d72a4788e1eeec474f5172e230bcf2ee8f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/git/commits/181c80dd40d2b068d2bfd28fd00b5bc04f562119","verification":{"payload":"tree 72bb47d72a4788e1eeec474f5172e230bcf2ee8f\nparent 4fc5820ef43208603a9e521af5655363f2cec65e\nauthor Giovani <giovanimcorrea18@gmail.com> 1781635531 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781635531 -0300\n\nchore(docker): slim runtime image 2.49GB→1.59GB (-36%) (#71)\n\n* chore(docker): slim runtime image 2.49GB->1.59GB (-36%)\n\nStrip non-runtime cruft in the SAME RUN that creates the files (a later RUN\nonly whiteouts): sourcemaps (*.map), markdown, test dirs from node_modules,\nthe frontend bundle, and baked dynamic plugins; plus *.d.ts EXCEPT config.d.ts\nand typescript/ (which @backstage/config-loader needs at runtime - stripping\nthem breaks boot with \"Cannot find global type ''Array''\"). Remove unused git\n(scaffolder uses isomorphic-git) and kubectl (k8s plugin talks HTTP). Add npm\ncache mount to the baked-plugins step.\n\nVerified: full boot + guest auth + catalog ingestion + dynamic-plugin (scalprum)\nparity vs baseline across before/after; Trivy 78->67 vulns (-8 HIGH, 0 CRITICAL).\n\ndeck (Kong) kept. TechDocs/mkdocs (-175MB) and integration-SDK->dynamic (-130MB+)\ndeferred as ADR decisions (rollout risk / arch trade-off), not done here.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(docker): drop kubectl from DOCKER_DEVELOPMENT — removed from runtime image\n\nThe slim commit removed the kubectl binary and the KUBECTL_VERSION build arg.\nNothing in the image spawns kubectl (the k8s plugin talks HTTP; the\nlocalKubectlProxy locator just targets localhost:8001 and never launched it),\nso the runtime-binary list and build-arg list are updated to match.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMZnLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAuq0QAAm1Qxd0B1gbYKAnApDaRYY0\ne9JWrFAzd1yug9H/KiCVEnoW//erWiuzu5Q9pMIYDrO8Qc8jaFTXyZJRpG3Yzp9G\nI5dO2vheug8r88cioRRkwD3d8h/lEg2f5O4OUU3jRlAfLOFdBVd/gdYlrjTeFXH8\nItE4D/OWWU4nWmCAI2LFopb3SHOJ25JYJ87KuyDKieZ54qp9xP/YdVCWvM507Jcz\nMaLZH25HWsHIhQyZ18Gq+eeXTyRHQTF63CC6IQkgX8MJPqemlZPYj