f43208603a9e521af5655363f2cec65e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","id":41898282,"login":"github-actions[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commit/4fc5820ef43208603a9e521af5655363f2cec65e","node_id":"C_kwDOSc5yKNoAKDRmYzU4MjBlZjQzMjA4NjAzYTllNTIxYWY1NjU1MzYzZjJjZWM2NWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commit/e9a52bbec76d39788b1cd0f92fd3a9d2753e71cf","sha":"e9a52bbec76d39788b1cd0f92fd3a9d2753e71cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commits/e9a52bbec76d39788b1cd0f92fd3a9d2753e71cf"}],"sha":"4fc5820ef43208603a9e521af5655363f2cec65e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commits/4fc5820ef43208603a9e521af5655363f2cec65e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63979266?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Elesiann","id":63979266,"login":"Elesiann","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzOTc5MjY2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commits/e9a52bbec76d39788b1cd0f92fd3a9d2753e71cf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-12T19:37:41Z","email":"giovanimcorrea18@gmail.com","name":"Giovani"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-12T19:37:41Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(catalog): central /alpha compat shim for graduated catalog-node symbols (#67)\n\n* fix(catalog): central /alpha compat shim for graduated catalog-node symbols\n\nplugin-catalog-node 2.2.0 graduated catalogProcessingExtensionPoint (and\ncatalogLocationsExtensionPoint, catalogAnalysisExtensionPoint, catalogServiceRef)\nfrom the /alpha subpath export to the package''s main entry. Dynamic plugins built\nagainst the older line (the V1 distro shipped catalog-node 2.1.0, whose /alpha still\ncarried them) still require them from /alpha, where they are now undefined -> the\nsymbol lands in a backend module''s registerInit deps and BackendInitializer crashes\nreading ''.id''. This hit runtime-loaded plugins (e.g. immobiliarelabs gitlab v6.13.0)\nthat the prior narrow per-module sed did not cover.\n\nAppend a compat shim to node_modules/@backstage/plugin-catalog-node/dist/alpha.cjs.js\nthat re-exports the main entry''s symbols on /alpha for any key it no longer carries.\nOne shim restores the 2.1.x /alpha surface for every dynamic plugin (the baked\ncatalog-backend-module-extensions and runtime OCI plugins alike), so the in-the-air\ngitlab v6.13.0 build loads unchanged on V2. Remove the now-redundant per-module sed\n(Dockerfile) and ensure_cbme_patch (scripts/dev-run.sh); update UPGRADING.md and\nDOCKER_DEVELOPMENT.md. Validated: local docker build green, shim verify passes, and\nthe built image resolves catalogProcessingExtensionPoint on /alpha at runtime.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(catalog): harden /alpha shim + sweep stale per-module-patch docs\n\nReview follow-up on the catalog-node /alpha compat shim:\n- Shim RUN: prefix `set -e` (a failed append now aborts the build instead of\n  falling through to the verify), guard the append with `grep -qF` so the RUN\n  is idempotent, and verify all four graduated symbols\n  (catalogProcessingExtensionPoint, catalogLocationsExtensionPoint,\n  catalogAnalysisExtensionPoint, catalogServiceRef) carry an id, not just one.\n- Sweep docs that still described the removed per-module sed patch / the\n  ensure_cbme_patch dev-run helper / dead ''mounting patched'' log line and stale\n  Dockerfile:217 line refs: DEVELOPMENT_GUIDE.md, ROADMAP_BACKLOG.md,\n  ROADMAP_FEATURES.md, UPGRADING.md, .github/prompts/docs-refresh.md, and a dated\n  update note in ADR-010 (history preserved). dev-run.sh header parenthetical fixed.\n\nValidated: local docker build green; shim verify reports all four symbols restored.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(catalog): qualify /alpha shim coverage (adversarial-review follow-up)\n\nCodex adversarial review flagged that ''one shim covers every dynamic plugin''\noverclaims: the shim patches only the host catalog-node copy, so a plugin that\nbundles its OWN @backstage/plugin-catalog-node (symbol missing from its /alpha)\nwould resolve the local copy first and bypass the shim.\n\nVerified the mechanism is real but the premise does not hold for any shipped\nplugin: catalog-backend-module-extensions and gitlab both declare\n@backstage/plugin-catalog-node as a peerDependency with no bundled node_modules\ncopy (the standard dynamic-plugin export contract), and install-dynamic-plugins.py\ncreates no intermediate node_modules — so they resolve the host copy, which is\nshimmed. Removing the per-module sed did not regress the extensions module.\n\nQualify the claim in the Dockerfile comment + docs (covers plugins that\nexternalize catalog-node to the host) and register the optional boot smoke as a\nROADMAP follow-up. No code/behavior change; the shim RUN is unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7a2a81709b1f4269f649d97149bd8d81b5ce2a50","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/git/trees/7a2a81709b1f4269f649d97149bd8d81b5ce2a50"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/git/commits/e9a52bbec76d39788b1cd0f92fd3a9d2753e71cf","verification":{"payload":"tree 7a2a81709b1f4269f649d97149bd8d81b5ce2a50\nparent bb0631f713133c614a5c0822302a00c0ca3c3bff\nauthor Giovani <giovanimcorrea18@gmail.com> 1781293061 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781293061 -0300\n\nfix(catalog): central /alpha compat shim for graduated catalog-node symbols (#67)\n\n* fix(catalog): central /alpha compat shim for graduated catalog-node symbols\n\nplugin-catalog-node 2.2.0 graduated catalogProcessingExtensionPoint (and\ncatalogLocationsExtensionPoint, catalogAnalysisExtensionPoint, catalogServiceRef)\nfrom the /alpha subpath export to the package''s main entry. Dynamic plugins built\nagainst the older line (the V1 distro shipped catalog-node 2.1.0, whose /alpha still\ncarried them) still require them from /alpha, where they are now undefined -> the\nsymbol lands in a backend module''s registerInit deps and BackendInitializer crashes\nreading ''.id''. This hit runtime-loaded plugins (e.g. immobiliarelabs gitlab v6.13.0)\nthat the prior narrow per-module sed did not cover.\n\nAppend a compat shim to node_modules/@backstage/plugin-catalog-node/dist/alpha.cjs.js\nthat re-exports the main entry''s symbols on /alpha for any key it no longer carries.\nOne shim restores the 2.1.x /alpha surface for every dynamic plugin (the baked\ncatalog-backend-module-extensions and runtime OCI plugins alike), so the in-the-air\ngitlab v6.13.0 build loads unchanged on V2. Remove the now-redundant per-module sed\n(Dockerfile) and ensure_cbme_patch (scripts/dev-run.sh); update UPGRADING.md and\nDOCKER_DEVELOPMENT.md. Validated: local docker build green, shim verify passes, and\nthe built image resolves catalogProcessingExtensionPoint on /alpha at runtime.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(catalog): harden /alpha shim + sweep stale per-module-patch docs\n\nReview follow-up on the catalog-node /alpha compat shim:\n- Shim RUN: prefix `set -e` (a failed append now aborts the build instead of\n  falling through to the verify), guard the append with `grep -qF` so the RUN\n  is idempotent, and verify all four graduated symbols\n  (catalogProcessingExtensionPoint, catalogLocationsExtensionPoint,\n  catalogAnalysisExtensionPoint, catalogServiceRef) carry an id, not just one.\n- Sweep docs that still described the removed per-module sed patch / the\n  ensure_cbme_patch dev-run helper / dead ''mounting patched'' log line and stale\n  Dockerfile:217 line refs: DEVELOPMENT_GUIDE.md, ROADMAP_BACKLOG.md,\n  ROADMAP_FEATURES.md, UPGRADING.md, .github/prompts/docs-refresh.md, and a dated\n  update note in ADR-010 (history preserved). dev-run.sh header parenthetical fixed.\n\nValidated: local docker build green; shim verify reports all four symbols restored.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(catalog): qualify /alpha shim coverage (adversarial-review follow-up)\n\nCodex adversarial review flagged that ''one shim covers every dynamic plugin''\noverclaims: the shim patches only the host catalog-node copy, so a plugin that\nbundles its OWN @backstage/plugin-catalog-node (symbol missing from its /alpha)\nwould resolve the local copy first and bypass the shim.\n\nVerified the mechanism is real but the premise does not hold for any shipped\nplugin: catalog-backend-module-extensions and gitlab both declare\n@backstage/plugin-catalog-node as a peerDependency with no bundled node_modules\ncopy (the standard dynamic-plugin export contract), and install-dynamic-plugins.py\ncreates no intermediate node_modules — so they resolve the host copy, which is\nshimmed. Removing the per-module sed did not regress the extensions module.\n\nQualify the claim in the Dockerfile comment + docs (covers plugins that\nexternalize catalog-node to the host) and register the optional boot smoke as a\nROADMAP follow-up. No code/behavior change; the shim RUN is unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLGAFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAiQEQAE5sldGnFJV8oQmuO6OyTpgI\nOjNlaBNo0KdpmP1/K2OiEbIc7+BjiK1CnuMK+iYFcQocAzfnmRI+wJyodggamxK6\nbF6KnpASmNzS0t1kNTUIOUvLoUnA+ykbEV6BSrrBeKc3SObyXzaa3PZifYmSBdBD\nWYeR4rNKYGVlp5VVe128hODt+suDpuguU6kaN/w7HOiecEe0GLSJSTm6d/27RiAN\noky9N8kLvvk+6e+TLwrUDUPEs/PVHvABLHsUeSwQmKcrUH3a58fuubmL6cvf9DQn\nJPVtlJyZtlThX8v8ZWDx3xFc8AKLyWV3BrVbTX6ECsw8gvA3mMoC9Tqap+Rw+ieU\nX41yIP7QBl25h4jhqMWPmd7bfsKbgZ4iqaGnzMgQZVZBgD4bQmeHPp+dgH7s3NFc\nTikJhgI7NFuHcHXcFIsWHTO