tps://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63979266?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Elesiann","id":63979266,"login":"Elesiann","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzOTc5MjY2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commits/bb0631f713133c614a5c0822302a00c0ca3c3bff/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-12T16:49:41Z","email":"giovanimcorrea18@gmail.com","name":"Giovani"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-12T16:49:41Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(presets): bump mcp-chat and ldap-ad to 2.0.0; document boot-contract changes (#66)\n\nPost-merge review finding on PR #63: enforcing requires.presets is a\ncontract change by SCHEMA.md''s own versioning rules — compositions that\npreviously booted broken-but-up (mcp-chat without mcp; ldap-ad alone or\nbefore ldap) now refuse to boot with exit 78. Bump both presets to\n2.0.0 and add a \"Behavior changes by image version\" section to\ndocs/UPGRADING.md covering the new enforcement, the boot preflight\nguards, and the removed theme env vars.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5dcd99c5cd2769fb07756efaa7eee4ed395531e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/git/trees/5dcd99c5cd2769fb07756efaa7eee4ed395531e3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/git/commits/bb0631f713133c614a5c0822302a00c0ca3c3bff","verification":{"payload":"tree 5dcd99c5cd2769fb07756efaa7eee4ed395531e3\nparent fa825a9e78aa19d7c3c9e3ff45a4af971c02e735\nauthor Giovani <giovanimcorrea18@gmail.com> 1781282981 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781282981 -0300\n\nchore(presets): bump mcp-chat and ldap-ad to 2.0.0; document boot-contract changes (#66)\n\nPost-merge review finding on PR #63: enforcing requires.presets is a\ncontract change by SCHEMA.md''s own versioning rules — compositions that\npreviously booted broken-but-up (mcp-chat without mcp; ldap-ad alone or\nbefore ldap) now refuse to boot with exit 78. Bump both presets to\n2.0.0 and add a \"Behavior changes by image version\" section to\ndocs/UPGRADING.md covering the new enforcement, the boot preflight\nguards, and the removed theme env vars.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLDilCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALnMQAK/UaJcYZSJa368XWtWBCqwy\ntre3hPal0gJdUtCBJxyolnbSjTS+8PSxiA5nIyA7c4XCjWmJBjvfgS03csjjCEwg\nyGQmhIOSLjgjIM4/kRm3G1yzHiXm5cH3U7CA86NYmhl7wZSi6UvVRH5xHX4U3hAG\n/fwGGQnDWOMlMRKW5apcaTfU680dar14X9q2i3/UR72U/TR8JOPnPqR1CEaDgyrM\nvnYTBf2+X6/oaFRpJPAIV+ypSm/JOA32A8pGiK40LrP4p3zRuovjMeC5kYbkEjnB\nPgRAPbES8DrnZ7rmOCnVGB8ynlacmYUD+zKOgWaqiLAdsfIOD1czYTUwaT3l4mHn\nFl/wd8ik0A8Iw8V1szhYqLcBhFxhEEHq/bB+jXrOVjc4YpNIjfxPsH3fzquuFF9g\ns8dFFju4HdVu7wmPA9tAXMqk81tR8O1x0UlB7uKum7pdOy30Z0iRv+AxSNImsh8H\nnjyO31+nQFOZHSMMUXtsVDOCfjTGPPsomwEAGQji79MIcYnNUZf7O+j8fDeHbbLn\nzmWnEVV+cVsmC34a1k+RJp+/tJzhZWl6qysxQJ6G1geb2OYKeRa5MzWj8IRCJrsm\n7JR6JkPDo1jd1N+bEQ8yRMk+zYT+AnrvGegaZCVbOSI96YXs+vmuwlDsa91WtzFj\nZDkxyoRPsD00EEsQeojA\n=d2Qo\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-12T16:49:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commit/bb0631f713133c614a5c0822302a00c0ca3c3bff","node_id":"C_kwDOSc5yKNoAKGJiMDYzMWY3MTMxMzNjNjE0YTVjMDgyMjMwMmEwMGMwY2EzYzNiZmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commit/fa825a9e78aa19d7c3c9e3ff45a4af971c02e735","sha":"fa825a9e78aa19d7c3c9e3ff45a4af971c02e735","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commits/fa825a9e78aa19d7c3c9e3ff45a4af971c02e735"}],"sha":"bb0631f713133c614a5c0822302a00c0ca3c3bff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commits/bb0631f713133c614a5c0822302a00c0ca3c3bff"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63979266?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Elesiann","id":63979266,"login":"Elesiann","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzOTc5MjY2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commits/fa825a9e78aa19d7c3c9e3ff45a4af971c02e735/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-12T16:26:00Z","email":"giovanimcorrea18@gmail.com","name":"Giovani"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-12T16:26:00Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(build): make the extensions module fetch build-fatal (#65)\n\nCodex adversarial review finding on the fragility-map round: the\ncatalog-backend-module-extensions OCI fetch tolerated failure at image\nbuild (WARN + skip), while dynamic-plugins.yaml declares the module\npreInstalled and the new boot guard (PR #62) refuses to start a\ncontainer whose preInstalled directories are missing. A registry flake\nduring build could therefore publish an image that can never boot.\n\nFail the build instead — same contract as the catalog-index fetch\nbelow. This moves the invariant up the mitigation hierarchy: a broken\nimage becomes impossible by construction, and the boot guard remains\nthe second line of defense (empty volume mounted over\ndynamic-plugins-root, inventory drift).\n\nVerified inside the image (skopeo available): the block with set -e and\na nonexistent tag exits 2 before any extraction (\"never prints\" guard\nconfirmed); the real bs_1.49.4 tag downloads, extracts and reaches the\n/alpha patch branch.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"82f900fb71626ffc5d1e4491b67cc425a5fc1506","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/git/trees/82f900fb71626ffc5d1e4491b67cc425a5fc1506"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/git/commits/fa825a9e78aa19d7c3c9e3ff45a4af971c02e735","verification":{"payload":"tree 82f900fb71626ffc5d1e4491b67cc425a5fc1506\nparent 48ef8c1519af20ccb059934e85f72a6f77837ca6\nauthor Giovani <giovanimcorrea18@gmail.com> 1781281560 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781281560 -0300\n\nfix(build): make the extensions module fetch build-fatal (#65)\n\nCodex adversarial review finding on the fragility-map round: the\ncatalog-backend-module-extensions OCI fetch tolerated failure at image\nbuild (WARN + skip), while dynamic-plugins.yaml declares the module\npreInstalled and the new boot guard (PR #62) refuses to start a\ncontainer whose preInstalled directories are missing. A registry flake\nduring build could therefore publish an image that can never boot.\n\nFail the build instead — same contract as the catalog-index fetch\nbelow. This moves the invariant up the mitigation hierarchy: a broken\nimage becomes impossible by construction, and the boot guard remains\nthe second line of defense (empty volume mounted over\ndynamic-plugins-root, inventory drift).\n\nVerified inside the image (skopeo available): the block with set -e and\na nonexistent tag exits 2 before any extraction (\"never prints\" guard\nconfirmed); the real bs_1.49.4 tag downloads, extracts and reaches the\n/alpha patch branch.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLDMYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAV+cQAF/vFkWxFmX5jjROvmwKO6Kc\n5MFTWlvYpa37BI4/OeaNooK0mgpuPrNsIr4UPeno/+e/41G45tRhPPAZhPmMsHbB\np7VTCUH2nv/U8pZ4oDcg16IxKW+bRzGZis5zc7TSI0D0dBCCXqakItVBEux4PSAa\nFR2heerEnDosg+0DwW+OaWaU/suJwIRMsu+dxus/sJmD/fKMVrNfRhlBwTvrizPW\nFjbP6Ehd5yp2C/YIQC2GKpi2xxo5DKLx9BoRzUnp4Pv6+0hUvl9SCNop8f5+oBFe\nRjD3QYnzP