":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commits/fa825a9e78aa19d7c3c9e3ff45a4af971c02e735"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63979266?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Elesiann","id":63979266,"login":"Elesiann","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzOTc5MjY2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commits/48ef8c1519af20ccb059934e85f72a6f77837ca6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-12T15:36:39Z","email":"giovanimcorrea18@gmail.com","name":"Giovani"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-12T15:36:39Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: assert EXTENSIONS_TAG matches backstage.json in CI; remove dead theme.json path (#64)\n\nFragility-map #8 and #14 (re-verified 2026-06-12).\n\n#8 — the extensions module baked at build (ARG EXTENSIONS_TAG, literal\nbs_1.49.4) and the runtime refs (bs_${BACKSTAGE_VERSION} from\nbackstage.json) are independent knobs nothing kept in sync; the\n/alpha-import stopgap patch in the Dockerfile is the scar of exactly\nthis skew, and the 1.50 bump on the roadmap would hit it again. New\nvalidate step fails the PR when they diverge.\n\n#14 — nothing reads /app/packages/app/dist/theme.json on V2: the file\ndoes not exist in the image, the app dropped the useLoaderTheme() fetch\n(Loader.tsx), and the theme ships as a dynamic frontend plugin\n(ADR-011). The THEME_CUSTOM_JSON/THEME_DOWNLOAD_URL/\nPLATFORM_DEVPORTAL_THEME_URL entrypoint blocks silently wrote a file no\ncode consumed — observed empirically: even VALID custom JSON produced a\n0-byte theme.json (the merge base never existed). Removed; setting the\nvars now prints a loud WARNING pointing at the ADR-011 path. Favicon\nvars (THEME_FAV_ICON, PLATFORM_DEVPORTAL_FAVICON) still work and stay.\nChart-side theme.customJson deprecation is a next-charts follow-up.\n\nVerified: local simulation of the CI assert passes on current main\n(bs_1.49.4 == bs_1.49.4); boot with THEME_CUSTOM_JSON set → WARNING\nprinted, no theme.json created; bash -n + workflow YAML parse clean.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f4ea569747212a2f618f067182820d3af00526a7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/git/trees/f4ea569747212a2f618f067182820d3af00526a7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/git/commits/48ef8c1519af20ccb059934e85f72a6f77837ca6","verification":{"payload":"tree f4ea569747212a2f618f067182820d3af00526a7\nparent 9f1e5d33bbf73bf730c8fc1dc4ee576074ab7931\nauthor Giovani <giovanimcorrea18@gmail.com> 1781278599 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781278599 -0300\n\nchore: assert EXTENSIONS_TAG matches backstage.json in CI; remove dead theme.json path (#64)\n\nFragility-map #8 and #14 (re-verified 2026-06-12).\n\n#8 — the extensions module baked at build (ARG EXTENSIONS_TAG, literal\nbs_1.49.4) and the runtime refs (bs_${BACKSTAGE_VERSION} from\nbackstage.json) are independent knobs nothing kept in sync; the\n/alpha-import stopgap patch in the Dockerfile is the scar of exactly\nthis skew, and the 1.50 bump on the roadmap would hit it again. New\nvalidate step fails the PR when they diverge.\n\n#14 — nothing reads /app/packages/app/dist/theme.json on V2: the file\ndoes not exist in the image, the app dropped the useLoaderTheme() fetch\n(Loader.tsx), and the theme ships as a dynamic frontend plugin\n(ADR-011). The THEME_CUSTOM_JSON/THEME_DOWNLOAD_URL/\nPLATFORM_DEVPORTAL_THEME_URL entrypoint blocks silently wrote a file no\ncode consumed — observed empirically: even VALID custom JSON produced a\n0-byte theme.json (the merge base never existed). Removed; setting the\nvars now prints a loud WARNING pointing at the ADR-011 path. Favicon\nvars (THEME_FAV_ICON, PLATFORM_DEVPORTAL_FAVICON) still work and stay.\nChart-side theme.customJson deprecation is a next-charts follow-up.\n\nVerified: local simulation of the CI assert passes on current main\n(bs_1.49.4 == bs_1.49.4); boot with THEME_CUSTOM_JSON set → WARNING\nprinted, no theme.json created; bash -n + workflow YAML parse clean.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqLCeHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3DIQAKxVNtgO14QnxafFEpqlJvct\nxaWxNKNLzC+ATZ6A/wtDF8Di3LrR6NXvEnVvFyxfJ8yibMVwBuLNXBDn0aPOFaZI\n8lBBU2hR1GjSTixnQ1qw69cVraezBY8+uE/x14CQ8BJR3efRullzJvT1OD5H/P7D\nwbhRbbFm8io/GsaP64Oj0Rq5iXPsO8atq50nVqIc/daJCvg5QfjF8ZMjkJO0OqZV\nclHYNPZUq6E+DtCFhyj7qaugBbpW5Hd58Aj1LhOKJvAOMo7qPwa6UdTLYpzqr0aO\nmDUFKKpsuU9TCWG/vKUUX/5X5bMHapdF1ZtenrEk/1aLZfeixW0re6HI0nT5XJtx\ni6C6nJ3jn2zkaLcfVuWhwuQKWvOXSRmqD29IKXOyTh8KUM3i4grELg/xB6AZ7ybi\nkRkF/eq8noUUN1Tc5bbvYywnUHZS/PuA8mOQo9ZtToFJDfFt1zFeF0bKAwGBl2FF\ngTEKgegfur7m2Fy1s73zSKNNpl82Ghze5/Z6uW9yBq9A6pWUpsYfEi4KnZRdn6hS\nyUiIsCV6oS4vzBOzEVd339DsojcJZtDyjXy7M0F0BT1fVzzTJsBMgE/sl389ad/R\nAH0b4Oe9gDhGvzvPbbEGJnv9dMt2qv6R+wVPH5mlehPz9hmXkq3RB1yc9l6NsJxU\nicpzR8xWTf8bo5N8t33D\n=roHR\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-12T15:36:40Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commit/48ef8c1519af20ccb059934e85f72a6f77837ca6","node_id":"C_kwDOSc5yKNoAKDQ4ZWY4YzE1MTlhZjIwY2NiMDU5OTM0ZTg1ZjcyYTZmNzc4MzdjYTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commit/9f1e5d33bbf73bf730c8fc1dc4ee576074ab7931","sha":"9f1e5d33bbf73bf730c8fc1dc4ee576074ab7931","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commits/9f1e5d33bbf73bf730c8fc1dc4ee576074ab7931"}],"sha":"48ef8c1519af20ccb059934e85f72a6f77837ca6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commits/48ef8c1519af20ccb059934e85f72a6f77837ca6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63979266?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Elesiann","id":63979266,"login":"Elesiann","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzOTc5MjY2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commits/9f1e5d33bbf73bf730c8fc1dc4ee576074ab7931/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-12T15:36:36Z","email":"giovanimcorrea18@gmail.com","name":"Giovani"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-12T15:36:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(presets): enforce composition dependencies via requires.presets (#63)\n\nFragility-map #1 (re-verified 2026-06-12): mcp-chat without mcp booted\n100% clean — the chat UI mounted, and GET /api/mcp-actions/v1 returned\n404 only when the user invoked a tool. The dependency lived in a YAML\ncomment that admitted \"we can''t enforce the dependency in YAML — the\nschema has no requires.presets\". The presets README already called for\nthis field; ADR-010 sanctioned it.\n\n- SCHEMA.md: new `requires.presets` field — each listed preset must be\n  selected in VEECODE_PRESETS BEFORE the dependent one (presence alone\n  is not enough: list order drives --config override order).\n- entrypoint resolver: dependency check per preset, exit 78 naming both\n  presets and printing the corrected example.\n- mcp-chat (requires mcp) and ldap-ad (requires ldap) migrate from\n  comment-only convention to enforced declarations.\n- smoke-presets-negative.sh: new mcp_chat_missing_mcp case.\n\nVerified on veecode/devportal:2.1.1 + overlay: mcp-chat alone → exit 78\nwith example; wrong order (mcp-chat,mcp) → exit 78; right order falls\nthrough to var validation (no false positive); ldap-ad alone → exit 78.\nFull negative smoke 10/10.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f57934d577716e831b7536ec341421113efaf4c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/git/trees/f57934d577716e831b7536ec341421113efaf4c4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/git/commits/9f1e5d33bbf73bf730c8fc1dc4ee576074ab7931","verification":{"payload":"tree f57934d577716e831b7536ec341421113efaf4c4\nparent 0df39ef08963a4cebc820641408ef0218b499879\nauthor Giovani <giovanimcorrea18@gmail.com> 1781278596 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781278596 -0300\n\nfeat(presets): enforce composition dependencies via requires.presets (#63)\n\nFragility-map #1 (re-verified 2026-06-12): mcp-chat without mcp booted\n100% clean — the chat UI mounted, and GET /api/mcp-actions/v1 returned\n404 only when the user invoked a tool. The dependency lived in a YAML\ncomment that admitted \"we can''t enforce the dependency in YAML — the\nschema has no requires.presets\". The presets README already called for\nthis field; ADR-010 sanctioned it.\n\n- SCHEMA.md: new `requires.presets` field — each listed preset must be\n  selected in VEECODE_PRESETS BEFORE the dependent one (presence alone\n  is not enough: list order drives --config override order).\n- entrypoint resolver: dependency check per preset, exit 78 naming both\n  presets and printing the corrected example.\n- mcp-chat (requires mcp) and ldap-ad (requires ldap) migrate from\n  comment-only convention to enforced declarations.\n- smoke-presets-negative.sh: new mcp_chat_missing_mcp case.\n\nVerified on veecode/devportal:2.1.1 + overlay: mcp-chat alone → exit 78\nwith example; wrong order (mcp-chat,mcp) → exit 78; right order falls\nthrough to var validation (no false positive); ldap-ad alone → exit 78.\nFull negative smoke 10/10.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAA