pics/plugin-selection-surfaces.md (operator-facing docs).\n\n* docs(topics): add plugin-selection-surfaces — the four selection\n              surfaces and their precedence\n\nOperator-facing map of how a plugin ends up loaded in DevPortal:\n- The vitrine (dynamic-plugins.default.yaml as catalog, not auto-enabled).\n- Three selection surfaces (preset / operator override / marketplace UI).\n- Their precedence rules, verified against install-dynamic-plugins.py.\n- The boot-time duplicate detector that guards against conflicts.\n- Pointer to ADR-013 for the deferred unification.\n\nCloses the gap where the precedence model was opaque (''which surface won?'')\nand lived only in conversation context.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: fix code-review findings (7 of 9; #8/#9 deemed low-impact)\n\nFrom the post-PR audit:\n\n1. RELEASE_CYCLE.md: smoke gate count \"13 preset boot tests\" was wrong —\n   actual matrix in publish.yml has 19 entries. Rephrased to reference\n   scripts/smoke-presets.sh#ALL_TESTS so the doc doesn''t drift again.\n\n2. PLUGINS.md: \"~180 plugins compiled into every image\" overstated by ~3x.\n   Actual backend.add() registration count is ~56. Updated to that with\n   a link to packages/backend/src/index.ts.\n\n3. docs/README.md \"Out of scope\" RBAC bullet contradicted docs/RBAC.md\n   (\"ships disabled\" vs \"enabled by default\"). Reframed to \"RBAC plugin\n   default-off\" with the permission-framework caveat — both docs now\n   consistent.\n\n4. tech-stack.md: link text \"ADR-011 § Phase 2\" pointed at a non-existent\n   section. Corrected to \"Phase the rest\" (actual heading at ADR-011:156).\n\n5. ADR-013 cross-references (line 220-224):\n   - Dropped fake section anchors on ADR-010 and ADR-011 links (neither\n     section name existed in the targets).\n   - Fixed broken GitHub org in PR #32 link (veecode-io → veecode-platform).\n   - Corrected entrypoint.sh line range for preset resolver (was 83-160,\n     actually 123-204).\n\n6. CLAUDE.md: added ADR-010 and ADR-013 to the ADR index (only 011/012\n   were listed before). Added a one-line doc-discipline statement — every\n   claim in docs is verified against this repo''s code at the time of\n   writing; do not infer from devportal-base/devportal-distro. Closes\n   the gap left by deleting PROJECT_CONTEXT.md''s \"verified against code\"\n   invariant.\n\n7. docs/RBAC.md: added one sentence at § \"Customising RBAC per deployment\"\n   stating that customer policies are deploy-time artifacts, not presets,\n   cross-referencing presets/README.md § Discipline. Preserves the framing\n   that lived only in the now-deleted PROJECT_CONTEXT.md.\n\nNot fixed (judged low-impact):\n- #8: the deleted \"Switching to tag-driven publishing\" section in\n  RELEASE_CYCLE.md is genuinely historical (tag-driven is now active).\n  Operators needing emergency disable can use git history.\n- #9: the architectural comparison table from PROJECT_CONTEXT.md is\n  redundant with ADR-010 § Context, which is already linked from\n  multiple places.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: fix frontmatter + regenerate index\n\n- tech-stack.md was missing frontmatter; added (type: reference,\n  audience: [operator, contributor]).\n- plugin-selection-surfaces.md had invalid audience ''platform-installer'';\n  collapsed to [operator] (the doc is purely operator-facing).\n- Regenerated docs/README.md indexes and llms.txt via\n  scripts/build-docs-index.py to pick up the two new files + ADR-013.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqELL+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAnxQQADxBImhT6NJMNJGMFpcxSqf8\nGOL77l03zT3xEJYLMpjKKeiox+PzNwXYmXSMOrvnd91HE8apK3M6hMmRq+kxd5uc\nwNSyWJ+HPVOeBW6HIOVyoHU5gLfxzisQYVPvVO01UUCPF9vxpGoWLxjQat5OO5uE\n/HI4VFLj81fz3Xc4tAY7U86/UoSiuceLP2f1nyUYhlQLW