pp.branding` example + caveats (build-time `app.title`, asset URL\n  reachability), linking to theming.md for the full white-label path.\n- Runtime-vs-build-time keys: added to \"What is NOT in this migration\"\n  with cross-ref to the pre-flight callout.\n- Helm/Kubernetes path: section restructured around two paths;\n  `examples/deploy/k8s.yaml` (new) is now the recommended path until a\n  first-party chart ships.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqEERgCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAev4QABSNz50s2vtbRcK48fdQyhX1\nXUZOmTHiKIrTe/eOSjzBKDNmqdZcaD1AjxTXO0UMLIb0uObP0HP22IpA04LzitCn\nNzLpUDzkbcnrZbBH9iQ+B1DYcpLA9nWULCUurnPoFQxqbIajLy1/o+/fAicm980l\n2YHdoYKdNyiSF5dL1pwTmwfD8HiqzqnrTcWMUbW+SxNjGSsv1ValNEB4u4yVdFfK\ntC4IO3WLzag2iq9Vx35awmGGaKp6dMCO5q91EpaE6RI7+8vOSECjkwDeqKu5gGHn\nuDmcU+dA+gv/Nb8AzzMm2vujoS/FVXzs18qBECJdtGl1UbnJ7FKV/T4OqFSh5C7g\nOKtJWUDPARic8PxORD2jm48QhcFDFZvqzk8MeVKlb953qDgdM5WgWs1vcSKsEtOk\nJK5LtuR/2AW8QmJ4Pf1CleA5lChHIMbJhXfycSqVgE8Ub+OfEy24tTotRoNIkgVG\nYeJZvYLP9FYKkqGprSsJGQIlnQJm2rC9koXDzG2H7Aw03fJJwiy9eCa2keQeACo4\nuTpiCEsnt8Ok+wFWYXJ8HC/05HuRTOYkLVhlL0bagn/J+vShHnjQ0HOQNKPo5vlM\n/+lh13/r5Y+JdQcEO3k2WT0HY33Wsocvi5eutxudmgRAm8A4qGC01btHI6nubNja\ndTLHqBmTu9ZAAcUDBER3\n=yQA5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-22T11:56:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commit/374652058a79e6387fd70e45dde06bcc696fbdd0","node_id":"C_kwDOSc5yKNoAKDM3NDY1MjA1OGE3OWU2Mzg3ZmQ3MGU0NWRkZTA2YmNjNjk2ZmJkZDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commit/fff52e539a16648e57d42fb1a4434a804682f659","sha":"fff52e539a16648e57d42fb1a4434a804682f659","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commits/fff52e539a16648e57d42fb1a4434a804682f659"}],"sha":"374652058a79e6387fd70e45dde06bcc696fbdd0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commits/374652058a79e6387fd70e45dde06bcc696fbdd0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63979266?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Elesiann","id":63979266,"login":"Elesiann","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzOTc5MjY2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commits/fff52e539a16648e57d42fb1a4434a804682f659/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-21T19:02:20Z","email":"giovanimcorrea18@gmail.com","name":"Giovani"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-21T19:02:20Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(plugins): persist plugin state across restarts; operator-owned dynamic-plugins.yaml (#33)\n\n* feat(plugins): persist plugin state across restarts; operator-owned dynamic-plugins.yaml\n\nOn-prem operators need to install / remove / reconfigure plugins by\nrestarting the container — not by reinstalling the product or rebuilding\nthe image. Two image-level changes deliver that.\n\nPersist DevPortal state across a restart\n- app-config.production.yaml now declares an on-disk backend.database;\n  the image shipped :memory:, so every restart wiped marketplace and\n  catalog state.\n- Dockerfile and entrypoint create /app/data; mounting a volume there\n  keeps the per-plugin sqlite databases and the marketplace''s\n  extensions-install.yaml across a restart or image upgrade.\n- extensions-install.yaml moved under /app/data — the marketplace\n  rewrites it via a temp-file + atomic rename, which fails on a\n  single-file bind mount.\n- entrypoint clears a stale install-dynamic-plugins.lock at boot, so an\n  unclean shutdown (SIGKILL/OOM) cannot hang the next boot.\n- examples/deploy/docker-compose.yml: reference deployment showing the\n  volume contract.\n\ndynamic-plugins.yaml is the operator''s file\n- The includes: chain (catalog + marketplace + presets) is now assembled\n  by the entrypoint on every boot, with or without presets. This folds\n  the previous preset/no-preset split into one path and fixes a\n  no-preset boot that skipped the catalog.\n- dynamic-plugins.yaml ships as just `plugins: []`; an operator supplies\n  only a plugins: list. includes: is no longer an operator-facing surface.\n- Operator-facing comments and docs rewritten to drop internal\n  vocabulary (shadow, includes-ownership, etc.).\n\nVerified: boot matrix (no-preset / recommended / operator-override),\npersistence checks (cold boot, fast restart, marketplace install\nsurvives restart, stale-lock recovery), and smoke-presets.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(plugins): wire DEVPORTAL_DB_PATH through; validate operator YAML; doc cleanup\n\nAddresses PR review findings.\n\n- DEVPORTAL_DB_PATH is now honored everywhere, not just for the database.\n  The entrypoint and the marketplace''s extensions.installation.\n  saveToSingleFile.file both derive extensions-install.yaml''s location\n  from ${DEVPORTAL_DB_PATH:-/app/data}, so the variable relocates the\n  whole persistent surface, not just the sqlite files.\n- entrypoint validates the operator''s dynamic-plugins.yaml is well-formed\n  YAML and that the includes rewrite succeeds — aborts boot with exit 78\n  instead of silently booting without the catalog.\n- Dockerfile no longer bakes an unused /app/extensions-install.yaml; the\n  orphan root extensions-install.yaml is removed.\n- ROADMAP_BACKLOG.md / DEVELOPMENT_GUIDE.md: removed/corrected text that\n  described the now-fixed in-place-rewrite behaviour as still open.\n- installing.md: corrected the no-preset boot log line and the\n  app-config.local.yaml precedence claim.\n- Dropped stale entrypoint.sh line-number citations from operator docs.\n\nVerified: boot with default and custom DEVPORTAL_DB_PATH (state lands in\nthe configured directory, marketplace included), and malformed operator\nYAML aborts the boot with exit 78.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"70f5a767b0feccf7e9817374d58da9bac52e0723","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/git/trees/70f5a767b0feccf7e9817374d58da9bac52e0723"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/git/commits/fff52e539a16648e57d42fb1a4434a804682f659","verification":{"payload":"tree 70f5a767b0feccf7e9817374d58da9bac52e0723\nparent 14e49c7fed1ceaab5d5f9fef46b750851266b4ab\nauthor Giovani <giovanimcorrea18@gmail.com> 1779390140 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779390140 -0300\n\nfeat(plugins): persist plugin state across restarts; operator-owned dynamic-plugins.yaml (#33)\n\n* feat(plugins): persist plugin state across restarts; operator-owned dynamic-plugins.yaml\n\nOn-prem operators need to install / remove / reconfigure plugins by\nrestarting the container — not by reinstalling the product or rebuilding\nthe image. Two image-level changes deliver that.\n\nPersist DevPortal state across a restart\n- app-config.production.yaml now declares an on-disk backend.database;\n  the image shipped :memory:, so every restart wiped marketplace and\n  catalog state.\n- Dockerfile and entrypoint create /app/data; mounting a volume there\n  keeps the per-plugin sqlite databases and the marketplace''s\n  extensions-install.yaml across a restart or image upgrade.\n- extensions-install.yaml moved under /app/data — the marketplace\n  rewrites it via a temp-file + atomic rename, which fails on a\n  single-file bind mount.\n- entrypoint clears a stale install-dynamic-plugins.lock at boot, so an\n  unclean shutdown (SIGKILL/OOM) cannot hang the next boot.\n- examples/deploy/docker-compose.yml: reference deployment showing the\n  volume contract.\n\ndynamic-plugins.yaml is the operator''s file\n- The includes: chain (catalog + marketplace + presets) is now assembled\n  by the entrypoint on every boot, with or without presets. This folds\n  the previous preset/no-preset split into one path and fixes a\n  no-preset boot that skipped the catalog.\n- dynamic-plugins.yaml ships as just `plugins: []`; an operator supplies\n  only a plugins: list. includes: is no longer an operator-facing surface.\n- Operator-facing comments and docs rewritten to drop internal\n  vocabulary (shadow, includes-ownership, etc.).\n\nVerified: boot matrix (no-preset / recommended / operator-override),\npersistence checks (cold boot, fast restart, marketplace install\nsurvives restart, stale-lock recovery), and smoke-presets.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(plugins): wire DEVPORTAL_DB_PATH through; validate operator YAML; doc cleanup\n\nAddresses PR review findings.\n\n- DEVPORTAL_DB_PATH is now honored everywhere, not just for the database.\n  The entrypoint and the marketplace''s extensions.installation.\n  saveToSingleFile.file both derive extensions-install.yaml''s location\n  from ${DEVPORTAL_DB_PATH:-/app/data}, so the variable relocates the\n  whole persistent surface, not just the sqlite files.\n- entrypoint validates the operator''s dynamic-plugins.yaml is well-formed\n  YAML and that the includes rewrite succeeds — aborts boot with exit 78\n  instead of silently booting without the catalog.\n- Dockerfile no longer bakes an unused /app/extensions-install.yaml; the\n  orphan root extensions-install.yaml is removed.\n- ROADMAP_BACKLOG.md / DEVELOPMENT_GUIDE.md: removed/corrected text that\n  described the now-fixed in-place-rewrite behaviour as still open.\n- installing.md: corrected the no-preset boot log line and the\n  app-config.local.yaml precedence claim.\n- Dropped stale entrypoint.sh line-number citations from operator docs.\n\nVerified: boot with default and custom DEVPORTAL_DB_PATH (state lands in\nthe configured directory, marketplace included), and malformed operator\nYAML aborts the boot with exit 78.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqD1a8CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKXUQAJpvX1xXYAOo7x4Bxzg9H+q0\nA4elTbgbIiE5QHn+S8Yc6GdllQJM5+MeuROkw5Jn9Z0cP5O0JVgQ/2gUGhI5HooY\nnY2GvYjd6Sp2o3oBBCS4rFD1D9koLv08jHVNclU8oRfWdHN1nBDj4r4cvEYSrPhQ\n1YFccKgraLpK+bx7E66z0rzd2Odui/94Ags49xte44kgXyrenaz5R+Iz21Orn0NE\n7qHrDAPhf5WdmTgkipgpBR8x8qCSKtXKxS45UfPo4uCHHAgnTyulhYFTBqdBKqa/\nEIr8fB/nFIDMpFM+e1OmgyrGAsIhrJKDOBt9Tr3G1DscAQ9Kc4sdKTn7WhTW4SqD\nzbyiprW/SGN7GEE3CUi12DvOFm+3i1AGmIYH90rz2x3T2gB2TvcxzDU/EXfPVd11\nmlPyIRkjorFxqY5WBWyG0FGZ7XDII3L+kwqgQgbPVGV/WvrBxPqX6T2Zwd4+9xIH\nQwpeRsUsYIdWn2+b+fWCusyYnPP62JSdENLIOXO5hsdQV7ti+GAgURbuvmJbXvTe\nb0oLqmnGaaCVxuRpE9HLvUXocyAR3hKlzIiHZJYJrdw7e9e/w9+Tc/qQUYaBv6au\nllmWc+pQ2yNTPRbLE1iN+GSvtCnh5YvVBkMU8G2OcCibFy+jam5za1hDZh8/R7AD\nnzUqdEtUhcuooMsqvO7Y\n=Uk3I\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-21T19:02:21Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commit/fff52e539a16648e57d42fb1a4434a804682f659","node_id":"C_kwDOSc5yKNoAKGZmZjUyZTUzOWExNjY0OGU1N2Q0MmZiMWE0NDM0YTgwNDY4MmY2NTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commit/14e49c7fed1ceaab5d5f9fef46b750851266b4ab","sha":"14e49c7fed1ceaab5d5f9fef46b750851266b4ab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commits/14e49c7fed1ceaab5d5f9fef46b750851266b4ab"}],"sha":"fff52e539a16648e57d42fb1a4434a804682f659","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commits/fff52e539a16648e57d42fb1a4434a804682f659"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63979266?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Elesiann","id":63979266,"login":"Elesiann","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzOTc5MjY2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commits/14e49c7fed1ceaab5d5f9fef46b750851266b4ab/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-20T13:55:45Z","email":"giovanimcorrea18@gmail.com","name":"Giovani"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-20T13:55:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(plugins): clarify catalog model + how to enable a plugin (#30)\n\n* docs(plugins): clarify the catalog model and how to enable a plugin\n\nA maintainer asked how to \"import a known plugin\" now that the legacy\nembedded-plugins workspace is gone, and suspected the entrypoint bakes\nevery dynamic-plugins.default.yaml entry into the image. Neither the\nfile headers nor PLUGINS.md answered this — and the dynamic-plugins.yaml\nheader still described the old devportal-base download/wrapper model.\n\n- dynamic-plugins.default.yaml: rewrite the header to state it is a\n  CATALOG — disabled entries are skipped entirely at boot, presets or\n  the operator override enable them, only baked-plugins.json is built\n  into the image.\n- dynamic-plugins.yaml: replace the stale devportal-base header with an\n  accurate description of the includes chain + operator override.\n- PLUGINS.md: add \"Enabling a specific plugin\" — the three cases\n  (preset / catalog plugin via override / plugin not in the catalog).\n\nNo behaviour change; verified install-dynamic-plugins.py:359-362 skips\ndisabled entries and docker/baked-plugins.json lists exactly 4 baked\nplugins.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci: skip comment lines in OCI ref validation\n\nThe new dynamic-plugins.default.yaml header describes `oci://...` example\nrefs in comments; the validation grep picked them up as real package refs\nand skopeo-failed on the literal placeholder. Drop full-line comments\nbefore extracting refs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"17f5123974cb7b0d025b4e955497ede49ad261ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/git/trees/17f5123974cb7b0d025b4e955497ede49ad261ad"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/git/commits/14e49c7fed1ceaab5d5f9fef46b750851266b4ab","verification":{"payload":"tree 17f5123974cb7b0d025b4e955497ede49ad261ad\nparent bc7f162b37202bb3e9966f5bd89189beaee0184a\nauthor Giovani <giovanimcorrea18@gmail.com> 1779285345 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779285345 -0300\n\ndocs(plugins): clarify catalog model + how to enable a plugin (#30)\n\n* docs(plugins): clarify the catalog model and how to enable a plugin\n\nA maintainer asked how to \"import a known plugin\" now that the legacy\nembedded-plugins workspace is gone, and suspected the entrypoint bakes\nevery dynamic-plugins.default.yaml entry into the image. Neither the\nfile headers nor PLUGINS.md answered this — and the dynamic-plugins.yaml\nheader still described the old devportal-base download/wrapper model.\n\n- dynamic-plugins.default.yaml: rewrite the header to state it is a\n  CATALOG — disabled entries are skipped entirely at boot, presets or\n  the operator override enable them, only baked-plugins.json is built\n  into the image.\n- dynamic-plugins.yaml: replace the stale devportal-base header with an\n  accurate description of the includes chain + operator override.\n- PLUGINS.md: add \"Enabling a specific plugin\" — the three cases\n  (preset / catalog plugin via override / plugin not in the catalog).\n\nNo behaviour change; verified install-dynamic-plugins.py:359-362 skips\ndisabled entries and docker/baked-plugins.json lists exactly 4 baked\nplugins.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci: skip comment lines in OCI ref validation\n\nThe new dynamic-plugins.default.yaml header describes `oci://...` example\nrefs in comments; the validation grep picked them up as real package refs\nand skopeo-failed on the literal placeholder. Drop full-line comments\nbefore extracting refs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqDb1hCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAfSsQADq7cNQZT2PPI4vm/gNcjE3s\nDOqdg4J6iwM/ON8iGNlxViSo8oaVc7I2zqpoQdJb5cNgjHDOXxxilaMXLOHRE8aM\n5L8aJ3Kj96geqEaoLH+vCVJZeAN4TpDACkPetMg9Nm/lyGWVLzYdlKIuvJVbf8F5\nfbw2waTSXa8vbFk2/TeqU5Rb6VVRjglpwfPDYFWWXSPYqFONbAlMNZaP7Ur6Ifoa\ndEpMUhOUpXti/B7YQbBP2nYemLnLyIXB+qGYAOXbxWZWx/NjuLX+MXLkVeUfHy+t\nWgh9JIZy47AO1eLqlHan9v+SdNsJDdjmPwBbDtQK/KU7iCqTI52e+PPdkVt8/E1c\nr/wVwk/ykWKmQzqkBGZTxWsEXxW/DcKpZ616mduWq41kaWrwC7n4ZcLTdiuleMwK\ncuCmWnHdaDpqcu3jmaYXBV8