tps://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63979266?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Elesiann","id":63979266,"login":"Elesiann","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzOTc5MjY2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Elesiann","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/commits/bc7f162b37202bb3e9966f5bd89189beaee0184a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-20T13:51:10Z","email":"giovanimcorrea18@gmail.com","name":"Giovani"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-20T13:51:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(plugins): detect duplicate dynamic-plugin refs at boot (#32)\n\n* docs(upgrade): clarify gap scope, env renames, and preset-owned config\n\nThe V0.11 operator-walkthrough bench flagged friction items in\nUPGRADING_FROM_BASE_DISTRO.md where the doc let an operator carry over\nconfig the preset already owns, or read the \"Gap\" column too broadly.\n\n- Quick reference: example now maps VEECODE_PROFILE=github to the full\n  github,github-auth composition the translation table mandates (was\n  github only — diverged from the table).\n- Translation table: a note that the \"Gap\" column scopes the\n  profile→preset translation only; app-config added beyond the profile\n  (branding, extra hosts, RBAC, catalog locations) carries over\n  independently. Plus an env-var-rename callout (GITHUB_TOKEN →\n  GITHUB_PAT) pointing at presets/*.yaml requires.variables as\n  authoritative.\n- New \"What the preset already configures\" section: the blocks an\n  operator should NOT copy over (integration base, catalog provider,\n  auth + signInPage, theme branding), so a stale carry-over doesn''t\n  drift against the preset.\n\nTwo V0.11 items deferred: the Helm Deployment/ConfigMap example (infra\nauthoring, own PR) and a branding-override how-to (three mechanisms,\nbelongs with ADR-011 theming docs, not a quick migration-guide note).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(plugins): detect duplicate dynamic-plugin refs at boot\n\nAn operator who enables a plugin a preset already enabled, but uses a\ndifferent `package` ref for it (different tag/typo), creates two distinct\nkeys in the merged plugin map — the same Module Federation bundle installs\ntwice and conflicts at runtime. install-dynamic-plugins.py now identifies\neach plugin by its OCI selector and aborts the boot when two enabled\nentries resolve to the same plugin via conflicting refs.\n\nAlso makes the install step boot-fatal: entrypoint.sh now checks the exit\ncode and exits 78 on any fatal install failure (duplicates, bad YAML,\nintegrity), instead of silently booting a half-installed plugin set.\n\nAdds the first unit tests for install-dynamic-plugins.py; guards the\nscript''s main() call so it is importable for testing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2bd1b54eb3e1f8892684dd375fbfbfc2b2142b53","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/git/trees/2bd1b54eb3e1f8892684dd375fbfbfc2b2142b53"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/veecode-platform/devportal-platform/git/commits/bc7f162b37202bb3e9966f5bd89189beaee0184a","verification":{"payload":"tree 2bd1b54eb3e1f8892684dd375fbfbfc2b2142b53\nparent 9ca0a33cd0889d5c8fda77004b23cdd767ddcfa3\nauthor Giovani <giovanimcorrea18@gmail.com> 1779285070 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779285070 -0300\n\nfix(plugins): detect duplicate dynamic-plugin refs at boot (#32)\n\n* docs(upgrade): clarify gap scope, env renames, and preset-owned config\n\nThe V0.11 operator-walkthrough bench flagged friction items in\nUPGRADING_FROM_BASE_DISTRO.md where the doc let an operator carry over\nconfig the preset already owns, or read the \"Gap\" column too broadly.\n\n- Quick reference: example now maps VEECODE_PROFILE=github to the full\n  github,github-auth composition the translation table mandates (was\n  github only — diverged from the table).\n- Translation table: a note that the \"Gap\" column scopes the\n  profile→preset translation only; app-config added beyond the profile\n  (branding, extra hosts, RBAC, catalog locations) carries over\n  independently. Plus an env-var-rename callout (GITHUB_TOKEN →\n  GITHUB_PAT) pointing at presets/*.yaml requires.variables as\n  authoritative.\n- New \"What the preset already configures\" section: the blocks an\n  operator should NOT copy over (integration base, catalog provider,\n  auth + signInPage, theme branding), so a stale carry-over doesn''t\n  drift against the preset.\n\nTwo V0.11 items deferred: the Helm Deployment/ConfigMap example (infra\nauthoring, own PR) and a branding-override how-to (three mechanisms,\nbelongs with ADR-011 theming docs, not a quick migration-guide note).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(plugins): detect duplicate dynamic-plugin refs at boot\n\nAn operator who enables a plugin a preset already enabled, but uses a\ndifferent `package` ref for it (different tag/typo), creates two distinct\nkeys in the merged plugin map — the same Module Federation bundle installs\ntwice and conflicts at runtime. install-dynamic-plugins.py now identifies\neach plugin by its OCI selector and aborts the boot when two enabled\nentries resolve to the same plugin via conflicting refs.\n\nAlso makes the install step boot-fatal: entrypoint.sh now checks the exit\ncode and exits 78 on any fatal install failure (duplicates, bad YAML,\nintegrity), instead of silently booting a half-installed plugin set.\n\nAdds the first unit tests for install-dynamic-plugins.py; guards the\nscript''s main() call so it is importable for testing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqDbxOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAn4YQAHPMw0CkDnqLLVPpKlQ3Yn9u\nzWdsmfKBSG/pmufK7L1Kek9CUTdP7APCHUPFwl2vuvuVdq3Lin3vfaH0SkSJxras\n9k0XtSwBcGOcbCeAmkz1Dk1YSiOJ58iC0s6yMCqrctxJgyB2nG6fzLlFNXhpIbtb\n+oxovYCiShkMAErkQDFAV/T9WdxFy1av6Y1kyItCVtvG2xMAzF2nddH1EueMUvxn\nDozf5aj2D6f5CK+y0HI6ePz2HH75z/7fiU3XiIo9Dg/snenYyxdQrrkW8I8eEtl5\n3oZvFHrGPBz1QarcqrBwzRfNC/zF0gjbDKJqJ1INfWr0iPXhozYXMAeb19EhDz/t\nNy3wNSkYUw+/7XHuVoGwzdLyJwfNahPVzBKwtJFE7gqeso3kxcuZBlpZ599i1rcP\nU5e/DdHxJOvgv7l5VMSleojXjLP/9VcJX53Y15YBuLIEKsLh9EXE9RFZeTeXPlQF\nfV63wU/IFdZdiDWIZRlA+30qJD2FzmtjInbcdiTD3LvJa2NEvIe3CczkArBhsh0P\nY+mucLoRol0X98yj98MoAFCgw/0ry3WaLwBBOEc4xGxo3608MK6OcTYlN1XAn0qr\n6+lvoURG2nlEaz7FsUSI8+uuc+5hTw11GKBWZOkLfcBSjZNqmBvoRrXvMd6A6DqW\n/oAa71YKWOvboHjpDDPo\n=tprx\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-20T13:51:12Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE