":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/millionco/deslop-js/commit/f5c637db360a92c4303f330a00c14573d7e6f3c5","node_id":"C_kwDOSc_djdoAKGY1YzYzN2RiMzYwYTkyYzQzMDNmMzMwYTAwYzE0NTczZDdlNmYzYzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/millionco/deslop-js/commit/eb62aac6c6214b766c3649f84904c22e64857c63","sha":"eb62aac6c6214b766c3649f84904c22e64857c63","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/millionco/deslop-js/commits/eb62aac6c6214b766c3649f84904c22e64857c63"}],"sha":"f5c637db360a92c4303f330a00c14573d7e6f3c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/millionco/deslop-js/commits/f5c637db360a92c4303f330a00c14573d7e6f3c5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17689267?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NisargIO","id":17689267,"login":"NisargIO","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3Njg5MjY3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/millionco/deslop-js/commits/eb62aac6c6214b766c3649f84904c22e64857c63/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-27T02:05:21Z","email":"awesomenisarg@gmail.com","name":"Nisarg Patel"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-27T02:05:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(deslop-js): port duplicate-blocks, complexity, feature-flags, TS smells, leaks + FP fixes (#12)\n\n* fix(deslop-js): narrow featureFlags matching to avoid DOM/test-harness API collisions\n\nTwo FP families found while scanning a wider corpus:\n\n1. Vercel Flags'' `flag` / `evaluate` matched any function with those names —\n   `runtime.evaluate(''Uint8Array'')` (vm2-style sandbox), `page.evaluate(...)`\n   (Playwright), and any unrelated local helper. Vercel Flags only ever\n   exposes `flag()` as a bare imported identifier, never as a method on\n   some client object; require the identifier callee AND the name to come\n   from a Vercel Flags import.\n\n2. Flagsmith''s `hasFeature` matched the DOM API\n   `document.implementation.hasFeature(''http://www.w3.org/TR/SVG11/feature#...'')`.\n   Skip chained member-expression callees (`a.b.c()`) — those plainly\n   aren''t an SDK client invocation.\n\nOn a 27-repo corpus, next.js featureFlags went from 10 (all FPs from\nplaywright/vm `evaluate` and similar) to 0; mobx from 3 to 1 (residual\ninside a bundled `react-with-addons.js` doc asset). Synthetic\nidentifier-style calls still match correctly.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(deslop-js): match bare ''stories.{ext}'' basename, not just ''*.stories.{ext}''\n\nStorybook supports two glob conventions for story files: the common\n`*.stories.{ts,tsx,...}` form and a directory-style `stories.{ts,tsx,...}`\nform picked up via custom globs. The regex was only catching the first.\nOne Story leak slipped through on storybookjs/storybook itself at\n`addons/vitest/src/stories.tsx`.\n\nMatch the basename against `^(.*\\.)?stories\\.(ext)$` case-insensitively\nso both conventions are skipped. Verified the residual storybook Story\nleak (1 → 0).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f32270581ae9c5aa7d3a3729b6c397be031a8ba7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/millionco/deslop-js/git/trees/f32270581ae9c5aa7d3a3729b6c397be031a8ba7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/millionco/deslop-js/git/commits/eb62aac6c6214b766c3649f84904c22e64857c63","verification":{"payload":"tree f32270581ae9c5aa7d3a3729b6c397be031a8ba7\nparent 3b44c2cc09b0d9efd82ed0c8835dfb71fb39d225\nauthor Nisarg Patel <awesomenisarg@gmail.com> 1779847521 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779847521 -0700\n\nfeat(deslop-js): port duplicate-blocks, complexity, feature-flags, TS smells, leaks + FP fixes (#12)\n\n* fix(deslop-js): narrow featureFlags matching to avoid DOM/test-harness API collisions\n\nTwo FP families found while scanning a wider corpus:\n\n1. Vercel Flags'' `flag` / `evaluate` matched any function with those names —\n   `runtime.evaluate(''Uint8Array'')` (vm2-style sandbox), `page.evaluate(...)`\n   (Playwright), and any unrelated local helper. Vercel Flags only ever\n   exposes `flag()` as a bare imported identifier, never as a method on\n   some client object; require the identifier callee AND the name to come\n   from a Vercel Flags import.\n\n2. Flagsmith''s `hasFeature` matched the DOM API\n   `document.implementation.hasFeature(''http://www.w3.org/TR/SVG11/feature#...'')`.\n   Skip chained member-expression callees (`a.b.c()`) — those plainly\n   aren''t an SDK client invocation.\n\nOn a 27-repo corpus, next.js featureFlags went from 10 (all FPs from\nplaywright/vm `evaluate` and similar) to 0; mobx from 3 to 1 (residual\ninside a bundled `react-with-addons.js` doc asset). Synthetic\nidentifier-style calls still match correctly.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(deslop-js): match bare ''stories.{ext}'' basename, not just ''*.stories.{ext}''\n\nStorybook supports two glob conventions for story files: the common\n`*.stories.{ts,tsx,...}` form and a directory-style `stories.{ts,tsx,...}`\nform picked up via custom globs. The regex was only catching the first.\nOne Story leak slipped through on storybookjs/storybook itself at\n`addons/vitest/src/stories.tsx`.\n\nMatch the basename against `^(.*\\.)?stories\\.(ext)$` case-insensitively\nso both conventions are skipped. Verified the residual storybook Story\nleak (1 → 0).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqFlFhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWNYQAEQ1iXdgoRXT+Uq5xcLeogvR\ntA7LhXJsvQEa6E3j7ypYsy8CJSFZCt1ybvzys34yMeUHxFpAybKCm+nzD80TUmbX\nAujc0s2FkdTvBYy7e7U5HGjKhZvJQSPA+k7ikaAJCU2VVzc+Fu9TJ8e8xktBj5rh\nzcEL6gv7jUm+6g8BvgxVYmzAsj0ubqI9v5vS4ag5YN5xF4ErfhdF4Bv8I1YSZbb+\n1HfjJspui/lQDaTzwPTNUQtP/bDSaqG0Yyy45kmKJbok35Cocls+qbSjanZp6qg+\n2xf750/WM5BgzbeN08u6F8lZ3Asx+DYkrFO7s/BbGQC092uvGTrXKlglh3rbHZKQ\nXz7hre5GiD9JXorJ0nfBHA/ZOR/it/7o2tQ01px1rPKo1BWf0PyS5fdGt4IwG4UV\n09RPS4d+/M+Z+VuT5U573jiKqkBQ3gpn0C9diuDrimQeveqVgizZLYntXNX5eH99\ndVuzZ3jaIlmu3/Fpzxd3aVOpVLXLH/ie3muAs+EltG/RamPWuYmYSCEGyFyWGM0E\ni59G96hkJA1HGhEJHZQPtnaEvD2TifjnwQEs8MO4Cn0XYj4RkeAgFzzGoX443FyZ\nsPCvL3guTfOGmyclJTgnLvjIUQGe/BAErGBQjeAKJB+QbF3ggssyb6WL8ynO+h57\niFdDq8f7vhtVcJPImUWe\n=EEG1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-27T02:05:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"h