DZmZmVkMmNmNTc0NGJlY2RlNWFkNTU0M2RkMDZiNzQwNzFjYTQ2OTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/millionco/deslop-js/commit/262761699ee8f73b76af66cd65fbacee933f2a17","sha":"262761699ee8f73b76af66cd65fbacee933f2a17","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/millionco/deslop-js/commits/262761699ee8f73b76af66cd65fbacee933f2a17"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/millionco/deslop-js/commit/1e8b4503b46acf22e3b89d073e45590f11d91828","sha":"1e8b4503b46acf22e3b89d073e45590f11d91828","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/millionco/deslop-js/commits/1e8b4503b46acf22e3b89d073e45590f11d91828"}],"sha":"6ffed2cf5744becde5ad5543dd06b74071ca4699","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/millionco/deslop-js/commits/6ffed2cf5744becde5ad5543dd06b74071ca4699"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/199161495?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cursoragent","id":199161495,"login":"cursoragent","node_id":"U_kgDOC972lw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/millionco/deslop-js/commits/1e8b4503b46acf22e3b89d073e45590f11d91828/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-26T05:48:48Z","email":"cursoragent@cursor.com","name":"Cursor Agent"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-26T05:48:48Z","email":"cursoragent@cursor.com","name":"Cursor Agent"},"message":"refactor(deslop-js): trim narrating comments, drop unnecessary type casts, extract shared utils\n\nAGENTS.md compliance pass on the new detectors:\n\n- Default-to-no-comments: removed inline narration, section dividers,\n  and doc blocks that just restated function names. Kept short doc\n  comments on public detector entry points where they document a\n  non-obvious filter rule (cross-file dup exports, re-export cycles,\n  shadowed-directory pairs) or a counter-intuitive invariant\n  (sentinel handling, FNV-1a tradeoff).\n\n- ''as'' casts: extended the AstNode type predicate with an index signature\n  ([field: string]: unknown) so AST traversal no longer needs\n  ''as Record<string, unknown>'' at every property access. Dropped 130+\n  call-site casts across 6 detectors plus one redundant\n  ''spanFallbackNode.start as number'' already narrowed by the\n  conditional.\n\n- DRY: extracted three shared utilities (one per file, per AGENTS rules):\n    utils/compute-line-starts.ts\n    utils/offset-to-line-column.ts\n    utils/is-ast-node.ts\n  Removed the local copies that had been duplicated across each\n  detector file.\n\n- CloneTokenKind -> SourceTokenKind to lose the last ''clone'' name.\n- Trimmed unused isReactLifecycleMethod / isAngularLifecycleMethod side\n  exports — only the combined predicate is used.\n\nBehavior unchanged. typecheck / build / lint clean. 443/443 tests pass.\n\nCo-authored-by: Aiden Bai <aidenybai@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"53002d259e1b3ed400cc54e4644899415e008833","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/millionco/deslop-js/git/trees/53002d259e1b3ed400cc54e4644899415e008833"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/millionco/deslop-js/git/commits/1e8b4503b46acf22e3b89d073e45590f11d91828","verification":{"payload":"tree 53002d259e1b3ed400cc54e4644899415e008833\nparent dc8c0c90fd8ce0ef7256b3ededfd40b4528a9c38\nauthor Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com> 1779774528 +0000\ncommitter Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com> 1779774528 +0000\n\nrefactor(deslop-js): trim narrating comments, drop unnecessary type casts, extract shared utils\n\nAGENTS.md compliance pass on the new detectors:\n\n- Default-to-no-comments: removed inline narration, section dividers,\n  and doc blocks that just restated function names. Kept short doc\n  comments on public detector entry points where they document a\n  non-obvious filter rule (cross-file dup exports, re-export cycles,\n  shadowed-directory pairs) or a counter-intuitive invariant\n  (sentinel handling, FNV-1a tradeoff).\n\n- ''as'' casts: extended the AstNode type predicate with an index signature\n  ([field: string]: unknown) so AST traversal no longer needs\n  ''as Record<string, unknown>'' at every property access. Dropped 130+\n  call-site casts across 6 detectors plus one redundant\n  ''spanFallbackNode.start as number'' already narrowed by the\n  conditional.\n\n- DRY: extracted three shared utilities (one per file, per AGENTS rules):\n    utils/compute-line-starts.ts\n    utils/offset-to-line-column.ts\n    utils/is-ast-node.ts\n  Removed the local copies that had been duplicated across each\n  detector file.\n\n- CloneTokenKind -> SourceTokenKind to lose the last ''clone'' name.\n- Trimmed unused isReactLifecycleMethod / isAngularLifecycleMethod side\n  exports — only the combined predicate is used.\n\nBehavior unchanged. typecheck / build / lint clean. 443/443 tests pass.\n\nCo-authored-by: Aiden Bai <aidenybai@users.noreply.github.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg+qImwGMCy/grKZ50VxRHz3VfWW\nAL3QNbzIy2Nwcn+nQAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQGOCeKWK0O9oDjAprU86BLbyRaay8itvsUa64j1X2+XbNXmTrqoHs7wVqpSTzAiv2k\nRzbucuMgLhzV51/c4GqA4=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-26T05:48:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/199161495?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cursoragent","id":199161495,"login":"cursoragent","node_id":"U_kgDOC972lw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/millionco/deslop-js/commit/1e8b4503b46acf22e3b89d073e45590f11d91828","node_id":"C_kwDOSc_djdoAKDFlOGI0NTAzYjQ2YWNmMjJlM2I4OWQwNzNlNDU1OTBmMTFkOTE4Mjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/millionco/deslop-js/commit/dc8c0c90fd8ce0ef7256b3ededfd40b4528a9c38","sha":"dc8c0c90fd8ce0ef7256b3ededfd40b4528a9c38","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/millionco/deslop-js/commits/dc8c0c90fd8ce0ef7256b3ededfd40b4528a9c38"}],"sha":"1e8b4503b46acf22e3b89d073e45590f11d91828","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/millionco/deslop-js/commits/1e8b4503b46acf22e3b89d073e45590f11d91828"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17689267?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NisargIO","id":17689267,"login":"NisargIO","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3Njg5MjY3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/millionco/deslop-js/commits/dc8c0c90fd8ce0ef7256b3ededfd40b4528a9c38/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-26T02:50:23Z","email":"awesomenisarg@gmail.com","name":"Nisarg Patel"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-26T02:50:23Z","email":"awesomenisarg@gmail.com","name":"Nisarg Patel"},"message":"fix(deslop-js): skip *.stories.* files in privateTypeLeaks\n\nStorybook CSF3 authoring convention declares `type Story = StoryObj<typeof meta>`\nas a local alias and exports each story as `Primary: Story = { ... }`. The\nStorybook runtime consumes the default export, so the `Story` alias is\nintentionally module-local — consumers never import it.\n\nOn storybook itself, the detector previously emitted 933 leaks of which\n913 (97.9%) were this single pattern. After this fix the same scan emits\n14 leaks, all from non-story files and pointing at real public-signature\nreferences to non-exported types.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a55ead026355687c9500c9dbfa8078a1af88cddd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/millionco/deslop-js/git/trees/a55ead026355687c9500c9dbfa8078a1af88cddd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/millionco/deslop-js/git/commits/dc8c0c90fd8ce0ef7256b3ededfd40b4528a9c38","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17689267?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NisargIO","id":17689267,"login":"NisargIO","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3Njg5MjY3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/millionco/deslop-js/commit/dc8c0c90fd8ce0ef7256b3ededfd40b4528a9c38","node_id":"C_kwDOSc_djdoAKGRjOGMwYzkwZmQ4Y2UwZWY3MjU2YjNlZGVkZmQ0MGI0NTI4YTljMzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/millionco/deslop-js/commit/afd49435bf2d7731c6b3e5ca5c4804993d99e918","sha":"afd49435bf2d7731c6b3e5ca5c4804993d99e918","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/millionco/deslop-js/commits/afd49435bf2d7731c6b3e5ca5c4804993d99e918"}],"sha":"dc8c0c90fd8ce0ef7256b3ededfd40b4528a9c38","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/millionco/deslop-js/commits/dc8c0c90fd8ce0ef7256b3ededfd40b4528a9c38"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17689267?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NisargIO","id":17689267,"login":"NisargIO","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3Njg5MjY3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/millionco/deslop-js/commits/afd49435bf2d7731c6b3e5ca5c4804993d99e918/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-26T02:49:24Z","email":"awesomenisarg@gmail.com","name":"Nisarg Patel"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-26T02:49:24Z","email":"awesomenisarg@gmail.com","name":"Nisarg Patel"},"message":"fix(deslop-js): detect @ts-*/escape-hatch markers in comments only, not in strings\n\nSwitched typeScriptEscapeHatches from a regex over raw source text to a\nwalk of oxc-parser''s comments array. Strings and template literals that\nquote the directives (`use // @ts-ignore`, `@ts-nocheck example`) are no\nlonger flagged. Real annotations still detected with the same line/column.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bb8458a2e302e7fbf4fbf67b50f84185f9b00aad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/millionco/deslop-js/git/trees/bb8458a2e302e7fbf4fbf67b50f84185f9b00aad"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/millionco/deslop-js/git/commits/afd49435bf2d7731c6b3e5ca5c4804993d99e918","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17689267?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NisargIO","id":17689267,"login":"NisargIO","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3Njg5MjY3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/millionco/deslop-js/commit/afd49435bf2d7731c6b3e5ca5c4804993d99e918","node_id":"C_kwDOSc_djdoAKGFmZDQ5NDM1YmYyZDc3MzFjNmIzZTVjYTVjNDgwNDk5M2Q5OWU5MTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/millionco/deslop-js/commit/2f1c05477298a28196d79a5de8e06fc0ed619c12","sha":"2f1c05477298a28196d79a5de8e06fc0ed619c12","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/millionco/deslop-js/commits/2f1c05477298a28196d79a5de8e06fc0ed619c12"}],"sha":"afd49435bf2d7731c6b3e5ca5c4804993d99e918","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/millionco/deslop-js/commits/afd49435bf2d7731c6b3e5ca5c4804993d99e918"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17689267?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NisargIO","id":17689267,"login":"NisargIO","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3Njg5MjY3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/millionco/deslop-js/commits/2f1c05477298a28196d79a5de8e06fc0ed619c12/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-26T02:47:53Z","email":"awesomenisarg@gmail.com","name":"Nisarg Patel"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-26T02:47:53Z","email":"awesomenisarg@gmail.com","name":"Nisarg Patel"},"message":"fix(deslop-js): gate duplicate-block extract-module hint on cross-file clusters\n\nA cluster whose only file is itself cannot be refactored into \"a shared\nmodule\" — there''s no second consumer. Single-file clusters now always get\nan extract-function hint (one per block) instead. The module-extraction\nthreshold still applies but only when files.length >= 2.\n\nBefore this fix, 51/68 tldraw editor clusters were single-file but still\nemitted \"Extract … into a shared module\" suggestions.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d47e551f29ec8839e06f6fd4aeeb48952868add9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/millionco/deslop-js/git/trees/d47e551f29ec8839e06f6fd4aeeb48952868add9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/millionco/deslop-js/git/commits/2f1c05477298a28196d79a5de8e06fc0ed619c12","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17689267?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NisargIO","id":17689267,"login":"NisargIO","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3Njg5MjY3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/millionco/deslop-js/commit/2f1c05477298a28196d79a5de8e06fc0ed619c12","node_id":"C_kwDOSc_djdoAKDJmMWMwNTQ3NzI5OGEyODE5NmQ3OWE1ZGU4ZTA2ZmMwZWQ2MTljMTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/millionco/deslop-js/commit/2cb886e69a0b26fe057116a9384d4938c939d4f2","sha":"2cb886e69a0b26fe057116a9384d4938c939d4f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/millionco/deslop-js/commits/2cb886e69a0b26fe057116a9384d4938c939d4f2"}],"sha":"2f1c05477298a28196d79a5de8e06fc0ed619c12","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/millionco/deslop-js/commits/2f1c05477298a28196d79a5de8e06fc0ed619c12"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17689267?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NisargIO","id":17689267,"login":"NisargIO","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3Njg5MjY3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/millionco/deslop-js/commits/2cb886e69a0b26fe057116a9384d4938c939d4f2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-26T02:47:00Z","email":"awesomenisarg@gmail.com","name":"Nisarg Patel"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-26T02:47:00Z","email":"awesomenisarg@gmail.com","name":"Nisarg Patel"},"message":"fix(deslop-js): drop duplicate-block siblings subsumed by a longer match\n\nThe suffix-array + LCP-interval scan emits one block per LCP interval, so\nnested intervals report the same set of source spans at multiple lengths\n(L, L-1, L-2, …). Without filtering, output blew up ~6× on every repo\ntested — and on storybook the JSON exceeded V8''s max string length and\ncrashed JSON.stringify outright.\n\nPost-filter pass: sort blocks by tokenCount desc and drop any whose every\ninstance is spatially contained in an already-kept block''s matching\ninstance. Measured impact across 13 repos:\n\n  bippy:        1947 → 100   blocks  (6.1× → 1.01×)\n  tldraw editor:14344 → 631  blocks  (6.0× → 1.01×) — 32 MB → 1.9 MB\n  storybook:    crashed → 5563 blocks (~30× fewer, 36 MB JSON)\n  react-scan:   2636 → 357   blocks\n  next bundle-analyzer: 716 → 91 blocks\n\nAll 443 unit tests still pass.","tree":{"sha":"1de3d8a614ec0c28c3e4b221c0bed74eb151c302","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/millionco/deslop-js/git/trees/1de3d8a614ec0c28c3e4b221c0bed74eb151c302"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/millionco/deslop-js/git/commits/2cb886e69a0b26fe057116a9384d4938c939d4f2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17689267?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NisargIO","id":17689267,"login":"NisargIO","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3Njg5MjY3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NisargIO","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/millionco/deslop-js/commit/2cb886e69a0b26fe057116a9384d4938c939d4f2","node_id":"C_kwDOSc_djdoAKDJjYjg4NmU2OWEwYjI2ZmUwNTcxMTZhOTM4NGQ0OTM4YzkzOWQ0ZjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/millionco/deslop-js/commit/cd2b2ce118dc8c99bc4c48e9c6d8fdf66768cdbc","sha":"cd2b2ce118dc8c99bc4c48e9c6d8fdf66768cdbc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/millionco/deslop-js/commits/cd2b2ce118dc8c99bc4c48e9c6d8fdf66768cdbc"}],"sha":"2cb886e69a0b26fe057116a9384d4938c939d4f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/millionco/deslop-js/commits/2cb886e69a0b26fe057116a9384d4938c939d4f2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/199161495?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cursoragent","id":199161495,"login":"cursoragent","node_id":"U_kgDOC972lw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/millionco/deslop-js/commits/cd2b2ce118dc8c99bc4c48e9c6d8fdf66768cdbc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-26T02:03:45Z","email":"cursoragent@cursor.com","name":"Cursor Agent"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-26T02:03:45Z","email":"cursoragent@cursor.com","name":"Cursor Agent"},"message":"feat(deslop-js)!: rename CodeClone* to DuplicateBlock*, enable detectors by default\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: rename and default-enable opt-in detectors.\n\nRenames (no behavioral change beyond naming):\n\n- CodeClone           -> DuplicateBlock\n- CodeCloneInstance   -> DuplicateBlockOccurrence\n- CodeCloneFamily     -> DuplicateBlockCluster\n- CodeCloneRefactoringSuggestion -> DuplicateBlockRefactoringHint\n- CodeCloneRefactoringKind       -> DuplicateBlockRefactoringKind\n- CodeCloneMode       -> DuplicateBlockDetectionMode\n- CodeClonesConfig    -> DuplicateBlocksConfig\n- MirroredDirectory   -> ShadowedDirectoryPair\n\nScanResult fields:\n- result.codeClones            -> result.duplicateBlocks\n- result.codeCloneFamilies     -> result.duplicateBlockClusters\n- result.mirroredDirectories   -> result.shadowedDirectoryPairs\n\nConfig:\n- defineConfig({ codeClones: ... })   -> defineConfig({ duplicateBlocks: ... })\n\nModule path:\n- src/clones/                  -> src/duplicate-blocks/\n- src/clones/families.ts       -> src/duplicate-blocks/clusters.ts\n- src/clones/mirrored-directories.ts -> src/duplicate-blocks/shadowed-directory-pairs.ts\n\nDefault behavior changes (BREAKING):\n\n- duplicateBlocks.enabled now defaults to true (was false)\n- featureFlags.enabled now defaults to true (was false)\n- complexity.enabled now defaults to true (was false)\n- semantic.enabled now defaults to true (was false). Loads the TS\n  program if a tsconfig.json is found; gracefully no-ops on JS-only\n  projects. Disable with semantic: { enabled: false } to skip the\n  ~1-3s program load.\n\nMigration: pass { enabled: false } to disable any individual detector.\n\nTests for the previous off-by-default semantics flipped to assert\nthe user can disable each detector via { enabled: false }.\n\nAlso reworks the README''s feature-flag section to spell out what the\ndetector does end-to-end and the actionable workflow (cross-reference\nresult.featureFlags with your live flag dashboard to retire dead\nflags and delete code their guards make unreachable).\n\nCo-authored-by: Aiden Bai <aidenybai@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"60ea6c683d421e74cabb9536c87db004c350b163","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/millionco/deslop-js/git/trees/60ea6c683d421e74cabb9536c87db004c350b163"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/millionco/deslop-js/git/commits/cd2b2ce118dc8c99bc4c48e9c6d8fdf66768cdbc","verification":{"payload":"tree 60ea6c683d421e74cabb9536c87db004c350b163\nparent 6cf9ade1109ad2cd7402f040e4ee897ba065a1d2\nauthor Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com> 1779761025 +0000\ncommitter Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com> 1779761025 +0000\n\nfeat(deslop-js)!: rename CodeClone* to DuplicateBlock*, enable detectors by default\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: rename and default-enable opt-in detectors.\n\nRenames (no behavioral change beyond naming):\n\n- CodeClone           -> DuplicateBlock\n- CodeCloneInstance   -> DuplicateBlockOccurrence\n- CodeCloneFamily     -> DuplicateBlockCluster\n- CodeCloneRefactoringSuggestion -> DuplicateBlockRefactoringHint\n- CodeCloneRefactoringKind       -> DuplicateBlockRefactoringKind\n- CodeCloneMode       -> DuplicateBlockDetectionMode\n- CodeClonesConfig    -> DuplicateBlocksConfig\n- MirroredDirectory   -> ShadowedDirectoryPair\n\nScanResult fields:\n- result.codeClones            -> result.duplicateBlocks\n- result.codeCloneFamilies     -> result.duplicateBlockClusters\n- result.mirroredDirectories   -> result.shadowedDirectoryPairs\n\nConfig:\n- defineConfig({ codeClones: ... })   -> defineConfig({ duplicateBlocks: ... })\n\nModule path:\n- src/clones/                  -> src/duplicate-blocks/\n- src/clones/families.ts       -> src/duplicate-blocks/clusters.ts\n- src/clones/mirrored-directories.ts -> src/duplicate-blocks/shadowed-directory-pairs.ts\n\nDefault behavior changes (BREAKING):\n\n- duplicateBlocks.enabled now defaults to true (was false)\n- featureFlags.enabled now defaults to true (was false)\n- complexity.enabled now defaults to true (was false)\n- semantic.enabled now defaults to true (was false). Loads the TS\n  program if a tsconfig.json is found; gracefully no-ops on JS-only\n  projects. Disable with semantic: { enabled: false } to skip the\n  ~1-3s program load.\n\nMigration: pass { enabled: false } to disable any individual detector.\n\nTests for the previous off-by-default semantics flipped to assert\nthe user can disable each detector via { enabled: false }.\n\nAlso reworks the README''s feature-flag section to spell out what the\ndetector does end-to-end and the actionable workflow (cross-reference\nresult.featureFlags with your live flag dashboard to retire dead\nflags and delete code their guards make unreachable).\n\nCo-authored-by: Aiden Bai <aidenybai@users.noreply.github.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg+qImwGMCy/grKZ50VxRHz3VfWW\nAL3QNbzIy2Nwcn+nQAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQEdm5xJORB13MfOTWDZJwBWCueushEICnsquLbOQN+KGNWLs8GG8LuAvZrydFtk5uB\ncpC10x+SCk4x1Xv/2QKAg=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-26T02:03:47Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/199161495?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursoragent/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://githu